/* Automatisch erzeugt – KI-übersetzt, nicht von Hand bearbeiten. */
window.MTEC_NEWS_I18N = {"_info": {"sprache": "en", "hinweis": "KI-übersetzt aus dem Deutschen. _src = Prüfsumme des deutschen Originals; weicht sie ab, zeigt die Website das deutsche Original (scripts/update-news.mjs check warnt)."}, "2026-11-23-gta5-rdr2-steam-boom": {"titel": "Since GTA 6 launched on consoles, player numbers for GTA 5 Enhanced and Red Dead Redemption 2 on Steam have risen sharply, a PC version of GTA 6 is still not announced", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 console-only: PC players flock to GTA 5 and Red Dead 2 on Steam", "kurz": "Since GTA 6 was released for consoles on November 19, significantly more people are playing GTA 5 and Red Dead Redemption 2 on Steam. According to PC Games, the peak for GTA 5 Enhanced rose from around 78,000 to almost 138,000 concurrent players. A PC version of GTA 6 is still not announced.", "zusammenfassung": "PC Games compared the Steam player numbers of Rockstar's games before and after the launch of GTA 6. On November 14, the peak for GTA 5 Enhanced was just over 78,000 concurrent players, and in the days after November 19 it was 137,993. The older Legacy version of GTA 5 also grew by around 38 percent. Red Dead Redemption 2 rose from around 40,000 to almost 70,000 concurrent players, an increase of about 75 percent. This briefly put the western back in the Steam top 25. GTA 4 is also seeing more players, according to PC Games. Why the numbers are rising is not proven. PC Games suspects that PC players without GTA 6 are turning to the older Rockstar games, which is an interpretation and not evidence. Rockstar has not announced a PC version of GTA 6 so far.", "_src": "4e013a76"}, "2026-11-23-windows-server-2028-ohne-32-bit": {"titel": "Windows Server 2028 no longer includes the WoW64 subsystem for 32-bit programs by default, it can be added back as a Feature on Demand, Windows 11 is not affected for now", "schlagzeile": "The end for 32-bit apps? Windows Server 2028 leaves them out by default", "kurz": "Windows Server 2028 will ship without the WoW64 subsystem that lets 32-bit programs run on 64-bit Windows. Anyone who needs it can install it later. Microsoft has not announced such a step for Windows 11 so far.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Windows Latest, Microsoft presented the change at Ignite 2026. Windows Server 2028 is due in fall 2027 alongside Windows 11 27H2. There, WoW64 becomes a Feature on Demand that administrators can add back for old 32-bit business applications. Microsoft justifies the step with security, above all against 32-bit malware. At the same time, Microsoft wants to ship Windows Server secure by default and apply the security baselines out of the box, starting with Server Core. SMB1 and VBScript are to be removed, and dropping legacy BIOS is also being considered. As background, Microsoft cites AI tools that find security flaws at a high pace, and very old components that cannot be secured without a rewrite. Windows 11 keeps WoW64 for now. Because Server and Windows 11 share the same code, Windows Latest considers a similar step later possible, but that is only an assessment. Many programs still use 32-bit parts, according to Windows Latest a Steam service, for example. Which programs on your own PC are 32-bit is shown by Task Manager in the Details view under Platform.", "_src": "af5a85c4"}, "2026-11-23-activision-patent-voice-chat-npc": {"titel": "Activision patent application describes how players' reactions in voice chat are recorded and used to make computer-controlled characters react like humans", "schlagzeile": "Activision patent: Should NPCs learn from your voice chat?", "kurz": "Activision has filed a patent application under which player reactions from voice chat would train a neural network. Computer-controlled characters could then cheer or curse like real players. Whether Activision will ever use this in a game is open.", "zusammenfassung": "The application is titled “Methods and Systems for Applying Machine Learning to Generate Gameplay Audio” and was published by the US Patent Office on November 12. The site Patentlyze drew attention to it, and TechPowerUp reports on it. The system detects important game moments such as a kill or one's own death and records the voice chat shortly before and after. As an example, the description cites ten seconds each. As possible sources, the application names separate voice apps such as Discord, with game and chat matched via timestamps. Using these pairs of moment and reaction, a neural network is meant to learn what believable reactions sound like. Offensive content is to be filtered out beforehand, and a player profile is meant to select the right language, for example. According to Patentlyze, the application is a continuation of an application from December 2023, on which, according to the patent database Justia, a patent was already granted in August 2026. According to Patentlyze, the application does not describe how players are supposed to give consent. A patent is not a product announcement, and Activision has not named any plans for a game.", "weitere_links": ["Patentlyze", "Justia Patents (Activision)"], "_src": "651066d6"}, "2026-11-23-gta6-gedenkstaette-entwickler": {"titel": "In GTA 6, a memorial honors late relatives of Rockstar developers, and players can visit the site", "schlagzeile": "Touching: GTA 6 hides a memorial for the late relatives of its makers", "kurz": "A memorial in GTA 6 bears the names of late relatives of Rockstar developers. Two developers made this public themselves. Players can visit the place in Leonida.", "zusammenfassung": "A Rockstar quality assurance employee wrote on Instagram that his mother is immortalized in the memorial. She had died eight months before GTA 6 launched. According to his post, she bought him Vice City as a child, which ultimately led him to Rockstar. A production designer shared on X that his father and his daughter, both of whom he lost during development, are also listed there. According to IGN, the place is called Deep Roots Memorial Sanctuary and lies north of Hamlet. Further names are written on a wall. Whether all names belong to developers' relatives is unclear. Rockstar itself has not commented. So anyone visiting will find it not as an Easter egg, but as a quiet remembrance by the team.", "_src": "6bd0be55"}, "2026-11-23-linux-7-4-rc4": {"titel": "Linux 7.4-rc4 is out, Torvalds calls the test candidate huge, and it also includes the CPU IDs for Intel's Razor Lake and Coral Rapids", "schlagzeile": "Linux 7.4-rc4 is “huge” – and already knows Intel's Razor Lake", "kurz": "Linus Torvalds has released the fourth test candidate for Linux 7.4. He calls it huge, and half of the changes concern drivers. New additions include the CPU identifiers for Intel's upcoming Razor Lake and Coral Rapids processors.", "zusammenfassung": "Torvalds writes in his announcement that rc4 is huge, which is no surprise. Around half of the many small fixes concern drivers, above all graphics and networking, but also USB, NVMe and sound. The rest is spread across core components, memory management, file systems and architectures. According to Phoronix, AI-generated bug reports and patches continue to drive the volume in this cycle. New are the family and model identifiers for Intel's Razor Lake client processors and Coral Rapids server CPUs. Such IDs are preparation and say nothing yet about release dates. In addition, the kernel now removes NVMe namespaces in parallel, which should speed up operations. According to Phoronix, the final Linux 7.4 is expected at the end of December. This is a test version and not intended for everyday use.", "weitere_links": ["LWN.net"], "_src": "606846f3"}, "2026-11-23-windows-wlan-treiber-user-mode": {"titel": "Microsoft wants to move Wi-Fi drivers out of the Windows kernel into user mode in 2027, so that a faulty driver no longer crashes the whole system", "schlagzeile": "No more Wi-Fi blue screens? Microsoft moves drivers out of the kernel in 2027", "kurz": "Starting in 2027, Wi-Fi drivers on Windows are to run in user mode instead of the kernel. A Microsoft manager confirmed this at Ignite 2026, reports Windows Latest. If such a driver crashes, Windows should keep running.", "zusammenfassung": "Today Wi-Fi drivers run in the kernel, so a bug can bring down the whole PC with a blue screen. Microsoft therefore announced an initiative for better driver quality in May. At Ignite 2026, Windows product manager Mehmet Kucukgoz said, according to Windows Latest, that work on Wi-Fi is underway and is due to be released in 2027. The basis is the User-Mode Driver Framework, which has existed since 2004 and is already used today for sensors, fingerprint readers, USB, Ethernet and input devices, for example. What is new is DMA support in user mode, which according to Microsoft should allow more device types without a loss of performance. Not every driver can move, as Microsoft itself admits. For drivers that stay in the kernel, Microsoft is working on more secure compiler options, driver isolation and DMA remapping. An exact date or which Windows version will get the change is not known. Whether Wi-Fi drivers in user mode add noticeable latency remains to be seen. Wi-Fi chip makers will have to adapt their drivers for this. Microsoft recently also paved the way for antivirus software to leave the kernel.", "_src": "37cb6578"}, "2026-11-23-gta6-darts-koerpertypen-rockstar": {"titel": "Rockstar explains in interviews why darts is missing from GTA 6, and that the many body types of the characters required a dedicated animation team", "schlagzeile": "No darts in GTA 6: Rockstar says it simply didn't have enough time", "kurz": "Darts is missing from GTA 6 because, according to Rockstar, it did not have enough time and money to do it well enough. Rockstar North co-studio head Rob Nelson told VGC this. In another interview, Rockstar explains that the characters' many body shapes needed a dedicated team.", "zusammenfassung": "Darts was playable in GTA 4, GTA 5 and GTA Online, and bowling in GTA 4. Rob Nelson told VGC that darts was a contentious decision. Even Rockstar does not have unlimited money or unlimited time, and sometimes you have to admit you cannot bring something to the level you want. Since Red Dead Redemption 2, Rockstar has built mini-games as activities that are meant to feel like an extension of the game mechanics. As examples, Nelson cites pool with real physics, weightlifting and basketball. It is better to leave something out than to not do it well enough, Nelson said. In an interview with IGN, reported on by PC Gamer, head of animation Mark Tennant spoke about the characters' many body types. To make animations work between characters of different sizes, for example when getting into vehicles or in melee combat, Rockstar developed new techniques. A dedicated team was built for this, working closely with the art and rigging teams. Rockstar has not said whether darts might be added later. The VGC interview was already published on November 19, and IGN picked it up on November 22.", "weitere_links": ["IGN", "PC Gamer (body types)"], "_src": "5ac7f2a4"}, "2026-11-23-dota2-patch-7-42": {"titel": "Valve releases Dota 2 patch 7.42 with more base health, passive experience and an item that summons mega creeps in all lanes", "schlagzeile": "Dota 2 patch 7.42: New item sends mega creeps down every lane", "kurz": "Valve has released patch 7.42 for Dota 2. A new item from the Tormentor summons mega creeps in all of your own lanes. Several changes could shorten matches, according to PC Gamer.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Valve's patch notes, patch 7.42 has been available since November 18, and PC Gamer has put the most important changes into context. The Tormentor now always drops the consumable Greater Horn of Battle. It summons a wave of mega creeps on each of your own lanes. According to PC Gamer, players have noticed that the stats do not quite match real mega creeps. The base health of all heroes rises from 120 to 200, while each point of strength gives slightly less health. Heroes are therefore sturdier early in the game but somewhat more vulnerable later. In addition, all heroes passively receive 50 experience points per minute after the start. At the same time, the experience needed for level 30 increases. PC Gamer compares the new item with similar objectives in League of Legends and Deadlock. Whether matches will really get shorter remains to be seen.", "weitere_links": ["Dota 2 (patch notes 7.42)"], "_src": "9466bf29"}, "2026-11-23-tlou2-twelve-weeks-mod": {"titel": "Fan mod Twelve Weeks brings a free 4v4 multiplayer mode in the style of Factions to The Last of Us Part II Remastered on PC", "schlagzeile": "The Last of Us Part II gets multiplayer on PC – via a free fan mod", "kurz": "The free fan mod Twelve Weeks adds team multiplayer to The Last of Us Part II Remastered on PC. Matches are 4 versus 4 in the style of the 2013 Factions mode. Around two months ago, Sony stopped a different multiplayer mod before its release.", "zusammenfassung": "According to its makers, Twelve Weeks is an unofficial fan project with no connection to Sony or Naughty Dog. You need your own Steam copy of The Last of Us Part II Remastered, and the mod says it contains no game files. Two teams of WLF and Seraphites face off in the Supply Raid and Interrogation modes. There is also crafting, melee and a clan system in which every match represents one day out of twelve weeks. At launch there are twelve maps from the campaign, and maps from Part I are to follow later via import from your own game. There are servers in Europe and on the US West Coast, and the server code is on GitHub. The mod runs on Windows 10 and 11 as well as on Linux and the Steam Deck. According to Wccftech, the makers admit to having relied heavily on the AI tool Claude Code for programming. The mod has been in development since the second half of September. Around two months ago, Sony had modder Speclizer's multiplayer mod stopped before release, and he was earning money from it via Patreon. Whether Sony will also take action against Twelve Weeks is open.", "weitere_links": ["Twelve Weeks (project page)", "Nexus Mods"], "_src": "1283fede"}, "2026-11-23-gta6-pc-cpu-60fps-hochrechnung": {"titel": "Hardware Unboxed projection: 60 fps in a PC version of GTA 6 would need roughly twice the CPU performance of the PS5, and even a Ryzen 7 5800X3D could narrowly fall short", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 at 60 fps on PC: Is your Ryzen 7 5800X3D enough? A projection doubts it", "kurz": "Hardware Unboxed has projected how much CPU performance a PC version of GTA 6 would need for 60 fps. Because the game runs CPU-limited at 30 fps on consoles, roughly twice the performance of the PS5 CPU would be required. On paper, a Ryzen 7 5800X3D would only reach around 54 fps.", "zusammenfassung": "GTA 6 runs at 30 fps on PS5, PS5 Pro and Xbox Series X|S, according to Rockstar because of the demanding simulation on the console CPU. Hardware Unboxed used this on X to work out what a PC would need for 60 fps, and PCGH broke down the calculation. Twice as many frames per second would require roughly twice the CPU performance at the same load. The channel estimates the Ryzen 7 5800X3D to be about 80 percent faster than the PS5 CPU, which works out to around 54 fps. According to 3DCenter's gaming index, all X3D models for AM5, some Ryzen 9000 chips without 3D cache and the fastest Raptor Lake and Arrow Lake CPUs would clear the bar. A faster graphics card does not help in a CPU limit. The projection has clear limits, though: it is based on measurements from other games. It only holds if the console really runs CPU-limited throughout, and a PC version could offer sliders such as population density. Benchmark specialist CapFrameX is more optimistic on X and considers a Ryzen 7 9800X3D about 2.5 times as fast as the PS5 CPU. Rockstar has not announced a PC version of GTA 6 so far. Before buying a CPU, it is therefore worth waiting for real benchmarks.", "weitere_links": ["CapFrameX on X (assessment)"], "_src": "4dddfd2c"}, "2026-11-23-ki-server-preisaufschlaege": {"titel": "Financial Times report: Dell, HPE, Lenovo and Supermicro are demanding surcharges of 25 to 45 percent on AI servers after contracts were signed, driven by higher memory prices", "schlagzeile": "Ordered but not paid: AI servers get up to 45% more expensive after the fact", "kurz": "Major server makers are said to be demanding surcharges of 25 to 45 percent on AI servers months after contracts were signed. This is reported by the Financial Times and summarized by ComputerBase. The main reason is the sharp rise in memory prices.", "zusammenfassung": "According to the Financial Times, Dell, HPE, Lenovo and Supermicro are in some cases asking customers for considerably more money shortly before delivery. People in the industry cite surcharges of 25 to 45 percent. One industry insider describes the current standard as a contract with a guide price that can rise until delivery. According to a JPMorgan analysis, memory has become more than 400 percent more expensive since the start of 2024. GPU servers have risen by at least 20 to 30 percent, and memory-heavy CPU servers sometimes cost at least three times as much. Trading firms such as Jane Street, Optiver and Hudson River Trading are also affected and mostly accept the prices because they need the computing power. One example is an ongoing lawsuit in Ireland: according to court documents, trading firm XTX Markets had agreed a fixed price of 549 million US dollars with Dell. Dell is then said to have demanded a further 62 to 70 million dollars. It is unclear which contract clauses allow such additional demands. The manufacturers did not comment to the FT. For PC buyers, the report shows how strongly the memory market is currently driven by data centers.", "_src": "3005dcd0"}, "2026-11-22-gta6-jason-steve-mcqueen": {"titel": "Rockstar narrative head: Jason's taciturn character in GTA 6 is inspired by Steve McQueen in “The Getaway” and by research into former Army Rangers", "schlagzeile": "Why Jason talks so little in GTA 6: Rockstar names Steve McQueen as a model", "kurz": "Jason Duval, one of the two protagonists of GTA 6, deliberately speaks little. According to Rockstar's narrative head Rupert Humphries, Steve McQueen in the film “The Getaway” served as the inspiration. Research into former Army Rangers was added to that.", "zusammenfassung": "Humphries is Senior Vice President of Narrative at Rockstar and commented to Destructoid by email; Eurogamer and PC Gamer picked it up. When the team wanted to tell a story about a couple on the run, it looked at similar films. Sam Peckinpah's 1972 “The Getaway” with Steve McQueen stood out in particular. McQueen was known for cutting lines of dialogue and expressing things through his presence alone. Rockstar wanted to see how close a game character could get to that, especially since many earlier protagonists were the opposite. That fit the research into veterans and especially former Army Rangers, who are called “Marauders” in the game. According to Humphries, such people only talk or react when necessary and still come across as strong. Writer Michael Wiafe names Florida's crime history as the obvious starting point for the characters. The protagonists are criminals on paper but also decent people, and the game does not make excuses for them. Writer Elizabeth Gauvey-Kern says the story takes heavy turns, but Jason and Lucia's goal stays the same. Some fans had criticized Jason as too bland before release, whereas Destructoid finds the restraint coherent in the finished game.", "weitere_links": ["Destructoid (original interview)", "PC Gamer"], "_src": "20c23428"}, "2026-11-22-crystalmark-cpuix": {"titel": "The developer of CrystalDiskMark is working on CrystalMark CPUix, a CPU benchmark for processors from the i386 to today", "schlagzeile": "From i386 to today: CrystalDiskMark creator builds a CPU benchmark for all eras", "kurz": "Noriyuki Miyazaki, developer of CrystalDiskInfo and CrystalDiskMark, is working on a new CPU benchmark called CrystalMark CPUix. It is meant to compare processors from the i386 to current models with a uniform score. The official website names March 31, 2027 as the date.", "zusammenfassung": "According to ComputerBase, Miyazaki announced the project on X for the 28th anniversary of his software studio Crystal Dew World. CPUix is meant to rate the performance of everything from i386 processors to the latest CPUs on a uniform scale. The i386 dates from 1985, which is why Miyazaki speaks of processors around 40 years old. For that to work, the benchmark is also supposed to run on Windows 95 and Windows NT 3.51. For development and testing, Miyazaki says he bought a PC more than 30 years old, an NEC PC-9821 with a Pentium processor. He plans to acquire more old and new hardware to test CPUix across many generations. A photo vaguely shows an early version of the program. There are no further details on test methods or scoring yet. CrystalDiskMark is considered the standard benchmark for SSDs, and according to ComputerBase, CrystalDiskInfo recently reached 100 million downloads. The earlier CPU info tool CrystalCPUID, on the other hand, was discontinued years ago. Whether the March 2027 date holds remains to be seen.", "_src": "895f1249"}, "2026-11-22-intel-arc-g3-play-leak": {"titel": "Report: Intel plans a cheaper Panther Lake-based handheld chip called “Arc G3 Play” with only four Xe3 graphics cores", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Intel's “Arc G3 Play” is said to enable handhelds under 800 dollars", "kurz": "According to VideoCardz, Intel is working on a third handheld processor called Arc G3 Play. It is said to have only four Xe3 graphics cores and enable Panther Lake handhelds under 800 dollars. Intel has not announced the chip.", "zusammenfassung": "Arc G3 Play would sit below the already available Arc G3 and Arc G3 Extreme. According to VideoCardz, Arc G3 uses the Arc B370 graphics unit with 10 Xe3 cores, Arc G3 Extreme the Arc B390 with 12 cores. The Play variant would thus have only a third of the graphics cores of the top model. There are two possible CPU layouts: in August, there was talk of four performance cores and four low-power cores. More recent is an HWiNFO entry called PTL-080, which according to leaker Jaykihn uses eight efficient cores and no performance cores. Both variants would have eight CPU cores, and VideoCardz considers the newer 0+8+0+4 version the more likely candidate. A power range of 8 to 25 watts had been mentioned for the older variant, while the existing models run at up to 30 and 35 watts. Whether these values apply to the new configuration is open. Intel is said to be targeting a cheaper price segment so that manufacturers can offer Panther Lake handhelds under 800 dollars. How much gaming performance remains with four graphics cores is unknown. For comparison: the GPD Win Mini Ultra with Arc G3 Extreme costs 1,699 dollars. Neither the name nor the specs or timing have been confirmed by Intel.", "ursprungsquelle": "VideoCardz (exclusive); core layout according to Jaykihn on X and HWiNFO entry PTL-080", "_src": "6941347c"}, "2026-11-23-badbox-3-tv-boxen": {"titel": "Security firm Human Security uncovers the Badbox 3.0 ad fraud: infected cheap Android TV boxes generated around 40 billion ad requests per day at peak and served as proxies", "schlagzeile": "Cheap TV box as an ad bot: Badbox 3.0 fakes billions of ads", "kurz": "Infected cheap TV boxes secretly played ads and faked ad slots. This is shown by a report from security firm Human Security on Badbox 3.0. At peak, around 40 billion ad requests per day were generated.", "zusammenfassung": "Human Security published the report on November 18, and ComputerBase summarizes it. The malware played commercials in the background without them being visible on the TV. For some of the requests, it posed as a real streaming app that was not even running on the box. The boxes also served as a relay for other people's internet traffic, showing the owner's IP address. Affected are devices with the open Android base AOSP without Play Protect certification. On devices from Chinese manufacturer TXCZ, the researchers found a factory-installed launcher with system privileges, and a domain of the manufacturer also appears in the report. The report does not say how many devices are infected or how large the damage is. According to Human Security, some command domains were already taken down at the end of October in an action by Google and partners. Anyone using a very cheap no-name TV box should check whether it is Play Protect certified. Badbox is already the third wave of this scheme, and Google sued the operators of Badbox 2.0 in 2025.", "weitere_links": ["Human Security (announcement)"], "_src": "cd132686"}, "2026-11-22-ram-preise-2027-prognose": {"titel": "Analysis by Korean financial firm BNK: full warehouses at retailers and manufacturers could push RAM prices down significantly from mid-2027", "schlagzeile": "Hope for upgraders: analysts expect falling RAM prices from mid-2027", "kurz": "South Korean financial firm BNK Investment & Securities expects significantly falling prices for memory chips from mid-2027. The reason is said to be overflowing inventories at retailers and manufacturers who stocked up out of fear of shortages. This is a forecast, not a drop in store prices.", "zusammenfassung": "According to PC Games, BNK analyst Lee Min-hee assumes that end-customer demand has already passed its peak. For this year, he expects DRAM demand measured in memory volume to grow by 24 percent, but shipped volume by 38 percent. According to the analysis, that would be the strongest increase since 2016. Because many companies expect even tighter supply for 2027, surplus inventories are said to have built up at retailers and buyers. BNK expects these stocks to be worked down by the third quarter of 2027, which means fewer new orders and pressure on prices. DDR5 kits and SSDs in particular could benefit. An analysis by Bank of America also sees NAND prices in short-term trading already down by 20 percent. Such declines do not reach the drives in stores immediately, however. Because of high memory costs, PC and smartphone makers recently equipped devices with less memory or raised prices. For memory makers such as SK Hynix, falling prices would mean lower margins. Analyst forecasts are uncertain; in the short term, RAM and SSDs remain expensive.", "_src": "692ccfda"}, "2026-11-22-tsmc-lieferstopp-16nm-regel": {"titel": "New US export rule treats chips made at 16/14 nm as potentially export-controlled: TSMC reportedly put shipments to several chip designers on hold for now", "schlagzeile": "New US rule also hits phone chips: TSMC reportedly halted shipments", "kurz": "A new rule from the US export authority BIS treats chips made at 16 and 14 nm and finer as a precaution like AI chips for data centers. According to Nikkei Asia, TSMC has therefore put several shipments to Chinese and other chip designers on hold for now while it reviews the requirements. Chips for smartphones, TVs and cars may also be affected.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Tom's Hardware, the rule from the Bureau of Industry and Security (BIS) has applied as an interim regulation since November 19. Its core is a presumption: contract manufacturers and packaging companies are to classify chips made at 16 or 14 nm and finer as export-controlled high-performance chips by default. Anyone wanting to avoid that needs a confirmation of the chip's computing performance from an approved chip designer. These are manufacturing processes that have been in use for around ten years and are found in many everyday devices. Nikkei Asia cites several industry executives saying the impact is much broader than initially expected. TSMC is said to have held back several shipments to Chinese and non-Chinese customers while the review is ongoing. The rule itself does not order a shipping stop; the pause is a company response whose exact scope has not been officially confirmed. There is no public statement from TSMC so far. In addition, the US now requires export licenses for AI chips to Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore, Brazil and Thailand, because these countries are considered transshipment points for deliveries to China. The regulation also bars Chinese companies from renting computing power in foreign data centers to gain access to modern US chips. Nothing changes for PC gamers in the short term, but longer delays for consumer electronics chips could weigh on supply chains and prices.", "weitere_links": ["Nikkei Asia"], "_src": "df9f4a77"}, "2026-11-22-cachyos-eac-linux-v2": {"titel": "CachyOS November 2026 supports Easy Anti-Cheat Linux v2 with its own signed kernel and brings a new recovery tool", "schlagzeile": "CachyOS gets Linux ready for Easy Anti-Cheat v2 – with its own gaming kernel", "kurz": "With its November release, the popular gaming Linux distribution CachyOS supports Easy Anti-Cheat Linux v2. For this, there is a dedicated signed kernel with a separate boot entry. Requirements include Secure Boot and TPM 2.0.", "zusammenfassung": "According to GamingOnLinux, EAC Linux v2 only lets games start if it can verify how the system was booted. Required are Secure Boot with a kernel signed with a key accepted by Epic, a TPM 2.0, an enabled IOMMU and a kernel in lockdown mode that loads only signed modules. CachyOS provides the linux-cachyos-eac kernel and a matching signed systemd-boot for this. The EAC kernel gets its own boot entry, and the normal entries are kept. So you only boot it when you want to play a game with EAC. The eac-setup script sets this up for systemd-boot, Limine and rEFInd; GRUB is only supported experimentally. DKMS modules do not work with the EAC kernel, so Nvidia, ZFS and r8125 modules are provided as separate packages. Anyone using BitLocker or unlocking their disk via TPM should read the guide in the CachyOS wiki first. Also new is a recovery tool that can test and restore Btrfs snapshots without a live USB stick. Package Installer 2.0 optionally supports AUR, Flatpak and AppImage. Included are Linux 7.3.5, Mesa 26.3.1 and the Nvidia driver 620.73.04. The background is Epic's new launcher with Linux support, with which EAC Linux v2 is set to arrive. Which games actually enable EAC v2 on Linux is still up to the respective studios.", "weitere_links": ["Phoronix", "9to5Linux"], "_src": "d72a03b3"}, "2026-11-22-gta6-circana-ueber-haelfte": {"titel": "Circana: on launch day, 61 percent of active US PS5 players and 56 percent of active Xbox players worldwide played GTA 6", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 on launch day: more than every second active console player joined in", "kurz": "According to market researcher Circana, 61 percent of active PS5 players in the US and 56 percent of active Xbox players worldwide played GTA 6 on November 19. On average, they spent more than eight hours in the game. Fortnite came second with 10 percent.", "zusammenfassung": "The figures come from Circana's Player Engagement Tracker; analyst Mat Piscatella published them on Bluesky, Eurogamer reports. What was measured is the share of players active that day who launched GTA 6. PS5 players averaged 513 minutes, more than eight and a half hours, and Xbox players 494 minutes. Piscatella called both the user rate and the playtime “absolutely bonkers”. Fortnite had the second-highest rate that day with 10 percent across both platforms. Before the release, the later GTA 6 players mainly played Fortnite, Call of Duty, GTA 5, Roblox and NBA 2K27, according to Circana. Note: the PS5 figures refer only to the US, the Xbox figures to all regions. These are not sales figures but shares of a day's active players. Rockstar had previously reported 32.5 million copies sold before launch and 3.79 billion dollars in revenue on the first day. At the same time, users are downrating the game on Metacritic over the 30 fps on consoles and political accusations.", "_src": "cab143f6"}, "2026-11-22-geforce-621-35-schreibflut-weiter": {"titel": "Test by a Neowin editor: GeForce hotfix 621.35 only reduces the SSD write load; after hours of idling the driver wrote 36 GB again", "schlagzeile": "GeForce hotfix 621.35 only half helps: 36 GB written to the SSD again at idle", "kurz": "GeForce hotfix 621.35 was supposed to stop the Nvidia driver from constantly writing to the SSD. A test by a Neowin editor shows that the bug returns after longer uptime, albeit weaker. So far this is a single test report, and Nvidia has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "Robbie Khan tested on a Windows 11 PC with an RTX 4090 and a 2 TB Samsung 990 Pro SSD. He compared drivers 621.24, 621.01 and the hotfix 621.35 and monitored the write activity of the NVDisplay.Container.exe process as well as the SSD's SMART values. In the first hour after installation, the hotfix wrote only 90.8 KB, so the bug seemed fixed. Over nine hours of idling with the monitor in standby, however, 40.85 GB of writes accumulated. According to HWiNFO64, the SSD's actual host writes rose by around 36 GB during this time. For comparison: with driver 621.24 it was around 1.18 TB in about five days. The hotfix thus reduces the problem significantly, but does not eliminate it in this test. With the older driver 621.01, the bug did not occur for Khan; the process wrote only 12.55 MB in 55 minutes. Neowin and Wccftech therefore still recommend rolling back to 621.01. Wccftech stresses that this is an isolated case and other systems may behave differently. Anyone wanting to check whether their own PC is affected can watch the write activity of NVDisplay.Container.exe in Task Manager or the SSD's host writes in HWiNFO. There is no statement from Nvidia or a further driver so far.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "8db2c56e"}, "2026-11-22-gta6-psn-sperre-fkk-foto": {"titel": "GTA 6 player reports 30-day ban from PSN social features after sending a nude photo taken in the game via PlayStation message", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 nudist beach photo sent: player reports 30-day PSN ban", "kurz": "A GTA 6 player reports that Sony has banned him from the PlayStation Network's social features for 30 days. He had sent a friend a photo taken with the in-game camera in the game's nudist area via PSN message. Sony's code of conduct makes no exception for content from adult-rated games.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Eurogamer, the player made the case public on X on Friday evening and explicitly warned others. He showed a screenshot of the notification from PlayStation Safety. According to it, content sent via “Messages on PlayStation” violated the code of conduct. The account is excluded from social features for 30 days due to “pornographic or obscene content”. According to the notice, further violations may lead to a temporary or permanent suspension from all of PlayStation. Sony's code of conduct prohibits sharing obscene, pornographic or illegal content. As Dexerto notes, there is no exception for images from games, not even those rated 18+. Sony has not commented on the specific case; the report is based on the player's statements. Just a few days ago, Xbox players had reported bans after clips with nude scenes from GTA 6 were uploaded automatically. So anyone wanting to share photos from the game should look carefully at what they show.", "_src": "27f43473"}, "2026-11-22-glinet-goodcloud-malware": {"titel": "Flaw in GL.iNet's cloud remote management exploited: attackers installed malware on routers and KVM devices, firmware updates to follow", "schlagzeile": "Malware on GL.iNet routers: attackers got in via cloud management", "kurz": "Through a flaw in GL.iNet's cloud remote management services, unknown parties installed malware on some of the manufacturer's routers and KVM devices. The cloud flaw has been closed, but devices already infected remain compromised. Owners should check their devices and install the new firmware.", "zusammenfassung": "According to its own security notice, GL.iNet discovered the incident on November 20. An unauthorized third party exploited a vulnerability in the cloud remote management to access devices and install malware. According to the manufacturer, the attack path is blocked and new infections through it are no longer possible. However, these measures do not remove malware from devices that are already infected, GL.iNet stresses. As an indicator, the manufacturer names a running process containing the text “crond -i /tmp/.log”, which can be found in the router's LuCI menu under Processes or via SSH. Anyone finding the entry should treat the device as infected and install the new firmware or reset it to factory settings. Beta firmware with the fixes is already available for KVM devices, and stable versions for routers and KVM were announced for November 22. GL.iNet recommends the update even without signs of infection. For infected KVM devices, the connected computer should also be checked. GL.iNet has not said how many devices are affected, since when the flaw was exploited or what exactly the malware does. Users in the manufacturer's forum also report further backdoors that the official check does not detect; this has not been confirmed by the manufacturer so far.", "weitere_links": ["GL.iNet (security notice)"], "_src": "83cec918"}, "2026-11-22-outlook-ausfall-abschlussbericht": {"titel": "Microsoft's final report on the November 12 Outlook outage: some emails to inactive consumer mailboxes were never delivered, Defender protections were also disrupted", "schlagzeile": "Outlook outage: Microsoft admits some emails never arrived", "kurz": "Microsoft has published its final report on the major Outlook and Exchange Online outage on November 12. For consumer customers with mailboxes inactive for a long time, some emails expired and senders received non-delivery reports. Protection features of Defender for Office were also disrupted.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Neowin, the trigger was a software defect from July 2026 that, combined with reduced server capacity and additional Teams traffic, caused a chain reaction. At times more than 80 percent of the networking gateways were unresponsive, and services were back after about 12 hours. Microsoft extended the window for delivery retries from 24 to 48 hours. According to Microsoft, no enterprise email was permanently lost. For consumer customers, however, delayed emails to mailboxes that had been inactive for more than 30 days expired. Microsoft does not say how many emails were affected. In addition, the automatic removal of malicious emails after delivery was delayed, and Safe Links sometimes offered the option to skip verification. Admins were temporarily unable to manage quarantine and block lists, and Purview features were delayed as well. By the end of 2026, Microsoft wants to limit Teams failover traffic to affected regions and speed up outage notifications. By the first quarter of 2027, the gateways are to be split into separate pools per service. According to the report, the first customer notification came about 20 minutes after the disruption began.", "_src": "50d409a9"}, "2026-11-22-phison-ssd-npu-weltraum": {"titel": "Phison shows an SSD with its own NPU for AI software at SC26, plus space SSDs with 488 TB for an orbital data center", "schlagzeile": "SSD with its own AI chip: Phison runs PyTorch directly on the drive", "kurz": "At the SC26 supercomputing show, Phison showed an enterprise SSD with a built-in NPU and 64 GB of its own memory that is meant to run AI frameworks such as PyTorch and vLLM directly. There is also the new Pascari Space line for satellites and data centers in orbit. Both are aimed at companies, not home PCs.", "zusammenfassung": "According to TechPowerUp, the NPU SSD has 64 GB of memory running at 130 GB/s on board and supports PyTorch, vLLM, OpenVINO and llama.cpp. The idea: the SSD searches and processes data itself and only sends the relevant results back to the server. Phison promises 10 to 100 times less data traffic depending on the task. Unusually, Phison rates the NPU's performance in DMIPS instead of TOPS. Controller, interface, form factor and memory type are not yet known; this is a concept still in development. Phison also showed a design that combines fast pSLC and cheap QLC flash behind a 16-channel controller and is meant to make dedicated cache drives unnecessary. According to a press release from November 17, Phison is also launching the Pascari Space line for spacecraft and data centers in space. For the first node StarVault-001 of provider Lonestar Data Holdings, scheduled to launch in the first half of 2027, Phison supplies 488 TB of raw capacity, with about 370 TB usable. Phison has not given prices for any of the products. Nothing changes for gamers for now, but the technology shows where storage in AI data centers is heading.", "weitere_links": ["Phison (Pascari Space press release)", "VideoCardz"], "_src": "daa0f725"}, "2026-11-22-windows11-bluetooth-mikrofon-48khz": {"titel": "Windows 11 Insider build: compatible LE Audio headsets play 48 kHz stereo even with the microphone active instead of phone-call quality", "schlagzeile": "No more phone-call sound? Windows 11 tests better Bluetooth audio with mic", "kurz": "Anyone who games on a PC with Bluetooth headphones and uses the microphone often hears only muffled phone-call sound. A Windows 11 test build now allows compatible headsets to play 48 kHz stereo with the microphone active. However, this requires newer LE Audio devices and suitable PCs.", "zusammenfassung": "Windows Latest found the feature in a current Insider build, so it is still a test. Until now, Windows switches from the Bluetooth profile A2DP to the hands-free profile HFP when the microphone is active, which sounds much worse. This affects Discord chats or in-game voice chat while music or game sound is playing, for example. In the test build, the Bluetooth device's output settings have a new option „2 channels, 16 bit, 48000 Hz“ under „Format when microphone is active“. This is meant to keep the sound playing in full stereo quality. You need a headset with Bluetooth LE Audio and 48 kHz playback as well as a PC with Super Wideband Stereo. Whether the PC supports LE Audio is shown by the toggle „Use LE Audio when available“ in the Bluetooth settings, but that is no guarantee for the new option. Older headsets do not benefit. Whether Microsoft will later extend the improvement to more devices is unclear. Windows Latest expects the feature for everyone by around March 2027; Microsoft has not given a date.", "_src": "d518f4ad"}, "2026-11-22-isaac-ki-musik-entfernt": {"titel": "The Binding of Isaac: Nicalis removes undisclosed AI music from Repentance+ after criticism from creator Edmund McMillen and review-bombing on Steam", "schlagzeile": "AI music in Binding of Isaac: creator knew nothing, patch deletes the songs", "kurz": "The new update for The Binding of Isaac: Repentance+ contained music created with the AI tool Suno without this being disclosed. After a wave of negative Steam reviews, Nicalis removed the files with a patch. Creator Edmund McMillen says he knew nothing about it.", "zusammenfassung": "According to IGN, the update was released on November 19, together with new versions for Switch 2, PS5 and Xbox Series X/S. The affected tracks belonged to a GTA-themed daily run, timed with the launch of GTA 6. A day later, a Reddit user found references to the AI tool Suno in the metadata of several tracks, including links to Suno pages. Valve requires developers to disclose AI use on the Steam page, which had not happened here. Afterwards, only about 8 percent of recent Steam reviews were positive. McMillen wrote that he had „no idea“ how the music got into the build and announced its removal. A few hours later, Nicalis released a patch that removes the „generated music files“. It is live on PC, and according to Nicalis it has been submitted for Xbox, Switch and PlayStation. When it will appear there is unclear. Nicalis has not given an explanation of how this happened. Recent reviews on Steam remain at „Overwhelmingly Negative“.", "_src": "d791da42"}, "2026-11-22-windows-antivirus-ausserhalb-kernel": {"titel": "Windows endpoint security platform generally available: antivirus software can run key protection functions outside the Windows kernel", "schlagzeile": "Lesson from the CrowdStrike chaos: antivirus can leave the Windows kernel", "kurz": "Microsoft has made the Windows endpoint security platform generally available for Windows 11. Security software can use it to run important protection functions in user mode instead of the kernel, so errors should less often take down the whole PC. Bitdefender, CrowdStrike, ESET, Sophos and others plan to use the interfaces.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft announced this at Ignite on November 17, and Windows Latest has now summarized the details. The trigger was July 19, 2024, when a faulty CrowdStrike update crippled around 8.5 million Windows devices with blue screens. The new platform gives security programs Windows interfaces in user mode through which they can observe and block events. The first version covers the file system, processes, the registry and the Object Manager. If a protection program or a rule causes problems at startup, Windows is to use built-in recovery mechanisms, according to Microsoft. According to Microsoft Learn, the platform has been part of Windows 11 25H2 and 26H2 since the October updates. Initially, only members of the Microsoft Virus Initiative may use it, and the programs must also be specially signed. Bitdefender and Sophos plan first products for the fourth quarter of 2026, other vendors partly not until 2027. CrowdStrike sees the platform as a supplement, so security software is not disappearing from the kernel entirely. Anti-cheat programs with kernel drivers are also not directly affected by the change.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft Windows IT Pro Blog", "Microsoft Learn (Windows endpoint security platform)"], "_src": "4894b14e"}, "2026-11-22-gta3-ps2-exklusiv-deal": {"titel": "Former Sony and Take-Two executives describe how GTA 3 became a PS2 exclusive: cash, a discount per disc and an initially hesitant US division", "schlagzeile": "GTA 3 exclusive on PS2: Sony paid cash and gave a discount – the US hesitated", "kurz": "In an interview with The Game Business, former executives recount how GTA 3 became a PlayStation 2 exclusive 25 years ago. Sony wanted it to fend off the new Xbox and paid Take-Two money plus a discount on the production costs of every disc. Of all teams, Sony's US team reportedly held back at first.", "zusammenfassung": "Christopher Dring of The Game Business spoke with former PlayStation and Take-Two executives, and Insider Gaming summarizes the interview. According to former Take-Two executive Kelly Sumner, Sony came asking for an exclusive title to fend off Microsoft. Besides a „substantial“ amount of money, Take-Two above all received a discount of 2.50 to 3 US dollars per unit produced. This brought Take-Two „tens and tens and tens of millions of dollars“. Sony's UK team under Chris Deering understood the game immediately, while the US division was „dragging their feet“. Former PlayStation executive Shuhei Yoshida says GTA 3, Vice City and San Andreas shaped the entire industry. Studios such as Naughty Dog, Insomniac and Sucker Punch then switched from character action to more mature, realistic games such as Uncharted, Resistance and Infamous. The three PS2 games later also came to Xbox, and from GTA 4 on the series launched on all platforms at the same time. The interview does not give concrete figures for the deal. These are recollections of those involved; no documents have been published.", "weitere_links": ["The Game Business (interview)"], "_src": "ebb75fc0"}, "2026-11-22-windows7-msi-claw-8": {"titel": "Modders get Windows 7 booting on the MSI Claw 8 AI+ handheld with Intel Lunar Lake after working around bugs in MSI's ACPI firmware", "schlagzeile": "Windows 7 on the MSI Claw 8 AI+: modders defy MSI's firmware bugs", "kurz": "Windows tinkerer Bob Pony has got Windows 7 running on the MSI Claw 8 AI+ gaming handheld with Intel's Lunar Lake chip. At first the system crashed with a blue screen, which he blames on bugs in MSI's ACPI firmware. Whether drivers, controls and games work is unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports on a post by Bob Pony from November 21. The Claw 8 AI+ uses a Core Ultra 7 258V with 4 performance and 4 efficiency cores as well as Arc 140V integrated graphics. MSI officially ships the device with Windows 11, and Lunar Lake came to market long after the end of support for Windows 7. According to Bob Pony, Windows 7 initially aborted with the blue screen 0xA5, which points to ACPI problems. He names an empty _CID field and duplicate _UID values for two devices in MSI's firmware as the cause. A second developer called EAZY BLACK helped work around the bugs, after which the system booted. So far the demonstration shows no more than booting. Bob Pony has not said whether graphics drivers, controller buttons, Wi-Fi or power-saving features work under Windows 7. He had previously pointed to the unofficial WDDM2Win7 project, which is meant to add DirectX 12 and modern graphics cards to Windows 7. Whether the two can be combined is unclear. This is not for everyday use: Windows 7 has not received security updates for years.", "_src": "6e154b01"}, "2026-11-22-neuralink-gta6": {"titel": "Neuralink study participant plays GTA 6 by thought control: video shows driving, flying and shootouts with the brain implant", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 with thoughts alone: Neuralink patient drives, flies and fights in Leonida", "kurz": "Neuralink has released a video in which a participant in its clinical trial plays GTA 6 with the brain implant. It shows boat rides, flights and shootouts. Neuralink stresses that the devices are investigational and not approved.", "zusammenfassung": "According to IGN, the roughly two-minute video shows how the participant steers the character Jason through Leonida using only the implant. He says he used to play with a mouth stick on an iPad, which made his jaw and body sore. With the chip, operating a computer was immediately possible, and he speaks of a „portal to the world“. Neuralink made clear that the participants are part of a very small clinical trial. The devices are investigational and have not been approved by the US FDA or other authorities. The experiences shown may not apply to all participants or future outcomes. According to IGN, the video does not explain exactly how the control is technically transferred to the console. Back in 2024, the first Neuralink patient played Civilization 6 and later Slay the Spire with the implant. The footage has not been independently verified; it is a promotional video from the company.", "_src": "8ee04f1e"}, "2026-11-21-entra-connect-health-datenleck": {"titel": "Microsoft confirms exploited flaw in Entra Connect Health: admin email addresses and tenant data leaked", "schlagzeile": "Microsoft Entra flaw: attackers grab company admin addresses", "kurz": "Attackers exploited a flaw in the Microsoft Entra Connect Health cloud service and obtained administrator email addresses and configuration data from company tenants. Microsoft closed the flaw on November 19 and has notified affected customers. Passwords and keys are said not to be affected.", "zusammenfassung": "BleepingComputer reports on a notification Microsoft sent to administrators; Microsoft confirmed the flaw when asked. Entra Connect Health monitors companies' on-premises identity infrastructure from the cloud. The vulnerability was in the service's API, was introduced on July 23 and discovered on November 9. According to Microsoft, there was unauthorized read access, but no configuration changes were detected. The leaked data includes email addresses of technical contacts and admins, tenant IDs, domain names, country information, license tiers and directory synchronization status. An expired certificate that was no longer in use was also returned via the API. According to Microsoft, passwords, password hashes, tokens and valid keys were not affected. Microsoft does not say how many organizations are affected or who is behind the attack. Customers do not need to install anything, but Microsoft warns of targeted phishing attacks on the stolen admin addresses. It recommends phishing-resistant multi-factor authentication for privileged accounts and a look at the Entra audit and sign-in logs. A PowerShell script from Microsoft shows which types of data could be affected.", "_src": "e9ebf74a"}, "2026-11-21-nioh-3-complete-edition-korea": {"titel": "Korean rating board rates unannounced Nioh 3 Complete Edition", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is a Nioh 3 Complete Edition coming soon?", "kurz": "Korea's age rating board GRAC has rated a Nioh 3 Complete Edition that Koei Tecmo has not even announced yet. According to the listing, it is a compilation of the action RPG's additional content. No release date is known.", "zusammenfassung": "Insider Gaming spotted the listing, and Eurogamer picked it up. The edition was submitted on November 2 and rated 19+ on November 17, citing graphic depictions of violence. According to a machine-translated description, it is a compilation of the additional content of the dark Sengoku action RPG. The listing also refers to a foreign rating, according to Insider Gaming a CERO 17+ rating from Japan. GRAC publishes ratings immediately, which is why games often show up there before their official announcement. For the predecessor, about ten months passed between the rating of the main game in January 2020 and the Complete Edition in November of the same year. Nioh 3 was released on February 6 and, according to Eurogamer, has sold over one million copies. The second DLC, \"Bloody Insurrection\", is announced for February 2027, and Eurogamer thinks a joint launch with the Complete Edition is possible. That is speculation; Koei Tecmo has not commented so far. Typically a Complete Edition contains the main game and all DLC, but the content has not been confirmed.", "ursprungsquelle": "Game Rating and Administration Committee (GRAC, Korea), spotted by Insider Gaming", "weitere_links": ["Eurogamer"], "_src": "4cbc4b54"}, "2026-11-21-hwinfo-rest-api": {"titel": "HWiNFO 8.61 Beta adds a built-in REST API server: sensor readings in the browser on phone, tablet or second screen, limited to 12 hours without a license", "schlagzeile": "HWiNFO sends sensor readings to your phone – free, but only for 12 hours", "kurz": "The diagnostic tool HWiNFO has gained a built-in REST API server in beta 8.61. Temperatures, clocks and power draw can be displayed in the browser on any device on the home network, including self-built dashboards. Without a license, the server only runs for 12 hours.", "zusammenfassung": "The developers presented the feature in the HWiNFO forum, and VideoCardz reports. The server provides all sensor readings including units, descriptions and hierarchy as JSON, over HTTP or HTTPS. Custom displays can be built with plain HTML and JavaScript, and a ready-made interface in the style of the familiar sensor window is included. The feature is enabled in the sensor window via the \"Remote Center\" button, where IP address, port and HTTPS can be set. A filter determines which readings are displayed, monitored and logged. This can turn an old tablet or a small second screen into a temperature display for the CPU and graphics card. The catch: without a license, the server stops after 12 hours. According to VideoCardz, the license costs 29 US dollars, or 52 US dollars for three years. The beta also includes improved support for Intel graphics and initial support for Intel's Coral Rapids. Documentation and sample dashboards are available on GitHub. Anyone using the server should only make it reachable on their own network.", "weitere_links": ["HWiNFO forum (announcement)", "HWiNFO REST API docs (GitHub)"], "_src": "52bab466"}, "2026-11-21-nova-lake-s-28c-h-16c": {"titel": "Nova Lake: 28-core desktop test sample runs at 5.2 GHz, Advantech data sheet lists 16-core laptop chip at 25 watts", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Nova Lake with 28 cores and 5.2 GHz – plus a 16-core chip for laptops", "kurz": "A test sample of Intel's Nova Lake-S with 28 cores and 5.2 GHz has appeared in the OpenBenchmarking database. At the same time, an Advantech data sheet lists a Nova Lake-H chip with 16 cores, 4.8 GHz and a 25-watt TDP. Intel has confirmed none of this.", "zusammenfassung": "Both finds go back to well-known hardware sleuth momomo_us, and TechPowerUp and Wccftech picked them up. The desktop chip shows up as \"Intel 0000\" with the abbreviation NVL, and the core count matches the expected split of 8 performance, 16 efficiency and 4 low-power cores. It was tested on an Intel reference board with an early BIOS, 32 GB of memory and Ubuntu 26.04, including Quake II RTX, Unigine and OpenCL workloads. TechPowerUp warns that test samples run with different firmware, power limits and clock profiles than retail versions. The listing does not reveal whether 5.2 GHz is a sustained clock or just a peak value. According to the Advantech data sheet, the laptop chip sits on a board for robotics and industrial use and is listed there as \"Core Ultra Series 4\". It lists 8 performance, 4 efficiency and 4 low-power cores, a 2.0 GHz base clock, 4.8 GHz turbo and 18 MB of cache. Added to that are support for DDR5-8000 with up to 128 GB and integrated graphics at 2.3 GHz. A specific model name is missing. Intel itself has not yet provided any details on clocks or specifications of the Nova Lake series.", "ursprungsquelle": "momomo_us on X (finds: OpenBenchmarking.org and Advantech data sheet)", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech (Nova Lake-H, Advantech data sheet)"], "_src": "c12c2fd6"}, "2026-11-21-gta6-ps5-absturz-ce-108255-1": {"titel": "GTA 6 crashes for some players on PS5 with error CE-108255-1, Rockstar has not yet commented", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 crashes on some PS5s – error CE-108255-1 halts the story", "kurz": "Some players report that GTA 6 regularly crashes on PS5 with error code CE-108255-1. In some cases this stops them from progressing in the story, also on PS5 Pro and occasionally on Xbox Series X. Rockstar has not confirmed the problems so far, and there is no patch.", "zusammenfassung": "Eurogamer has collected reports from Reddit and from Dexerto. One player writes that the game initially runs fine and then crashes to the PS5 home screen after about 40 minutes. Another cannot get past an early mission because the game crashes at the same spot every time. PS5 Pro owners report crashes as early as the prologue. There are also individual reports of crashes after about 15 minutes on Xbox Series X. How many players are affected is unclear; these are individual reports. Rockstar has not commented on the crashes and refers console errors to Sony or Microsoft. Sony describes CE-108255-1 only generally as an application error and advises checking for game updates. Other general tips are a system update, restoring licenses, clearing the cache and rebuilding the database in safe mode. If the game is on an external SSD, moving it to internal storage may help. According to Eurogamer, some affected players have already tried all of this without success.", "_src": "028ab63a"}, "2026-11-21-silverstone-nova-lake-netzteil": {"titel": "Silverstone launches HELA 1350Rz power supply with three CPU power cables, citing the high power demand of Intel's Nova Lake-S", "schlagzeile": "Three CPU cables for Nova Lake: Silverstone gears up PSU for Intel's appetite", "kurz": "Silverstone has introduced the 1,350-watt HELA 1350Rz power supply, which explicitly supports Intel's upcoming Nova Lake-S processors. It comes with three CPU power cables, which is unusual for home PC power supplies. Silverstone justifies this with the high power demand of the new chips.", "zusammenfassung": "According to the product page, the HELA 1350Rz has three 4+4-pin CPU cables to cover the \"high power demands\" of Nova Lake-S, VideoCardz and Wccftech report. Desktop power supplies usually have one or two such cables. The PSU is ATX 3.1 certified, achieves 80 Plus Platinum and has two 12V-2x6 connectors for graphics cards. The report does not mention a price. Intel has not yet officially stated the power consumption of Nova Lake-S. Earlier, unconfirmed reports spoke of up to 474 watts in the short-term PL2 turbo limit for the top model with 52 cores. For comparison: the current Core Ultra 9 285K is at 250 watts. According to earlier reports, some Z990 motherboards are to get two or three CPU power connectors, with the third considered optional for overclockers. So anyone buying a power supply today does not necessarily need a new one for Nova Lake; what matters is the motherboard and processor model.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "a0000314"}, "2026-11-21-zen6-1usmus-widerspruch": {"titel": "Ryzen tool developer 1usmus contradicts reports of Zen 6 delay to summer, N2X manufacturing and over 6 GHz", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Zen 6 not delayed to summer after all? Ryzen insider disagrees", "kurz": "Developer 1usmus calls three current rumors about AMD's Zen 6 for AM5 \"not accurate\". According to him, Zen 6 is not being delayed to summer, the first chips do not use TSMC N2X and do not exceed 6 GHz. AMD has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "1usmus is known for tools such as the Ryzen DRAM Calculator and Hydra and posted his assessment on X on November 20; Wccftech picked it up on Saturday. He thereby contradicts a Chiphell post we reported on November 19. It claimed AMD had moved the Olympic Ridge desktop series to the clock-optimized 2 nm variant N2X and was therefore delaying the launch until after Computex 2027. According to 1usmus, the first Zen 6 processors for AM5 do not use N2X. Wccftech interprets this to mean that N2 or N2P will be used initially and N2X might follow later at most; that is an interpretation, not a statement by 1usmus. A delay into the summer is also not true, he says. He does not give a specific date. He also calls rumors about clock speeds beyond 6 GHz false. 1usmus provides no evidence for his statements, so it is one claim against another. Officially, AMD has only announced an appearance at CES 2027 without naming products.", "ursprungsquelle": "1usmus on X", "weitere_links": ["1usmus on X (hint, 20.11.2026)"], "_src": "80df7c8c"}, "2026-11-21-debian-13-8": {"titel": "Debian 13.8 \"Trixie\" released: 122 bug fixes and 150 security updates in new installation images", "schlagzeile": "Debian 13.8 is here: 150 security updates for \"Trixie\"", "kurz": "The Debian project has released the eighth point release of Debian 13 \"Trixie\". It bundles 122 bug fixes and 150 security updates in new installation images. Existing systems do not need a new image; a normal update is enough.", "zusammenfassung": "Debian 13.8 arrives two months after version 13.7, 9to5Linux and Phoronix report, citing the official announcement. Point releases do not bring new features but collect security and bug fixes that were previously published individually. The new images are mainly intended for new installations so that hundreds of updates do not have to be downloaded afterwards. Installation images are available for six architectures, including amd64, arm64 and RISC-V 64-bit. Live images are only released for 64-bit PCs, including with KDE Plasma 6.3, GNOME 48 and Xfce 4.20. Anyone already using Debian 13 updates as usual via the package manager, for example with \"apt update\" and \"apt full-upgrade\". The Debian announcement lists which packages are affected in detail. The project advises all users of Debian 13 to update their installations.", "weitere_links": ["Debian (announcement)", "Phoronix"], "_src": "f081abc5"}, "2026-11-21-gta6-xbox-quick-resume-60fps": {"titel": "Quick Resume bug on Xbox Series X unlocks GTA 6 to over 60 fps, but the game then runs twice as fast", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 at over 60 fps on Xbox – via glitch, but in fast-forward", "kurz": "A Reddit user has found a bug in the Xbox Series X Quick Resume feature that removes GTA 6's 30 fps cap. The catch: because game speed is tied to frame rate, the game then runs too fast. Cutscenes, on the other hand, are said to play normally.", "zusammenfassung": "Wccftech reports on the instructions from Reddit user Meowwie64. Requirements are an Xbox Series X, a 120 Hz display and game version 1.002.001. You start GTA 6 at 60 Hz, switch to 120 Hz after the intro, launch another game via the guide menu and then switch back via Quick Resume. After that, GTA 6 runs without a frame rate cap. Because animations and game speed are tied to frame rate, the game speeds up accordingly at more than 30 frames per second. According to the shared videos, cutscenes also work at over 60 fps. Whether the trick works on Series S or with later patches is unclear. Rockstar designed GTA 6 for 30 fps on all consoles, including PS5 Pro. Wccftech suspects fluctuating frame rates are the reason, since even 30 fps is not always held; Rockstar has not commented. The basis is a Reddit post and videos; the trick has not been independently verified. It is not really playable, but it shows that the console manages more frames in some scenes.", "_src": "e4e8b50f"}, "2026-11-21-amdlss5-2-5-frame-generation": {"titel": "Unofficial mod AMDLSS5 2.5: DLSS 5-style neural rendering runs up to 60 percent faster on Radeon, plus up to sixfold frame generation", "schlagzeile": "Radeon mod AMDLSS5 2.5: faster AI graphics and up to 6x frame generation", "kurz": "Version 2.5 of the unofficial mod AMDLSS5 brings a new Vulkan engine for DLSS 5-style neural rendering on Radeon cards. The network is said to compute up to 60 percent faster, and games run about 10 percent faster according to the developer. New is frame generation with two- to sixfold frame multiplication.", "zusammenfassung": "The mod has been released for free on GitHub, VideoCardz and Wccftech report. The new engine builds on the open-source DLSSNR-AMD runtime by developer Mochizuki. The 60 percent refers to the computing time of the neural network, not the overall frame rate. The developer measured in Resident Evil Requiem on a Radeon RX 9070 XT: around 10 percent more frames per second than with version 2.0 and about 0.5 GB less video memory. The frame generation comes from Apex Compute and also works in games without their own frame multiplication. An overlay shows the additional input lag. Newly supported games include Baldur's Gate 3, Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 and The Last of Us Part I. Officially, Radeon RX 9000 cards are supported, the RX 7800 XT is considered compatible, other RX 7000 models only experimentally, and RX 6000 and older not at all. The developer admits visual artifacts in some games. AMD itself does not offer a comparable feature, and VideoCardz has not tested the mod itself. As with all mods: use at your own risk, and better not in online games with anti-cheat.", "weitere_links": ["AMDLSS5 2.5 (GitHub, release notes)", "Wccftech"], "_src": "fc16f92c"}, "2026-11-21-gpd-win-mini-ultra-preis": {"titel": "GPD announces price of the Win Mini Ultra: 1,699 US dollars for the version with Intel Arc G3 Extreme, 32 GB RAM and 1 TB SSD", "schlagzeile": "GPD Win Mini Ultra: handheld with Intel Arc G3 Extreme costs 1,699 dollars", "kurz": "GPD has announced the price of the Win Mini Ultra: 1,699 US dollars with 32 GB RAM and 1 TB SSD via Indiegogo. Inside is Intel's handheld chip Arc G3 Extreme. The campaign starts in December, and a 64 GB version will only be sold at retail.", "zusammenfassung": "GPD published the price itself on X, and TechPowerUp and VideoCardz report on it. The Win Mini Ultra is a small clamshell handheld with a full keyboard. It features Intel's Arc G3 Extreme with integrated Arc B390 graphics, two USB4 v2 ports with 80 Gbit/s and a slot for PCIe 5.0 SSDs. There are also Hall effect triggers and VRR support. The 1,699 US dollars apply to the Indiegogo version with 32 GB RAM and 1 TB SSD including shipping. The campaign is set to start in December, with shipping to follow right afterwards. According to GPD, a variant with 64 GB RAM will not be sold via Indiegogo but only through retail. GPD has not yet announced European prices. The company attributes the high price to rising memory prices and warns that it could become more expensive later. Crowdfunding generally carries the risk of delays.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz"], "_src": "4d3af437"}, "2026-11-21-geforce-hotfix-621-35-ssd": {"titel": "Nvidia releases GeForce Hotfix 621.35 against the excessive SSD writes of drivers 621.14 and 621.24", "schlagzeile": "GeForce Hotfix 621.35 stops the flood of writes to the SSD", "kurz": "Nvidia has released the GeForce hotfix driver 621.35. It fixes the bug that caused drivers 621.14 and 621.24 to write huge amounts of data to the SSD while idle. The hotfix is optional and only available via Nvidia's customer support.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Nvidia, the driver contains exactly one fix: excessive writes to the file nvlog.nvlgstg could occur in the background. This was caused by the NVDisplayContainer.exe process, which kept writing even on idle PCs. According to TechPowerUp, in extreme cases this amounted to up to 30 GB per hour, compared to only around 2 MB in five minutes with the older driver 621.01. The hotfix is based on the current Game Ready driver 621.24 from November 12. Like all hotfixes, it has gone through a shortened quality assurance process and is only offered via Nvidia's support page. Previous workarounds were rolling back to 621.01 or stopping the NVIDIA Display Container LS service. Anyone affected should install the hotfix, while everyone else can wait for the next WHQL driver. A few days earlier, AMD had a similar problem with its Radeon drivers and also released optional fixes.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz", "NVIDIA Customer Care on X"], "_src": "6e1b1d53"}, "2026-11-21-gta6-review-bombing-ultimate-laeden": {"titel": "GTA 6: User score on Metacritic drops to around 5 out of 10, players criticize shops locked for the Standard Edition", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: critics give 99, users only 5 – plus anger over locked shops", "kurz": "While GTA 6 sits at 99 with critics on Metacritic, the user score has dropped to around 5 out of 10. Some of the ratings look like deliberate review bombing. In addition, buyers of the Standard Edition are annoyed because four shops remain completely locked for them.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Insider Gaming, the user score on Metacritic stood at 5.1 out of 10 after more than 10,000 ratings, almost half of them negative. The critic score of the PS5 version remains at 99 from 152 reviews. Many low ratings consist of only one sentence or attack the story and characters for political reasons, some with racist and sexist comments. But there is also criticism of performance, bugs, lost progress and the closeness to Red Dead Redemption 2. Metacritic had already removed fake user reviews before launch, VGC reported. A second point of contention: the Ultimate Edition for 99.99 US dollars unlocks four shops, including a hair salon and a tattoo parlor. According to IGN, owners of the Standard Edition for 79.99 US dollars face locked doors and cannot even enter the furnished shops. Rockstar had announced the content in advance, but many players had expected at least access without the ability to buy. On social media, words like greedy are being used. Rockstar has not commented on either issue so far. User scores fluctuate strongly in the first days, so the figures are a snapshot.", "weitere_links": ["IGN (locked shops)", "VGC (fake reviews removed)"], "_src": "a80f0d8b"}, "2026-11-21-trump-rechenzentren-ausland": {"titel": "Trump threatens US companies with a heavy tax if they build data centers abroad – he gives no details", "schlagzeile": "Trump wants to put US companies off building data centers abroad", "kurz": "US President Donald Trump has announced that US companies will no longer be allowed to build data centers abroad or will face a heavy tax. He gave no details, tax rate or legal basis. Companies such as Microsoft, Amazon, Google and Oracle, which also operate data centers in Europe, would be affected.", "zusammenfassung": "The statement was made on Friday at a press conference at the White House, as reported by AP, The Verge and Dr. Windows. Trump said US companies would not be allowed to build data centers outside the USA. Anyone who does so anyway would face an enormous tax. By his own account, he had not informed his team beforehand. How high the levy would be and how it would be introduced is open. Companies such as Microsoft, Amazon, Google, Meta and Oracle already operate many data centers abroad, including in Europe. Dr. Windows points out that the costs could ultimately end up with customers. It is also unclear what this would mean for arrangements such as the Delos Cloud, where Microsoft acts as a technology supplier. Whether the plan will make it politically is questionable, as a Democratic majority will soon be sworn in in Congress. So far it is only an announcement, not a law or a regulation.", "weitere_links": ["AP News", "The Verge"], "_src": "04b11ca3"}, "2026-11-21-nvidia-sec-bilanzpruefung": {"titel": "Reuters: US Securities and Exchange Commission examines possible accounting issues at Nvidia, stock loses 23 percent in one week", "schlagzeile": "SEC scrutinizes Nvidia's accounting – stock posts record weekly loss", "kurz": "According to Reuters, the US Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) is examining possible accounting issues at Nvidia. It is unclear which transactions are affected, and neither the SEC nor Nvidia commented. The stock lost 23 percent this week, more than at any time since October 2008.", "zusammenfassung": "Reuters cites two people familiar with the matter, and ComputerBase and Wccftech picked up the report. The review is reportedly being conducted by staff of the SEC's Enforcement Division. Which transactions are in focus and since when the review has been running is not known. The SEC declined to comment, and Nvidia did not respond at first. The Wall Street Journal had already reported on an SEC review on Tuesday without knowing its subject. According to ComputerBase, attention is focused in particular on a change in regional revenue reporting: since last year, Nvidia has assigned revenue by the customer's headquarters instead of the billing address, which made Singapore disappear from the breakdown. Whether this is connected to the review has not been established. The financing and guarantees Nvidia uses to support AI companies and cloud providers are also drawing criticism from investors. According to Reuters, interim CEO Colette Kress announced that the company will be more selective here in the future. The stock lost 14 percent on Friday alone and 23 percent over the week. An investigation does not mean an accusation or wrongdoing; there are no results so far.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "4b615fd6"}, "2026-11-21-deltarune-kapitel-6-durchspielbar": {"titel": "Toby Fox: Deltarune Chapter 6 is playable from start to finish, localization and first tests are underway, work on Chapter 7 has begun", "schlagzeile": "Deltarune: Chapter 6 is fully playable, Chapter 7 already in the works", "kurz": "Developer Toby Fox reports that Deltarune Chapter 6 is playable from start to finish as a complete draft. Localization and first tests have begun, but some important scenes still need work. There is no release date yet; Fox hopes for 2027.", "zusammenfassung": "The information comes from Toby Fox's autumn newsletter, which Insider Gaming summarized. According to Fox, all maps, events and battles of Chapter 6 exist, and only one optional event is still dragging on. Localization and preliminary testing are said to have started in the meantime. However, some important scenes are not yet finished in their presentation, so it will take a little longer before full testing. Fox again emphasizes that Chapter 6 is rather short. Team members who have finished their work on Chapter 6 are already working on Chapter 7. Fox writes that with this chapter he feels for the first time that he knows what he is doing. There is no release date for either chapter; for Chapter 6, Fox hopes for 2027.", "_src": "faa98515"}, "2026-11-21-gta6-3-79-mrd-rekord": {"titel": "Rockstar: GTA 6 generates 3.79 billion US dollars on day one and sold 32.5 million copies before release", "schlagzeile": "Official: GTA 6 makes 3.79 billion dollars on its first day", "kurz": "Rockstar Games reports revenue of 3.79 billion US dollars for GTA 6 on its first day of sales. Before launch, 32.5 million copies were sold. According to the company, this makes it the biggest entertainment launch of all time across all media.", "zusammenfassung": "The figures come from a press release by Rockstar Games and Take-Two, as reported by Eurogamer and AP. They refer to worldwide retail sales through the end of November 19, based on company estimates. According to Rockstar, the 32.5 million copies sold in advance on PS5 and Xbox Series X/S are a record across all platforms. For comparison: 13 years ago, GTA 5 made around 800 million US dollars on its first day. The figures are well above the Sensor Tower estimate, which assumed around 25 million games and 2.36 billion US dollars. Rockstar does not say how many copies were sold after launch without a pre-order. There were also records in data traffic: US provider Comcast reports the busiest traffic day in its history, with a peak 31 percent above a normal day. According to Comcast, 24 percent of internet traffic at peak times was accounted for by downloading and playing GTA 6. Rockstar has still not announced a PC version.", "weitere_links": ["Business Wire (Rockstar/Take-Two press release)", "AP News", "IGN (Comcast record)"], "_src": "ac69773b"}, "2026-11-21-persona-schnellere-entwicklung": {"titel": "Atlus promises shorter waits between future Persona games, still hardly any details on Persona 6", "schlagzeile": "Persona 6 is not the end: Atlus no longer wants fans to wait so long", "kurz": "Atlus wants to shorten the gaps between major Persona games. P-Studio producer Kazuhisa Wada said this in an interview. For Persona 6 itself, there is still only a teaser and no release date.", "zusammenfassung": "Wada spoke in an interview with the Sega magazine Samania, and Eurogamer reports based on a translation by GamesRadar+. Persona 6 is not the end, and the team is working to ensure that fans will not have to wait as long for the next game as before. Large RPGs like Persona take five years or more to develop, which is why there are often long gaps between numbered entries. Wada does not say how Atlus intends to change this. It is open whether the next main entry is already being developed in parallel or whether only processes are being streamlined. He could say little about Persona 6, but the team wants to create something better than ever before. So far there is only a short teaser from the Xbox Games Showcase 2026. Atlus has not announced a release date or platform details.", "_src": "719cd5d5"}, "2026-11-21-microsoft-pc-assist": {"titel": "Microsoft releases the PC Assist app for Windows 11: good system overview, but many features just open Get Help or Bing", "schlagzeile": "Microsoft PC Assist: new Windows app with good ideas and a lot of Bing", "kurz": "With PC Assist, Microsoft offers a new optional app for Windows that is meant to solve problems and monitor performance, storage and network. Windows Latest praises the overviews but criticizes that troubleshooters only open the Get Help app and tools point to Bing. By default, the installer wants to set Bing as the search engine.", "zusammenfassung": "Windows Latest tested PC Assist version 0.4.4.0, and the app is a separate download from Microsoft's website. During installation, an option is preselected that sets Bing as the home page and search engine in several browsers. Microsoft points this out on the download page and also announces promotional notifications in the app. To launch, the app needs the .NET 10 Desktop Runtime. According to the test, the performance, storage and network sections clearly show usage, large and duplicate files, and data consumption per app. The troubleshooters for audio, network, printers or Bluetooth, on the other hand, only open the existing Get Help app. All ten tools, such as translator, weather or speed test, open the respective Bing page in the browser. The interface runs partly via WebView2, and there is no dark mode or freely resizable window. Microsoft advertises the app on Bing as an AI assistant, but in the test Windows Latest found no AI feature in the app. The app is optional and is not installed automatically.", "_src": "13b96d1c"}, "2026-11-20-cairn-ki-agenten-zero-day": {"titel": "Amazon: suspected Chinese attackers had autonomous AI agents of the Cairn platform find a zero-day flaw in MONAI Label and take over a server", "schlagzeile": "“Obtain shell access”: AI agents find zero-day and hijack server", "kurz": "According to Amazon, attackers used a platform for autonomous AI agents called Cairn to find and exploit a previously unknown flaw. The agents were only given the task of obtaining shell access. Within eleven minutes they found a way in via medical imaging software and later took over the server.", "zusammenfassung": "Amazon Threat Intelligence discovered the campaign because the attackers had left their Cairn instance openly accessible online without a password, BleepingComputer reports. Cairn is actually a legitimate penetration testing tool that coordinates multiple AI agents. The attacks ran from September 8 to 10 and mainly targeted educational institutions in East Asia outside China. The agents found a path traversal flaw in MONAI Label, an open-source application for labeling medical images. According to Amazon, eleven minutes passed from exploring the interface to exploitation. Later, they used the flaw to write a backdoor into a Python startup file and gained root privileges. Not everything worked: a 16-hour attempt with 148 actions against a Redis server failed, as did six hours of password guessing against a university GPU server. Amazon attributes the attackers to China with moderate confidence, based on language, timestamps and targets. The flaw in MONAI Label has been fixed since an update on November 18. Amazon warns that AI agents find and exploit flaws faster than security teams can react.", "_src": "c3315844"}, "2026-11-20-nvidia-kalifornien-nyt-huang": {"titel": "California's attorney general serves Nvidia an investigative subpoena over possible deliveries to China; at the same time, a New York Times report accuses former CEO Jensen Huang of decades of humiliating employees", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia: California investigates, NYT levels serious accusations at Huang", "kurz": "California Attorney General Rob Bonta is examining whether Nvidia chips or confidential data reached China and whether investors were misled. In parallel, the New York Times reports decades of verbal abuse by former CEO Jensen Huang. A spokesperson for Huang rejects the allegations.", "zusammenfassung": "Bonta served Nvidia an investigative subpoena on November 19, his office said in a press release. It asks whether advanced Nvidia chips or confidential information may have reached China and whether Nvidia misinformed investors and the public about this risk. The trigger is the former CEO's affair with a manager who, according to suspicions of US security agencies, is said to have been recruited by Chinese intelligence, heise reports. According to heise, there was initially no response from Nvidia. On Friday, a New York Times report followed, covered by PC Gamer and Eurogamer. In it, more than a dozen current and former employees accuse Huang of insulting staff in front of colleagues for decades and threatening them with drastic violent fantasies. A former head of HR is said to have been fired in 2005 after criticizing this and to have reached a confidential settlement of more than one million dollars. Huang's spokesperson calls the account fabrications that thousands of supporters inside the company refute. According to PC Gamer, a public petition for Huang's return now has over 200,000 signatures. The board chair had previously stated, according to reports, that the company does not intend to reinstate Huang as CEO. The newspaper's allegations have not been examined in court, and the investigation in California is only at the beginning.", "weitere_links": ["heise online", "California Department of Justice (press release)", "Eurogamer"], "_src": "ec7eb499"}, "2026-11-20-openai-amd-chipdesign-ki": {"titel": "OpenAI models reworked circuit code from AMD GPU and CPU designs; according to OpenAI up to 14 percent PPA gain, with some changes already in a chip handed off for manufacturing", "schlagzeile": "AI as co-designer: OpenAI squeezes up to 14 percent out of an AMD graphics chip", "kurz": "OpenAI had its AI models work on circuit designs from AMD. On a flagship GPU they reportedly achieved up to 14 percent better PPA figures, on an upcoming CPU a single-digit percentage. According to OpenAI, AMD has already adopted some changes in a chip that went to manufacturing.", "zusammenfassung": "The figures come from a technical report by OpenAI, covered by ComputerBase, PC Gamer, PCGH and Wccftech. PPA stands for power, performance and area, the three metrics against which every change to a chip design is measured. The 14 percent therefore does not automatically mean 14 percent more gaming performance, and OpenAI does not break down how the three values changed individually. Which AMD GPU is meant also remains open. The models worked directly on the SystemVerilog code, i.e. the description of the circuits, and the results were checked with design tools from Synopsys. According to OpenAI, the result equalled roughly a year of optimization work, done in less than five months. For key blocks of an upcoming AMD flagship CPU, the improvements are said to be in the single-digit percent range. AMD reportedly adopted some changes in a chip recently submitted for manufacturing, and more are to flow into future products. Whether upcoming architectures such as RDNA 5 or Zen 6 will benefit is speculation by ComputerBase and not confirmed. OpenAI had previously tested the method on its own AI accelerator Jalapeño, where the area of the vector unit, for example, shrank by around 13 percent. Together with Synopsys, OpenAI is now developing a specialized model for chip design tools. A statement from AMD with details is not yet available.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "PC Games Hardware", "Wccftech"], "_src": "652d4ddb"}, "2026-11-20-sockel1700-undervolting-cep": {"titel": "Gigabyte confirms to PCGH: with new Socket 1700 BIOS versions, undervolting remains possible on K processors and upcoming Raptor Lake re-releases, CEP can be switched off manually", "schlagzeile": "Intel Socket 1700: undervolting stays possible with new BIOS – with a catch", "kurz": "New BIOS versions for Socket 1700 motherboards enable Intel's CEP protection by default, which costs performance when undervolting. According to Gigabyte, it can be switched off on K processors of the Core i-12000 to 14000 series and upcoming refresh CPUs. Anyone with a non-K CPU who undervolts should stick with the old BIOS.", "zusammenfassung": "PCGH had asked Gigabyte about the consequences of the new microcode 0x137, which ships with BIOS updates for upcoming Intel processors. With previous versions using this microcode, users complained about a permanently active Current Excursion Protection, CEP for short. The feature lowers the clock speed when the core voltage drops below a minimum threshold and is meant to prevent crashes. Anyone who deliberately runs their CPU at lower voltage to save power and heat loses performance as a result. According to Gigabyte, CEP stays enabled by default for the time being but can be switched off manually. This applies to K models of the Core i-12000, 13000 and 14000 series as well as to the upcoming refresh processors. For models without the K suffix, PCGH advises undervolters to keep using the old BIOS. The statement is subject to Intel issuing new requirements. Intel has not yet officially confirmed the Raptor Lake re-releases for budget DDR4 PCs expected for 2027. Anyone who does not want to test stability extensively themselves is better served with CEP enabled, according to PCGH. The statement comes from Gigabyte; things may look different for other motherboard manufacturers.", "_src": "18d970a1"}, "2026-11-20-dnd-beyond-optimizely-malware": {"titel": "D&D Beyond briefly served malicious code on November 16 via the compromised service Optimizely; payment data not affected according to the operator", "schlagzeile": "D&D Beyond served malicious code – via a third-party website tool", "kurz": "The official Dungeons & Dragons platform D&D Beyond was among almost 200 websites where attackers injected malicious code via the Optimizely service. The code could capture card entries and swap crypto addresses. According to the operator, payments ran through a separate provider and were not affected.", "zusammenfassung": "On November 16, attackers exploited a flaw in the account signup of Optimizely Web Experimentation, a widely used tool for website testing, GameStar and GamesRadar+ report. This let them inject malicious JavaScript into customer projects, which those customers' websites then delivered to visitors. According to security researchers at Report URI, 178 organizations were affected, including D&D Beyond and the Magic shop Secret Lair. The code could read card data from payment forms, swap crypto wallet addresses and load known exploits on older iPhones and iPads. Optimizely says it closed the flaw within three hours of detection, and fewer than five percent of customers were affected. D&D Beyond has removed the service, and executive producer Brian Perry stresses that payments are handled by a separate payment provider. D&D Beyond intends to contact players directly if they need to take action. For Secret Lair, Wizards of the Coast reports that no customer data was affected. As a precaution, GameStar recommends logging out and back in, a new password and up-to-date Apple systems. How many visitors actually executed the code is not known.", "weitere_links": ["GamesRadar+"], "_src": "c5b7e321"}, "2026-11-20-ruby-kritische-luecken": {"titel": "Ruby fixes seven flaws in string and regex handling, six allow code execution; updates to 4.0.10, 3.4.13 and 3.3.14, Rails applications, GitHub and GitLab also affected", "schlagzeile": "Ruby: dangerous flaws in search patterns – Rails apps must update too", "kurz": "The Ruby project has fixed seven security vulnerabilities, six of which can allow attackers to execute their own code. Proof-of-concept exploits exist for five. Developers should update to Ruby 4.0.10, 3.4.13 or 3.3.14.", "zusammenfassung": "According to heise, the flaws lie in the processing of strings and regular expressions, i.e. search patterns. It becomes dangerous above all when an application lets users supply their own search patterns, for example in a Rails web application. A crafted pattern can then free memory twice or write past a buffer while it is being compiled and thus inject code. Other bugs affect upper and lower case conversion. The GitHub advisory rates several flaws as critical. For the only flaw with a CVE number already assigned, the rating is considerably more cautious at CVSS 7.4 with a local attack vector. The bugs were fixed on November 18. Four of them were reported by researcher Stephan Lipp and the AI company Anthropic, and one fix commit even names an AI model as co-author. According to heise, large Ruby applications such as GitHub and GitLab are also affected. Anyone running Ruby or Rails themselves should update promptly. There is no direct need for action for regular Windows or gaming users.", "_src": "25afad94"}, "2026-11-20-gta6-xbox-auto-upload-sperren": {"titel": "Xbox players receive two-day suspensions after automatically uploaded GTA 6 clips with beach scenes were apparently flagged by automated content moderation", "schlagzeile": "Filmed GTA 6 at the beach, banned on Xbox: automatic upload as a trap", "kurz": "Some Xbox players received a two-day suspension after the launch of GTA 6. The trigger was apparently automatically uploaded gameplay clips with beach scenes and characters in swimwear. Anyone who wants to avoid this can switch off automatic uploads in the settings.", "zusammenfassung": "Affected players have posted on Reddit, and Pure Xbox and Dr. Windows picked up the cases. At first the suspensions seemed arbitrary; later it turned out that the clips had been recorded on the beaches of Leonida. On Xbox, captures are automatically uploaded to the servers by default. There, Microsoft checks them for prohibited content such as hate speech, drugs, excessive violence as well as nudity and sexual content. One affected player writes that his clip showed no nudity at all, just normal beach scenes. Pure Xbox points out that GTA 6 does contain nudity elsewhere; whether individual clips showed such scenes is unclear. The decisions appear automated and, according to Pure Xbox, cannot be appealed. Microsoft has not commented publicly so far, and how many players are affected is unknown. Automatic uploads can be switched off under Settings, Preferences, Capture and share. According to the reports, the suspensions last two days, and accounts are not deleted.", "weitere_links": ["Pure Xbox"], "_src": "b7031703"}, "2026-11-20-windows11-26h2-automatisch": {"titel": "Since this week, Microsoft has been automatically installing Windows 11 26H2 on personal and unmanaged PCs running Windows 11 24H2 and 25H2", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 26H2 now arrives automatically – no need to click update", "kurz": "Microsoft is now automatically distributing Windows 11 26H2 to personal PCs and those not managed by an IT department. Devices running Windows 11 24H2 and 25H2 are affected. Until now, the update only came if you searched for it yourself.", "zusammenfassung": "According to an entry on the Windows release health dashboard reported by BleepingComputer, Microsoft started the next phase of the rollout on November 18. Since the end of October, all eligible devices could get 26H2 manually via Windows Update. Now automatic delivery is being expanded gradually, first for unmanaged devices running Windows 11 24H2 and 25H2. Whether and when a PC gets the update depends on its Windows Update settings. Anyone who wants it right away checks for updates under Settings and Windows Update and enables the option for the latest updates. Windows 11 26H2 has been generally available since September and installs as a small enablement package, which is supposed to be quick. It contains all the features Microsoft announced for 24H2 and 25H2. Support for 26H2 ends in October 2029. Last month, Microsoft had also urged users to update unsupported versions, because they will no longer receive security updates after a certificate rotation next year. This week, Microsoft also confirmed problems with hotpatches, which however only affect managed business devices.", "_src": "89f06a41"}, "2026-11-20-total-war-40k-sternensysteme": {"titel": "Total War: Warhammer 40,000 splits the campaign into star systems with their own mini-campaigns, stories and victory objectives; Creative Assembly shows fleets and Space Marine armies in a livestream", "schlagzeile": "Total War: Warhammer 40,000 breaks the galaxy into mini-campaigns", "kurz": "Creative Assembly showed the campaign of Total War: Warhammer 40,000 in an hour-long livestream. Each star system is its own self-contained campaign with a story and victory objectives. Units and abilities carry over to the next system.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Eurogamer, the developers justify the structure by saying the size of the whole galaxy cannot be represented on a single Total War map. Each system therefore has its own starting situation, its own narrative and its own victory objectives. The stream focused on the Praevoss system with several planets, on three of which you can land and fight battles. One objective shown required holding a planet with Space Marines while wiping out an Ork scourge. Much time went to the space fleets, which transport troops, can be upgraded and support armies with orbital bombardments, for example. Space Marine armies are few, expensive and powerful units. Losing an entire army is meant to hurt deliberately, because in the Warhammer universe it equals a whole chapter. After a system you move on and keep units and unlocked abilities. The game is due in 2027, with no exact date yet. How many star systems and playable factions there will be at launch is not clear from the report.", "_src": "337fc242"}, "2026-11-20-vulkan-1-4-369-amd-raytracing": {"titel": "Vulkan 1.4.369 brings the experimental AMD extension VK_AMDX_multi_level_acceleration_structure for additional levels in ray tracing acceleration structures", "schlagzeile": "Vulkan 1.4.369: AMD extension aims to speed up ray tracing in large worlds", "kurz": "The new Vulkan update 1.4.369 contains an experimental AMD extension for ray tracing. It allows up to two additional levels in the acceleration structure. This is meant to reduce build times and memory usage in complex, animated game worlds.", "zusammenfassung": "The Khronos Group published the specification on November 20, and Phoronix highlighted the addition. Ray tracing needs an acceleration structure, a kind of search tree over all objects in the scene, which has to be constantly rebuilt or updated when things move. So far, two levels are provided for this, which according to the proposal document forces developers to limit the complexity of their ray-traced worlds. The main problems are long build and update times and high memory usage, especially with lots of animated geometry. The extension VK_AMDX_multi_level_acceleration_structure allows up to two additional instance levels. This gives finer control over which parts of large worlds need to be rebuilt together. Because geometry can be reused multiple times, memory usage is also expected to drop. The AMDX prefix shows that the extension is still experimental and may change. Whether and when it will arrive in drivers and games is open. At the end of October, Microsoft had also presented new features for ray tracing acceleration structures in a DirectX preview with clustered geometry and partitioned TLAS. Apart from that, Vulkan 1.4.369 mainly contains clarifications and fixes to the specification.", "weitere_links": ["Khronos Vulkan-Docs (GitHub, v1.4.369)", "DirectX Developer Blog (ray tracing preview, Oct 28, 2026)"], "_src": "61e18ad7"}, "2026-11-20-f5-big-ip-kritische-luecken": {"titel": "F5 releases emergency hotfixes for five critical buffer overflows in BIG-IP APM and iRules that let attackers execute code without authentication", "schlagzeile": "F5 BIG-IP: five critical flaws, no workaround – admins should patch now", "kurz": "F5 warns of five critical vulnerabilities in BIG-IP that let attackers without authentication crash systems or execute code. There is no workaround, only hotfixes. According to F5, the flaws are not being exploited so far.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, the affected components are BIG-IP's Access Policy Manager, which companies use to control access to their applications, and the iRules scripting feature. The five flaws with the identifiers CVE-2026-121805, CVE-2026-120292, CVE-2026-120285, CVE-2026-116953 and CVE-2026-123637 are stack buffer overflows. Unauthenticated attackers can use them to crash the central traffic process and, with a suitable configuration, execute their own code. In addition, there is a hotfix for a high-severity SAML flaw that can cause denial of service. F5 names no countermeasures other than the hotfixes released on Wednesday. According to Shadowserver, more than 177,000 BIG-IP instances are reachable online, and more than 14,600 addresses show characteristics of the Access Policy Manager. How many of them are already patched is unknown. According to F5, the new flaws are not being exploited so far, but F5 devices are regularly targeted by criminals and state attackers. The US agency CISA has listed seven actively exploited F5 flaws since 2021. This is not an issue for home users, but for corporate admins the update has top priority.", "_src": "458304ca"}, "2026-11-20-rocm-10-2-radeon-780m": {"titel": "AMD ROCm 10.2 officially supports 18 more Ryzen processors with Radeon 780M, 760M and 740M for PyTorch and vLLM on Windows and Linux", "schlagzeile": "Local AI without a graphics card: ROCm now officially supports Radeon 780M", "kurz": "With ROCm 10.2, AMD has extended official support to 18 more Ryzen processors with integrated graphics. This means AI tools such as PyTorch and vLLM can be used without tinkering on many laptops and mini PCs with Radeon 780M. This applies to Windows and Linux.", "zusammenfassung": "ROCm is AMD's software platform for computing on the graphics unit; PCGH cites AMD and Phoronix for the report. Newly supported are, among others, the Ryzen 9 180, Ryzen 7 165, Ryzen 7 155, Ryzen 5 125 as well as models such as the Ryzen 7 253 and their Pro variants. The basis is the official enablement of the gfx1103 graphics architecture on which the Radeon 780M, 760M and 740M are based. Until now, users of such devices often had to compile software themselves or use workarounds. Supported are the HIP interface as well as PyTorch and vLLM, which ROCm 10.2 raises to versions 2.15 and 0.32. AMD also improves communication between up to eight Radeon cards in PCIe systems. The enablement, however, says nothing about speed. Integrated graphics shares system memory with the processor, so its size and bandwidth limit which language models run sensibly. For smaller models, these devices are now officially an option, though. The update has nothing to do with gaming performance.", "_src": "302faa15"}, "2026-11-20-usa-ki-chips-china-genehmigt": {"titel": "US Commerce Department approved the export of 879,000 AI chips from Nvidia and AMD to China, including to Alibaba and Tencent, which the Pentagon lists as military companies", "schlagzeile": "879,000 AI chips for China: US approved Nvidia and AMD sales", "kurz": "The US government allowed Nvidia and AMD to sell 879,000 AI chips to China. These include deliveries to Alibaba and Tencent, which are on the US Department of War's list of Chinese military companies. The two manufacturers had applied for 3.4 million chips.", "zusammenfassung": "The figures were published by Brian Mast, chairman of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the US House of Representatives, ComputerBase reports. He had requested the export applications from the Commerce Department's responsible agency, the BIS. According to them, Nvidia and AMD applied for approvals for a total of 3.4 million chips, and 879,000 were allowed. Among those rejected were Nvidia applications for 610,000 chips for Alibaba and 508,000 for TikTok owner ByteDance. Other sales to Alibaba and Tencent, however, were approved, even though both companies are classified as linked to the Chinese military. Mast sees this as contradicting the goals of US export policy. For some Nvidia applications he also suspects that intermediaries would have resold the chips to blocked companies, while the manufacturers rated this risk as low in each application. Since this week, a new US rule has also banned Chinese companies from remotely accessing chips in foreign data centers. Tencent and Alibaba expect less computing power and a slower expansion as a result. Approved exports do not automatically mean delivery, because Beijing must also allow the import and has sometimes refused. Which chip models exactly are affected is not clear from the reports.", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de"], "_src": "10add17c"}, "2026-11-20-moore-threads-lushan-teaser": {"titel": "Moore Threads teases the desktop graphics card “Lushan” with what the manufacturer calls the largest video memory of any consumer GPU; unveiling on December 29", "schlagzeile": "China's Lushan graphics card is said to have more video memory than any other", "kurz": "Chinese manufacturer Moore Threads announces a new desktop graphics card codenamed Lushan. It is said to offer the largest video memory in the history of consumer graphics cards and to be intended for both gaming and local AI. The teaser does not reveal exactly how much memory it will have.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Wccftech, a Moore Threads product manager published the teaser on social media on November 18, and IT Home picked it up. Lushan is to be fully unveiled on December 29 at the company's own MUSA developer conference. The card is positioned for demanding PC games as well as for running AI language models locally. For the latter in particular, lots of video memory matters, because larger models otherwise do not fit into the graphics card's memory. According to the translated teaser, AI computing performance is to increase 64-fold, and a new rendering architecture called UNITE and a self-developed ray tracing unit are also mentioned. What the factor of 64 refers to is open. Moore Threads has not yet named the exact amount of memory, bandwidth, price or availability. Whether Lushan will get more memory than the 32 gigabytes of an RTX 5090 is only an obvious assumption. The previous cards MTT S80 and S90 have improved significantly through driver updates but do not play in the high end performance-wise. Moore Threads cards have so far hardly been available in Europe. Reliable data will only come after the unveiling at the end of December.", "_src": "9e1861de"}, "2026-11-21-windows-rdma-usb4-ki": {"titel": "Microsoft introduces RDMA over USB4 for Windows: several PCs are to run a large AI model together via USB4 cable", "schlagzeile": "Windows links PCs via USB4 cable – for AI models that don't fit on one", "kurz": "Microsoft has announced a developer preview of RDMA over USB4 for Windows. This is intended to let several PCs connected via USB4 cable run a large AI model together, pooling memory and graphics power. The required Windows test build is to be released soon for Insiders in the Experimental channel.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft introduced the technology in a blog post on November 19, as reported by Neowin and VideoCardz. RDMA allows direct data exchange between the main memory of two systems, bypassing the usual network stack. Until now, this required special server network cards on Windows, but now ordinary USB4 ports are supposed to be enough, including Thunderbolt 4 and 5. According to Microsoft, the latency of small messages drops to about 28 to 50 microseconds, around four times less than with UDP over the same connection. In tests, three mini PCs with Ryzen AI Max+ 395 and 128 GB of memory each ran the Qwen3-235B model at around 18.5 tokens per second. Intel showed GPT-OSS-120B on three and four systems with Core Ultra Series 3. Each PC must be connected directly to every other one, and a chain costs considerable performance. The USB4 driver provider and an adapted llama.cpp are already available as open source. According to Neowin, the preview requires a registry entry and test signing, which means temporarily disabling Secure Boot. The feature is off by default and is aimed at developers for now.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft Tech Community (blog)", "Microsoft on GitHub", "VideoCardz"], "_src": "8b01c683"}, "2026-11-20-fastunlock-windows-sperrbildschirm": {"titel": "Unpatched Windows 11 flaw FastUnlock: the Narrator screen reader can be used to run code on the lock screen if an attacker has physical access", "schlagzeile": "FastUnlock: new Windows flaw bypasses the lock screen via Narrator", "kurz": "A security researcher has published an unpatched flaw in Windows 11 that lets someone start programs on a locked PC. Physical access and a user account linked to a Microsoft account are required. There is no patch yet.", "zusammenfassung": "FastUnlock was published by the former Microsoft employee known as MSNightmare or Nightmare Eclipse, who regularly makes flaws public without warning. The attack starts on the lock screen via \"I forgot my PIN\", after which the Narrator screen reader is opened with the Windows key and U. According to the researcher, its redesigned interface wrongly also runs in the lock screen context and leads through hidden windows into Settings. From there, programs can be started, for example from a USB stick, under the restricted WsiAccount account, not as administrator. The security firm ThreatLocker reproduced and confirmed the method. According to the researcher, it was tested on Windows 11 26H2 with the November updates. The researcher speaks of a BitLocker bypass; The Hacker News and Cybersecuritynews clarify that the encryption is not cracked. The attack works because the drive, unlocked automatically via TPM, is already readable at the lock screen. According to the researcher, anyone who only uses local accounts is not affected. Until a patch arrives, experts recommend a BitLocker PIN at startup and shutting down or hibernating instead of locking when devices are unattended. There are no signs of real-world attacks so far, and no statement or CVE from Microsoft either.", "weitere_links": ["The Hacker News", "Tom's Hardware", "ThreatLocker"], "_src": "9655aaf1"}, "2026-11-20-gta6-remote-play-dlss5-mod": {"titel": "Modder streams GTA 6 to a PC via PS5 Remote Play and boosts the image to 60 fps there with an unofficial DLSS 5 integration and Frame Generation", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 at 60 fps on PC: modder runs the PS5 stream through DLSS 5", "kurz": "A modder runs GTA 6 on the PS5, streams the image to a PC via Remote Play and doubles the frame rate there to around 60 fps with an RTX 5080. To do this, he uses an experimental, unofficial DLSS 5 integration. The controls, however, remain at 30 fps and even become more sluggish.", "zusammenfassung": "According to ComputerBase, the modder Phosphen has published a setup script on GitHub that installs the open-source software Veyra with suitable settings. The PS5 transmits the game via Remote Play at 1080p and 60 Hz to the Windows PC; since the console only renders 30 frames per second, every second frame is a duplicate. Veyra removes these duplicates and generates new intermediate frames with Frame Generation, and no capture card is needed. For the visual upgrade, Veyra uses a neural rendering runtime signed by Nvidia according to the project, but the integration itself comes from the community and is not certified. According to the modder's measurements on around 80 seconds of footage, the average frame rate rose from 29.5 to 59 fps, and processing on the RTX 5080 takes about 12 milliseconds per frame. These values have not been independently verified. The catch: inputs still run through the console at 30 fps, and the stream plus post-processing increase input latency. In addition, the stream is limited to 1080p and compressed, DLSS cannot reliably restore lost detail, and without depth and motion data from the engine, artifacts threaten during fast movement. So this is a technical experiment, not a PC version of GTA 6.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz"], "_src": "1204794c"}, "2026-11-20-legion-go-beam-leak": {"titel": "Rumor: Lenovo is said to be planning a cheaper handheld, the Legion Go Beam, with fixed controllers, wide display bezels and no touchpad", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Lenovo Legion Go Beam said to be a cheaper handheld without touchpad", "kurz": "Leaked product images show a previously unannounced handheld called Legion Go Beam. It looks like a stripped-down version of the Legion Go S with fixed controllers and no touchpad. Lenovo has not confirmed the device, and there are no technical specifications.", "zusammenfassung": "The three images were published by Windows Latest and picked up by ComputerBase, TechPowerUp and VideoCardz. They show a white handheld with green accents that resembles the Legion Go S but is more rounded and has differently placed analog sticks. Two front-facing speakers, four shoulder buttons and two extra buttons on the back are visible. The bezels above and below the display are noticeably wider than on the Legion Go S; Notebookcheck therefore suspects a 16:9 screen instead of 16:10. On top, only one USB-C port, a headphone jack and a microSD reader can be seen; whether a second USB-C port is missing or just placed elsewhere is unclear. Processor, memory, display, battery and operating system are unknown. Because of the small vents and the name, The Verge speculates about a device mainly intended for cloud gaming or streaming; there is no evidence of a partnership with Microsoft or Nvidia. The visible cutbacks suggest a position below the Legion Go S, while price and date are missing. A reveal at CES in January is considered possible, as Lenovo holds its Tech World there on January 6. Everything comes from a single image source and is unconfirmed.", "ursprungsquelle": "Windows Latest (exclusive product images)", "weitere_links": ["Windows Latest", "TechPowerUp", "VideoCardz"], "_src": "802ceaec"}, "2026-11-20-gta6-sensor-tower-2-36-mrd": {"titel": "Market researcher Sensor Tower estimates GTA 6 at around 24.6 million copies sold and 2.36 billion dollars in revenue after the first day, including pre-orders", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: Estimate sees 24.6 million copies sold and 2.36 billion dollars", "kurz": "According to Sensor Tower, GTA 6 had sold around 24.6 million copies and grossed about 2.36 billion dollars by the evening of launch day. The figure includes pre-orders and is an estimate that Take-Two has not confirmed. For comparison: GTA 5 made around 800 million dollars on its first day in 2013.", "zusammenfassung": "Sensor Tower gave the estimate to Deadline, and the BBC also reports on it. On the Wednesday before launch, the figure was still around 17.1 million copies and 1.65 billion dollars, and on Thursday morning 19.1 million and 1.84 billion. About three quarters of sales are said to be on PS5, the rest on Xbox; GTA 6 has not yet been released on PC. Sensor Tower speaks of the most successful launch of an entertainment product ever. According to the company, it relies on data from email purchase receipts and public profiles on the gaming platforms, among other things. The catch is important: the 2.36 billion dollars were not generated within 24 hours of launch but include all pre-orders. Take-Two usually publishes its own sales figures with its quarterly results, so official confirmation is still pending. According to Sensor Tower, GTA 6 is expected to reduce playtime in other single-player titles by around 10 percent. The provider's earlier estimates have also changed several times over the past few days.", "weitere_links": ["BBC", "PC Games"], "_src": "2163f633"}, "2026-11-20-vmware-vcenter-zero-day": {"titel": "Broadcom fixes a critical flaw in VMware vCenter Server that suspected Chinese state hackers have been exploiting for attacks since September, according to Mandiant", "schlagzeile": "VMware vCenter: emergency patch for flaw hackers have used since September", "kurz": "Broadcom has fixed a critical flaw in VMware vCenter Server that allows attackers to gain administrator rights without logging in. According to Mandiant, a suspected Chinese hacking group has been exploiting it since early September. Admins should patch immediately.", "zusammenfassung": "The flaw is tracked as CVE-2026-123890 and resides in the VMware Directory Service of vCenter Server, which companies use to manage their virtual machines. According to BleepingComputer, an attacker with network access can bypass authentication and obtain a session as administrator. Broadcom fixes it in security advisory VMSA-2026-0009 from November 19, along with four other flaws in SDDC Manager and VMware Tools for Windows. Broadcom classifies the update as an emergency, there are no official workarounds, and network and firewall restrictions can only reduce the risk. Mandiant and Google's Threat Intelligence Group attribute the attacks to the group Armory Castle, formerly known as UNC5221. According to them, the attackers first got in through another flaw in BeyondTrust Remote Support and then moved to internal Linux systems and the VMware infrastructure. With their own tools, they created administrator accounts, stole the directory database and, using stolen signing keys, were able to forge login tokens and thus also bypass multi-factor authentication. In the end, they reached ESXi hosts and data from virtual machines. Broadcom itself has not confirmed the exploitation, but Mandiant has documented it. This is not an issue for home users, but for corporate admins the update has top priority.", "_src": "96532db8"}, "2026-11-20-crusader-kings-3-gratis-wochenende": {"titel": "Crusader Kings 3 is free to play on Steam until Monday, November 23; at the same time, the base game costs 14.99 euros with a 70 percent discount until November 30", "schlagzeile": "Crusader Kings 3 free this weekend – then 70 percent off", "kurz": "Paradox's medieval strategy game Crusader Kings 3 can be tried for free on Steam until Monday. Anyone who wants to buy it afterwards pays 14.99 instead of 49.99 euros until November 30. The free weekend comes shortly after the new expansion Silk & Silver.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Polygon, the free weekend runs until Monday, November 23, at 10 a.m. Pacific Time, which is 7 p.m. in Austria and Germany. On the Steam page, the game is currently listed with the option to play for free and a weekend deal. According to Steam, the 70 percent discount applies until November 30, and in the Austrian store the price drops from 49.99 to 14.99 euros. This is a time-limited free weekend, not a permanent giveaway. Crusader Kings 3 was released in September 2020 and lets players lead a medieval noble family across generations. The focus is on diplomacy, marriage politics, succession and intrigue, with war being only one part of it. When the ruler dies, you continue playing as the heir. Shortly before the free weekend, the paid expansion Silk & Silver and the free update 1.21 \"Florin\" were released on November 17.", "weitere_links": ["Steam (Crusader Kings III)"], "_src": "8678efa8"}, "2026-11-20-steam-machine-ohne-reservierung": {"titel": "Valve ends Steam Machine reservations: the 512 GB model can be ordered freely, the 2 TB waitlist is closed, prices could rise", "schlagzeile": "Steam Machine now without reservation – Valve warns of higher prices", "kurz": "Valve is now selling the 512 GB Steam Machine without a reservation while stocks last. The waitlist for the 2 TB model no longer accepts new sign-ups. Because memory and SSD costs are rising sharply, Valve says it does not yet know how many units it can build and at what price.", "zusammenfassung": "Due to the memory crisis, Valve had so far only sold the Steam Machine through a reservation system with random selection. According to PC Gamer, all reservations for the 512 GB model have now been fulfilled, and there is even remaining stock that can be added to the cart directly. Once this production run sells out, the device will be marked out of stock until new units are ready. For the 2 TB model, the waitlist exceeds current production. Anyone already on the list keeps their place, but new sign-ups are no longer possible, and Valve stresses that no one on the waitlist is guaranteed a unit. Anyone who buys the 512 GB model instead loses their place on the 2 TB list. Valve writes that memory and storage costs continue to rise at unprecedented levels. It therefore does not yet know how many Steam Machines it can build and at what price they will be offered. Even if more units are built, Valve says it will be in smaller quantities than planned. Valve plans to share new information on 2 TB availability in January. Valve has not announced a specific price increase so far.", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp", "GamingOnLinux"], "_src": "6a525997"}, "2026-11-20-gta6-cyberleek-xbox-build": {"titel": "Hacker group CyberLeek claims to have released a nearly finished Xbox version of GTA 6 via torrent – without the executable, which is supposed to follow later", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Hackers claim to have put a near-final GTA 6 Xbox build online", "kurz": "The group CyberLeek, which had already leaked GTA 6 gameplay before launch, claims to have released a development build of the game from November 2026. According to media reports, the executable is missing, so the game cannot run for now. Whether the files are genuine is unconfirmed.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Eurogamer, VGC and PC Gamer, CyberLeek is offering a download of around 209 GB on its own site, allegedly the Xbox version from November 2026 and thus very close to the retail version. Eurogamer was able to see the download page but could not verify the existence of actual game files. According to the group, one file is deliberately missing: the main executable, which is supposed to appear only after a countdown. It would come earlier if a crypto token of the group reaches a certain value; many of the group's leaks so far have been tied to such crypto schemes. CyberLeek also claims the community will emulate the game on PC within a week and threatens a PS5 version if necessary. Whether that works technically is completely open. Rockstar had called earlier leaks by the group heartbreaking, and Take-Two tried to obtain clues about the identity from Discord via a subpoena. There is no statement from Rockstar or Take-Two on the new leak so far. Important: downloading pirated copies is illegal, and supposed leak downloads are a popular way to spread malware. GTA 6 has officially only been released for PS5 and Xbox Series, and Rockstar has not yet announced a PC version.", "ursprungsquelle": "CyberLeek (own website/statement)", "weitere_links": ["Video Games Chronicle (VGC)", "PC Gamer", "Neowin"], "_src": "5da86e6a"}, "2026-11-20-intel-it-entlassungen": {"titel": "Intel continues job cuts: according to Business Insider, a new round of layoffs hits the global IT department, the number affected is unknown", "schlagzeile": "Intel keeps cutting: now the global IT department is said to be hit", "kurz": "According to Business Insider, Intel has started another round of layoffs, this time in its global IT department. Intel does not say how many jobs will be cut. Since the end of 2024, the workforce has already shrunk by around 27,800 people.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Business Insider, the cuts in Intel's IT organization began on November 16, as reported by Tom's Hardware and Wccftech. The department has around 2,607 employees at 55 sites in 53 countries. Alleged employees speak of a double-digit percentage, meaning at least around 260 jobs; these claims have not been independently confirmed. Intel names neither figures nor affected teams and only states that it regularly reviews its workforce in line with strategic priorities. It is not the first round this year: in July, the data center and AI division was hit, and between July and October Intel filed nine layoff notices in California covering a total of 222 employees. At the end of September, Intel still had 81,100 employees, compared with 108,900 at the end of 2024. CEO Lip-Bu Tan has been pushing a strict cost-cutting course since taking office. Nothing changes for customers in the short term, but the cuts show how much Intel still wants to reduce costs.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "5d1e45e7"}, "2026-11-20-xbox-aco-shader-compiler": {"titel": "Microsoft offers developers the AMD shader compiler ACO from the Linux project Mesa experimentally in the October 2026 Xbox GDK, first tests show a 2 to 16 percent gain", "schlagzeile": "Xbox tests Linux shader compiler: up to 16 percent more performance possible", "kurz": "Microsoft is providing game developers for Xbox Series X and S with an experimental shader compiler based on ACO from the Linux graphics project Mesa. In initial tests, the improvements ranged from 2 to 16 percent. Existing games will not automatically become faster as a result.", "zusammenfassung": "The new feature is listed in Microsoft's documentation for the October 2026 Game Development Kit and was picked up by ComputerBase, Wccftech and TechSpot. ACO stands for AMD Compiler and was developed for Linux with Valve's involvement; it is used by default in the RADV Vulkan driver for AMD graphics and thus also in the Steam Deck. Shaders are small programs that calculate lighting, surfaces and effects and must be translated into machine instructions for the GPU before they run. ACO is tailored to AMD architectures and fits the RDNA 2 graphics of the Xbox Series X and S. Microsoft does not need the Linux driver itself for this, as the compiler is integrated into the DirectX 12-based Xbox development environment. According to Microsoft, both compile time and runtime performance can benefit, depending on engine, content and shader bottlenecks. Microsoft does not name specific games, measurement methods or FPS comparisons. A faster compiler therefore does not automatically mean 16 percent more frames per second. Developers have to try ACO themselves and ship adapted game versions for players to benefit. Whether and when ACO becomes the standard in the Xbox tools is open.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft Learn (GDK, What's new)", "Wccftech", "TechSpot"], "_src": "fa977df9"}, "2026-11-20-windows11-kb5132057-suche": {"titel": "Optional Windows 11 update KB5132057 brings a rewritten, native Windows Search, a modern Run dialog and a way to turn off the Sticky Keys prompt", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 update: new search without Edge underneath, modern Run dialog", "kurz": "Microsoft is rolling out the optional update KB5132057 for Windows 11 25H2 and 26H2. It gradually brings a completely rebuilt Windows Search, a modern Run dialog and other new features. Anyone who waits will get everything with Patch Tuesday on December 8.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Windows Latest, the taskbar search was previously based on WebView2, essentially Edge, and has now been rewritten natively in WinUI. In Windows Latest's test, it used 15 to 20 percent less memory and responded faster. The new search shows results in a single list and can perform actions directly, such as toggling Bluetooth or dark mode; according to Microsoft, it initially launches in English. The redesigned Run dialog must be turned on under Settings, System, Advanced, and the Browse button is gone. Handy for gamers: the Sticky Keys prompt that appears after pressing Shift five times can now be turned off directly. Windows Hello can briefly brighten the display in the dark, and the search under \"This PC\" in File Explorer now uses the search index. In Xbox mode, Quick Settings are now also available in the Gaming Task View. There are also bug fixes, for example for Miracast with too low a resolution and the false warning that someone else is still using the PC. Many features are rolled out gradually and are not immediately visible after installation. According to Windows Latest, the package is almost 5 GB in size, and Microsoft lists SQL connections that remain open as a known issue.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Latest"], "_src": "e89583d7"}, "2026-11-19-amd-hunterbrook-aktie": {"titel": "AMD shares briefly fall 15 percent after a report by short seller Hunterbrook; allegation: AMD firmware appears in server updates from a Chinese company on the US Entity List", "schlagzeile": "Short-seller report on China: AMD stock briefly plunges 15 percent", "kurz": "AMD's stock dropped by around 15 percent within about 30 minutes on Thursday and then recovered. The trigger was a report by Hunterbrook, which itself is betting on falling AMD shares. The report explicitly states that it does not prove a violation of export controls.", "zusammenfassung": "Hunterbrook Media accuses AMD of having its own China problem and draws a comparison with the Megaspeed affair at Nvidia. The core of the report: Chinese server maker IEIT Systems has been on the US Entity List since March 2025 and may not do business with US companies without a license. Even so, IEIT is said to have built at least six newer versions of AMD's startup firmware into its own BIOS updates since then, most recently in October 2026. Hunterbrook found nearly identical files at three unlisted companies that are linked to IEIT according to corporate records: Aivres, Kaytus and Maginfra. The report does not clarify how IEIT obtained the code or whether licenses exist; TechPowerUp considers it possible, for example, that it was passed on by third parties or extracted from publicly distributed firmware. Hunterbrook also lists AMD's China business, including 67 million dollars in 2025 licensing income from two listed joint ventures and 22.4 percent of revenue from customers in China and Hong Kong. The conflict of interest is important: Hunterbrook has disclosed a short position in AMD and therefore profits from falling prices. The available reports do not include a statement from AMD. According to TechPowerUp, the share price recovered after the brief crash. For PC buyers nothing changes for now; the allegations concern servers and export rules.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "a08f2a52"}, "2026-11-19-ubisoft-halbjahr-verlust-motherbrain": {"titel": "Ubisoft reports a net loss of 254.5 million euros and 16.5 percent lower net bookings for the first half of fiscal 2026/27, cuts 166 jobs in Montréal and Québec and founds the AI subsidiary Motherbrain", "schlagzeile": "Ubisoft: 254M euro loss, 166 jobs gone – and its own AI studio", "kurz": "Ubisoft posted a loss of 254.5 million euros in the first half of its fiscal year, and net bookings fell by 16.5 percent. Shortly before, the company confirmed cutting 166 jobs at its Montréal and Québec studios, which work on Assassin's Creed and Far Cry. At the same time, the generative AI unit Motherbrain becomes a separate subsidiary.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Insider Gaming, net bookings for the half year came to 644.7 million euros, after 772.4 million a year earlier. The second quarter, at 388.9 million euros, came in better than the company's own forecast of around 370 million, mainly thanks to Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced. Older games were weak, with revenue down 40.8 percent, as was recurring player spending at minus 33.4 percent. For the full year Ubisoft is sticking to its targets: net bookings down by a high single-digit percentage and a cash outflow of no more than 500 million euros. From fiscal 2027/28 the company wants to be operationally profitable again. According to GamesIndustry.biz, the 166 positions in Montréal and Québec correspond to around 4 percent of the workforce there and affect projects that were cancelled or heavily reworked, partly including the joint venture Vantage Studios with Tencent. Ubisoft cites changed production priorities and promises severance and support. The cuts are part of the restructuring announced in January, which has already brought studio closures and six cancelled projects. Motherbrain is new: according to VGC, the team behind the AI experiment Teammates is now a separate subsidiary for AI-driven gameplay. Whether this will lead to games of its own or whether the technology will go into other Ubisoft titles is unclear.", "weitere_links": ["Eurogamer", "VGC"], "_src": "16685f62"}, "2026-11-19-zen6-desktop-nach-computex": {"titel": "Rumor: AMD's Zen 6 desktop processors (Olympic Ridge) are said to arrive only after Computex 2027 due to a switch to TSMC N2X", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Zen 6 for desktop PCs said to slip until after Computex 2027", "kurz": "According to a leaker on the Chinese forum Chiphell, AMD has moved its Zen 6 desktop CPUs to TSMC's N2X process. This is said to push the launch past Computex in early June 2027. AMD has not confirmed this.", "zusammenfassung": "The claim comes from Chiphell user Zhang Zhonghao and was picked up by Wccftech and TechPowerUp. According to it, Olympic Ridge, the codename of the desktop series, will no longer use N2 or N2P but N2X, a 2 nm variant designed for high clock speeds. This switch is said to push the launch beyond Computex 2027. Wccftech itself speculates about July or August 2027 but stresses that this is its own guess based on earlier launches. Until now, a launch in the first quarter of 2027 with an unveiling at CES had been expected; AMD has confirmed its CES appearance but has not named any products. According to TechPowerUp, the Zen 6 server chips will continue to use N2 and N2P. It is still expected that Zen 6 will stay on the AM5 socket and bring up to 12 cores per CCD. None of this is confirmed, and both outlets explicitly treat the delay as a rumor. If it is true, Intel would have the field of new desktop generations to itself for a few months with Nova Lake in early 2027.", "ursprungsquelle": "Zhang Zhonghao on the Chiphell forum", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp"], "_src": "1b942d45"}, "2026-11-19-gta6-japan-zensur": {"titel": "Japanese version of GTA 6 tones down blood, dismemberment and nudity with no option to change it back", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 in Japan: Less blood, no decapitations, swimwear in the shower", "kurz": "The Japanese version of GTA 6 is significantly toned down in terms of violence and nudity. Blood and injuries are reduced, decapitations are missing, and Jason and Lucia shower in swimwear. Unlike in other regions, this cannot be changed in the options.", "zusammenfassung": "According to VGC, screenshots and videos from Japan show that blood and gore are heavily reduced. The Japanese site GameSpark has published a detailed overview of the changes, including less blood on injured and defeated enemies and decapitations removed entirely. The version also intervenes on nudity: when showering, the main characters wear swimwear, while they are naked in other regions. In terms of gameplay, the game remains just as violent according to reports so far; the changes are cosmetic. In other regions, players can turn blood and gore down themselves in the display settings and switch off dismemberment; in Japan there is no way to turn them up. The censorship had been expected because the Japanese version has a slightly smaller file size. According to VGC, however, the same applies to New Zealand and Australia, without any drastic changes being known there so far. According to the available reports, Rockstar itself has not commented on the differences. There are no indications of a cut version for players in Germany and Austria.", "_src": "a5f61d49"}, "2026-11-19-fallout-wasteland-full-of-cats": {"titel": "Australian age rating lists the unannounced hidden object game 'A Wasteland Full of Cats' by studio Devcats, according to the description in partnership with Bethesda and the Fallout series", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is a Fallout hidden object game about finding cats on the way?", "kurz": "A game called 'A Wasteland Full of Cats' has appeared at the Australian age rating board. According to the description, you search for runaway cats from a Vault in the wasteland; it is developed by Brazilian studio Devcats in partnership with Bethesda. The game has not been announced.", "zusammenfassung": "Users on the Fallout subreddit discovered the listing, and PC Gamer reported on it. According to the rating board's description, you play one of the cats from a Vault: after an accident, all the cats escape into the wasteland, and you have to find them and bring them back with the help of a few characters. It mentions 14 locations and 33 rooms plus a Vault with familiar settings from the Fallout series, as well as light puzzles that unlock hidden levels. Devcats is known for the 'Full of Cats' series, simple hidden object games in which you look for cats in drawings. The listing explicitly mentions a partnership with Bethesda and the Fallout brand. Bethesda and Devcats have not commented so far; platforms, price and date are unknown. PC Gamer considers the listing credible because the rating board is not known for jokes, but itself leaves open whether everything will turn out that way. In any case, this is not a big new Fallout game but rather a small spin-off.", "ursprungsquelle": "Australian Classification Board (discovered on the Fallout subreddit)", "_src": "b64de8d8"}, "2026-11-19-gta6-neuseeland-trick": {"titel": "Ampere Analysis: around 2.1 million Xbox players from the US and UK used the 'New Zealand trick' to play GTA 6 early; Sensor Tower estimates around 20 million pre-orders", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: Over two million Xbox fans 'moved' to New Zealand for an early start", "kurz": "According to Ampere Analysis, around 1.5 million Xbox users in the US and 600,000 in the UK switched their console region to New Zealand to start GTA 6 early. Because the game unlocked everywhere at midnight local time, New Zealand went first. On PlayStation the trick was much more complicated and less common.", "zusammenfassung": "Rockstar unlocked GTA 6 worldwide on 19 November at midnight local time in each region. On Xbox, changing the region in the settings is enough to land in the New Zealand store and play the game many hours earlier. In addition to the US and the UK, Ampere Analysis counted around 200,000 players in Canada, 200,000 in Brazil and 100,000 in Mexico. On PlayStation you need a new account with the region set to New Zealand and matching credit; according to Ampere, only about 100,000 players in the US used the trick there. Formally the method violates the terms of use, but Microsoft and Sony have not taken action against it so far. New Zealand's tourism board even welcomed the virtual visitors with a wink on Instagram. According to IGN Germany, Sensor Tower estimates that GTA 6 had been pre-ordered around 17 million times by 16 November and likely reached about 20 million before launch. Rockstar and Take-Two have not yet released official sales figures. All figures come from analytics firms and are estimates.", "weitere_links": ["IGN", "IGN Deutschland"], "_src": "0a2150e5"}, "2026-11-19-rtx-spark-mini-pcs": {"titel": "First mini PCs with Nvidia RTX Spark N1X from Asus, Dell and MSI are available; Asus charges 9,299 euros for the ProArt GR1X with 128 GB and 4 TB", "schlagzeile": "RTX Spark arrives as a mini PC – Asus asks up to 9,299 euros", "kurz": "After the laptops, Nvidia's Arm platform RTX Spark is now also available as compact desktop PCs from Asus, Dell and MSI. All of them use the larger N1X chip with up to 128 GB of shared memory. The Asus ProArt GR1X costs 9,299 euros in its top configuration and, as a special feature, offers a second M.2 slot.", "zusammenfassung": "Nvidia markets the mini PCs as always-on machines for local AI agents, image and video generation and fine-tuning models under Windows. According to Thurrott, all devices use the N1X with 20 CPU cores and 6,144 GPU cores, plus up to 128 GB of unified memory and 10 Gbit Ethernet. Unlike DGX Spark, several units cannot be linked together. ComputerBase tested the MSI EdgeMesa N AI+ with 128 GB and a 4 TB SSD for 7,999 euros; Asus charges 9,299 euros for the same configuration. In return, Asus uses its own board layout with a second M.2 slot in the 2280 format, allowing up to 12 TB of SSD storage. Asus also cools with copper and five heat pipes, which pushes the weight to 1.48 kilograms, compared to 0.55 kilograms for the MSI. Acer, Gigabyte, HP and Microsoft, with a Surface RTX Spark Dev Box, are expected to follow with similar devices. Thurrott had rated the platform critically in his laptop review and sees at least a more sensible use case in the desktop format. The devices are not intended for classic gaming; they target AI developers and creators.", "weitere_links": ["Thurrott.com"], "_src": "8e057bd7"}, "2026-11-19-amd-adrenalin-26-11-2": {"titel": "AMD Adrenalin 26.11.2 WHQL now fixes the SSD write bug for Radeon RX 5000 and RX 6000 under Windows 10 too, adds ROCm 10.2 and fixes disabled Smart Access Memory", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver 26.11.2: SSD bug now fixed on RX 5000 and RX 6000 too", "kurz": "AMD has released the WHQL driver Adrenalin 26.11.2. It now also fixes excessive writes to the system drive at idle for Radeon RX 5000 and RX 6000 under Windows 10. RX 7000 and RX 9000 already received the fix with 26.11.1.", "zusammenfassung": "The bug was in the driver service AMD External Events Utility and, according to PCGH, could in the worst case cause several hundred gigabytes of writes per day. With 26.11.2, all RDNA graphics cards since 2019 are now covered. The driver also fixes Smart Access Memory possibly being disabled after installation under Windows 10. Further fixes concern a memory leak from RX 5000 onwards that makes programs launch more and more slowly over time, crashes when streaming with OBS Studio on RX 9000 and driver timeouts in War Thunder on RX 5000. New is support for ROCm 10.2, Phantom Blade Zero and the Crimson Desert expansion Charting the Unknown. Known issues remain: Crimson Desert may not launch on RX 6000, and here AMD recommends staying on 26.11.1. Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced may crash on RX 7000. Anyone using an RX 5000 or RX 6000 under Windows 10 should install the update because of the SSD bug.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware"], "_src": "2de804a0"}, "2026-11-19-windows7-treiber-rtx50-rx9000": {"titel": "Hobby developers port current graphics drivers from AMD, Nvidia and Intel to Windows 7; for the first time Radeon RX 7000/9000, GeForce RTX 40/50 and newer Intel graphics should run under Windows 7", "schlagzeile": "Six years after end of support: RTX 5090 and RX 9070 XT run on Windows 7", "kurz": "A small group of private developers has modified Windows 10 graphics drivers from AMD, Nvidia and Intel so that they work under Windows 7. This makes it possible for the first time to use cards such as the Radeon RX 9070 XT or the GeForce RTX 5090 under the old system. It is an unofficial project with very little testing so far.", "zusammenfassung": "According to PCGH, the developers ported the AMD driver Adrenalin 25.8.1, a variant of 26.5.2 for Polaris and Vega, an Intel driver from June 2024 and GeForce driver 582.35. To do so, drivers were transferred from the WDDM 2.x model to Windows 7's older driver model. Officially, AMD ended Windows 7 support after the RX 6000 series, Nvidia before the RTX 40 generation, and Intel does not even support the graphics of the Core i-8000 generation under Windows 7. According to PCGH, two Greek developers from the Hackintosh scene are behind the project, with the X account TheBobPony acting as its mouthpiece. The port was reportedly done by hand and without AI. So far it has only been tested with the UHD 770 of a Core i5-14500, a GeForce RTX 5060 and a Radeon RX 9060 XT. There are no promises regarding driver quality, and PCGH is preparing its own test. Windows 7 has not received regular security updates since 2020, so the system is not a good choice for everyday internet use. The project is mainly interesting for retro fans and tinkerers with old games or programs.", "_src": "305b45de"}, "2026-11-19-powershell-7-windows": {"titel": "Microsoft will ship PowerShell 7 with the next Windows version and deprecates Windows PowerShell 5.1; Windows 11 26H2 and Server 2025 are the last versions with 5.1 built in", "schlagzeile": "Windows gets PowerShell 7 built in – the end of 5.1 has begun", "kurz": "Microsoft plans to ship PowerShell 7 with the next Windows version and has deprecated the old Windows PowerShell 5.1. It will initially remain available as an optional feature and continue to receive security updates. When it will disappear completely has not yet been decided.", "zusammenfassung": "PowerShell product manager Jason Helmick presented the plans on the PowerShell blog; Microsoft does not name a specific Windows version number. According to heise, Windows Server 2025 and Windows 11 26H2 are the last versions with PowerShell 5.1 built in. In the next version, 5.1 becomes a Feature on Demand, which is still to be enabled by default on new installations. Deprecated does not mean end of support: there will be no new features, but security updates continue in line with the lifecycle of the respective Windows version. Microsoft wants to decide on final removal based on usage data and announce it in advance. Both versions can run side by side, but full compatibility is not guaranteed because 5.1 is based on the .NET Framework and 7 on cross-platform .NET. Administrators should therefore check which scripts and tasks still call powershell.exe instead of pwsh.exe. PowerShell 7 comes as an MSIX package that still lacks some functions, such as running under the SYSTEM account. Little changes for normal users at first, but for admins and script tinkerers it is a clear to-do.", "_src": "84a98f9d"}, "2026-11-19-anno117-patch-3-0-1": {"titel": "Anno 117: Pax Romana gets update 3.0.1 with better performance on PS5, fewer crashes, bug fixes and more harbor space in Aegyptus", "schlagzeile": "Anno 117: New patch smooths out the PS5 version – with side effects", "kurz": "Update 3.0.1 for Anno 117: Pax Romana has been available for PC, PS5 and Xbox Series X/S since 18 November. It is meant to make extreme frame rate drops on PS5 rarer, reduce CPU load and fix many bugs. However, Ubisoft itself warns of some new problems.", "zusammenfassung": "According to PC Games, the patch also covers the recently released expansion 'Erwachen des Deltas'. On performance, Ubisoft promises fewer severe frame rate drops on PS5 and lower CPU load, which should mainly help large save games. There are also fixes for memory problems and freezes on consoles and for crashes with certain Intel Arc graphics cards. Among dozens of other fixes, PC Games mentions faulty ship routes and problems with specialists. In terms of gameplay, three islands in the north of Aegyptus get more coastline for harbor buildings, making trade hubs easier to build. In addition, the build menu in Latium has been reworked, cisterns in Aegyptus show their irrigation range, and the bonuses of multiple granaries can no longer be stacked. At the same time, Ubisoft lists known new bugs that may occur with the patch. Anyone with large save games should keep an eye on the granary change because it can affect supply.", "_src": "5e4ba383"}, "2026-11-19-microsoft-agent-framework-malware": {"titel": "Attackers slip an infostealer into versions 1.26.1 and 1.26.2 of the Python package of Microsoft's Agent Framework; credentials for Azure, Git, Docker and Hugging Face at risk", "schlagzeile": "Malware in Microsoft's AI framework: affected developers need to act", "kurz": "Two versions of the Python package of Microsoft's Agent Framework contained an infostealer. It grabs credentials for services such as Azure, Git, Docker and Hugging Face. Anyone who installed versions 1.26.1 or 1.26.2 should isolate their systems and renew all credentials.", "zusammenfassung": "Developers use the Agent Framework to build their own AI agents in Python, .NET and Go; according to heise, the packages are downloaded around 200,000 times a month on average. The malware was discovered by security firm OX Security and the site Opensource Malware. The Python package contained a file called agent_framework_meta.pth whose single line is executed every time Python starts. This allowed the malicious code to entrench itself across several Python projects. Microsoft rolled back the first infected version 1.26.1 to the clean 1.26.0, but the attackers then managed to upload 1.26.2 with a different startup mechanism and the same infostealer. OX Security suspects that the attackers obtained Microsoft access to the package index; this is not confirmed. Microsoft told The Register that it is investigating the attack and temporarily set some GitHub repositories to private. Those affected should stop running projects, isolate infected systems, renew all credentials used there and check the affected services for unfamiliar activity. There is no direct need for action for normal Windows users; developers with the package are affected.", "weitere_links": ["Neowin"], "_src": "14bd4fee"}, "2026-11-19-edge-lockdown-webgpu": {"titel": "Microsoft tests a lockdown mode in Edge Canary that disables WebGL, WebGL2 and WebGPU to make attacks via the GPU process harder", "schlagzeile": "Edge tests Lockdown Mode: WebGL and WebGPU switched off for protection", "kurz": "Microsoft is developing an optional lockdown mode for the Edge browser modeled on Apple's. In the first test version, it blocks the graphics interfaces WebGL, WebGL2 and WebGPU, through which attackers could escape the sandbox. Browser games and interactive maps may then no longer work properly.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, the mode builds on Edge's enhanced security mode, which already disables JIT compilation in the V8 JavaScript engine. It is intended for particularly at-risk users such as journalists, executives, security researchers and administrators who accept compatibility problems in exchange for more protection. The first protective measures target the GPU process, a more privileged component that handles complex graphics tasks between browser code, libraries and device drivers. According to Microsoft's estimate, the mode would have blocked around 60 percent of the privilege escalation attacks observed in the wild against Edge users. It can be tested in Edge Canary via the flag edge-sdsm-plus and the strict security mode with WebGL and WebGPU graphics blocked. A notice then appears in the address bar when a page is affected. Microsoft plans to extend the mode in upcoming versions and allow exceptions for trusted sites. Nothing changes for normal users and gamers as long as they do not switch the mode on themselves. When it will reach the stable version of Edge is unclear.", "_src": "59aaf15d"}, "2026-11-19-gta6-ps5-pro-cpu-30fps": {"titel": "Rockstar technology lead Marc Chambers: the PS5 Pro's CPU is too weak to run GTA 6's simulation at higher frame rates; no 60 fps mode on current consoles", "schlagzeile": "Rockstar explains the 30 fps: The PS5 Pro's CPU isn't enough for GTA 6", "kurz": "Rockstar has confirmed that GTA 6 stays at 30 frames per second even on the PS5 Pro. According to technology lead Marc Chambers, the console's processor is only slightly stronger than that of the standard PS5 and is not enough to run the complex simulation at more frames. There will therefore be no performance mode on current consoles.", "zusammenfassung": "Chambers, Technology Production Director at Rockstar, spoke to Kotaku, and Wccftech picked up the statements. According to Chambers, the base version uses ray-traced reflections and global illumination. On the PS5 Pro, ray-traced shadows and a sharper image via Sony's upscaler PSSR are added. The Pro's stronger graphics unit is therefore used for image quality, but the processor is only slightly better than in the standard PS5. It is not powerful enough to run the game's complex simulation at higher frame rates. With this, Rockstar rejects requests for a 40 or 60 fps mode with reduced graphics. Wccftech also sees this as an answer to accusations of poor optimization and points to the aging Zen 2 processors in current consoles. According to Wccftech's review, PS5, Xbox Series X and Series S do not always hold 30 fps steadily. Higher frame rates are therefore likely to come only with a PC version or the next console generation; Rockstar has still not given a date for a PC version.", "_src": "a8a35595"}, "2026-11-19-trendforce-nand-2027": {"titel": "TrendForce expects NAND contract prices to fall by 0 to 5 percent from the first quarter of 2027 and across all product groups from the second quarter; the reason is reduced SSD orders from Chinese cloud providers", "schlagzeile": "Market researchers: SSD storage should get cheaper again in 2027", "kurz": "According to TrendForce, the NAND market will tip into oversupply in 2027. Contract prices are expected to fall by 0 to 5 percent in the first quarter of 2027 and across all product groups from the second quarter. For consumers this is a forecast, not a price cut in stores.", "zusammenfassung": "TrendForce attributes the turnaround mainly to China: cloud providers there have cut their 2027 orders for server SSDs by more than US providers are ordering additionally. At the same time, NAND bit supply is expected to grow by 25 to 30 percent in 2027, for example through more QLC memory and chips with more layers. According to the forecast, industry investment will rise by 26.7 percent to 29.9 billion dollars. TrendForce already lowered the expected rise in contract prices for the fourth quarter of 2026 to 8 to 13 percent, and spot prices have recently fallen by more than 20 percent. For end devices, on the other hand, TrendForce expects rather rising prices in 2027 because cheap memory stocks are used up and manufacturers are reducing storage configurations. heise sees this as first signs that SSD prices could fall in early 2027. According to TrendForce, it remains uncertain how quickly China reduces inventories, how GPU export rules change and what consequences US policy after the midterm elections will have for planned data centers. Store prices react to contract prices only with a delay anyway. The forecast says nothing about RAM (DRAM).", "weitere_links": ["heise online"], "_src": "ed53a871"}, "2026-11-19-nvidia-gentlemen-ransomware": {"titel": "Ransomware group The Gentlemen lists Nvidia on its leak site and threatens to publish data on 28 November; Nvidia is investigating a possible incident at a third-party partner", "schlagzeile": "Extortionists threaten Nvidia with a data leak – countdown runs to 28 November", "kurz": "The ransomware group The Gentlemen has listed Nvidia on its dark web extortion site since Wednesday and threatens to publish allegedly stolen data, with a countdown running until the end of next week. The group has not shown any evidence of an attack so far. Nvidia says it is investigating a possible incident at a third-party provider and has found no indication that its own systems were compromised.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, The Gentlemen added Nvidia to its leak site and started a countdown that ends on 28 November. File lists, data volumes or other verifiable evidence are still missing. An Nvidia spokesperson told BleepingComputer that the company is investigating an incident that may have affected a third-party partner. There is no indication that Nvidia's own systems or networks were affected, and the company continues to monitor the situation. Nvidia does not say which partner is meant. PCGH points to an observation by the portal Ransomnews: since 6 October the group has listed the Taiwanese supplier Jentech Precision Industrial, which describes itself as a partner in the Nvidia MGX ecosystem and makes cooling components for AI systems. Whether there is a connection is unclear. The Gentlemen has been active since 2025, operates as ransomware-as-a-service and relies on double extortion, meaning data theft plus encryption. Its leak site now lists more than 1,100 alleged victims, which is not the same as proven attacks. Nvidia had already confirmed a break-in by Lapsus$ in 2022 and, in May of this year, a data leak at a regional GeForce NOW partner. Whether data will actually appear on 28 November cannot be predicted at this point.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware"], "_src": "170f0926"}, "2026-11-19-intel-foundry-microsoft-emib-18a-p": {"titel": "Intel Foundry wins Microsoft as the first announced EMIB packaging customer and an unnamed first customer for 18A-P; 18A yield is said to be above 70 percent", "schlagzeile": "Intel's fabs: Microsoft signs up for packaging, first 18A-P customer on board", "kurz": "According to Intel, Microsoft is the first company to publicly use Intel Foundry's EMIB packaging technology for its own Azure chips. There is also a first external customer for the 18A-P process, whose name has not been disclosed. CEO Lip-Bu Tan put 18A yield at over 70 percent.", "zusammenfassung": "EMIB stands for Embedded Multi-die Interconnect Bridge: small bridge chips that let two larger dies communicate inside one package. According to Intel's announcement, Microsoft will use EMIB for Azure chips of its own design; exactly what will be connected is still unclear. The agreement also secures Microsoft multi-year Xeon capacity, including the upcoming Diamond Rapids server generation. Lip-Bu Tan mentioned the first external 18A-P customer at a conference without naming it; Intel CTO Pushkar Ranade confirmed it on X with a short \"Yes\". 18A yield is now above 70 percent, Tan said. ComputerBase takes a critical view: 18A has been in volume production for about a year, and the earlier claim of an improvement of around 7 percent per month does not quite fit this figure. Keeping the 18A-P customer anonymous is common in the industry, but Intel has had several foundry partners in the past that ended up amounting to little. For PC gamers the news is mainly an indicator: if its own manufacturing works, Intel can build future desktop CPUs with less dependence on TSMC.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "dbd459f0"}, "2026-11-19-gta6-release-de-cix-psn": {"titel": "GTA 6 is out on PS5 and Xbox Series X/S; the pre-load set a data record at DE-CIX, and many PS5 users reported PSN problems the evening before", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 is here: download record at DE-CIX, PSN already wobbled the night before", "kurz": "Since midnight, GTA 6 has officially been playable in Germany and Austria on PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X/S. The pre-load alone set a new throughput record at the DE-CIX internet exchange. The evening before, many PS5 users reported login and download problems on the PlayStation Network.", "zusammenfassung": "According to DE-CIX CTO Thomas King, throughput reached 22.3 terabits per second in Frankfurt and 33.01 terabits per second across all locations worldwide, both records, heise reports citing dpa. In Frankfurt the peak was around 19 percent above the previous record from January 2026. On Wednesday evening, according to Polygon, reports of PSN problems piled up, such as \"Sony services are busy\" or connection errors during login and downloads, while Sony's official status page at times showed the network as normal. Sony has not given an official cause in the sources used. According to heise, anyone who set their Xbox region to New Zealand could already play on Wednesday; on PS5, early unlocking depends on the store region of the purchase. PlayStation Europe and Xbox also announced the launch on X. The Standard Edition costs 80 euros, the Ultimate Edition 100 euros. On all consoles the game runs at a maximum of 30 frames per second, and Rockstar has still not announced a PC version. According to heise, GTA 6 still stands at 99 out of 100 points on Metacritic.", "weitere_links": ["Polygon (PSN outage)", "PlayStation Europe on X"], "_src": "52075601"}, "2026-11-19-microsoft-to-do-eingestellt-2027": {"titel": "Microsoft is retiring its To Do task app on June 30, 2027; work and school accounts move to Planner, personal users get no replacement", "schlagzeile": "Microsoft buries To Do, leaving personal users without a replacement in 2027", "kurz": "Microsoft is shutting down its To Do task app on all platforms at the end of June 2027. Microsoft Planner is to take over for work and school accounts. Personal users, even with a Microsoft 365 subscription, get no successor app, only an export function.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft confirmed the end in a dedicated support document, Dr. Windows and Neowin report. Affected are the apps for Windows, Mac, iOS, Android and the web as well as personal accounts, including Microsoft 365 Personal and Family. Microsoft explicitly recommends that personal users look for another task app. An export function is to arrive before the deadline; which data it supports is still open. For business and education customers, Microsoft will roll out a revamped \"My tasks\" view in Planner starting in December 2026. Even there, however, there is no automatic migration, and features such as shared lists, list groups or file attachments are partly missing in Planner. According to Neowin, native Planner apps for Windows and Mac are not planned. Until the deadline, To Do is to keep running as usual. To Do launched in 2017 as the successor to Wunderlist, which Microsoft bought in 2015 and shut down in 2020.", "weitere_links": ["Neowin", "Windows Latest"], "_src": "7560a295"}, "2026-11-18-nginx-zehn-luecken": {"titel": "Security updates for nginx Open Source and nginx Plus close ten vulnerabilities, five of them rated CVSS 9.2; attackers could execute code in some cases", "schlagzeile": "nginx web server: ten flaws, five of them critical, update now", "kurz": "Security updates have been released for the widely used nginx web server, closing ten vulnerabilities. Five of them are rated 9.2 under CVSS 4.0, and some may allow malicious code to be executed. Admins should update immediately.", "zusammenfassung": "The updates affect both nginx Open Source and the commercial nginx Plus, heise reports. Some of the bugs have been in the code for years, two of them since 2007. Four of the ten flaws are so-called use-after-free bugs, where memory that has already been freed is used again. This can allow attackers to run their own code on other people's servers. Combined with other known vulnerabilities, root privileges can reportedly be obtained this way, which is why the name \"nginx2root\" is being used. The remaining bugs range from buffer overflows and memory corruption to infinite loops and bypassing the Server Name Indication check. They are registered under ten CVE numbers, including CVE-2026-113425 and CVE-2026-125283. For gamers at home nginx is rarely directly relevant, but many websites, game server panels and home server setups rely on it. Anyone running nginx themselves should update the packages from their distribution or directly from nginx.", "_src": "fa48bee5"}, "2026-11-18-nvidia-treiber-ssd-schreiblast": {"titel": "Users report that current GeForce drivers write up to 30 GB per hour to the SSD at idle via NVDisplay.Container.exe; AMD extends its SSD fix to RX 5000 and RX 6000 with Adrenalin 26.11.2", "schlagzeile": "After AMD, now Nvidia: GeForce driver said to flood SSDs with data", "kurz": "After the Radeon driver, the GeForce driver is now also said to write unusually large amounts to the system drive at idle, in some cases up to 30 GB per hour. Versions 621.14 and 621.24 are mentioned. Nvidia has not commented yet; according to users, rolling back to 621.01 helps as a stopgap.", "zusammenfassung": "According to user reports, the culprit is the NVDisplay.Container.exe process, which belongs to the \"NVIDIA Display Container LS\" service. It repeatedly rewrites a log file named nvlog.nvlgstg in the ProgramData/NVIDIA Corporation folder instead of just appending to it, ComputerBase and TechPowerUp report. That is why the write volume depends on the file size and differs between users. In one comparison, the process wrote less than 2 MB in five minutes at idle with driver 621.01 and around 515 MB with 621.14; with 621.24, as much as 30 GB per hour is said to have been measured. Other users see hardly any activity with the same drivers, so the problem does not occur everywhere. You can check it on the Disk tab of the Windows Resource Monitor. Stopping the service and deleting the file only helps until the service restarts, and a permanently disabled service can interfere with the Nvidia Control Panel and the Nvidia App. Nvidia does not list the behavior among its known issues and has not commented so far. In parallel, AMD has extended the fix for its own SSD write problem to Radeon RX 5000 and RX 6000 under Windows 10 with Adrenalin 26.11.2, Neowin reports. The new AMD driver also adds support for Phantom Blade Zero and fixes a memory leak, among other things.", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp", "PC Games Hardware", "Neowin (AMD Adrenalin 26.11.2)"], "_src": "8101af43"}, "2026-11-18-nand-spotpreise-minus-20": {"titel": "Report: NAND spot prices for consumer storage fall by around 20 percent within a month; Bank of America expects contract prices to drop another 5 to 10 percent in the first quarter of 2027", "schlagzeile": "A glimmer of hope in the memory crisis: NAND prices fall by around 20 percent", "kurz": "Spot prices for NAND flash, the memory SSDs are built from, have fallen by around 20 percent within one month, according to a Korean business report. Bank of America expects consumer NAND contract prices to drop another 5 to 10 percent in the first quarter of 2027. Store prices will only follow with a delay.", "zusammenfassung": "The figures come from the Seoul Economic Daily and were picked up by Wccftech. According to the report, 512 Gbit NAND wafers fell by 32 percent compared with the previous quarter and 1 Tbit products by 19 percent. The report cites weak consumer demand, with buyers postponing purchases at very high prices, and manufacturers shrinking the storage in their devices. Added to this is competition from Chinese manufacturer YMTC, which is said to have taken around 14 percent of NAND revenue in the second quarter. According to the report, Bank of America expects contract prices for consumer NAND to fall another 5 to 10 percent in the first quarter of 2027. Important: spot and contract prices only reach SSD store prices after weeks or months, because inventories sit in between. The opposite applies to server SSDs, where TrendForce expects contract prices to rise by 15 to 20 percent in the fourth quarter. System memory (DRAM) is not covered by the report; there is no comparable signal there so far. For comparison: just a few days ago, some SSDs were said to cost three times last year's price.", "_src": "0cf65aa9"}, "2026-11-18-8bitdo-gamecube-controller-switch2": {"titel": "8BitDo unveils the GC Bluetooth Gamepad, a wireless GameCube-style controller for Switch, Switch 2 and Windows PCs for 49.99 US dollars", "schlagzeile": "GameCube feel for Switch 2 and PC: 8BitDo launches a wireless GC controller", "kurz": "Accessory maker 8BitDo has unveiled a wireless controller styled after the GameCube pad. It works with Switch, Switch 2 and Windows PCs and costs 49.99 US dollars. Shipping is set to begin on December 10, 2026.", "zusammenfassung": "According to the manufacturer, the GC Bluetooth Gamepad adopts the classic GameCube design and button layout, including the familiar purple-and-orange color scheme. It connects via Bluetooth 5.0, a 2.4 GHz wireless adapter or a USB-C cable. All three methods work on the original Switch and the Switch 2, while on PC only the cable and the 2.4 GHz adapter work. Nintendo already sells its own wireless GameCube controller for the Switch 2, but according to Polygon it does not work with the original Switch or Windows out of the box. The 8BitDo version is also 20 dollars cheaper than Nintendo's model. The pad is mainly interesting for Nintendo Switch Online with GameCube classics, for Smash Bros. players and for emulation on PC. Whether it feels like the original can only be judged after testing. The source did not give a euro price.", "_src": "004c0c68"}, "2026-11-18-devolver-gta6-loeschen-volvy": {"titel": "Devolver Digital is giving away Steam keys for Volvy's Adventure: Reslimed to players who share a video of themselves deleting their GTA 6 pre-load", "schlagzeile": "Delete GTA 6, win an indie game: Devolver takes a jab at the launch", "kurz": "Publisher Devolver Digital is releasing its platformer Volvy's Adventure: Reslimed on the same day as GTA 6. Anyone who shares a video of themselves deleting the GTA 6 pre-load can win a Steam key. The game, however, is only coming to PC.", "zusammenfassung": "The campaign runs on X: users are asked to share Devolver's post with a video of deleting the GTA 6 download and the hashtag #MakeRoomForVolvy, Eurogamer reports. According to Eurogamer, the GTA 6 pre-load is 212 GB. The punchline: Volvy's Adventure is only coming to Steam, so freeing up space on PS5 or Xbox achieves nothing. Devolver itself points out that only Steam keys are being given away. There is also a parody trailer that, according to PC Gamer, recreates the GTA 6 launch trailer shot by shot. The game is developed by doinksoft, known for Gunbrella and Gato Roboto. Volvy was long a running gag in Devolver's showcases and is now the star of his own game. Devolver had announced back in 2025 that it would release a game on GTA 6's launch day and moved the plan along with every delay. Check the terms of participation directly with Devolver before taking part.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "3dcb7448"}, "2026-11-18-nvidia-exportkontroll-ausschuss": {"titel": "Nvidia sets up a standing board committee for national security, export controls and global trade risks", "schlagzeile": "After the Megaspeed affair: Nvidia creates its own export control committee", "kurz": "Nvidia has created a standing board committee for national security and export controls. It is meant to oversee policies and compliance programs around trade risks at the highest level. Nvidia does not name a specific trigger.", "zusammenfassung": "The new body is called the National Security and Export Control Oversight Committee. It is chaired by board member Suzanne Nora Johnson, joined by Stephen C. Neal and John O. Dabiri. The committee is to meet at least once a quarter, including in closed sessions. The existing national security and trade compliance departments will in future report directly to the committee and to interim CEO Colette Kress. External experts in law, security policy and international trade are to provide support. The announcement comes after Jensen Huang's resignation and the investigation into data center company Megaspeed, which allegedly passed Nvidia chips on to China; Megaspeed denies this. Whether these events triggered the committee is not confirmed; according to ComputerBase, Nvidia did not respond to a Reuters inquiry about it. No new product restrictions or changes to export procedures were announced. Board chair Harvey Jones spoke of a special responsibility as a leading provider of computing technology.", "_src": "93ae3e25"}, "2026-11-18-gta6-cheats-erst-nach-story": {"titel": "GTA 6 only unlocks cheats after the end of the main story; active cheats block saving as well as trophies and achievements", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: cheats only after the story, and then without saving", "kurz": "In GTA 6, cheats can only be used once the main story is finished, Eurogamer and GameStar report. Each cheat must also be unlocked through a task. While a cheat is active you cannot save, and trophies and achievements are disabled.", "zusammenfassung": "Eurogamer says it checked this with save files from various points in the story. Only after the credits does a previously hidden cheats tab appear in the map's progress menu. There the cheats are sorted by category, according to GameStar 61 in total across five categories, each with a description and the task needed to unlock it, such as 100 workouts for body armor. As in GTA 5, they are entered via the phone by holding the shoulder buttons and pressing D-pad combinations. When activating one, the game warns that you cannot save in this session and that trophies and achievements are disabled. Unlike GTA 5, there is a money cheat again according to Eurogamer, which probably explains the lock until the end of the story, since money plays a role in the plot. This is a departure from earlier entries and from Red Dead Redemption 2, where about half of the cheats were available from the start. There is no official explanation from Rockstar for this decision in the sources used. According to GameStar, matching tasks completed during the story already count toward unlocking.", "weitere_links": ["GameStar", "GamePro"], "_src": "b2b8c9b0"}, "2026-11-18-gta6-streaming-rekord": {"titel": "GTA 6 breaks streaming records: according to Streams Charts, 3.29 million concurrent Twitch viewers and around 7.9 million across all platforms before the worldwide launch", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 breaks the streaming world record before it even launches", "kurz": "Before GTA 6 is even playable in most countries, it has broken the record for livestream viewers. According to Streams Charts, almost 7.9 million people watched simultaneously on Twitch, YouTube, Kick and other platforms, 3.29 million of them on Twitch alone.", "zusammenfassung": "GTA 6 is launching in staggered regions; it was already playable in New Zealand on November 18, and later in Singapore and Hong Kong as well. According to preliminary data from analytics service Streams Charts, reported by Polygon, the game peaked at 7,886,402 concurrent viewers across all platforms. Twitch led with 3.29 million, followed by YouTube with 3.19 million and Kick with 1.48 million. According to this data, GTA 6 is also the most-watched game category in Twitch history, ahead of League of Legends at 3.11 million and Fortnite at 3.04 million. According to Streams Charts, the previous cross-platform record for a game launch was held by Valorant's closed beta in 2020 with 1.74 million viewers; back then, however, beta access was handed out for watching. Eurogamer had reported 6.38 million viewers in the early afternoon, so the number kept rising over the day. Because more regions are still being unlocked, the figures could rise further. These are preliminary measurements from a third party, not official figures from Twitch or Rockstar. The official launch on PS5 and Xbox Series is on November 19.", "weitere_links": ["Eurogamer"], "_src": "9a3f4ea0"}, "2026-11-18-jedec-ddr6-vorschau": {"titel": "JEDEC reveals first DDR6 specs: start at 12.8 GT/s, 96-bit data bus, 74 mm modules, RDIMM, UDIMM and CAMM form factors possible", "schlagzeile": "DDR6 takes shape: 50% more bandwidth and much shorter modules", "kurz": "Standards body JEDEC has officially presented the first key specifications for the upcoming DDR6 memory. RDIMMs are set to start at 12.8 GT/s, the data bus grows from 64 to 96 bits, and bandwidth is supposed to rise by more than 50% at launch. These are explicitly development plans, not a finished standard.", "zusammenfassung": "On November 18, the JEDEC Solid State Technology Association published a preview of the DDR6 standard being developed in its JC-42 committee. According to JEDEC, DDR6 RDIMMs are to start at 12.8 GT/s, up from 9.2 GT/s with DDR5; the roadmap extends to 14.4 GT/s and beyond. The data bus is widened from 64 to 96 DQ, an increase of 50%. Together with the higher data rates, this is supposed to deliver more than 50% additional bandwidth at launch. JEDEC itself stresses that this bandwidth target does not equal a corresponding performance gain in applications. New features include a pseudo-channel architecture, and the number of banks doubles. DRAM chips are to reach densities of up to 128 Gbit. Notable for PC builders: at 74 mm, the modules are much shorter than 133 mm DDR5 sticks. JEDEC lists RDIMM, UDIMM and CAMM as possible form factors, so not only CAMM. There are also flexible ECC options and better efficiency thanks to VSS-terminated I/O and low-power modes for data centers. The focus is clearly on servers and AI data centers. According to JEDEC, all details may still change during the standardization process. The press release gives no date for the finished standard or the first products.", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp"], "_src": "15fdb014"}, "2026-11-18-rockstar-gewerkschaft-abstimmung": {"titel": "About 1,600 Rockstar employees in the United Kingdom are voting on union recognition; the ballot closes on November 26", "schlagzeile": "1,600 Rockstar staff in the UK are voting on a union", "kurz": "As GTA 6 launches, more than 1,600 Rockstar employees in the United Kingdom are voting on whether to recognize a union. The deadline is November 26. Nothing has been decided yet; if the vote succeeds, it would be the country's largest games union, according to PC Gamer.", "zusammenfassung": "PC Gamer and Polygon report on the vote, which coincides with GTA 6's review and launch day. In a Guardian op-ed, Rockstar animation programmer and union representative Nestor Uriarte writes that thousands of people stand behind the record figures and should see a fair share of the success. A recognized union, he argues, would better protect wages, working conditions and bonuses and would also allow staff to negotiate the use of AI in development. Uriarte cites ongoing concerns about crunch, a possible gender pay gap and unclear bonus rules; at the same time he stresses that the initiative comes from people inside the studio, not from outside. Whether a majority agrees will only be known after November 26. In parallel, a tribunal in Glasgow is hearing allegations that Rockstar disadvantaged or dismissed staff involved in organizing; that dispute has not been finally decided in court. Uriarte also points to the Firaxis layoffs in the same corporate group. The reports at hand do not include a Rockstar statement on the vote itself.", "weitere_links": ["Polygon"], "_src": "242f70b2"}, "2026-11-18-gta6-technik-fsr4-series-s": {"titel": "Rockstar confirms GTA 6's tech: 1440p upscaled to 4K on PS5, PS5 Pro and Series X, 720p with FSR 4 to 1080p on Series S, with a target of 30 frames per second", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: 1440p on PS5 and Series X, Series S starts at 720p with FSR 4", "kurz": "Rockstar has confirmed GTA 6's console technology to Wccftech. PlayStation 5, PS5 Pro and Xbox Series X render internally at 1440p and upscale to 4K; Series S starts at 720p and is the first game on that console to use AMD FSR 4 for 1080p. The target is 30 frames per second, and according to analyses only the PS5 Pro holds that mark consistently.", "zusammenfassung": "The figures come from Rockstar and have been picked up by ComputerBase and Tom's Hardware. On PS5 and Series X a first-party TAA solution is used, on PS5 Pro Sony's PSSR, and on Series S FSR 4. A 4K user interface is then composited on all platforms. Ray-traced global illumination is also planned for Series S, with the implementation adjusted to each platform's hardware. ComputerBase lists ray-traced shadows only for the PS5 Pro. The 30 fps target is not always held consistently on the cheaper Xbox and the base PS5, according to the table; the PS5 Pro is said to hold the mark. Speaking to Kotaku, technology production director Marc Chambers said, according to VGC, that the “base presentation” on PS5 Pro includes ray-traced reflections and global illumination plus the extra sharpness from PSSR. The PS5 Pro's processor is slightly better than in the base PS5, but not powerful enough to run the complex simulation at a higher frame rate. Lowering the graphics in favor of 60 fps does not sound like a planned path in that remark. Rockstar describes the often darker screen edges as an artistic choice; the vignette cannot currently be turned off. A bug that made it too strong at times has been fixed, the studio says. A PC version with its own graphics options remains without a date. The comments confirm earlier reports that GTA 6 stays at 30 fps even on PS5 Pro.", "weitere_links": ["Tom's Hardware", "Video Games Chronicle"], "_src": "f08fa2d7"}, "2026-11-18-am5-agesa-vcore-14-ryzen-8000": {"titel": "AGESA 1.3.0.1f Patch A caps core voltage at 1.4 volts on selected Ryzen 8000 processors; MSI and Asus are already shipping matching BIOS versions", "schlagzeile": "New AM5 BIOS caps Vcore at 1.4 V on some Ryzen 8000 CPUs", "kurz": "A new AGESA update caps core voltage at 1.4 volts on selected Ryzen 8000 processors. MSI mentions the change in its release notes but does not say which models are affected. Asus is already distributing beta BIOS versions and warns against importing older profiles.", "zusammenfassung": "The firmware is called AGESA 1.3.0.1f Patch A, PCGH reports. MSI's release notes state that maximum Vcore will be limited to 1.4 volts for selected Ryzen 8000-series CPUs. Which models those are, and whether the rule comes from AMD, is still open. The cap applies to the cores' supply and is separate from the already known 1.3-volt SoC voltage limit. It is also unclear whether only manually set values are restricted, or automatic regulation and Precision Boost Overdrive as well. Effects on everyday performance have not been demonstrated; for manual overclocking the cap may be noticeable. The update also adds a new POST display for DDR5 memory training: during initialization the two-digit display runs through 00 to 09 once a second, then starts over. That is not a percentage indicator, but it should help show whether the board is still training or has hung. Asus already offers the firmware as a beta for selected X870, X870E and X670E boards and explicitly warns against importing saved UEFI profiles from older AGESA versions. Anyone with a stable system does not need to switch to a beta just for the POST display.", "_src": "f31019a5"}, "2026-11-18-gta6-tests-metacritic-99": {"titel": "GTA 6 reviews are out: Metacritic currently stands at 99, the release on PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S is November 19, 2026, and a PC date is still missing", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 launches: reviews rave, and Metacritic currently stands at 99", "kurz": "Reviews for Grand Theft Auto 6 are in, and Metacritic currently has the game at 99 points, tying The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time. The official launch on PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S is November 19, 2026; it is already playable in New Zealand. Rockstar has still not named a date for the PC version.", "zusammenfassung": "Many major outlets are awarding top scores, Polygon reports among others. OpenCritic currently stands at 98. Those figures can still change as more reviews arrive. Praise focuses on the density of the Leonida world, the relationship between Jason and Lucia, and the level of detail; some critics mention a slow opening, awkward controls or clumsy combat. Rockstar president Sam Houser issued a rare statement for the launch, which IGN has; the studio wants to exceed expectations, show what games can do, and looks ahead to “many more years” of shared experiences. What that means, for example an online mode, Rockstar does not say. In some time zones, such as New Zealand, players can already start the game; in Europe that is typically during the night into November 19. Reports of more than $1.5 billion in pre-order revenue come from market watchers, not from an official Rockstar statement. The PC version remains undated, with Xbox cloud streaming mentioned as an interim option. Anyone citing scores and sales figures should keep the November 18, 2026 snapshot in mind; both can change quickly. PlayStation has officially dated the launch to Thursday, November 19. Support points out that a PS5 system software update is required before playing.", "weitere_links": ["IGN (Sam Houser)", "PC Games Hardware", "PC Games (Test)", "PlayStation", "PlayStation Support"], "_src": "8303d6cb"}, "2026-11-20-wow-forever-15-jahre-rekord": {"titel": "Blizzard: World of Warcraft Forever has more weekly active players than WoW has had in the past 15 years, and over 15 million characters were created after two weeks", "schlagzeile": "WoW Forever: more weekly players than at any time in the past 15 years", "kurz": "Two weeks after launch, Blizzard reports a record for World of Warcraft Forever: more people are playing WoW per week than at any time in the past 15 years. On top of that, more than 15.16 million characters have been created. However, Blizzard does not give a specific player count.", "zusammenfassung": "The record was announced by Holly Longdale, vice president and executive producer of World of Warcraft, on X on November 18. According to PC Games and GamesRadar+, WoW was last at this level in the early 2010s, during Cataclysm; back then Blizzard reported around 12 million subscribers. An infographic shows figures as a snapshot from November 18: 15,160,147 characters created, around 1.48 billion quests completed and almost 9.8 billion enemies defeated. In addition, there are more than 140,000 guilds, more than 71 million groups and almost 29 million camping items used from the new camping system. The player characters died almost 197 million times, around 29 million of them in fights against other players. The deadliest dungeon boss is Archmage Arugal from Shadowfang Keep. Important: characters are not players, as many create several characters. WoW Forever launched on November 4 and builds on the early world of Azeroth, expanded with new zones and dungeons. According to Blizzard, the first new raids are due to follow on December 9.", "weitere_links": ["GamesRadar+"], "_src": "08fa3246"}, "2026-11-18-windows-server-2028-vorschau": {"titel": "Microsoft has released a public preview of Windows Server 2028 with a harder default security posture, on-premises AI and new storage technology, but has not yet named a date for the finished version", "schlagzeile": "Windows Server 2028 is out as a public preview — with no final date", "kurz": "Microsoft has released a public preview of Windows Server 2028. It aims at a harder default security posture, on-premises AI and faster storage, including native NVMe. The company has not named a date for the finished version.", "zusammenfassung": "That is what Microsoft writes in the Windows Server Tech Community blog, heise reports. Interested customers can also apply for the Technology Adoption Program. It also makes clear that Microsoft is still offering a server operating system for use in a customer's own data center, not only cloud services. On security, a hardened Server Core configuration is to be the default, along with a new security baseline, Trusted Launch for Generation 2 VMs and the start of support for confidential virtual machines on suitable on-premises hardware. Automatic certificates and preparations for post-quantum cryptography are also planned. More speed is promised by a native NVMe stack that is on by default, NVMe over TCP and RDMA, and the ability to boot from ReFS volumes. Server management is to arrive in Microsoft Intune as a preview, and Windows Admin Center's virtualization mode is generally available. In AI, Microsoft talks about “hybrid intelligence”: inference should be able to run closer to the data or under a customer's own control, including with Foundry Local, Windows ML, vLLM and llama.cpp. As a hardware preview, Microsoft names AMD's Instinct MI350P card for the first half of 2027. Microsoft eXecution Containers are meant to isolate on-premises inference as well. If the usual cadence holds, the finished version could appear in about a year; that is not a commitment. The preview runs through the Windows Insider program for servers.", "_src": "5da9242a"}, "2026-11-18-amd-ces-2027-zen6-teaser": {"titel": "AMD has scheduled a CES 2027 appearance for January 5 in Las Vegas; a teaser shows a very thin notebook, and official chip details are still missing", "schlagzeile": "AMD locks in its CES 2027 slot — Zen 6 laptops are widely expected", "kurz": "AMD has firmly committed to an appearance at CES 2027 in Las Vegas. The date is January 5, 2027, at 10 a.m. local time, 7 p.m. Central European Time. A teaser shows a very thin, slightly opened notebook; which chips AMD will actually present has not been confirmed yet.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD executive Jack Huynh named the date on X on November 17, ComputerBase reports; PCGH also covers the announcement. Huynh writes about a “next era of computing” and wants to offer a glimpse at CES in the Mandalay Bay. The accompanying image points to especially slim notebooks. In recent years AMD has typically used CES to show new mobile processors, with retail availability often following only months later. ComputerBase links the teaser to the already known Medusa Point code names for upcoming notebook chips and to unofficial sample listings from recent weeks, including 10-, 8- and 6-core variants. Those configurations and clocks have not been confirmed by AMD. It is equally unconfirmed whether desktop Zen 6 derivatives will be shown at CES; PCGH raises that question, and there is no official answer. Reports of additional very efficient cores below Zen 6 and Zen 6c also remain speculation for now. Until January 5, the firm facts are mainly the date and the notebook teaser; technical data will have to wait until AMD itself announces them.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware"], "_src": "c30de252"}, "2026-11-18-nvidia-q3-huang-bleibt-draussen": {"titel": "In its first earnings report after Jensen Huang's resignation, Nvidia posts $115.8 billion in revenue; the board does not intend to reinstate him as CEO", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia record quarter: board rules out Huang's return as CEO", "kurz": "Nvidia posted $115.8 billion in revenue and $65.3 billion in profit for its third fiscal quarter, beating expectations. Board chair Harvey Jones said the board does not intend to reinstate resigned CEO Jensen Huang. Huang had earlier said he would be honored to return if the board decided that was the right course.", "zusammenfassung": "This is the first earnings report since Huang stepped down last week. Nvidia officially reports revenue of $115.8 billion, up 103 percent from a year earlier and 20 percent from the prior quarter; profit rose to $65.3 billion. The data-center segment alone accounted for $107.6 billion, up 110 percent. The former standalone gaming business is now part of Edge Computing, which together generated $8.2 billion, up 42 percent. Interim CEO and CFO Colette Kress spoke of a strong start for the Vera Rubin server platform and an unchanged product roadmap. For the fourth quarter, which is one week longer, Nvidia expects $130 billion in revenue, plus or minus 3 percent, with no data-center chips for China. Gross margin is expected to fall to 71 to 72 percent. Commitments for upcoming components rose to $390 billion from $279 billion in the previous quarter, mainly because of expensive memory contracts, according to ComputerBase. At the start of the analyst call, board chair Harvey Jones made clear that the board had unanimously accepted Huang's resignation and does not intend to reinstate him as CEO; he would not answer questions about the ongoing internal investigation. A few hours earlier, Huang had written that he would be honored to return if the board judged that to be in the interest of shareholders, employees, the company and the United States. The search for a permanent leader continues internally and externally, with Kress remaining in the interim role. Converted, the quarterly figures amount to about 105.3 billion euros in revenue and 59.4 billion euros in profit, according to ComputerBase.", "weitere_links": ["Nvidia IR (Quartalsbericht)", "heise online", "TechPowerUp"], "_src": "2b860864"}, "2026-11-18-windows11-baseline-protection": {"titel": "Windows 11 is testing Baseline Protection: apps receive a yes-or-no report on eight security features and may warn, limit functions or refuse to launch; general availability is planned for 2027", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 tests a security check that apps may use to block launch", "kurz": "Microsoft is testing Windows Baseline Protection in an Insider preview. It rolls eight existing protections into a single report that programs can query. Developers may then warn, restrict features or block the launch; general availability is planned for 2027.", "zusammenfassung": "Windows Latest describes the preview in detail. The eight checks include Secure Boot and memory integrity, among others. Anyone who has turned those features off, for example to dual-boot Linux, will fail the check. Apps receive a clear yes-or-no answer, a list of missing items, or a harder-to-spoof hardware-backed attestation that a vendor can verify on its servers. Microsoft stresses that the system only reports the state; the policy stays with each developer. Adobe, Battle.net, 1Password and Schoolyear are already testing the interface. None of these companies has announced that it will blanket-block PCs that fail the check; Battle.net, according to the report, talks about raising security while keeping friction low for players. In Settings, a new “Security > Baseline protection” page is meant to show the status and turn on many of the missing features with one switch and a restart. Microsoft plans general availability for 2027; until then this remains an Insider test that can still change. For players and tinkerers, the key point is that a protection you can switch off may no longer trigger only a local warning, but can prevent individual programs from starting if the vendor so decides.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware"], "_src": "578e7024"}, "2026-11-17-java4shell-rce": {"titel": "A critical Java4Shell flaw in OpenJDK can allow remote code execution through faulty Base64 decoding on some x86-64 systems with AVX-512; Oracle has released patches", "schlagzeile": "Java4Shell: a serious flaw in Java, and Oracle's patches are out", "kurz": "OpenJDK has a vulnerability known as Java4Shell that can let attackers execute code remotely on affected systems. It sits in a hardware-accelerated Base64 function on certain x86-64 processors with AVX-512. Oracle released patches on November 17; as a temporary workaround the acceleration can be turned off.", "zusammenfassung": "The flaw is tracked as CVE-2026-114938. Research firm Calif rates it 9.2 under CVSS 4.0, which is critical, while Oracle assigns 8.1 (high) under CVSS 3.1, BleepingComputer reports; heise and PCGH also cover the case. Affected are OpenJDK from version 17.0.6 and builds based on it, including Oracle Java SE, Amazon Corretto, Eclipse Temurin, Microsoft's OpenJDK build, Azul Zulu and Red Hat's OpenJDK. The bug is in an accelerated Base64 decoder that only runs on x86-64 processors with certain AVX-512 instructions; newer Ryzen and Intel systems may therefore be more exposed than older machines without those instructions. Calif says it was able to demonstrate unauthenticated code execution on, among others, Jenkins, Jira, Confluence, Keycloak and JFrog Artifactory, and only with a login on further services. There is no single exploit for every program; the crafted data has to reach the vulnerable function in each case. Oracle published fixes in its November security update. Anyone who cannot update immediately can temporarily disable the acceleration with the startup options that turn off Base64 intrinsics or AVX-512, according to the researchers. A general proof of concept for the memory corruption exists; Calif has not published ready-made attacks against the named applications.", "weitere_links": ["heise online", "PC Games Hardware", "Phoronix"], "_src": "91436d41"}, "2026-11-17-game-awards-2026-nominierte": {"titel": "The Game Awards 2026: GTA 6 nominated in eight categories; GOTY nominees are 007 First Light, Control Resonant, GTA 6, Phantom Blade Zero, Resident Evil Requiem and Zelda: Ocarina of Time; show on December 10", "schlagzeile": "Game Awards 2026: GTA 6 scoops up eight nominations", "kurz": "The nominees for The Game Awards 2026 have been announced. GTA 6 appears in eight categories, including Game of the Year. The winners will be revealed on December 10 in Los Angeles.", "zusammenfassung": "On November 17, Geoff Keighley published the nominees of The Game Awards 2026 in all categories. Grand Theft Auto 6 leads the field with eight nominations, including Game of the Year, Game Direction, Narrative, Art Direction, Score and Music, and Audio. Competing for Game of the Year are 007 First Light, Control Resonant, GTA 6, Phantom Blade Zero, Resident Evil Requiem and The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time. Control Resonant and 007 First Light also received multiple nominations. The Most Anticipated Game category includes Fable, God of War Laufey and The Witcher 4, among others. Best Ongoing Game features titles such as Arc Raiders, Fortnite and The Witcher 3. Winners are decided 90% by an international jury and 10% by fan voting, which is already open. The Player's Voice category is determined entirely by fans. The show airs on December 10 from the Peacock Theater in Los Angeles and, as usual, is expected to bring new game announcements. Notably, GTA 6 only releases on November 19 and thus just barely qualifies for this year's period. The linked sources offer a full list of all categories.", "weitere_links": ["IGN Deutschland"], "_src": "a391820a"}, "2026-11-17-doom-dark-ages-fsr41-vulkan": {"titel": "Update 5 of Doom: The Dark Ages is the first Vulkan game with official AMD FSR 4.1 and Frame Generation 4; AMD has also updated its Unreal Engine plugin", "schlagzeile": "Doom: The Dark Ages is the first Vulkan game with native FSR 4.1", "kurz": "With Update 5, Doom: The Dark Ages is the first Vulkan game to officially support AMD's FSR 4.1 and Frame Generation 4. That removes the workaround through third-party tools that was often needed until now. At the same time AMD has updated its Unreal Engine plugin to version 4.1.2, although that plugin still supports only DirectX 12.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD executive Jack Huynh confirmed the news on X, ComputerBase reports. At the end of October AMD had already shipped a Vulkan interface in FSR SDK 2.4.0, but games still had to integrate it. Machine-learning upscaling in FSR 4.1 runs on Radeon RX 9000, RX 7000 and RX 6000 cards as well as selected Ryzen APUs. The AI-based Frame Generation 4 requires at least Radeon RX 9000-series cards. id Software also says Frame Generation can be enabled on Intel graphics if the hardware and drivers play along; the studio does not name specific models. Unreal plugin 4.1.2 brings the SDK changes to Unreal Engine 5.3 through 5.8, extends upscaling to RX 6000 and certain Ryzen processors with integrated graphics, and improves frame pacing on RX 9000. The Vulkan path from the SDK is not yet in this plugin. Update 5 also adds Slaughter mode for the Revelations story expansion released in July 2026, with endless waves of enemies that get harder. For the ticker, the first native use of FSR 4.1 under Vulkan is the main point, not just another game patch.", "_src": "0f86c167"}, "2026-11-18-firaxis-entlassungen": {"titel": "Firaxis is laying off about a third of its staff, around 60 people, according to Bloomberg; studio head Heather Hazen is leaving, and 2K has confirmed the restructuring", "schlagzeile": "Civilization studio Firaxis is laying off about a third of its staff", "kurz": "Civilization and XCOM studio Firaxis has laid off around 60 people, about a third of its staff, according to Bloomberg. Studio head Heather Hazen is leaving, a 2K spokesperson confirmed. Bloomberg, citing people familiar with the matter, also reports development trouble on a new XCOM game.", "zusammenfassung": "The cuts came on November 17, shortly before the launch of GTA 6 at parent company Take-Two. 2K confirms the restructuring but not the number of people affected. In a statement, 2K says Firaxis is recentering on its strength of designing world-class strategy games, is reducing the size of the studio and must say goodbye to talented colleagues. These decisions are never easy, but they are necessary. On Hazen's departure, 2K says she is handing over leadership now so that a new head can own the next chapter from the start. Bloomberg, citing people familiar with the matter, also reports that a new XCOM game has faced development struggles and missed an important milestone in the summer; work is continuing, but the project may change again because of the cuts. Those points have not been confirmed officially. The studio's most recent game, Civilization VII, launched in February 2025 and divided players. Firaxis had already reduced staff in previous years. The next studio leader has not yet been named.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "Eurogamer"], "_src": "71672269"}, "2026-11-23-valve-amdgpu-weniger-ruckler": {"titel": "Valve developer submits revised AMDGPU kernel patches meant to reduce stutter in some Windows games under Proton by batching memory mapping updates", "schlagzeile": "Less stutter on Linux: Valve patches aim to smooth out Radeon games", "kurz": "Valve developer Natalie Vock has released new patches for the Linux graphics driver AMDGPU. They are meant to reduce noticeable stutter in some Windows games under Proton. The patches are still under review, and there are no measurements.", "zusammenfassung": "Many new games use so-called sparse bindings and map or unmap parts of textures or other graphics resources as needed. According to Vock, the driver currently synchronizes these updates with other graphics work, so under heavy load the graphics and compute queues stall for a long time. In addition, every change needs its own system call, which costs a lot of CPU time. The ten patches introduce a new interface called AMDGPU_GEM_VA2 that bundles many changes into one call and synchronizes more selectively. According to Vock, this results in a significant reduction in stutter, but she gives no numbers or affected games. The first version appeared back in May, and batching was added with the November 17 revision, report Phoronix and VideoCardz. For players to benefit, a driver such as Mesa RADV also has to use the new interface. Whether the patches will land in Linux 7.5 is open. The news is a few days old, and we are including it because of its importance for Linux gaming with Radeon cards.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz"], "_src": "be341a3f"}, "2026-11-21-fsr-4-1-2-unreal-rx6000": {"titel": "AMD releases FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 as an Unreal Engine 5 plugin, bringing ML upscaling to Radeon RX 6000 and Ryzen handhelds", "schlagzeile": "FSR 4.1 for Unreal Engine 5: ML upscaling now also for Radeon RX 6000", "kurz": "AMD has updated its FSR plugin for Unreal Engine 5 to version 4.1.2. This makes the ML-based FSR upscaling run on Radeon RX 6000 and select Ryzen processors with integrated graphics for the first time. The plugin supports Unreal Engine 5.3 to 5.8, for now only with DirectX 12.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD published the update on GPUOpen on November 16, and VideoCardz reported on November 17. The plugin is based on the FSR SDK 2.4, codenamed Redstone. For Radeon RX 6000 and Ryzen AI Max, AMD uses the full INT8 model, and for weaker integrated graphics in laptops and handhelds an optimized model less than half the size. The selection is made automatically depending on the hardware, and FSR 3 serves as a fallback on unsupported graphics cards. The package also includes FSR Frame Generation 4.0.2 and a new swapchain that hands frame presentation over to the driver on Radeon RX 9000. This feature requires Adrenalin driver 26.10.1 or newer, and FSR Frame Generation 4.0.2 requires Windows 11. The Anti-Lag 2 plugin has also been updated to version 2.0.6. The SDK already supports Vulkan, but the Unreal plugin does not yet, and AMD has not given a date. Because the plugin integrates FSR via the FSR interface, games can later also receive newer FSR versions via driver updates. Whether and when individual games adopt the update is up to the developers.", "weitere_links": ["AMD GPUOpen"], "_src": "97119f61"}, "2026-11-16-gta6-hacker-schuldig": {"titel": "Hacker behind the 2022 GTA 6 leak pleads guilty in a British court; attacks on Rockstar, Uber and EE/BT caused an estimated £10 million in damage", "schlagzeile": "2022 GTA 6 leak: hacker pleads guilty", "kurz": "The now 21-year-old who hacked Rockstar Games in 2022 and released early GTA 6 videos has pleaded guilty in a London court. Sentencing is still pending.", "zusammenfassung": "On November 16, the man pleaded guilty at Woolwich Crown Court in south-east London to hacking Rockstar Games and other companies, including Uber and EE/BT. According to the report, the estimated damage from the cyberattacks is around £10 million. At the time of the Rockstar hack, he was 16 to 17 years old. According to Eurogamer, citing the BBC, he was staying in a hotel under police protection at the time and used only an Amazon Fire Stick, the hotel TV and a Bluetooth keyboard and mouse for the attack. He reportedly also got into Rockstar's Slack channels and threatened to release the GTA 6 source code. The 2022 leaks showed around an hour of unfinished gameplay and made protagonist Lucia public for the first time. Due to a severe autism diagnosis, he had initially been committed to a hospital, but has since been declared fit to stand trial and was moved to a regular prison earlier this year. Sentencing is still pending. The case should not be confused with the 2026 leaks, which are attributed to a different actor. Rockstar confirmed the intrusion in 2022 and said development would not be affected in the long term.", "_src": "bd2dd5e0"}, "2026-11-16-speicherpreise-ssd-dreifach": {"titel": "ComputerBase price check for November: RAM on average 446 percent, SSDs 162 percent and hard drives 151 percent more expensive than in mid-September 2025", "schlagzeile": "Memory crisis: RAM costs 446 percent more, some SSDs cost triple", "kurz": "ComputerBase has checked the prices of RAM, SSDs and hard drives again. On average, memory is 446 percent above its mid-September 2025 level, SSDs 162 percent. Some memory kits cost more than six times as much, some SSDs three times as much.", "zusammenfassung": "Since mid-September 2025, ComputerBase has been tracking online prices of twelve RAM kits, SSDs and hard drives each that were especially popular at the time. According to the new analysis, prices hit new highs in November. On average, RAM costs 446 percent more than at the start of tracking, and some kits are above 500 percent, meaning more than six times the price. SSDs have risen from plus 146 percent in mid-October to plus 162 percent, and individual models cost three times as much. Hard drives are on average 151 percent above the starting value and have recently become only slightly more expensive. Some memory kits did get a little cheaper, but others rose all the more. Offers from small eBay sellers and Amazon Marketplace sellers are not included because they could distort the trend and are risky for buyers. The editors suspect that many of these offers come from sellers who stocked up during the crisis. There is no end in sight: according to ComputerBase, AMD is also set to raise prices for Radeon graphics cards again in November.", "_src": "0a0a2c9f"}, "2026-11-16-subnautica-2-ea2-gruselbiome": {"titel": "Subnautica 2: developer video shows the new, especially eerie underwater areas of Early Access 2.0, the update is due in December 2026", "schlagzeile": "Subnautica 2: biggest update brings the creepiest deep-sea areas yet", "kurz": "Unknown Worlds shows the areas of Early Access 2.0 for Subnautica 2 in a new developer video. Fog, sightlines and lighting are meant to make them especially menacing. The update is due in December 2026, but there is no exact date yet.", "zusammenfassung": "Early Access 2.0 is the biggest update yet for the underwater survival game, PC Games reports. In the new video, the developers explain how the biomes are made: first, a greybox defines where creatures live and which areas are protected. Then underwater fog, deliberate sightlines and lighting effects create an oppressive atmosphere. The colors reveal where it is safe: warm tones stand for safe areas, cool ones for dangerous areas. Hidden caves and niches hold rewards such as new resources, while striking rocks, light sources and plants point the way. There is also a mysterious plague that drains almost all color from affected parts of the world until they are healed. This way, the world is meant to tell its own story without logs or cutscenes. The video also shows the new FROG chassis for the Tadpole vehicle. Early Access 2.0 is planned for December 2026.", "_src": "88c1897c"}, "2026-11-16-huang-comeback-ft": {"titel": "Financial Times report: days after resigning, Jensen Huang is considering a return as Nvidia CEO; investors push for it, Washington opposes it", "schlagzeile": "Comeback after resigning? Jensen Huang reportedly weighs a return to Nvidia", "kurz": "Just days after his resignation, Jensen Huang is reportedly considering a return to the top of Nvidia, according to the Financial Times. Investors and Silicon Valley figures are pressuring the board, while US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent wants a new chief from outside. Nothing has been decided.", "zusammenfassung": "Jensen Huang stepped down as Nvidia CEO last week after reports emerged of several affairs, including one with a manager at Singapore-based Nvidia customer Megaspeed. According to the Financial Times, cited by ComputerBase and heise, Huang has already discussed a possible return with confidants and supports the efforts. An online initiative under the motto “Bring Jensen back” now reports more than 170,000 supporters, including, by its own account, over 8,200 Nvidia employees; these numbers cannot be independently verified. Uber founder Travis Kalanick is among the initiators, and Elon Musk also supports the campaign. Major investors Brad Gerstner (Altimeter Capital) and Gavin Baker (Atreides Management) urge the board in an open letter not to rule out reappointing Huang. Opposition comes from Washington: on Sunday, US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the next CEO should be found outside the company. According to the report, he also demands information within ten days on whether Nvidia complied with US export rules. The US Senate Banking Committee has also called Huang and Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick to a hearing. An independent investigation commissioned by the board is still ongoing. Huang does not hold a majority stake and cannot overturn the board's decisions on his own. Until this is resolved, CFO Colette Kress is leading the company on an interim basis, and Nvidia reports quarterly results on Tuesday.", "weitere_links": ["heise online", "IGN", "TechPowerUp"], "_src": "50d29cce"}, "2026-11-16-phantasialand-chlor-microsoft-ausfall": {"titel": "Consequences of the Microsoft cloud outage: alarm emails from a pool system at a Phantasialand hotel never arrived, 15 people were injured after a chlorine overdose", "schlagzeile": "Alarm email never arrived: Microsoft outage led to 15 injuries", "kurz": "Because of the Microsoft cloud outage on Thursday and Friday, an alarm email at the Hotel Ling Bao of the Phantasialand theme park in Brühl, Germany, reached no one. A faulty dosing system had added too much chlorine to a pool. 15 guests complained of respiratory problems, and four were taken to hospital.", "zusammenfassung": "According to German broadcaster WDR, cited by heise, the maintenance and safety system of the sauna area raised the alarm by email. Because of the prolonged outage of Microsoft's cloud services, however, these emails never arrived. The pool's automatic dosing system was defective and added far too much chlorine to the water. On Friday afternoon, this caused chlorine gas to escape in the pool area of the hotel, which belongs to Phantasialand. Initially 13 guests complained of respiratory problems, and the number later rose to 15. Four people were taken to hospital, and one had to stay for observation with moderate injuries. The Brühl fire department was on site with 40 responders for about two hours; the pool was closed and the water replaced, and it has since reopened. The Microsoft outage lasted from Thursday afternoon until at least Friday noon. According to heise, it thus had real and dangerous consequences, and criminals have also been using it for phishing emails since Friday.", "_src": "9e40db29"}, "2026-11-16-playstation-controller-bezahlen-patent": {"titel": "Sony patent application: PlayStation controller to read payment data from smartphones and cards via NFC, Bluetooth or QR code", "schlagzeile": "Pay by controller? Sony patent turns PlayStation pad into a card reader", "kurz": "Sony has filed a patent application for a PlayStation controller that reads payment data from a smartphone or card via NFC, Bluetooth or QR code. This is meant to make console purchases work without tedious typing. No such product has been announced.", "zusammenfassung": "The application “Video Game Controller-Driven Information Transfer” (US 2026/0273403 A1) dates from March 17, 2025 and was published by the US Patent Office on September 17, 2026, Golem and Engadget report. When the console requests a payment, you hold a smartphone or card to the controller. It detects the device via NFC, Bluetooth or touch, and one variant reads a QR code from the phone display with an image sensor. Light, sound or vibration confirm the connection, after which the console verifies the data with a server. Credit and bank accounts, gift cards, and digital and crypto wallets are listed; the remaining balance of a gift card should appear directly on screen. Besides game purchases, Sony lists in-app purchases, merchandise, food delivery and credits for tournaments, trade shows and arcades. Sharing player profiles, joining multiplayer sessions or sending screenshots to a phone should also work with a tap. Sony justifies the idea by saying today's processes often require several devices and keyboard input. However, a patent application only protects an idea, and whether Sony ever implements it is open.", "weitere_links": ["Engadget"], "_src": "464cad26"}, "2026-11-16-intel-sammelklage": {"titel": "Shareholders file class action in San Jose against Intel, CEO Lip-Bu Tan and other executives, alleging the company disclosed the PC sales slump too late", "schlagzeile": "29 percent stock plunge: shareholders sue Intel and CEO Lip-Bu Tan", "kurz": "Intel shareholders have filed a class action in a US federal court in San Jose against the company, CEO Lip-Bu Tan and other executives. They accuse Intel of disclosing the slump in PC sales too late. After the quarterly results on October 29, the stock fell almost 29 percent.", "zusammenfassung": "The lawsuit was filed by the law firm Robbins Geller Rudman & Dowd, heise reports, citing the BBC; Reuters is also reporting on it. It covers all shareholders who bought Intel stock between July 23 and October 29, 2026. The complaint alleges “materially false and/or misleading” statements about the decline in PC sales and the impact of data center projects. According to Wccftech, the suit names CFO David Zinsner alongside CEO Lip-Bu Tan and points to a 23 billion dollar stock sale in August. On October 29, Intel admitted that even fewer PCs were sold than expected because of the memory crisis and reported supply problems with data center chips. For the current quarter, the company expects revenue of only 15 to 16 billion dollars, while analysts had expected around 17 billion. The stock then lost almost 29 percent in a single day. Intel has not commented on the lawsuit so far. The plaintiffs seek damages of an unspecified amount, and it is now up to the court to rule on the allegations.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "0fdca8b2"}, "2026-11-16-razor-lake-12p-bllc": {"titel": "Leak: Intel Razor Lake reportedly gets a gaming chip with 12 P-cores, 4 LP E-cores and a large bLLC cache but no regular E-cores, made on Intel 18A-P", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Intel reportedly plans a gaming CPU with 12 P-cores and a huge cache", "kurz": "Leaker Jaykihn reports a Razor Lake desktop chip with twelve P-cores, four low-power cores and a large cache (bLLC), but no regular E-cores. It would be Intel's answer to AMD's X3D processors. Razor Lake is not expected until 2028, and none of this is official.", "zusammenfassung": "According to TechPowerUp and VideoCardz, well-known Intel leaker Jaykihn named a “12+0+4” configuration for Razor Lake on X. This means twelve P-cores, no regular E-cores and four efficient LP E-cores, combined with Intel's big last level cache (bLLC). The bLLC concept is seen as Intel's counterpart to AMD's X3D chips with extra cache, which are especially strong in games. The unlocked chip is said to replace a previously rumored locked 8+0+4 model with bLLC. All twelve P-cores are said to sit on a dedicated compute die that, according to Jaykihn, is made on Intel's 18A-P process, while most Razor Lake tiles are reportedly produced at TSMC. In addition, a 125-watt model with 6+12+4 cores and bLLC has allegedly been moved from Nova Lake to Razor Lake. Nova Lake-S would then have one bLLC variant fewer than expected. Razor Lake-S is expected in 2028 and should use the same LGA 1954 socket as Nova Lake-S. Intel has listed Razor Lake model numbers in an ISA reference, but the specifications are not confirmed. Plans this far out can still change.", "ursprungsquelle": "Jaykihn on X", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz on X"], "_src": "b4662c61"}, "2026-11-16-pokepark-fishing-rally-gefunden": {"titel": "Lost Pokémon game found: collector discovers a test cartridge with PokéPark Fishing Rally DS from 2005, PSA Video Games confirms its authenticity", "schlagzeile": "Lost Pokémon game resurfaces after 20 years – and it's playable", "kurz": "A collector has found a test cartridge with PokéPark Fishing Rally DS, a fishing game that was only available at a Japanese theme park in 2005. PSA Video Games has confirmed its authenticity. This preserves a long-lost piece of Pokémon history.", "zusammenfassung": "PokéPark Fishing Rally DS was only available for a few months in 2005 at the PokéPark in Nagoya. Visitors downloaded the fishing minigame to their Nintendo DS via Download Play at stations in the park. After twelve hours, or when the console was switched off, it deleted itself again. Players caught Pokémon and competed for prizes on leaderboards. After the park closed, the game was considered lost because it was only stored on special test cartridges for staff. A cartridge offered on eBay for 9,000 dollars in July contained only the leaderboard software. Now collector Daniel Quadri owns a cartridge with the actual game, according to Polygon, and PSA Video Games has confirmed it is genuine. With it, he can send the game to other DS consoles via Download Play just like back then. For now, the cartridge remains in a sealed case for protection.", "_src": "0c147818"}, "2026-11-16-wireview-pro-ii-garantie": {"titel": "Thermal Grizzly publishes the terms of the extended GPU warranty for the WireView Pro II: 24 months of coverage for connector damage, but only with monitoring enabled", "schlagzeile": "Melted connector? Thermal Grizzly explains when its GPU warranty applies", "kurz": "Thermal Grizzly has published the terms of the extended graphics card warranty for the WireView Pro II. It covers damage to the 12VHPWR or 12V-2x6 connector and resulting GPU damage for 24 months. Monitoring must stay enabled, and shunt mods and mining are excluded.", "zusammenfassung": "The WireView Pro II sits between the PSU cable and the graphics card and measures the current on each individual 12-volt line. Thermal Grizzly promises buyers an extended warranty for power connector damage, and according to TechPowerUp the manufacturer has now explained the terms in an FAQ. Neither the USB cable nor the Y-splitter to the motherboard has to be connected; the splitter lets the device shut down the PC in an emergency, but it is only recommended. Monitoring must remain switched on: thresholds for current, temperature or power may be lowered, but not raised above the defaults. Extensions between the WireView and the graphics card are allowed as long as each 12-volt line stays separate; adapters that merge lines internally are not covered. A 90-degree connector is not a problem in itself, and on the PSU side cables approved for the specific PSU model are fine. The warranty runs for 24 months from the WireView purchase, even beyond the graphics card's own warranty, but only for the original buyer with proof of purchase. Shunt mods, XOC BIOS with a raised power target and commercial mining are excluded, as is damage unrelated to the connector. For a claim, Thermal Grizzly first tries a repair; otherwise you get a card with comparable performance, not necessarily from the same brand. Anyone who spots melting should switch off the PC, unplug the PSU, leave the connector attached, take photos and contact support.", "_src": "c3d9a0f0"}, "2026-11-16-windows11-remote-lock-intune": {"titel": "Windows 11 Insider build 29708.1001 tests Remote Lock: IT can lock lost company PCs via Intune without deleting data; only IT can lift the lock", "schlagzeile": "Laptop gone? Windows 11 tests a remote lock that only IT can lift", "kurz": "Microsoft is testing a feature called Remote Lock in an Insider preview. It lets IT departments lock lost or stolen company PCs via Intune without deleting any data. Password, PIN or a local admin account will no longer get you in.", "zusammenfassung": "Windows Latest spotted the feature in build 29708.1001 in the experimental “Future Platforms” channel from November 13. When locked, Windows signs out all sessions, hides the sign-in options and shows a lock screen saying the organization has locked the device. According to Microsoft, nothing is erased, BitLocker stays on and the device remains managed in Intune. Restarting or disconnecting from the internet does not lift the lock; only IT can unlock it via Intune. The user account itself stays active, so if credentials are stolen, IT has to disable it separately in Entra ID. Requirements are Windows Pro, Enterprise or Education and a device managed via Entra ID or MDM; setup currently works in a clunky way through a custom Intune profile. The catch: a device that is offline only receives the lock the next time it connects. In addition, Remote Lock blocks neither the recovery environment, Safe Mode nor booting from a USB drive, which is why Microsoft still considers BitLocker necessary. As recently as March 2025, a Microsoft employee had said there were no plans for a remote lock on Windows. As an Insider test, the feature may still change before release.", "_src": "9f3701ee"}, "2026-11-16-linux-7-4-rc3-zen5": {"titel": "Linux 7.4-rc3 released: TSA mitigation for AMD Zen 5, power-saving features for AMD graphics, workarounds for ARM cores and better sensor support", "schlagzeile": "Linux 7.4-rc3: protection for Zen 5 CPUs and power saving for AMD graphics", "kurz": "Linus Torvalds has released the third release candidate of Linux 7.4. According to Neowin, it brings a mitigation for AMD's Zen 5 processors and power-saving features for certain AMD graphics chips. The final version is expected after seven release candidates.", "zusammenfassung": "Torvalds describes the past week as fairly normal, with most changes affecting networking and graphics drivers and being small. In the file system area, a large but essentially trivial change to the iomap calling convention stands out. According to Neowin, rc3 includes a mitigation described as critical against the TSA microarchitectural vulnerability on AMD's Zen 5 processors. For AMD graphics with IP version 11.0.2, power-saving features such as Multi-Coarse Gate Clock and Fine-Grain Clock Gating are enabled. On the ARM cores Cortex-A715 and Cortex-A720, the kernel works around faulty performance counters that can cause wrong readings and kernel warnings. For upcoming Intel graphics platforms, there are fixes for display detection on USB-C ports. The kernel also reads voltages, fan speeds and temperatures more reliably on motherboards with NCT6775 sensor chips. This marks roughly the halfway point of the development cycle. Distributions such as Arch and Fedora usually adopt new kernels only after the first point release.", "weitere_links": ["Phoronix"], "_src": "55a0b07f"}, "2026-11-16-project-helix-konsole-pc-spiele": {"titel": "Xbox vice president Jason Ronald: Project Helix is a console that also runs PC games, not a PC for console games; neural rendering is meant to help against high component costs", "schlagzeile": "Project Helix: the next Xbox is a console that can also play PC games", "kurz": "Microsoft has shared new details on Project Helix in its magazine for the 25th Xbox anniversary. According to Xbox vice president Jason Ronald, Helix is a console that can also run games from your PC, not a PC for console games. To counter high component costs, Microsoft is relying on neural rendering, among other things.", "zusammenfassung": "For the Xbox's 25th birthday, Microsoft surprisingly published an anniversary magazine, and IGN and Insider Gaming have summarized its statements on Project Helix. “Helix is designed to be a console that is also capable of playing games from your PC. It is not a PC that can also play console games,” says Jason Ronald, vice president of next generation. Players should be able to bring their library from four Xbox generations along with their progress, and the boundaries between console and PC games are meant to disappear. Power users should still get deeper settings for graphics and performance. Ronald calls the ROG Xbox Ally a precursor whose concepts and feedback are feeding into Helix. Preserving older games is central, he says: compatibility already determines how the platform is being designed. On the component crisis, Ronald says new technology has to be invented to keep consoles affordable. Neural rendering can generate frames without requiring more computing power or memory. Microsoft gives no date or price; according to IGN, there is speculation about a launch in late 2027 at the earliest. What the devices in the Helix family will look like is still unknown.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming (console first)", "Insider Gaming (neural rendering)", "Insider Gaming (game preservation)"], "_src": "e894d330"}, "2026-11-16-gta6-jason-lucia-kleinkriminelle": {"titel": "GTA 6: according to a Rockstar interview with The Guardian, Jason and Lucia start as small-time criminals and have to work their way up to big heists", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: Jason and Lucia start as small-time crooks – big heists come later", "kurz": "In GTA 6, Jason and Lucia do not start as professional robbers but as small-time criminals. The Guardian reports this after talks with Rockstar. Lucrative jobs such as jewelry store robberies are only possible later.", "zusammenfassung": "British newspaper The Guardian spoke with Rob Nelson, co-studio head of Rockstar North, and head of publishing Jennifer Kolbe, and IGN summarizes the report. According to it, the two main characters can initially only hotwire basic cars and pick simple locks. Robbing jewelry stores in Vice City or driving sports cars through Leonida only becomes possible once they have worked their way up. Nelson describes Jason and Lucia as a young couple with “their backs against the wall”. Robberies, from gas stations to luxury boutiques, should be easier or more profitable if you prepare them, for example by disabling cameras, stealing surveillance footage or scouting discreet entrances. Skip the preparation and a robbery can quickly descend into chaos. According to The Guardian, there will also be mechanics that encourage empathy for the first time in the series. Rockstar has not yet said what that means in practice or how long the rise takes. GTA 6 launches on November 19 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S.", "_src": "b6c3d707"}, "2026-11-16-xbox-boot-animationen-25": {"titel": "For the 25th anniversary: Xbox Series X|S and Xbox One get the original Xbox boot animation and two Xbox 360 boot animations", "schlagzeile": "For its 25th birthday, Xbox brings back the original boot animation", "kurz": "For the 25th anniversary of Xbox, owners of an Xbox Series X|S and Xbox One can once again use the boot animation of the first Xbox. Two Xbox 360 boot animations from 2005 and 2010 are also included. According to Xbox, the update is rolling out throughout the day.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft celebrated 25 years of Xbox on November 15 and announced three classic boot animations on the official Xbox account on X. Besides the sci-fi intro of the original Xbox, there are two Xbox 360 variants, one from the 2005 launch and one from 2010. According to IGN, they are largely untouched rips of the original videos. The animations are coming to all Xbox Series X|S and Xbox One consoles and are being rolled out gradually. If you don't see them yet, you need a little patience. For the anniversary, Microsoft also published a magazine with a look back and ahead, including new details on the next generation, Project Helix. Microsoft had already added a first new boot sequence earlier this year.", "weitere_links": ["Xbox on X"], "_src": "d0945bc7"}, "2026-11-16-librem-5-v2-risc-v": {"titel": "Purism launches crowdfunding for the Librem 5 v2 Linux smartphone with the eight-core RISC-V SoC SpacemiT K1, 8 GB RAM and 128 GB storage from 1,599 US dollars", "schlagzeile": "Linux phone Librem 5 v2 switches to RISC-V – for a hefty 1,599 dollars", "kurz": "Purism is raising money for the second generation of its Librem 5 Linux smartphone. Instead of an Arm chip, it uses an eight-core RISC-V processor from SpacemiT, plus 8 GB RAM and 128 GB storage. Backers pay at least 1,599 dollars and will not get the device before 2028.", "zusammenfassung": "The Librem 5 v2 uses the SpacemiT K1 with eight RISC-V cores, replacing the quad-core Arm chip from NXP in the first model. Purism promises more performance, longer battery life and less heat. RAM increases from 3 to 8 GB, internal storage from 32 to 128 GB. The case, the 5.7-inch IPS display with 720 × 1440 pixels and the removable 4,500 mAh battery stay the same to make repairs and upgrades between generations easier. The hardware kill switches for camera, modem and GPS, USB-C and the headphone jack also remain. New are an improved 4G modem, dual SIM and hardware encoding, which is said to enable 13-megapixel photos and HD video for the first time; a 5G module is planned as a swappable module. The operating system is the Debian-based PureOS with the Phosh interface. OMG! Ubuntu points out that the first generation suffered from delays, price increases and inconsistent build quality. The switch to RISC-V also means a lot of work on graphics drivers, power management and browser performance. The crowdfunding campaign runs until February 2027.", "_src": "79ec4d2b"}, "2026-11-16-fbi-artex-ki-angriffe": {"titel": "FBI warns of ARTEX: AI-powered pentesting framework has been abused for automated attacks worldwide since August 2026, including in the ConnectWise supply chain attack", "schlagzeile": "FBI warns: AI tool ARTEX is automating hacker attacks worldwide", "kurz": "The FBI is warning about ARTEX, an AI-powered penetration testing framework that attackers have been abusing since at least August 2026. Some intrusions reached privileged access in under three hours. The October supply chain attack on ConnectWise is also said to have used it.", "zusammenfassung": "In a FLASH advisory released on Friday, the FBI writes that several threat groups are using the open-source framework against organizations in finance, government, technology, defense, healthcare and other sectors, BleepingComputer reports. ARTEX is written in Go and lets AI agents handle reconnaissance, vulnerability discovery, exploitation, privilege escalation and data theft largely on their own. It has no AI model of its own but connects to external language models such as Claude, GPT, DeepSeek, GLM, Grok and Kimi. According to the FBI, this allows even attackers with little expertise to target several organizations at once. The tool is particularly good at finding weaknesses in neglected systems such as partner portals, employee apps, legacy services and third-party integrations. The developer “Autumn-27” released ARTEX on GitHub in July and removed it on October 8, but forks, archived copies and a commercial version called ARTEX PRO are still circulating. In early November, researchers counted more than 1,600 publicly exposed ARTEX consoles. The attacks cited include the October supply chain attack on ConnectWise Cloud Backup, through which attackers gained access to customers' Microsoft 365 environments. The FBI recommends securing internet-facing applications and cloud admin interfaces, reviewing permissions and authentication logs, and rate-limiting sensitive APIs. Security researcher MalwareMustDie has also released a free pack of detection rules for common security tools.", "_src": "05be065b"}, "2026-11-15-cyberpunk-torrent-regen-mod": {"titel": "Cyberpunk 2077 mod “Torrent” replaces the rain in Night City with individual 3D drops and adds thunderstorms with lightning", "schlagzeile": "Cyberpunk 2077: new mod finally makes it really rain in Night City", "kurz": "The Torrent mod replaces Cyberpunk 2077's flat rain effects with individual 3D drops, spray and thunderstorms. The drops react to wind, light and driving speed. The mod is available for free on Nexus Mods.", "zusammenfassung": "Modder CyanideX has released the Torrent mod for Cyberpunk 2077, Eurogamer reports, citing DSOGaming. It replaces the previously rather flat rain effects with individual 3D drops, each with its own size and falling speed. The drops react to the player's movement: at high speed they pelt toward the windscreen, and strong wind pushes them sideways. Street lamps, neon signs and car headlights are reflected in the drops, and rain no longer falls through roofs or into buildings. Drops splash on the ground, heavy rain leaves mist in the distance, and cars throw up spray on wet roads. There is also a new thunderstorm system with branching lightning bolts whose frequency can be set across ten levels. With the AudioXL mod, each strike is followed by thunder timed to its distance. For light-sensitive players, the Reduce Flashes option replaces the flicker with a slow glow and halves the number of strikes. Torrent works with Nova City 2 and other weather mods. The reports do not mention performance on weaker PCs. The mod is available now for free on Nexus Mods.", "_src": "84dc6ca1"}, "2026-11-15-dawn-of-war-4-systemanforderungen": {"titel": "Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War 4 – system requirements released, 32 GB RAM and 125 GB on an NVMe SSD recommended", "schlagzeile": "Dawn of War 4 wants 32 GB RAM and a 125 GB SSD – in the middle of the RAM crisis", "kurz": "King Art and Deep Silver have published the PC requirements for Dawn of War 4. The strategy game is modest on CPU and graphics card, but not on memory: 32 GB RAM and 125 GB on an NVMe SSD are recommended. The game launches on December 3.", "zusammenfassung": "Shortly before the launch of Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War 4, developer King Art and publisher Deep Silver have revealed the PC system requirements, PC Games Hardware reports. The minimum is a Core i5-10600K or Ryzen 5 2600X, a GeForce GTX 1660 or Radeon RX 5700 and 16 GB RAM. Recommended are a Core i7-12700 or Ryzen 5 7600X, a GeForce RTX 3060 Ti or Radeon RX 9060 with 8 GB and 32 GB of RAM. In both cases the game needs 125 GB on an NVMe SSD; according to King Art, around 25 GB of that is a buffer for DLC and updates. It is not known which resolution and frame rate the specs are meant for. Officially, Windows 11 is listed even in the minimum requirements, but in a Steam post the developers clarified that the game also runs on 64-bit Windows 10. Because Microsoft has ended support for Windows 10, however, King Art cannot guarantee compatibility with future updates there. The high memory recommendations come at a time when RAM has become significantly more expensive. If you don't want to install it, you can also stream Dawn of War 4 via GeForce Now. The game costs 59.99 euros on Steam, the Commander Edition with the Year 1 expansion 89.99 euros, and pre-orders get ten percent off. Nvidia has already released a Game Ready driver for the game with GeForce driver 621.24.", "_src": "c938792d"}, "2026-11-16-madden-gta6-nicht-loeschen": {"titel": "EA shows a “Don't Delete!” pop-up with a Vice City look in Madden NFL 27 and announces an update for November 17, two days before GTA 6", "schlagzeile": "“Don't Delete!”: Madden 27 fights for its storage space just before GTA 6", "kurz": "EA shows a new pop-up in Madden NFL 27 with the message “Don't Delete!” and announces an update for November 17. EA does not name GTA 6, but palm trees and pink-purple colors strongly recall Vice City. GTA 6 needs more than 200 GB and launches two days later.", "zusammenfassung": "Players spotted the pop-up over the weekend, CharlieIntel made it known, and IGN reports on it. It says, in essence, that a crew is preparing a big score and that players should await a signal from an insider on November 17. A new update for Madden NFL 27 is due on that day, a Tuesday. EA does not explicitly mention GTA 6, but the design and wording clearly allude to the Rockstar game. On November 10, the official Madden account on X had already promoted an update for November 18 by saying 210 GB should not come between players and their league. Background: depending on the console, GTA 6 needs more than 200 GB, and many players have to delete other games for it. In early screenshots, the pop-up also contained the typo “awating signal”, which was apparently fixed quickly. Many players are reacting with amusement on social media. GTA 6 launches on November 19 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S.", "_src": "9feb44ca"}, "2026-11-15-kongress-ki-chip-exporte": {"titel": "After the Megaspeed case, the US Congress pushes stricter export controls for AI chips with bipartisan support; parts could end up in the NDAA defense bill", "schlagzeile": "After the Megaspeed affair: US Congress wants tighter rules on AI chip exports", "kurz": "Democrats and Republicans want to tighten controls on exports of powerful AI chips, ComputerBase reports, citing the Financial Times. Some proposals could be added to the annual US defense bill. Whether that happens before the end of the year is open.", "zusammenfassung": "The case surrounding Nvidia customer Megaspeed from Singapore is shaking up US export policy. According to ComputerBase, citing the Financial Times, several bills to control AI chips are gaining support from both parties in Congress. They aim to limit sales abroad and give Congress more say over deals that have already been approved. US authorities have been examining for more than a year whether Megaspeed passed Nvidia chips on to China. One proposal, the Remote Access Security Act, would make it harder for Chinese companies to remotely access AI accelerators in foreign data centers if they are not allowed to buy these chips themselves. Some proposals could be added to the annual NDAA defense bill, which is considered very hard to block. Lawmakers are also demanding that Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick explain why Nvidia was allowed to supply Megaspeed. According to the Financial Times, the proposals were already making progress, but the Megaspeed case has significantly improved their chances. It is unclear whether Congress has enough time before the end of the year. There are no known direct consequences for gaming graphics cards so far. The debate hits Nvidia at a delicate time, though: the company reports its quarterly results on November 17.", "_src": "33b7866c"}, "2026-11-15-playstation-black-friday-zubehoer": {"titel": "PlayStation Black Friday from November 16: discounts on DualSense, Pulse headsets, PS VR2 and games, but no price cut for PS5 and PS5 Pro", "schlagzeile": "PlayStation Black Friday: deals on controllers and PS VR2, not on the PS5", "kurz": "Sony's Black Friday promotion starts at midnight local time on the night to Monday and runs until the end of November. There are discounts on DualSense controllers, headsets, PS VR2 and games, but the PS5 itself does not get cheaper. Sony has not yet announced euro prices.", "zusammenfassung": "Sony has announced the details of its Black Friday promotion, which starts on November 16 at midnight local time and runs until November 30. On the PlayStation Blog, Sony lists US discounts: 20 dollars off the DualSense, 30 dollars off the DualSense Edge, 40 dollars off the Pulse Elite headset, 30 dollars off the Pulse Explore earbuds, 30 dollars off the Access controller and 100 dollars off PS VR2. According to Polygon, that puts the DualSense at 54 dollars and PS VR2 at 299 dollars in the US. The PS5 and PS5 Pro themselves get no official discount, unlike last year with a discounted bundle, as Push Square notes. Games such as Marvel's Wolverine, Saros, Ghost of Yōtei Complete Edition and Marvel Tōkon: Fighting Souls are also reduced, and the PlayStation Store offers up to 75 percent off PS5 and PS4 games. According to Push Square, PS Plus members in Germany and Austria, among other countries, get an extra five percent off the sale price when buying through PlayStation Direct. There are also offers for new PS Plus members and upgrades to Premium or Deluxe. Sony will only publish euro prices and the exact duration of individual offers at launch on the regional Black Friday page, and they may differ by country and retailer. The 27-inch monitor with charging hook is only available in the US and Japan.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation.Blog", "Push Square", "PlayStation on X"], "_src": "8e3329d9"}, "2026-11-15-rtx4090ti-es-china": {"titel": "Alleged engineering sample of the never-released GeForce RTX 4090 Ti with 18,176 CUDA cores offered on a Chinese marketplace", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Never-released RTX 4090 Ti reportedly up for sale in China", "kurz": "According to VideoCardz, a pre-production RTX 4090 Ti is being offered on a Chinese second-hand marketplace. The seller lists 18,176 CUDA cores, around eleven percent more than the RTX 4090. These claims have not been independently verified.", "zusammenfassung": "Nvidia never brought the GeForce RTX 4090 Ti to market, but prototypes keep turning up. According to VideoCardz, another alleged engineering sample is now listed on a Chinese second-hand marketplace. The listing was spotted by X user @meiei_nowa, and UNIKO's Hardware published more photos. According to the seller, the card has 18,176 CUDA cores, 192 ROPs and 568 TMUs. That matches the rumors about the RTX 4090 Ti that circulated years ago and works out to about eleven percent more shaders than the regular RTX 4090 with 16,384 cores. The professional RTX 6000 Ada Generation has the same core count. The full AD102 configuration with 18,432 cores, by contrast, was only found in the never-released TITAN Ada prototype tested by overclocker der8auer. The seller says the card needs an internal Nvidia driver but ran without obvious problems in testing. Earlier RTX 4090 Ti samples stood out with a four-slot design and a rotated circuit board; one sample tested by Gamers Nexus, however, ran with normal RTX 4090 specs. Nvidia never officially explained why the card was cancelled. Whether this really is an RTX 4090 Ti cannot be proven from the listing alone.", "ursprungsquelle": "Listing on a Chinese second-hand marketplace, spotted by @meiei_nowa on X, photos from UNIKO's Hardware", "_src": "a774e6e2"}, "2026-11-15-game-awards-nominierungen-gta6": {"titel": "The Game Awards announce nominees on November 17; GTA 6 is eligible despite its November 19 release", "schlagzeile": "Game Awards: nominees arrive Tuesday – and GTA 6 can still compete", "kurz": "The nominees for The Game Awards 2026 will be announced in a livestream on Tuesday at 6 p.m. Central European Time. GTA 6 only launches two days later, but under the official rules it is still eligible. The show itself takes place on December 10 in Los Angeles.", "zusammenfassung": "Geoff Keighley will present the nominees for The Game Awards 2026 on Tuesday in a dedicated livestream on YouTube and Twitch. It starts at 6 p.m. Central European Time; in previous years the broadcast lasted only about ten minutes. Awards are handed out in more than 30 categories, and the Game of the Year candidates traditionally come last. This is exciting because of GTA 6, which only launches two days later for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. According to the official rules quoted by Polygon, a game qualifies for the main categories if it is available by Friday at 9 p.m. Pacific Time. GTA 6 just makes it, although a nomination is not guaranteed. For the fan award Players' Voice, the cut-off is even the end of the month. Nominees are chosen by a jury of more than 100 media and creator organizations, and according to PC Games the winners are determined 90 percent by the jury and 10 percent by fan vote. Whether Rockstar sent game codes to the jury in advance is not known. A similar case happened in 2014, when the Wii U Smash Bros was nominated shortly before its US launch. The ceremony takes place on December 10 at the Peacock Theater in Los Angeles, which is the night to December 11 in our time zone.", "weitere_links": ["Polygon"], "_src": "18002e56"}, "2026-11-15-phishing-microsoft-365-ausfall": {"titel": "Microsoft warns of a phishing campaign sending fake status notices about the Microsoft 365 outage", "schlagzeile": "Phishing wave exploits Microsoft 365 outage – Microsoft warns", "kurz": "Criminals are using this week's Microsoft 365 outage for phishing, Microsoft's Threat Intelligence team warns. Fake outage notices claim that held-back emails will be deleted unless you click a link. Genuine outage information is only available in the Microsoft 365 admin center.", "zusammenfassung": "Shortly after the major outage of Microsoft's cloud services, phishing emails about it are appearing, heise online reports. Microsoft's Threat Intelligence team warns on Bluesky of a campaign imitating Microsoft 365 status notices. The emails refer to the real Exchange Online incident with the ID EX1550543. Some of the messages Microsoft discovered on Friday claim that emails were held back during the outage and will be deleted within 24 hours unless restored via a link. Subject lines often follow the pattern “Outage” plus a six-character code, and sender names such as “Outage Notification” or “Service Health” are used. According to Microsoft, the emails come from three domains, and the click links redirect via SendGrid to another site. So far the campaign has targeted organizations in various industries in the US. The pattern matches typical credential phishing, but Microsoft has not yet been able to confirm that passwords were actually stolen or malware distributed. Microsoft Defender blocks the domains used, and Defender for Office 365 moves such emails to quarantine. Admins should check their Safe Links policies and only read outage notices in the Microsoft 365 admin center. For everyone: don't click links in emails that threaten deletion and put you under time pressure.", "_src": "a428b950"}, "2026-11-15-dawnwalker-1-2-new-game-plus": {"titel": "The Blood of Dawnwalker: Update 1.2 brings New Game Plus, a level cap of 100 and balance changes in the week of November 16", "schlagzeile": "Blood of Dawnwalker: New Game Plus and level 100 arrive this week", "kurz": "With update 1.2 for The Blood of Dawnwalker, Rebel Wolves delivers the most requested feature: New Game Plus. The level cap also rises to 100. The update is due sometime this week, but there is no exact day yet.", "zusammenfassung": "The Polish studio Rebel Wolves, founded by former Witcher developers, has announced update 1.2 for its vampire RPG The Blood of Dawnwalker. It is due in the week of November 16; the studio has not given an exact date. The most important new feature is a New Game Plus mode that unlocks after the epilogue. Level, skills and inventory carry over into the new run. The level cap rises to 100, enemies are scaled uniformly across all regions, and items get their own New Game Plus versions with adjusted stats. The update also changes a lot without New Game Plus: Rebel Wolves is adjusting enemy health and how often enemies use their special abilities. Terrain geometry is also being reworked so that movement in combat and exploration feels smoother. Owners of the Eclipse Edition get additional songs in the in-game soundtrack, which is also set to come to Spotify and other streaming services later. Full patch notes are not out yet, so exact numbers for the balance changes are missing. It is also unclear whether New Game Plus can be played several times in a row. According to GamesRadar+, the game finished second in two categories at the Golden Joystick Awards this week.", "weitere_links": ["Polygon", "GamesRadar+"], "_src": "3dd042af"}, "2026-11-15-gta6-album-tracklist-leak": {"titel": "Track list of the official GTA 6 album leaks via video before release; Rolling Stone and Billboard consider the list genuine according to their own sources", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Lana Del Rey, Dua Lipa, Jennie – is this the GTA 6 track list?", "kurz": "A video from a store apparently shows the vinyl edition of “Grand Theft Auto VI: The Album” including the complete track list. According to PC Gamer, sources at Rolling Stone and Billboard confirm the list. Rockstar itself has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "A few days before the launch of GTA 6, the track list of the official album has apparently leaked. According to IGN, a video shared on social media from a store shows the front and back of the double LP “Grand Theft Auto VI: The Album”, which is not due out until November 19 for around 50 dollars. According to Insider Gaming, the album comprises 34 tracks. Among those named are Lana Del Rey with the previously unreleased song “Crazy For You”, Dua Lipa and Jennie of Blackpink; PC Gamer also names Playboi Carti and Keith Richards. The first tracks include two songs by the French duo Justice, one with Michael McDonald and one with Tame Impala, SZA and King Gizzard & the Lizard Wizard. According to PC Gamer, sources at Rolling Stone and Billboard have described the list as accurate. Rockstar Games and Take-Two have not confirmed the track list; under our rules it therefore still counts as a leak. Important: the album is not the game's complete soundtrack. The in-game radio stations also contain licensed songs, and the score by Justice will be released separately on December 11, according to IGN. GTA 6 launches on November 19 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S; there is still no PC date.", "weitere_links": ["IGN", "Insider Gaming (Tom Henderson)"], "_src": "2d952e53"}, "2026-11-15-ubuntu-pro-ki-sicherheitspatches": {"titel": "Canonical launches Edge archive: Ubuntu Pro users can test AI-generated security patches before regular review", "schlagzeile": "Ubuntu tests AI security patches – if you want them, you get them sooner", "kurz": "Canonical is offering Ubuntu Pro users a new, opt-in package archive called Edge. It contains security fixes created by an AI system called Surge before they have been fully reviewed. According to Canonical, regular updates will continue to be reviewed by humans.", "zusammenfassung": "Canonical is now having some security holes in Ubuntu patched by AI agents. According to OMG! Ubuntu, the company has built a system of several AI agents called Surge that backports fixes for known vulnerabilities in userspace packages to older versions. These machine-generated patches land in a new archive called Edge. The archive is opt-in and disabled by default; anyone who wants to use it has to enable it on their system themselves. Surge does not patch the Linux kernel. According to Canonical, regular Ubuntu updates will continue to be reviewed and tested by humans as before, and Surge fixes will not automatically move into the stable releases. Canonical cites the sharp rise in vulnerability reports found with the help of language models, as well as attacks using AI agents, as the reason; the security team has already shipped twice as many fixes as last year. Users of the Edge archive are meant to help test the AI patches in everyday use before they are released generally. Ubuntu Pro is free for private users on up to five devices, and Edge is available for Ubuntu 18.04 to 26.04 LTS. Updates from it are not installed automatically by default. A risk remains: unreviewed patches can contain bugs, so Edge is more for testers than for production systems.", "_src": "6705813e"}, "2026-11-15-lol-new-dawn-blg-weltmeister": {"titel": "Riot announces “League of Legends: New Dawn” at the Worlds final, the biggest overhaul of the game since 2009; BLG become world champions", "schlagzeile": "League of Legends gets a complete overhaul in 2027 – BLG win the title", "kurz": "At the final of the LoL World Championship, Riot Games unveiled “New Dawn”, a major update for 2027. The client, Summoner's Rift, graphics and gameplay are set to change significantly. The final itself was won 3-1 by Bilibili Gaming against Gen.G.", "zusammenfassung": "At the final of the 2026 League of Legends World Championship in Brooklyn, Riot Games announced “League of Legends: New Dawn”. According to IGN, it is a comprehensive update that is due in 2027 and will change the client, Summoner's Rift, visuals and gameplay. Executive producer Paul Bellezza spoke of the beginning of a new era for League in the first trailer. Among other things, the trailer shows a redesigned champion select reminiscent of the mobile game Wild Rift, as well as reworked minions, dragons and Baron Nashor. The footage also hints at a new or heavily rebuilt rune system and bigger changes to the map terrain. Riot is not yet revealing exactly what will change in the gameplay; the full presentation is planned for January 2027. There have been several major overhauls since the 2009 launch, such as the new map in 2014, but nothing on this scale. GameStar is therefore already talking about a “League of Legends 2”, while Riot itself calls it an update. Whether the player base will embrace the changes remains to be seen. On the competitive side, Bilibili Gaming from China took the title: according to Insider Gaming, BLG beat Gen.G 3-1 in the final. Mid laner Knight was named the tournament's most valuable player.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming (Tom Henderson)", "IGN Deutschland"], "_src": "cb4615e1"}, "2026-11-15-zephyr-4070tis-ein-luefter": {"titel": "Zephyr launches the RTX 4070 Ti Super Sakura Snow X with a single fan for 285 watts in China after all, despite an earlier cancellation", "schlagzeile": "One fan for 285 watts: mini RTX 4070 Ti Super launches after all", "kurz": "Chinese manufacturer Zephyr is now selling its RTX 4070 Ti Super Sakura Snow X after all, after the model was put on hold in March due to expensive GDDR6X memory. According to Zephyr, it is the only mass-produced card of this type that cools 285 watts with just one axial fan. For quiet operation, the manufacturer recommends a 220-watt power limit with less than five percent performance loss.", "zusammenfassung": "Zephyr has brought the GeForce RTX 4070 Ti Super Sakura Snow X to market after all, following several delays and a temporary cancellation, reports PC Games Hardware. According to the manufacturer, it is the only mass-produced RTX 4070 Ti Super that dissipates 285 watts of board power with a single axial fan. To do so, however, the fan has to spin fast. Zephyr therefore recommends lowering the power limit to 220 watts for quieter operation; this is said to cost less than five percent of gaming performance. The manufacturer does not say which games it tested. In March 2026, Zephyr had halted the model for the time being due to sharply higher GDDR6X prices and announced an RTX 4070 Super with 12 GB instead. The card sits in a housing milled from a block of metal and targets compact PCs that cannot fit a triple-fan card. The small first batch was sold through a retailer on Douyin and, according to Techtesters, is already sold out. There is no official price; in July, 6,199 to 6,499 yuan was mentioned, roughly 795 to 835 euros before taxes and customs. Zephyr has not announced a launch in Germany. Incidentally, the 220-watt limit can be set on any RTX 4070 Ti Super yourself, for example with a power limit of around 77 percent in MSI Afterburner at reference TGP.", "_src": "bc4ac344"}, "2026-11-15-inxile-buero-schuesse": {"titel": "Shots fired at office building of Xbox studio inXile in California: nobody hurt, police arrest a suspect", "schlagzeile": "Shots hit Xbox studio inXile's building – police arrest a suspect", "kurz": "The office building in Tustin, California, that houses Xbox studio inXile was hit by gunfire on Wednesday. Nobody was injured. Police arrested a suspect two days later; the motive is still unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "The office building of Microsoft studio inXile Entertainment in Tustin, California, has been hit by gunfire. According to Insider Gaming, local media reported the incident on the afternoon of November 11, with several bullets striking the building. Police told the magazine Aftermath it was a drive-by shooting and found several shell casings. Nobody was injured. On the morning of November 13, police arrested a suspect; the name and motive are not known, and the investigation is ongoing. Whether the studio was deliberately targeted has not been determined. A spokesperson said they were relieved that nobody was hurt, were looking after the team and were working closely with the authorities. inXile is known for the Wasteland series and is working on Clockwork Revolution, an Xbox exclusive planned for 2027. Xbox has not announced any impact on the game.", "_src": "349ed63a"}, "2026-11-15-inoffizielle-pc-ports-astro-bot-totk": {"titel": "Unofficial native PC ports: Astro Bot runs on Windows as the first PS5 exclusive, Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom even on a GeForce MX550", "schlagzeile": "Astro Bot and Zelda on PC: fan ports without an emulator take off", "kurz": "With Astro Bot, a PS5-exclusive game runs as an unofficial native PC port for the first time, including DLSS and Frame Generation. At the same time, a user shows Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom via recompilation on a notebook GPU with just 2 GB of memory. Neither project is authorized by Sony or Nintendo.", "zusammenfassung": "Instead of emulating console games, fan projects are increasingly translating them directly into native PC code. According to ComputerBase, there is now such a port of Astro Bot, the 2024 Game of the Year, for Windows. The developer says he used a PS5 copy of the game; the graphics are translated to Vulkan via a component from the KytyPS5 project. An add-on integrates Nvidia DLSS, Frame Generation and Reflex. With a Ryzen 5 5500 and RTX 5060, the port reaches only 32 to 34 fps at 1440p in the demanding Sky Garden level, according to the developer, and mostly 40 to 50 fps elsewhere, i.e. less than the 60 fps of the PS5. With Frame Generation it is just over 60 fps, with Multi Frame Generation up to 128 fps. Meanwhile, according to PC Games Hardware, a Reddit user shows Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom via the TotK Recomp project on a notebook with a GeForce MX550 and 2 GB of video memory. He reports around 30 fps with drops; he does not state the resolution. According to the release notes, version 0.4.0 of the port needs only 3.4 instead of 4.8 GB of VRAM on a Radeon RX 9070. Both projects are unofficial and not approved by Sony or Nintendo; how long they will remain available is unclear. According to ComputerBase, many are already hoping for similar ports of GTA 6, which launches on November 19 initially only for consoles.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware (PCGH)"], "_src": "af19c7e6"}, "2026-11-14-huang-petition-musk": {"titel": "Petition for Huang's return to the top of Nvidia: over 100,000 signatures, backed by Elon Musk, more than 1,600 comments internally", "schlagzeile": "“Bring back the boss”: 100,000 want Jensen Huang back at Nvidia", "kurz": "According to Golem, a public petition for Jensen Huang's return to Nvidia has more than 100,000 signatures, including over 2,000 from current and former employees. Elon Musk announced on X that he would sign it. Many employees are also calling for the founder's return in the internal forum.", "zusammenfassung": "Just days after Jensen Huang's resignation, resistance to the board's decision is growing. According to Golem, a petition under the motto “33 years deserve an answer” had more than 100,187 signatures on the evening of 14 November. Over 2,000 current and former Nvidia employees are said to be among them, which cannot be verified from the outside. Elon Musk had pointed to the petition on X on 13 November and announced he would sign it. According to Wired, there is also a post in Nvidia's internal suggestion forum calling for Huang's return with more than 1,600 comments, most of them in favour. Heise reports that interim CEO Colette Kress has announced an all-hands meeting for 18 November. The board had announced Huang's resignation after reports of a second affair with a manager who reported directly to him; Reuters later reported a third relationship. Huang himself has not commented since his email to staff on Sunday. Nvidia and board chair Harvey Jones have not yet responded to the petition. A petition has no legal effect; the decision lies solely with the board.", "weitere_links": ["heise online", "PC Games Hardware (PCGH)"], "_src": "cb2772ff"}, "2026-11-14-gta6-codes-fehlen-box": {"titel": "Some physical GTA 6 copies contain no readable download code, and retailers are reacting differently", "schlagzeile": "Bought GTA 6, but no code in the box? First buyers report misprints", "kurz": "Several buyers report that their physical copy of GTA 6 contains no readable download code. Instead of the code, there is only a grey strip that cannot be scratched off. According to Polygon, both PlayStation and Xbox versions are affected, but the problem does not seem to be widespread.", "zusammenfassung": "GTA 6 is a fully digital release; even the retail box contains no disc, just a download code. The code is printed on the back of the cover and is meant to be visible through the transparent case. Retailers have been shipping pre-orders since 12 November so that buyers can preload the game. According to Polygon, several buyers now report that their code is missing: instead of characters there is only a grey strip that looks like a scratch-off field but cannot be scratched off. This reportedly affects both PlayStation and Xbox copies. Retailers are reacting differently: some Best Buy stores reportedly refused returns, Amazon refunded the purchase price, and GameStop is referring customers to Rockstar. Two Reddit users report that Rockstar's support closed their tickets without a solution. Rockstar has not yet commented publicly. Polygon assumes that only a few copies are affected. Anyone who bought a box should therefore check the code before the launch on 19 November.", "_src": "fc2b8517"}, "2026-11-14-xbox-25-spiele-pc-kauf": {"titel": "For the Xbox anniversary: 25 games free with the purchase of a new Windows PC, but only in the US", "schlagzeile": "25 free Xbox games – but only with a new PC and only in the US", "kurz": "Microsoft is celebrating 25 years of Xbox with a bundle of 25 PC games, including Skyrim, Halo: Combat Evolved Anniversary and Gears of War: Reloaded. They are only available with the purchase of a qualifying new Windows PC by the end of 2026, counting from the start of November. The offer applies exclusively in the US.", "zusammenfassung": "Xbox head Asha Sharma presented the “25 Years of Xbox Bundle” on X. According to Microsoft's offer terms, anyone who buys and activates a qualifying new Windows PC receives 25 digital PC games. These include Skyrim Special Edition, Oblivion, Halo: Combat Evolved Anniversary, Gears of War: Reloaded, Age of Empires 2, Doom, Quake, Fallout 76 and Call of Duty: WWII, among others. Eligible devices are selected Windows Home devices from participating retailers and manufacturers, including some handhelds; Windows Pro devices are excluded with one exception. Refurbished, open-box, returned and demo units do not count. The purchase must be made between 2 November and 31 December 2026. The bundle will appear in the Microsoft Store under “Included with device” by 30 November at the latest and must be redeemed by 12 February 2027. The licences are tied to the Microsoft account and cannot be transferred. According to PC Games, the offer only applies in the US, so not in Germany or Austria. Whether it will be extended is not known. The community has been rather critical of the offer, partly because new PC hardware is currently especially expensive.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft (offer terms)", "Asha Sharma on X"], "_src": "5e070100"}, "2026-11-14-12v2x6-pinprotect-november": {"titel": "More than ten new cases of melted GeForce power connectors in November; Corsair's special cable shows when PinProtect shuts down", "schlagzeile": "Melted again: more than ten connector cases in November alone", "kurz": "VideoCardz has counted more than ten reported cases of damaged 16-pin power connectors on GeForce cards in November alone, down to the RTX 5070. At the same time, a test with a special Corsair cable shows that its PinProtect safety feature does actually shut down under overload.", "zusammenfassung": "The problems with the 12V-2×6 connector keep coming. VideoCardz has gathered reports compiled by the UNIKO's Hardware channel from Reddit, Chinese forums and other communities, counting more than ten cases in November alone. Affected cards include an RTX 5090 D, several RTX 4090s, an RTX 5080, an RTX 5070 Ti and two RTX 5070s. The RTX 5070 stands out, as Nvidia rates it at only 250 watts, compared with 575 watts for the RTX 5090. Some of the damage was on the graphics card, some on adapters or on the power supply side. The individual reports do not show how common such failures are overall, and the causes have not been checked case by case. Fittingly, Professional Review has shown a previously unknown Corsair test cable on which each of the six 12-volt lines can be cut off with a switch. On an RTX 5080 under a load of around 250 watts, the lines were switched off one after another. Only when just a few pins were still carrying current and one pin exceeded the threshold of around 9.5 amps did Corsair's PinProtect in the RM1200e power supply shut the card down. According to Wccftech, the cable is not available in stores and apparently serves internal testing.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "bc31497b"}, "2026-11-14-geforce-freeman-nope": {"titel": "Nvidia's GeForce evangelist Jacob Freeman dismisses speculation about the end of GeForce after Huang's resignation", "schlagzeile": "End of GeForce after Huang's exit? Nvidia's Freeman says: “Nope”", "kurz": "Since Jensen Huang's resignation, many gamers have been wondering whether Nvidia will give up on GeForce. GeForce evangelist Jacob Freeman answered exactly that question on X with a curt “Nope”. However, there is no official roadmap on the matter.", "zusammenfassung": "Since Jensen Huang stepped down as Nvidia CEO, there has been speculation that the company might focus even more on AI hardware and scale back its gaming business. Jacob Freeman, GeForce evangelist at Nvidia and formerly a product manager at EVGA, has commented on this on X. He was at the PDXLAN LAN party in the US and wrote that a lot had happened this week, but the work with colleagues who love PC gaming continues. When a user asked him directly whether this was the end of GeForce, he replied with “Nope” and a smiley. This is a personal reply on X, not an official announcement by Nvidia. Nvidia has not presented a new gaming roadmap. According to VideoCardz, Nvidia had previously cancelled several products already discussed with board partners, including a SUPER series with 3 GB memory chips; this is unconfirmed. Freeman's statement won't make graphics cards any cheaper either: the RTX 5090 currently costs more than three times its MSRP in the US.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "52c2591a"}, "2026-11-14-tarkov-konsole-mobile": {"titel": "Escape from Tarkov: console version to be announced in 2027 but released no earlier than 2028; mobile spin-off will be a top-down extraction shooter", "schlagzeile": "Tarkov: console version not before 2028, mobile spin-off top-down", "kurz": "Battlestate head Nikita Buyanov wants to unveil the console version of Escape from Tarkov next year, but it is not expected to release before 2028. According to Insider Gaming, the planned mobile game will not be a port but an extraction shooter with a top-down perspective. This game is also set to be announced in 2027.", "zusammenfassung": "In an interview with Insider Gaming, Battlestate Games revealed new details about its Tarkov plans. According to PC Games, studio head Nikita Buyanov is close to finding a partner for the console port. He firmly expects to officially unveil the console version in 2027, possibly as early as the start of the year. He ruled out a release in 2027, so 2028 at the earliest is realistic. Battlestate has still not said definitively which consoles the version is coming to. Buyanov had previously announced that the console version would not be simplified and would even do without aim assist; whether that stays the case is open. The studio is also working on a Tarkov game for smartphones. According to Buyanov, it is an extraction game with the look of Tarkov, but from a top-down third-person perspective, similar to Escape from Duckov or Zero Sievert. Playable prototypes already exist, and an announcement is planned for next year. In addition, the second PvP season of Escape from Tarkov starts in December.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games"], "_src": "957c3f7e"}, "2026-11-14-rtx5090-usa-dreifach-uvp": {"titel": "RTX 5090 back in stock at Newegg, but at more than three times MSRP; in Japan, prices for the RTX 5090 and RTX 5080 are falling", "schlagzeile": "RTX 5090 back in stock – at three times the MSRP", "kurz": "The GeForce RTX 5090 is once again directly available at Newegg in the US. The cheapest model, however, costs $6,249.99, more than three times the $1,999 MSRP. In Japan, by contrast, prices for the RTX 5090 and RTX 5080 have recently dropped significantly.", "zusammenfassung": "After weeks of barely any stock, US retailer Newegg is once again listing several RTX 5090 models for direct purchase, according to VideoCardz. The cheapest is an ASUS ROG Astral RTX 5090 OC for $6,249.99. Models from GIGABYTE and MSI range from around $6,600 to $7,000, and an MSI SUPRIM SOC costs $7,349.99. Nvidia's official MSRP is still $1,999, so even the cheapest offer costs a good 3.1 times as much. In September, Newegg itself had almost no stock left, and buyers mostly had to rely on marketplace sellers. In Japan, prices are heading down: according to Wccftech, citing ITmedia and Gazlog, a Palit RTX 5090 GameRock dropped at Dospara from 1,288,000 to 1,048,000 yen, and at the Akihabara store even to 999,800 yen. The RTX 5080 fell from as much as 359,800 to 299,800 yen. The timing coincides with Jensen Huang's resignation, but the reports see no direct connection. According to them, prices had already peaked at the end of October, after which inventories grew. Whether this turns into a broad price decline remains open.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "2a354308"}, "2026-11-14-steamos-3-10-hdmi21-amd": {"titel": "SteamOS 3.10.0 Preview: HDMI 2.1 with VRR, FRL and ALLM for AMD graphics, mesh shaders for Nvidia from Turing onwards", "schlagzeile": "SteamOS 3.10 Preview: AMD graphics finally get HDMI 2.1 with VRR", "kurz": "Valve has released SteamOS 3.10.0 as a public preview. With AMD graphics, the system now supports HDMI 2.1 with VRR, FRL and ALLM. Nvidia cards from Turing onwards get mesh shaders, plus there is a kernel based on Linux 7.3.", "zusammenfassung": "According to GamingOnLinux, Valve has released the preview of SteamOS 3.10.0. For users with AMD graphics, the most important new feature is support for HDMI 2.1 with variable refresh rate (VRR), Fixed Rate Link (FRL) for high bandwidths and the automatic low latency mode ALLM. As a known issue, Valve notes that the Dell G3223Q monitor may stay blank. For Nvidia graphics there are stability and performance improvements, mesh shaders from the Turing generation onwards, and fixes for rendering errors in Shadow of the Tomb Raider and The Surge 2. Game Mode adds the Vulkan extension VK_EXT_present_timing. Valve also improves frame timing with the frame rate limiter under VRR and reduces flickering in the Steam interface. The ASUS ROG Xbox Ally X20 gets HDR and brightness settings. Desktop Mode moves to KDE Plasma 6.8.2, and the kernel to Linux 7.3. This is an early test build; Valve advises switching only if you can live with possible bugs.", "_src": "9372f312"}, "2026-11-14-gta6-fake-pc-download-malware": {"titel": "Fake GTA 6 PC download spreads an infostealer that grabs Steam logins and crypto wallets", "schlagzeile": "Warning: “GTA 6 for PC” is malware – it steals Steam logins", "kurz": "Security researchers at Cynet are warning about a supposed GTA 6 PC download that is actually malware. Among other things, it steals passwords, Steam and Roblox accounts and crypto wallet data. There is no PC version of GTA 6; the game launches on 19 November for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S only.", "zusammenfassung": "Shortly before the launch of GTA 6, scammers are trying to exploit the excitement. According to Neowin, security firm Cynet has examined a supposed “GTA 6 EXE FILE DOWNLOAD” distributed via a Google Colab notebook. The link leads to a page posing as a software portal, which uses a version number, a download counter and badges such as “Virus-free” and “Verified” to look legitimate. Only 72 MB are offered, and the archive contains a tiny EXE file and a text file. The text file asks the user to run the EXE as administrator, ignore security warnings and add an exception in the antivirus software. Anyone who does so installs an infostealer that detects virtual machines and sandboxes and hooks into browser processes. It steals passwords, cookies, browsing data, secrets from browser extensions, Steam and Roblox credentials and crypto wallet data. It can also swap copied crypto addresses and download further malware. Important: no PC version of GTA 6 has been announced. At launch on 19 November, the game will only be released for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S, so any Windows or Mac download is very likely a scam.", "_src": "0ac2cf10"}, "2026-11-14-wine-11-22-avx-arm": {"titel": "Wine 11.22 emulates AVX on ARM64 and fixes 34 bugs, including in Guild Wars 2 and Star Citizen", "schlagzeile": "Wine 11.22: Windows programs with AVX now also run on ARM", "kurz": "The development release Wine 11.22 can emulate AVX instructions in x86 emulation on ARM64. This lets more modern Windows programs run on ARM computers under Linux. There are also 34 bug fixes, including for games.", "zusammenfassung": "The Wine project has released development version 11.22. The most important new feature, according to Phoronix, is support for AVX instructions in x86 emulation on ARM64. Many modern Windows programs require AVX and previously did not run, or only with limitations, on ARM systems with Wine. With ARM64EC builds, these instructions can now be emulated. This is especially interesting for Linux on ARM computers. Wine 11.22 also updates the locale data to Unicode CLDR 49, introduces address space randomization and improves the rendering of the Tahoma font. In total, the release fixes 34 known bugs, including in Guild Wars 2, Star Citizen and Logos Bible Software. Wine is the basis of Valve's Proton, which runs Windows games on Linux and the Steam Deck. However, new Wine features only reach Proton over time. This is a development release; the stable Wine 12.0 is being prepared for early 2027.", "_src": "c3cec6af"}, "2026-11-14-windows11-neuer-ausfuehren": {"titel": "Windows 11 gets the new Run dialog in December, the Browse button is dropped", "schlagzeile": "Win+R goes modern: new Run dialog coming to everyone in December", "kurz": "The redesigned Run dialog of Windows 11 has arrived in the Release Preview channel. It is set to reach all PCs with 25H2 and 26H2 with the Patch Tuesday on December 8. The old dialog remains available via a toggle.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft is bringing the modernized Run dialog (Win+R) to all Windows 11 users. According to Windows Latest, it is now included in Release Preview builds 26200.10066 (25H2) and 26300.10066 (26H2). Normally, this is followed by an optional update at the end of the month and the rollout to everyone on Patch Tuesday on December 8. The rollout is gradual, so not every PC gets the dialog right away. The new dialog is based on WinUI 3, supports dark mode and, according to Microsoft, opens in a median of 94 milliseconds instead of 103 milliseconds for the old one. The Browse button is dropped: according to Microsoft, only 0.0038 percent of users in a sample of 35 million ever clicked it. Paths can still be typed, and the new shortcut ~\\ jumps to the user folder. Previous commands appear above the input field and can be browsed with the arrow keys. Anyone who prefers the old dialog can switch back under Settings > System > Advanced. Microsoft plans to gradually move more old dialogs to WinUI 3, such as the properties in File Explorer.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Insider Blog"], "_src": "3c051621"}, "2026-11-14-blade-runner-aaa-spiel": {"titel": "Blade Runner rights holder Alcon is in talks about a AAA video game based on the film series", "schlagzeile": "Blade Runner as a AAA game? Rights holder confirms talks", "kurz": "Alcon Entertainment, owner of the Blade Runner brand, is in talks about a big AAA game. The two Alcon CEOs confirmed this in an interview with IGN. Details such as studio, platforms or timing are not yet known.", "zusammenfassung": "The Blade Runner film series could get a big video game. Andrew Kosove and Broderick Johnson, the CEOs of rights holder Alcon Entertainment, confirmed to IGN that there are talks about a AAA game. The statement came in an interview about the new series Blade Runner 2099, which starts on Prime Video on November 25. Asked why there has been no big Blade Runner game after the success of Cyberpunk 2077, Kosove answered \"Yes\" and explicitly emphasized the \"AAA\". Players should be able to interact with the world of Blade Runner. He would not reveal more. A developer, platforms or a time frame are therefore not known, and talks do not yet mean an announced game. The brand has had little luck with games so far: only Westwood's 1997 adventure is considered a classic, and it received a remaster in 2022. Annapurna's Blade Runner 2033: Labyrinth, announced in 2023, is considered canceled.", "_src": "df74a8ea"}, "2026-11-14-pearl-abyss-ki-pipeline": {"titel": "Crimson Desert studio Pearl Abyss wants to expand AI across its entire development, DokeV is targeted for 2028", "schlagzeile": "Despite the Crimson Desert backlash: Pearl Abyss doubles down on AI", "kurz": "Pearl Abyss, the studio behind Crimson Desert, wants to use AI throughout its entire game development in the future. That is stated in its quarterly earnings letter. The studio also gives a target for DokeV: the second half of 2028.", "zusammenfassung": "Pearl Abyss is expanding its use of AI in game development. According to PC Gamer and Eurogamer, this comes from the studio's letter on its third-quarter 2026 results. The team now tests new game systems with AI before implementing them manually at great effort. AI is also meant to automate repetitive tasks, help with content creation and optimize testing, across the entire development pipeline. Pearl Abyss stresses that AI is only a tool and not a replacement for developers; gameplay and content will continue to be designed by the team. The topic is sensitive: earlier this year the studio had to apologize after AI-generated 2D graphics were discovered in Crimson Desert. At the time it said they should have been replaced before release and that it had not disclosed its AI use clearly enough. The letter does not say which games exactly are affected or how much AI content will end up in the finished games. Pearl Abyss also gives a target for DokeV: the colorful action game is set to release in the second half of 2028.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming"], "_src": "2e134a95"}, "2026-11-14-nvidia-ceo-suche-haas": {"titel": "Nvidia CEO search: board reportedly approached Arm CEO Rene Haas, Nvidia calls speculation premature", "schlagzeile": "Will Arm's CEO become Nvidia's new boss? The board pumps the brakes", "kurz": "According to the Financial Times, Nvidia's board approached Arm CEO Rene Haas as a possible successor to Jensen Huang. Nvidia itself says it is only now selecting a search firm and has not formally contacted any candidates. At the same time, an alleged employee letter calling for Huang's return is circulating, which an Nvidia executive calls a fake.", "zusammenfassung": "After Jensen Huang's resignation, Nvidia is looking for a new CEO. According to a Financial Times report summarized by Tom's Hardware, the board approached Arm CEO Rene Haas as a possible successor. Haas is said to be one of several candidates; whether he will get an offer or would accept it is unclear. He worked at Nvidia for about seven years until 2013, including on notebook GPUs and Tegra chips, and has led Arm since 2022. Nvidia has responded to the report: the board told CNBC that it is only now selecting a search firm and has not formally contacted any candidates. Speculation about individual names is premature, it said. For the time being, CFO Colette Kress is running the company on an interim basis. According to WIRED, cited by PCGH, the mood inside the company is divided: a post in Nvidia's internal suggestion box collected more than 1,600 comments, mostly in favor of Huang's return. A letter circulating online, allegedly signed by Nvidia executives, is a fake according to Nvidia research VP Bryan Catanzaro; he says he did not sign it and stands behind the board. According to Wccftech, Elon Musk announced he would sign a petition for Huang's return. Nvidia has not announced any reinstatement of Huang. According to PCGH, there are no known effects on GeForce products or prices so far. On November 17, Nvidia will report quarterly results without Huang for the first time.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware", "Wccftech", "CNBC"], "_src": "5f97b49c"}, "2026-11-14-pioner-eingestellt": {"titel": "Survival shooter Pioner is shutting down, the studio has no money left for development and servers", "schlagzeile": "Over after eleven months: survival shooter Pioner is shutting down", "kurz": "The survival shooter Pioner is being shut down less than a year after its early access launch. Developer GFAGames could not find funding for further development and servers. When the servers will go offline is still open.", "zusammenfassung": "The survival shooter Pioner has reached its end. According to PC Gamer, developer GFAGames announced on Steam that it is ending development and closing the game. Talks with existing and new partners about funding failed. The studio no longer has enough money of its own to continue development and run the servers. Since its reveal in 2021, Pioner was seen as a mix of Stalker, Metro and Escape from Tarkov, with a single-player campaign as well as co-op and PvP modes in a late-Soviet world. It had been in early access since December 2025 and peaked at 1,686 concurrent players on Steam. After technical problems and slow updates, the numbers collapsed in the summer, and by mid-September only a few dozen people were still playing. Many buyers are demanding refunds under the announcement. GFAGames has not yet commented on that. A date for shutting down the servers is also still missing.", "_src": "4a2ae3c6"}, "2026-11-14-euro-office-desktop": {"titel": "European office alternative Euro-Office is now available as a desktop app for Windows, macOS and Linux", "schlagzeile": "Europe's office alternative now also works offline on the desktop", "kurz": "Euro-Office, the European alternative to Microsoft 365, is now available as a free desktop app called Nextcloud Office Desktop. It runs offline on Windows, macOS and Linux. Technically, it is a fork of ONLYOFFICE.", "zusammenfassung": "Euro-Office is now also available as a classic desktop application. According to OMG! Ubuntu, the app is called Nextcloud Office Desktop and is free and open source. Euro-Office was announced in March 2026 as a European alternative to Microsoft 365 and previously only ran via a server in the browser or as a mobile app. The desktop version, on the other hand, works without your own server and offline. It offers word processing, spreadsheets, presentations and PDF tools. Microsoft formats such as DOCX, XLSX and PPTX are supported as well as open formats like ODT. In addition, the app can be connected to Nextcloud or other servers for collaborative editing. Installers are available for Windows and macOS on x86 and ARM64 as well as for Linux on x86 as DEB and RPM packages. Technically, Euro-Office is based on ONLYOFFICE, whose maker views the fork critically. There is also criticism from the LibreOffice camp. OMG! Ubuntu notes that the app currently feels mainly like a renamed ONLYOFFICE.", "weitere_links": ["Dr. Windows"], "_src": "cc9ac9bc"}, "2026-11-14-m365-stoerung-ursache": {"titel": "Microsoft apologizes for the Microsoft 365 mass outage and names a network upgrade as the cause", "schlagzeile": "Microsoft 365 outage: no hack, no AI – a network upgrade was to blame", "kurz": "Microsoft has apologized for the worldwide outage of Outlook, Teams and more. According to Microsoft, the cause was a fault from an earlier network upgrade, not an attack or AI. A detailed report is to follow.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft has named the cause of the major Microsoft 365 outage on November 12. According to PC Gamer, the company explicitly apologized to customers and partners in a statement. The fault was introduced during an earlier network capacity expansion and only became a problem after a later network change. A cyberattack or AI agents were not involved. Online, there had been speculation about whether AI-generated code caused the outage. Microsoft says it has fixed the underlying cause and reports broad recovery of its services. The restoration was deliberately gradual to verify stability and therefore took longer. On Saturday, Microsoft said it had fully restored service for the remaining affected customers and regions. Affected services included Outlook, Teams, SharePoint and Copilot. Microsoft plans to publish a detailed report once its internal review is complete. Business customers can check for an SLA credit depending on their contract.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Latest", "Associated Press"], "_src": "8b4d83fb"}, "2026-11-14-windows-oob-aktivierung": {"titel": "Microsoft releases emergency update against activation errors after November Patch Tuesday", "schlagzeile": "Emergency update: Microsoft fixes Windows activation after Patch Tuesday", "kurz": "Microsoft has released out-of-band updates that fix activation error 0x80041008 after November's Patch Tuesday. Mainly companies that activate Windows via slmgr.vbs were affected. The updates are available for Windows 11 23H2, Windows 10 and Windows Server.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft has fixed the activation error after November's Patch Tuesday with an emergency update. Neowin reports this. After the security updates, activation and licensing commands via the slmgr.vbs tool failed with error 0x80041008. Mainly companies that manage activation and product keys via scripts were affected. The out-of-band updates are available for Windows Server 2025 (KB5136489), Windows Server 2022 (KB5136487), Windows Server 2019 and Windows 10 Enterprise LTSC 2019 (KB5136490), Windows 11 23H2 (KB5136483) as well as Windows 10 22H2 with ESU and Windows 10 Enterprise LTSC 2021 (KB5136493). They are cumulative updates that also contain all previous fixes. Windows Server and Windows 10 get them via the Microsoft Update Catalog, Windows 11 23H2 additionally via the optional updates in Windows Update. The report does not mention a separate update for the newer versions 24H2, 25H2 and 26H2. According to the report, this update does not fix the also confirmed printing problem after Patch Tuesday. Microsoft recommends using PowerShell instead of slmgr.vbs for automation anyway.", "_src": "2b8d555d"}, "2026-11-14-nvidia-wsj-knappheit": {"titel": "WSJ report: Huang allegedly financed AI startups so they would absorb Nvidia's surplus GPUs", "schlagzeile": "Report: Did Nvidia pay AI startups to buy its GPUs?", "kurz": "According to the Wall Street Journal, Jensen Huang used Nvidia's money to finance AI startups and data centers that then bought Nvidia GPUs. The background is said to have been an oversupply of chips ordered from TSMC. CFO Colette Kress reportedly pushed back.", "zusammenfassung": "A new Wall Street Journal report sheds light on Nvidia's financial practices under Jensen Huang. TechPowerUp and Wccftech summarize it. According to the report, Nvidia financially backed AI startups and smaller cloud providers, which in turn used the money to buy Nvidia GPUs and build data centers. The reason is said to be that large cloud companies are increasingly using their own chips and Nvidia had ordered more chips from TSMC than it had immediate buyers for. Huang reportedly spoke internally of an \"avalanche\" coming at him. According to the report, there was a dispute in August with CFO and now interim CEO Colette Kress, who wanted to scale back such circular financing, including the multibillion-dollar deal with OpenAI. According to Wccftech, Kress got the guarantees for OpenAI compute reduced from up to 250 to up to 125 billion US dollars. Huang then reportedly criticized her in a disparaging way. Kress is also said to have warned that many of the small cloud providers cannot really afford the GPUs. The report does not prove whether this practice directly drove up GPU and memory prices for gamers; that is Wccftech's interpretation. According to the available reports, Nvidia has not commented. The allegations come from anonymous sources and have not been officially confirmed.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "638a0a69"}, "2026-11-14-core-ultra-7-260k": {"titel": "Intel Core Ultra 7 260K appears without announcement, for now only in two Newegg prebuilt PCs", "schlagzeile": "Quietly launched: Intel's Core Ultra 7 260K only comes in prebuilt PCs", "kurz": "Intel has quietly launched a new desktop CPU, the Core Ultra 7 260K. So far it is only found in two gaming PCs from Newegg and is not sold separately. Technically, it is a slightly throttled Core Ultra 7 265K.", "zusammenfassung": "Intel has launched a new desktop CPU without announcing it. According to TechPowerUp, the Core Ultra 7 260K is only available in two gaming PCs from Newegg's in-house brand ABS. The Kaze II Aqua pairs it with an RTX 5060 for 1,699.99 US dollars, the Flux II Aqua with an RTX 5070 for 1,999.99 US dollars. Newegg confirms that the processor remains exclusive and will not be sold separately. According to Tom's Hardware, Intel describes it as a limited-availability model without a boxed version. Technically, the chip largely matches the Core Ultra 7 265K: 8 performance and 12 efficiency cores, 30 MB of L3 cache and 125 watts base power. However, the maximum P-core clock is 100 MHz lower at 5.4 GHz. Since it only supports DDR5-6400, it belongs to the original Arrow Lake family rather than the refresh with DDR5-7200. The first Newegg listings were contradictory, sometimes showing 260KF or a 5.2 GHz boost. There are no benchmarks yet. This makes the CPU uninteresting for DIY builders, and prices or availability in Europe are not known.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz", "Wccftech"], "_src": "98b50ecf"}, "2026-11-13-rainbow-six-vegas-leak": {"titel": "Report: Ubisoft Montreal is working on a new Rainbow Six: Vegas codenamed Spades", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Rainbow Six: Vegas returning after 18 years?", "kurz": "According to Insider Gaming, Ubisoft has greenlit a new Rainbow Six: Vegas, codenamed Spades. The game is said to be in early development at Ubisoft Montreal. Ubisoft has not confirmed this, and an announcement is likely still years away.", "zusammenfassung": "The Rainbow Six: Vegas series could return after almost two decades. Citing anonymous sources, Insider Gaming reports that Ubisoft has greenlit a new Vegas game codenamed Spades. It is said to be in early development at Ubisoft Montreal. A total of three new projects have reportedly been started there, and another one is also said to be set in the Rainbow Six universe. According to the sources, it is more likely a Vegas 3 than a remake, but that is not certain. The last entry, Rainbow Six: Vegas 2, was released in 2008. Since then, the focus has mainly been on Rainbow Six Siege. The brand now belongs to Vantage Studios, a Ubisoft subsidiary in which Tencent holds 26.32 percent. Ubisoft has not commented, so the project is unconfirmed. Insider Gaming itself expects an official announcement to take several more years.", "ursprungsquelle": "Insider Gaming (Tom Henderson), anonymous sources", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp"], "_src": "84094430"}, "2026-11-13-word-kompatibilitaet-layout": {"titel": "Microsoft removes old compatibility options from Word, older documents may lose their layout from December", "schlagzeile": "Word will break the layout of old documents from December – how to save them", "kurz": "Microsoft is removing some old compatibility settings from Word. Documents saved with Word 2010 or older may then break lines differently. On Windows the change starts in December 2026, on Mac in early 2027.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft is cleaning up Word and removing some older compatibility options. heise reports this, citing Message Center notice MC1551147. Affected are documents that were created or last saved in Word 2010 or earlier and use these settings. In such files, text may wrap differently in the future. Spacing and page numbers can change, and images and shapes can slip onto another page. Microsoft does not say exactly which options will be removed. Compatibility mode itself remains. On Windows the change rolls out during December 2026, on Mac in early 2027. Microsoft does not mention any way to postpone it. Anyone who relies on the exact layout should check important old documents beforehand and export them as PDF. According to heise, converting to the new Word format does not help, because the old compatibility settings are also lost in the process.", "weitere_links": ["Neowin"], "_src": "9f271045"}, "2026-11-13-ps5-qssr-sechs-spiele": {"titel": "Sony's AI upscaling QSSR comes to six more games on the standard PS5, including Spider-Man 2 and Arc Raiders", "schlagzeile": "AI upscaling for the standard PS5: six games get sharper", "kurz": "Sony's AI upscaler QSSR is coming to six more PS5 games, including Marvel's Spider-Man 2, Control Resonant and Arc Raiders. QSSR is based on the PS5 Pro's PSSR but runs on the standard PS5. Spider-Man 2 has already received the update.", "zusammenfassung": "Sony is bringing its AI upscaling Quick Spectral Super Resolution, QSSR for short, to more games on the standard PS5. Confirmed are Marvel's Spider-Man 2, Control Resonant, The Finals, ARC Raiders, No Man's Sky and Hell Let Loose: Vietnam. According to PlayStation on X, Spider-Man 2 starts today; VGC reports the others as updated or coming shortly. QSSR is built on the same foundation as the PS5 Pro's PSSR. The first games with QSSR were Marvel's Wolverine and Ghost of Yōtei. Insomniac promises a more stable and sharper image in both the fidelity and performance modes of Spider-Man 2. Remedy speaks of noticeably better image stability and finer detail in Control Resonant. The studios behind Arc Raiders, No Man's Sky and Hell Let Loose: Vietnam also cite a sharper, cleaner image. Digital Foundry had called the technology's potential remarkable, precisely because many games of this generation struggle with low resolution and weak upscaling. The studios give no measurements of frame rate or resolution. Whether QSSR costs performance is therefore still open.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation on X", "Insider Gaming"], "_src": "010812aa"}, "2026-11-13-gta6-day-one-patch-macca": {"titel": "GTA 6 one week before release: first update 1.002 rolls out, first teaser for the in-game cartoon series Macca & Friends", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: First update before release – and its own cartoon series", "kurz": "One week before launch, Rockstar is rolling out a first update for GTA 6 of around 1 GB, without patch notes. There is also a first look at Macca & Friends, a cartoon series that runs in the game. According to the Guardian, almost 5,000 people worked on GTA 6.", "zusammenfassung": "Shortly before its release on November 19, GTA 6 is already getting its first update. According to Polygon, some players received a notification on Friday about version 1.002, which is around one gigabyte in size. Rockstar has not published any patch notes, presumably also to avoid spoilers. The update apparently rolls out in stages, so not everyone sees it immediately. According to Polygon, further updates before launch are possible. In addition, the X account DiscussingFilm released a first teaser for Macca & Friends, a series Rockstar produced for the game, IGN reports. The cartoon about Macca the alligator and his friends airs in the game on the Weazel channel. According to the New York Times, Rob Nelson, one of the studio heads of Rockstar North, needed around 80 hours for one playthrough. According to a Guardian report summarized by Golem, almost 5,000 people were involved in development. How many of them were external contractors is not known. According to Bloomberg, Rockstar now has 4,711 employees at twelve locations. GTA 6 is coming to PS5 and Xbox Series X/S; a PC version has not been announced.", "weitere_links": ["IGN", "Golem.de"], "_src": "eed94cb0"}, "2026-11-13-gow-sons-of-sparta-ps4": {"titel": "God of War: Sons of Sparta launches on PS4 on November 16 and gets two new game modes", "schlagzeile": "God of War: Sons of Sparta comes to PS4 – with two new modes", "kurz": "The 2D spin-off God of War: Sons of Sparta is also coming to PS4 on November 16. At the same time, PS4 and PS5 get two new modes via a free update: a speedrun mode and a mode in which every hit is fatal.", "zusammenfassung": "Sony is bringing God of War: Sons of Sparta to another platform. The 2D action platformer launches for PlayStation 4 on November 16 at midnight local time, PlayStation confirmed on X. At the same time, a free update with two new modes arrives for the PS4 and PS5 versions. Hermes Mode is a speedrun mode with a split timer and a persistent leaderboard. It is unlocked after finishing the game or via a code in the start menu, VGC reports. In Erebus Mode, a single hit is enough to take down Kratos and his enemies alike. This mode is selected when starting a new game. Sons of Sparta was developed by Mega Cat Studios together with Santa Monica Studio and was released for PS5 in February. The game tells a canonical story from Kratos' youth during his training in Sparta with his brother Deimos. The report does not mention a price for the PS4 version.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation on X", "Polygon"], "_src": "2fba3bd2"}, "2026-11-13-tsmc-mitarbeiterdaten-leak": {"titel": "TSMC confirms data leak: employee data appears online, reportedly offered for three bitcoin", "schlagzeile": "TSMC data leak: employee data reportedly up for sale for three bitcoin", "kurz": "In a mandatory filing with the US Securities and Exchange Commission, TSMC confirmed that data of current and former employees appeared on an external website without authorization. According to TSMC, the data came from services of a cloud provider and its own systems were not compromised. TSMC says customer data is not affected.", "zusammenfassung": "The world's largest contract chipmaker has confirmed a data leak. In a Form 6-K filing with the US SEC, TSMC writes that data of current and former employees was made available on an external website without authorization. According to Seeking Alpha, cited by PC Gamer, it involves more than 46,000 records. TSMC says the data matches information stored with an unnamed cloud service provider. There is no evidence of a breach of its own systems. Those affected have been informed, and the company is working with the cloud provider, investigating authorities and an external security firm. Taiwan's United Daily News reports that hackers offered 6.9 GB of data on an underground forum for three bitcoin. A published sample allegedly contains national ID numbers, addresses and bank details, among other things; TSMC has not confirmed this. According to TSMC, the data has nothing to do with its operations or customer information. Based on what is known so far, chip designs or customer data of companies such as Nvidia, AMD or Apple are therefore not affected. TSMC already made headlines in 2023 through a hacked supplier.", "_src": "581609d8"}, "2026-11-13-intel-desktop-marktanteil": {"titel": "Mercury Research: Intel wins back around five percentage points of desktop market share from AMD in Q3 2026", "schlagzeile": "Surprise: Intel takes desktop CPU market share from AMD", "kurz": "According to Mercury Research, AMD's share of desktop processors fell from around 35 to 29.9 percent in the third quarter of 2026. The analysts suspect that Intel diverted more chips to the desktop market. AMD may also be suffering from the weak gaming PC market.", "zusammenfassung": "Intel gained significant ground in desktop processors in the third quarter of 2026. According to new figures from Mercury Research reported by PC Gamer, AMD's desktop share fell from around 35 percent in the second quarter to 29.9 percent. That is a drop of about five percentage points within three months. Mercury Research itself is not entirely sure why. The analysts suspect that weak notebook demand allowed Intel to steer more chips into the desktop market, which is seasonally stronger in the third quarter. AMD, on the other hand, showed no seasonal growth. As a second reason, Mercury cites AMD's greater dependence on the gaming market, which suffers from scarce and expensive graphics cards. On top of that, high prices for RAM and SSDs are keeping many people from buying a new PC. Intel is strongly represented among PC makers, who also build cheap systems on older DDR4 platforms. PC Gamer stresses that this is not a sign of a healthy market: both manufacturers reportedly shipped more than ten percent fewer notebook chips in the third quarter. In gaming performance, AMD remains ahead with its X3D models.", "_src": "abc6b821"}, "2026-11-13-huang-kongress-anhoerung": {"titel": "US Congress summons ex-Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang under threat of subpoena, Trump suggests Tim Cook as successor", "schlagzeile": "Congress threatens Huang with subpoena – Trump wants Tim Cook as Nvidia CEO", "kurz": "Three US House committees want to question Jensen Huang in early December and threaten a subpoena if he does not appear. He is also set to testify publicly before the Senate Banking Committee. Meanwhile, US President Trump recommends Apple's Tim Cook as Nvidia's new CEO.", "zusammenfassung": "The pressure on Nvidia's departed founder Jensen Huang keeps growing. According to PC Gamer, the chairmen of three US House committees have called Huang and Nvidia's general counsel Tim Teter to closed-door transcribed interviews on December 1 and 2. If they do not appear, a subpoena is threatened. The topics are alleged AI chip smuggling, the use of Nvidia products by adversary militaries and reports of interference with US export controls, including around the Singapore company MegaSpeed. An earlier letter sent before Huang's resignation was worded much more politely. In addition, Senator Tim Scott has invited Huang to a public hearing of the Senate Banking Committee on December 3, along with Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick. According to the BBC, cited by PC Gamer, Huang is willing to appear before Congress. At the same time, US President Donald Trump named his preferred successor on Truth Social: Tim Cook, who was Apple's CEO until September and is now executive chairman, Golem reports. The decision, however, rests with Nvidia's board, which wants to consider internal and external candidates. Until then, CFO Colette Kress is leading the company on an interim basis. Whether Cook is interested at all is not known.", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de"], "_src": "210eda80"}, "2026-11-13-november-patch-druck-aktivierung": {"titel": "Microsoft confirms: November Windows updates cause printing failures and activation problems", "schlagzeile": "November Windows patch: printing and activation cause trouble", "kurz": "Microsoft has confirmed two new problems with the November security updates. Documents with invisible images sometimes cannot be printed, and certain activation commands fail with error 0x80041008. A fix for activation is due in the coming days.", "zusammenfassung": "The November Patch Tuesday is causing more problems. According to BleepingComputer, Microsoft has confirmed that printing can fail after the updates. Affected are documents with images that have a height or width of zero at the selected print resolution. Such invisible images are found, for example, in watermarks or layout anchors of Word documents. The problem mainly affects printing via the Windows graphics interface GDI, on Windows 10 and later and Windows Server 2016 and later. In addition, activation commands via the slmgr.vbs tool fail with error 0x80041008. This mainly affects companies that automate activation and KMS servers. According to Microsoft, devices that are already activated stay activated. A fix is due in the coming days; until then, only business support can help. The report does not yet give a date for the printing problem. This week, Microsoft also confirmed that the November updates do not install on systems with the October preview update. Home users are mainly affected by the printing bug.", "weitere_links": ["BleepingComputer (activation)"], "_src": "5b5d312a"}, "2026-11-13-xbox-25-konsole-ausverkauft": {"titel": "25th anniversary Xbox Series X sells out in seconds, scalpers ask up to 2,500 dollars", "schlagzeile": "Anniversary Xbox gone in seconds – scalpers ask up to 2,500 dollars", "kurz": "The translucent green 25th anniversary Xbox Series X sold out within seconds in the Microsoft Store. Fans are angry about the small quantity and the lack of protection against bots. According to IGN, consoles have already sold on eBay for 1,500 to 2,500 dollars.", "zusammenfassung": "The launch of the limited Xbox Series X for the brand's 25th birthday went wrong for many fans. According to IGN, the console was gone within seconds in the Microsoft Store. Microsoft had announced in advance only a limited quantity that varies by market and retailer. The console normally costs 999 dollars. According to IGN, GameStop temporarily offered its allocation for 4,950 dollars; that is now sold out too. On eBay, IGN found dozens of copies already sold for 1,500 to 2,500 dollars. Fans mainly criticize that Microsoft introduced neither a queue nor a restriction to genuine Xbox accounts. Some report that their shopping cart simply disappeared during checkout. Xbox CEO Asha Sharma said in October that demand for consoles was greater than supply. Whether Microsoft will restock is not known. The report does not mention prices or availability in Europe.", "_src": "b36d434d"}, "2026-11-13-gdc-ps6-helix-ki": {"titel": "GDC survey: 10 percent of developers already work on PS6 games, 8 percent on Project Helix, 40 percent use generative AI", "schlagzeile": "Already in the works: one in ten developers is making a PS6 game", "kurz": "In the GDC survey, 10 percent of developers with an active project say their game is planned for the next PlayStation. 8 percent name Microsoft's Project Helix. In addition, 40 percent use generative AI, but 55 percent consider it harmful.", "zusammenfassung": "The new State of the Game Industry report from the Game Developers Conference shows that the next console generation is already in the works. According to Golem, 10 percent of respondents with an active project say their game is planned for Sony's upcoming PlayStation. 8 percent name Microsoft's next Xbox, codenamed Project Helix. Multiple answers were possible, so it is unclear how many different games this means. The most important platform remains PC at 81 percent, followed by PS5 at 45 and Xbox Series X/S at 37 percent. Steam Deck reaches 32, Switch 2 29 and Valve's Steam Machine 21 percent. The second big topic is AI: according to Eurogamer, 40 percent of respondents use generative AI at work, four percentage points more than last year. At the same time, 55 percent say AI is harming the games industry. In AAA studios, 27 percent feel pushed or encouraged to use AI, compared to only 9 percent of indie developers. For the number of respondents, Golem cites more than 2,600 and Eurogamer more than 2,300. The layoff figures from the same survey were already in the ticker yesterday.", "weitere_links": ["Eurogamer"], "_src": "bdc4eaf1"}, "2026-11-13-microsoft-365-grossstoerung": {"titel": "Major Microsoft 365 outage: Outlook, Exchange, Teams and Copilot disrupted for hours, recovery only gradual", "schlagzeile": "Outlook and Teams down: Microsoft 365 battles a major outage", "kurz": "Since Thursday evening, Microsoft 365 has been massively disrupted worldwide, affecting Outlook, Exchange Online, Teams and Copilot among others. According to Microsoft, numerous servers unexpectedly went down, and it was not a cyberattack. As of Friday morning, Microsoft's status page still shows a service degradation; a sustained recovery has not yet been reached.", "zusammenfassung": "On Thursday, November 12, one of the biggest Microsoft 365 outages in recent times occurred. According to BleepingComputer, the incident with the ID MO1550821 began at 1:26 pm US Eastern Time, which is the evening in Central Europe. Affected were Exchange Online and Outlook, Teams, SharePoint Online, Microsoft 365 Copilot and Defender XDR, among others, in all regions. Microsoft cites a number of servers that unexpectedly became unavailable and thus overloaded the remaining infrastructure. The company halted all deployments, redistributed traffic and restarted servers. According to Neowin, initial countermeasures did not work as hoped, with a core process on the affected servers being overwhelmed. Microsoft executive Charles Lamanna apologized and said there was no indication of an attack. Overnight Microsoft reported a slow recovery, but as of Friday morning the official status page still shows a service degradation; Microsoft speaks only of partial success, and a sustained recovery has not yet been reached. Business customers can request an SLA credit via the Microsoft 365 admin center, according to Windows Latest. Whether and how much money comes back depends on the actual number of affected users and the duration. Private Outlook.com users generally have no claim.", "weitere_links": ["Neowin", "heise online", "Golem.de", "Windows Latest (SLA credit)"], "_src": "e59ef834"}, "2026-11-13-nvidia-doj-ermittlungen": {"titel": "Reports: US Justice Department investigates Nvidia, Supermicro and Megaspeed after Huang's resignation", "schlagzeile": "After Huang's exit: US Justice Department reportedly opens Nvidia probes", "kurz": "According to Semafor, several divisions of the US Justice Department have opened investigations involving Nvidia, Supermicro and Megaspeed. At the core are AI accelerators allegedly delivered to China. So far there are no signs of charges against Nvidia or ex-CEO Jensen Huang.", "zusammenfassung": "One day after Jensen Huang's resignation, things are not getting quieter for Nvidia. According to heise, Semafor reports, citing two government officials, that various divisions of the US Justice Department have opened investigations. They reportedly concern Nvidia, the server maker Supermicro and the Singapore-based company Megaspeed. Megaspeed is accused of delivering Nvidia AI accelerators to China despite US export restrictions. The focus is said to be the role of a former senior Megaspeed employee with whom Huang allegedly had a relationship. According to heise, there are so far no signs that the department will bring charges against Nvidia or Huang. Nvidia and the Justice Department declined to comment. Supermicro said Megaspeed has never been a customer and pledged to cooperate with the authorities. In addition, Reuters reports a further relationship between Huang and an Nvidia employee. For buyers of GeForce cards there are no known consequences for now. Nvidia presents its quarterly results on November 17, where the topic is likely to come up.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware (quarterly results on Nov 17)"], "_src": "3049650e"}, "2026-11-13-codex-radeon-r600-fix": {"titel": "With help from OpenAI Codex: nearly 20-year-old video decoder bug on Radeon HD 2000/3000 cards fixed under Linux", "schlagzeile": "AI finds ancient Radeon bug: fix for HD 2000/3000 coming in Linux 7.5", "kurz": "A hobby developer used OpenAI Codex to find and fix a video bug on nearly 20-year-old Radeon GPUs from the R600 era. The patch keeps video data in VRAM and lands in Linux 7.5. AMD has not maintained these cards for years.", "zusammenfassung": "Among the AMD graphics driver patches for Linux 7.5 is an unusual fix, according to Phoronix. It concerns the UVD video decoder of R600-generation Radeon cards, i.e. the Radeon HD 2000 and 3000 from almost 20 years ago. Developer Ted Bullock noticed corrupted video frames on an old iMac with an RV610 chip. The errors occurred when the decoder read compressed video data from system memory while the GPU was drawing at the same time. With the data in video memory, videos played cleanly. His patch therefore keeps the UVD buffers in VRAM for the RV610, RV620, RV630, RV635 and RV670 chips. He only tested on his own hardware, confirmation for the other chips is still missing. Bullock openly writes that he used OpenAI Codex for the analysis, testing and patch. The patch was accepted and comes with Linux 7.5. The merge window for it opens around the turn of the year.", "_src": "f0dd1006"}, "2026-11-13-windhawk-patchday-fix": {"titel": "November Patch Tuesday breaks Windhawk mods, developer delivers workaround", "schlagzeile": "Patch Tuesday breaks Windhawk mods – here's how to fix them", "kurz": "After the November update KB5132061, many mods of the customization tool Windhawk no longer work, especially for the taskbar and Explorer. The cause is missing debug symbols from Microsoft. The developer has released a workaround, just turn the mods off and on again.", "zusammenfassung": "Windhawk is a popular tool for customizing Windows with mods, for example the taskbar or File Explorer. Since the November Patch Tuesday, users have reported to Neowin that their mods no longer load. The problem appeared in a GitHub issue on November 10, shortly after update KB5132061, and affects Windows 11 and Windows 10. Windhawk developer Michael Maltsev confirmed the bug. The cause is that Microsoft has not published some debug symbols for the new Windows versions. Windhawk needs these symbols to find the places in the system a mod changes. According to Maltsev, this is not the first time Microsoft has provided symbols late or not at all. As a fix there is a manual mapping via Windhawk's symbol cache, which gets most affected mods working again. It is already included in the online cache. If you still have problems, disable and re-enable the affected mods in Windhawk.", "_src": "ea0f7eeb"}, "2026-11-13-wolfenstein-3-offiziell": {"titel": "Xbox confirms: Wolfenstein 3 is officially in production at MachineGames", "schlagzeile": "Finally official: Wolfenstein 3 is in the works at MachineGames", "kurz": "At its FanFest for the 25th anniversary, Xbox confirmed that Wolfenstein 3 is in production at MachineGames. The actors behind B.J. Blazkowicz and Grace Walker are back. There is no release date or platform list yet.", "zusammenfassung": "It was rumored for a long time, now it is official: Wolfenstein 3 is in production. Xbox CEO Asha Sharma confirmed the project on X as part of the Xbox FanFest in Seattle. It is once again being developed by the Swedish studio MachineGames, which most recently made Indiana Jones and the Great Circle. MachineGames showed a page from the script with the line \"His reputation precedes him\". A photo from the motion capture studio shows Brian Bloom and Debra Wilson, who once again play B.J. Blazkowicz and Grace Walker. The predecessor Wolfenstein 2: The New Colossus was released in 2017. Studio head Jerk Gustafsson had said before that B.J.'s story was always planned as a trilogy. Xbox has not yet announced a trailer, release date or platforms. A Wolfenstein series is also in the works at Amazon.", "weitere_links": ["IGN Deutschland", "Asha Sharma on X"], "_src": "28db60dc"}, "2026-11-13-pocketpair-gta6-urlaub": {"titel": "Palworld studio Pocketpair sends its staff on a \"business trip to Vice City\" for the GTA 6 launch", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 fever: Palworld studio gives everyone time off for launch", "kurz": "Palworld studio Pocketpair is giving all employees who want to play GTA 6 time off during launch week. Officially, it is called an \"urgent business trip to Vice City\". Logitech and other companies are also giving time off for the launch.", "zusammenfassung": "GTA 6 launches on November 19 for consoles, and some companies are already planning around it. Japanese studio Pocketpair, known for Palworld, published a tongue-in-cheek notice on X. All employees who want to play GTA 6 are released from their duties from November 19 to 23 and encouraged to take a \"business trip to Vice City\". Since the period includes a weekend, it effectively amounts to three days off. Pocketpair stresses that the updates for Palworld and Craftopia will still arrive as planned. According to PC Gamer, the studio is not alone: Logitech is giving its roughly 7,000 employees November 19 off as \"Logi Game Day\", with any game allowed. US performance parts maker Burger Motorsports and Canadian truck maker Edison Motors have also announced days off for the launch. Rockstar still has not dated a PC version of GTA 6.", "_src": "ba5c4541"}, "2026-11-13-og-xbox-pc-21-spiele": {"titel": "Xbox brings 21 more original Xbox games to PC, four classics get achievements for the first time", "schlagzeile": "KOTOR, Morrowind & co.: 21 original Xbox classics now run on PC", "kurz": "Via backward compatibility on PC, 21 more original Xbox games now run, for a total of 25. They include Morrowind, both KOTOR games and TimeSplitters 2. Four games get achievements for the first time.", "zusammenfassung": "Four months after the launch of backward compatibility for original Xbox games on PC, Microsoft is adding more. 21 more titles have been added, bringing the PC catalog to 25 games. According to VGC and Thurrott, they include The Elder Scrolls III: Morrowind, Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic I and II, Jedi Academy, Jedi Outcast, TimeSplitters 2 and Crimson Skies. Morrowind and Grabbed by the Ghoulies are also included in Game Pass. For the first time there are achievements for four classics: both KOTOR games, Blinx: The Time Sweeper and Conker: Live and Reloaded. According to Xbox, they can be unlocked on PC and on console. Xbox vice president Jason Ronald also writes that the first four games now run more stably and faster, and all titles support mouse and keyboard. More games are to follow. The announcement is part of the Xbox FanFest around the 25th anniversary on November 15.", "weitere_links": ["Thurrott.com", "Xbox on X"], "_src": "92b056c0"}, "2026-11-13-geforce-621-24": {"titel": "Nvidia GeForce 621.24 WHQL: Game Ready for Dawn of War 4 and Assetto Corsa Rally, preparation for DLSS 5 in Where Winds Meet", "schlagzeile": "GeForce 621.24: new driver for Dawn of War 4 and DLSS 5", "kurz": "Nvidia has released GeForce driver 621.24 WHQL, just eight days after 621.14. It is Game Ready for Dawn of War 4 and Assetto Corsa Rally and prepares DLSS 5 in Where Winds Meet. Only two bugs are fixed, mainly affecting professional and video applications.", "zusammenfassung": "With GeForce 621.24 WHQL, Nvidia delivers its fourth driver within 22 days. According to PCGH, the focus is Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War 4, which launches on December 3, with Commander Edition buyers able to play from November 30. Assetto Corsa Rally is also optimized, and the rally sim is due to get an update with DLSS 4.5 and Dynamic Multi Frame Generation on November 19. This frame generation requires a GeForce RTX 5000. On November 23, Where Winds Meet is due to get DLSS 5 with new neural rendering, according to PCGH only for Blackwell cards and RTX Spark systems. Two bugs were fixed: the OptiX denoiser in Chaos Vantage could fail at high resolutions, and H.265 videos from DJI in the D-Log profile were shown with wrong colors in Windows apps. The release notes list no open issues at launch. CUDA 13.5 is also new. Supported are desktop cards from the GTX 1630 to the RTX 5090, Pascal and Maxwell are no longer included. If you don't play any of the games mentioned, there is no need to update immediately.", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp"], "_src": "ba5b256f"}, "2026-11-13-amd-china-gpu-kuerzung": {"titel": "Report: AMD is said to have cut gaming GPU shipments in China by 20 to 50 percent since October", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is AMD cutting Radeon supply in China by up to 50%?", "kurz": "AMD is said to have cut its gaming GPU shipments to board partners in China by 20 to 50 percent since October. That is what the Chinese forum Board Channels reports, adding that the shortage should last until January. AMD has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "According to a November 12 post on the Chinese industry forum Board Channels, AMD has significantly reduced the number of gaming graphics chips for its board partners in China since the start of the fourth quarter. The post speaks of at least 20 to 50 percent less, with monthly allocations said to keep shrinking. The situation is said to be as tight as at Nvidia now. The source expects supply to remain very tight until January. Radeon prices in China are said to rise every quarter, attributed to higher memory and GPU costs. AMD is reportedly raising the price of its GPU and GDDR6 kits again this month, after an increase in October. TechPowerUp points out that the report gives no concrete unit numbers, affected models or reasons. It also only concerns China, and whether Europe or the US will see similar cuts is open. AMD has not commented on the report. The information is unconfirmed and should be seen as a hint about the market situation, not as fact.", "_src": "96b17733"}, "2026-11-13-fable-gameplay-4-minuten": {"titel": "Xbox shows four minutes of new Fable gameplay, release on February 23, 2027", "schlagzeile": "Four minutes of new Fable: combat, magic and a dark forest", "kurz": "Xbox has released four minutes of new gameplay from Playground Games' Fable reboot. It shows melee, ranged combat and magic, captured on PC at ultra settings. Fable launches on February 23, 2027 for Xbox Series X|S, PS5 and PC.", "zusammenfassung": "For the 25th Xbox anniversary, Xbox CEO Asha Sharma shared a new gameplay video for Fable. According to IGN, the four minutes mainly show combat with swords, ranged weapons and magic. It was captured on PC with ultra graphics settings. Story-wise, the Hero of Briar Hill and a local hero investigate strange magical incidents in the Deepwood forest. The game is developed by Playground Games, known for the Forza Horizon series. Fable was originally planned for this fall and was delayed to February 23, 2027. It is coming to Xbox Series X|S, PS5 and PC and can already be pre-purchased on Steam. Reactions are mixed: PC Gamer finds the video dark and rather conventional, with little of the colorful, quirky Fable series about it. In the YouTube comments, however, the response was mostly positive. A short clip naturally shows only a small slice of the game.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "Asha Sharma on X"], "_src": "083ecad5"}, "2026-11-13-id-software-neues-spiel": {"titel": "id Software confirms new game directed by Hugo Martin, Doom: The Dark Ages gets Slaughter Mode", "schlagzeile": "Doom maker id Software is already working on its next game", "kurz": "id Software is working on a new game, once again led by game director Hugo Martin. Which franchise it will be is open. Before that, Doom: The Dark Ages gets a free Slaughter Mode on November 16 for owners of the Revelations expansion.", "zusammenfassung": "Xbox CEO Asha Sharma confirmed during the Xbox FanFest that id Software is already working on its next game. The studio itself wrote on X that the project is being made by its teams in Texas and Frankfurt, with Hugo Martin once again as game director. Martin was creative director on Doom (2016) and Doom Eternal and game director of Doom: The Dark Ages. Whether it will be a new Doom, a Quake or something else entirely, id is not saying. According to id it will be some time before there is more to show, so the project is probably still at an early stage. VGC recalls that id Software was recently hit hard by the Xbox layoffs, with 136 people losing their jobs in total. Before that, Slaughter Mode for Doom: The Dark Ages arrives on November 16. The endless single-player mode is a free update for everyone who owns the Revelations expansion.", "weitere_links": ["VGC", "PC Gamer", "Asha Sharma on X"], "_src": "1b3eaa23"}, "2026-11-13-cmp170hx-80gb-hack": {"titel": "Hardware hack: Nvidia's CMP 170HX mining card can be unlocked to 80 GB HBM2e and up to 126 SMs", "schlagzeile": "From 8 to 80 GB: hack turns Nvidia's mining card into an AI card", "kurz": "A developer has used a voltage trick to unlock the full 80 GB of HBM2e instead of 8 GB on Nvidia's old CMP 170HX mining card. Up to 126 instead of 70 compute units could also be enabled. The mod requires soldering, is permanent and can destroy the card.", "zusammenfassung": "Nvidia sold the CMP 170HX in 2021 as a pure Ethereum accelerator, but inside it uses the same GA100 chip as the A100 data center card. Out of the box only 8 GB of the 80 GB HBM2e actually installed are usable, along with 70 of 128 streaming multiprocessors. The software tool cmpunlocker has been able to unlock up to 64 GB since the summer. A developer named Kate goes further with a hardware hack published on November 10: a small add-on board with an STM32 microcontroller creates targeted voltage dips and gets the eFuse controller to accept locked settings again. According to ComputerBase, nine of ten tested cards then delivered the full 80 GB, one reached 64 GB. Depending on the sample, 120 to 126 SMs also became active. In an OpenCL FP16 test the modified card reached 85.9 TFLOPS, ahead of a regular A100 at 72.5 TFLOPS. According to ComputerBase, this figure cannot be transferred directly to real AI applications. PCIe 4.0 x16 and NVLink can reportedly also be unlocked with additional tweaks. The catch: the mod requires soldering and, according to the developer, between one and 48 hours of attempts. The eFuse changes are permanent, and a mistake can render the card unusable. There is no guarantee that other samples have as much working hardware.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware"], "_src": "d1af15c7"}, "2026-11-13-game-awards-disney-plus": {"titel": "The Game Awards 2026 will also stream on Disney+ for the first time", "schlagzeile": "The Game Awards 2026 will also stream on Disney+ for the first time", "kurz": "The Game Awards 2026 will be broadcast on Disney+ for the first time. Twitch, YouTube and other platforms remain on board, and the show takes place on December 10 in Los Angeles.", "zusammenfassung": "The Game Awards have a new partner this year: according to IGN, the show will stream on Disney+ for the first time. It will also run as usual on Twitch and YouTube and on Steam, TikTok, X, Facebook and Kick, among others. The ceremony takes place on Thursday, December 10, at the Peacock Theater in Los Angeles. It starts at 7:30 pm Eastern Time, which is 1:30 am on December 11 in Central Europe. Geoff Keighley hosts again. According to Variety, Disney wants to use the partnership to promote its own games and animation projects. IGN counts Resident Evil Requiem, 007 First Light and the Ocarina of Time remake among the favorites. GTA 6 launches on November 19 and so just qualifies for this year's awards.", "_src": "862b9826"}, "2026-11-13-halo-ce-firefight": {"titel": "Halo: Campaign Evolved gets Firefight as a free update this winter", "schlagzeile": "Halo: Campaign Evolved gets a free Firefight mode", "kurz": "The Halo remake Campaign Evolved gets the Firefight mode as a free update this winter. Up to four players fight waves of enemies together. More details are due at Halo Fest in mid-December.", "zusammenfassung": "Xbox announced at its FanFest that Halo: Campaign Evolved is getting a Firefight mode. Firefight is a cooperative PvE mode for up to four players that has appeared in several Halo games. The update arrives for free sometime this winter, there is no exact date yet. According to VGC, FanFest attendees should already be able to try the mode on site. Xbox plans to share more details at Halo Fest on December 12 and 13. Halo: Campaign Evolved is a remake of the original Halo's campaign and was released in July. VGC points out that the smaller Halo Studios now only looks after existing Halo games following the Xbox layoffs. According to VGC, a new Halo is being made at Activision.", "weitere_links": ["Thurrott.com", "Asha Sharma on X"], "_src": "3a3814c4"}, "2026-11-12-amd-26-11-1-ssd-fix": {"titel": "AMD Adrenalin 26.11.1 fixes the constant writing to SSDs", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver 26.11.1: AMD finally stops the constant SSD writes", "kurz": "AMD has released the optional driver Adrenalin 26.11.1. It officially fixes the bug that made the driver constantly write data to the SSD in the background. However, the list of known issues has grown.", "zusammenfassung": "Radeon users had discovered that the Adrenalin driver constantly writes data to the drive in the background, even when idle. Heise warned that this can endanger SSD lifespan, and until now only a free community tool helped. Now, according to Wccftech and Neowin, AMD has released the optional driver 26.11.1, which is supposed to officially fix the problem. According to the release notes, owners of Radeon RX 7000 and RX 9000 were affected, and the bug also occurred when moving or resizing windows. The list of known issues includes nine new entries, mainly crashes and driver timeouts in certain games such as Cyberpunk 2077 and War Thunder. On RX 9000 cards, AMD also lists graphical artifacts in Phantom Blade Zero. Anyone affected by the SSD problem should install the update and can then remove the community tool.", "weitere_links": ["Neowin", "heise online"], "_src": "336a15b3"}, "2026-11-12-gdc-umfrage-entlassungen": {"titel": "GDC survey: one in three people surveyed in the games industry was laid off within two years", "schlagzeile": "GDC survey: one in three respondents in the games industry was laid off", "kurz": "In the new GDC survey of more than 2,600 industry professionals, 34 percent said they had been laid off in the past two years. More than half of them are still without a job. According to the survey, morale in the industry is poor.", "zusammenfassung": "The 15th edition of the GDC's State of the Game Industry survey questioned more than 2,600 industry professionals worldwide, VGC reports. 34 percent said they had been laid off in the past two years, and in the US as many as 39 percent. In the January survey, the figure was still 28 percent. Of those laid off, 54 percent are still unemployed, and 27 percent have submitted at least 100 job applications. 17 percent were even laid off twice in two years. Only 45 percent of those employed consider their job at least somewhat secure for the next twelve months. 81 percent are worried about their future in the industry.", "_src": "f0c14b73"}, "2026-11-12-steam-pruefstau-ki": {"titel": "Steam review backlog due to flood of AI games: more indie games have to be delayed", "schlagzeile": "Flood of AI games on Steam: indie games stuck in Valve's review queue", "kurz": "Valve's review of new games on Steam currently takes up to twelve days, according to developers because of a flood of low-quality AI games. Several indie titles have had to postpone their release. Valve has tightened its submission rules, but critics say that is not enough.", "zusammenfassung": "Since the beginning of November, developers have been complaining about long waiting times for Valve's approval of new games and builds on Steam. According to Eurogamer, Valve explained that reviews can take up to twelve days due to the number of submissions that need to be reviewed again. A flood of cheap games created with generative AI is seen as the cause. The tower defense game Australia Did It by Rami Ismail and Aesthetician Labs was supposed to launch on November 10 and is still waiting for approval. Amazing Slot Survivor also had to withdraw its November 13 date, and more indie games are affected. Valve has introduced stricter submission rules to weed out fully AI-generated games earlier. Ismail believes Valve cannot stay neutral on AI without harming genuine developers.", "_src": "5412161f"}, "2026-11-12-windows-signdrop-zero-day": {"titel": "SignDrop: new Windows zero-day grants SYSTEM privileges, no patch yet", "schlagzeile": "Windows zero-day SignDrop: SYSTEM privileges and no patch yet", "kurz": "A security researcher has published SignDrop, a new unpatched Windows flaw including an exploit. It is said to give attackers SYSTEM privileges and bypass the self-protection of antivirus software. According to the researcher, around 80 percent of Windows installations are affected.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, researcher Abdelhamid Naceri, known as Nightmare Eclipse, has published a new zero-day exploit for Windows. SignDrop abuses, of all things, a protection measure that Microsoft introduced in October 2025 for the Common Log File System driver (CLFS). Through a detour, privileged processes such as Windows Defender can be made to create files with SYSTEM privileges. According to Naceri, this can also be used to bypass the tamper protection of antivirus and EDR software. He tested Windows 11 26H2 and Windows Server 2025 and estimates that around 80 percent of installations are vulnerable. Systems where the registry value for the CLFS authentication mode is set to 0 or 1 are vulnerable. According to Naceri, there is no workaround, and users have to wait for a patch from Microsoft. The report does not mention a statement from Microsoft.", "_src": "d8efd221"}, "2026-11-12-gta6-karte-leak": {"titel": "GTA 6: printed map from the Collector's Edition reportedly leaked via a merch event", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is the GTA 6 map online a week before release?", "kurz": "Photos of a printed, stylized map of Leonida are circulating online, said to come from the GTA 6 Collector's Edition. The pictures reportedly come from a merch event at Selfridges in the UK. Rockstar has not commented, and the map is probably not an exact copy of the game world.", "zusammenfassung": "One week before the release of GTA 6 on November 19, photos of a map are appearing, according to VGC and Insider Gaming. They are said to show the printed map from the Collector's Edition and to come from a GTA 6 event at the department store chain Selfridges. According to VGC, the clearest image came from a now-deleted Instagram account, and another photo shows the map folded in a display case in Manchester. According to Insider Gaming, a Selfridges employee is said to be the source, but this has not been proven. The map shows Leonida in stylized form with counties and clipart-like motifs, such as monster trucks, a UFO and planes. Insider Gaming assumes that it does not accurately reflect the game world. Rockstar has not confirmed the images. Anyone who wants to avoid spoilers should be careful on social media.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming", "Polygon"], "_src": "a2e2106c"}, "2026-11-12-xbox-25-sharma-memo": {"titel": "25 years of Xbox: Asha Sharma hints at AI development in a memo, plus Halo Firefight and Xbox Playback", "schlagzeile": "25 years of Xbox: boss wants small teams to build huge worlds", "kurz": "For Xbox's 25th birthday, boss Asha Sharma has published a memo that sounds a lot like generative AI. Small teams are supposed to build worlds that today require hundreds of developers. Xbox also announced a Firefight mode for Halo: Campaign Evolved and the year-in-review feature Xbox Playback.", "zusammenfassung": "Xbox boss Asha Sharma has published a memo titled \"25 Years of Xbox\" for the 25th anniversary. At the end, she writes that too many ideas never become games and that this must change. Soon, a single person will have capabilities that once required entire nations, and small teams could build worlds that today demand hundreds of developers. According to Eurogamer, the term generative AI is not used, but the wording strongly suggests it. Sharma comes from Microsoft's AI division, but when she started as Xbox boss she said she had \"no tolerance for bad AI\". For the anniversary, she also announced on X a Firefight mode for Halo: Campaign Evolved, coming as a free update this winter; according to Insider Gaming, it is a four-player PvE mode. In addition, Xbox Playback is rolling out, a look back at your own games and achievements on Xbox. Xbox did not name any specific AI projects in the memo.", "weitere_links": ["IGN", "Insider Gaming", "Asha Sharma auf X (Halo Firefight)"], "_src": "0b7ff29f"}, "2026-11-12-gta6-suedkorea-freigabe": {"titel": "GTA 6 almost did not get an age rating in South Korea because of nude scenes", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 almost banned? South Korea argued for weeks over nude scenes", "kurz": "South Korea's rating board GCRB struggled for a long time to agree on a rating for GTA 6. The sticking point was nudity without sexual context. In the end, it received an adults-only rating by eight votes to one.", "zusammenfassung": "According to IGN Germany, Rockstar applied for an age rating in South Korea on September 1. The first vote of the GCRB rating board on September 10 ended in a tie: three members wanted to refuse a rating, three were in favor of adults only. According to meeting minutes obtained by InvenGlobal, some members objected to nude scenes without sexual context. The decision was postponed until a playable version was available, and several dates were pushed back. On October 18, the committee then decided on an adults-only rating by eight votes to one. A refusal would have completely prevented sales in South Korea. GTA 6 launches on November 19 for PS5 and Xbox Series X and S.", "weitere_links": ["Polygon"], "_src": "c47f9d24"}, "2026-11-12-nvidia-linux-nvroot-forgeptr": {"titel": "NvRoot and ForgePtr: two security flaws in Nvidia's Linux driver published, 25 more announced", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia Linux driver: flaw turns container processes into root", "kurz": "Security firm Stealthium has published two flaws in Nvidia's open Linux kernel modules. Through ForgePtr, a process in a GPU container can become root on the host. Patches are already available, and 25 more disclosures are to follow.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Phoronix, the first two of a total of 27 announced security flaws in Nvidia's driver stack are now public. ForgePtr (CVE-2026-47501) allows an unprivileged process in a GPU container to gain root privileges on the host. With NvRoot (CVE-2026-47591), the GPU can overwrite files that the operating system has marked as read-only. Both flaws have been in Nvidia's open kernel modules for around four years and are rated high (CVSS 7.8). Cloud providers that rent out GPUs to multiple customers are particularly affected. NvRoot is fixed with drivers 610.57.04, 595.91.07 and 580.178.04, and ForgePtr with 615.71.09. According to Phoronix, Stealthium has announced 25 more disclosures concerning Nvidia's AI software stack. Anyone using Nvidia GPUs on Linux, especially in containers, should update the driver.", "_src": "fa81fb4c"}, "2026-11-12-huang-ruecktritt-kress": {"titel": "Jensen Huang steps down as Nvidia CEO after 33 years, CFO Colette Kress takes over on an interim basis", "schlagzeile": "End of an era: Jensen Huang resigns from Nvidia", "kurz": "Nvidia has announced the resignation of co-founder and CEO Jensen Huang, who is leaving all his positions with immediate effect. CFO Colette Kress will lead the company as interim CEO for now. Harvey C. Jones takes over as chairman of the board.", "zusammenfassung": "After days of crisis, it is official: Jensen Huang is stepping down after 33 years at the helm of Nvidia. According to ComputerBase, he is giving up his roles as president, CEO and board member, and according to PC Gamer with immediate effect. Huang was not fired; according to TechPowerUp, he signed a letter of resignation. The trigger was reports of two extramarital relationships, including one with a manager who reported directly to him. Before that, the board had met in an unscheduled session, and according to Bloomberg an outside firm had already been hired for the search for a successor. CFO Colette Kress is running the business as interim CEO and remains CFO at the same time. Harvey C. Jones takes over as chairman of the board. Kress said she would build on the foundation Huang created over 33 years. The announcement does not say whether Huang will play any future role at the company. Who will become permanent CEO is open; so far there is only speculation. Any impact on GeForce products, prices or drivers is currently not known.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware", "TechPowerUp", "PC Gamer", "heise online"], "_src": "330d1f5e"}, "2026-11-12-paradox-wester-ruecktritt": {"titel": "Paradox CEO Frederik Wester steps down, Mattias Lilja takes over in January", "schlagzeile": "After the Bloodlines 2 flop: Paradox gets a new boss", "kurz": "Paradox Interactive CEO Frederik Wester is giving up his post and moving to the board. His deputy Mattias Lilja takes over on January 4, 2027. The publisher has several difficult years behind it.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Eurogamer, Frederik Wester is stepping down as CEO of Paradox Interactive and will focus on long-term development as a board member. His successor will be the current deputy CEO Mattias Lilja from January 4, 2027, and Wester will remain in office until then. Wester led Paradox from 2009 to 2018 and again since 2021. His second term saw the difficult development of Vampire: The Masquerade Bloodlines 2, whose commercial failure caused operating profit to drop sharply. On top of that came the cancellation of Life by You, the delay of Prison Architect 2 and the bumpy launch of Cities: Skylines 2, whose console version is still missing. Lilja wants to invest more in the core business and work more closely with players and modders. Next up are Lego Skylines and the strategy game Afterworld.", "_src": "b6ea62b9"}, "2026-11-12-siren-halo-gddr7": {"titel": "Rumor: AMD's Siren Halo is said to use GDDR7 graphics memory instead of only LPDDR5X", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Will AMD's mega APU Siren Halo get real GDDR7 memory?", "kurz": "According to a leaker, AMD's upcoming Halo APU Siren Halo will use GDDR7 memory. Current Halo chips use shared LPDDR5X memory for CPU and GPU. Nothing is confirmed.", "zusammenfassung": "Hardware leaker Gotou_kai3 claims that AMD's Siren Halo will get GDDR7 memory, Wccftech and PCGH report. Like Medusa Halo, Siren Halo is said to use Zen 6 and RDNA 5, but to be a true successor rather than a simple refresh. Current Halo chips such as Strix Halo use LPDDR5X as shared memory for CPU and GPU. GDDR7 would bring much more memory bandwidth, which could especially help the graphics unit in games. According to Wccftech, it is unclear whether CPU and GPU could both use both memory pools or whether GDDR7 would be reserved for graphics only. For AI workloads, a GDDR7-only graphics solution might be less flexible than the large shared memory of today's Ryzen AI Max chips. AMD has not announced Siren Halo, and dates and specifications are unknown.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "6fee7dbc"}, "2026-11-12-apache-http2-luecke": {"titel": "Critical flaw in Apache's HTTP/2 module: update to 2.4.71 recommended", "schlagzeile": "Critical Apache flaw: update web servers with HTTP/2 now", "kurz": "The Apache web server has a critical flaw in the mod_http2 module that could allow remote code execution. Only servers with HTTP/2 enabled are affected. Version 2.4.71 fixes the bug.", "zusammenfassung": "According to heise, the flaw CVE-2026-119618 is located in the assign_headers() function of the mod_http2 module. Memory manipulation there could lead to remote execution of malicious code. According to Golem, Red Hat rates the flaw 9.8 out of 10. It was found by an OSS scanner from Anthropic and two researchers from Google Cloud Vulnerability Research. Since mod_http2 is not enabled by default, only servers using HTTP/2 are affected. Experts such as Kevin Beaumont consider an exploit difficult because of protections such as ASLR. Still, admins should update to Apache 2.4.71, which closes two more flaws. Anyone who cannot update right away should disable HTTP/2 for now.", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de"], "_src": "8ac52b3f"}, "2026-11-12-rtx5090-96gb-mod": {"titel": "Modified RTX 5090 with 96 GB of memory shows up on a Chinese second-hand marketplace", "schlagzeile": "RTX 5090 with 96 GB: China mod listed for around 900,000 dollars", "kurz": "A modified GeForce RTX 5090 with 96 GB of video memory is being offered on the Chinese platform Xianyu. The placeholder price is around 900,000 US dollars, with the real price negotiated privately. Whether the card actually works has not been proven.", "zusammenfassung": "Chinese modders move desktop GPUs onto their own boards and multiply the memory for AI workloads. Now, according to Wccftech and PCGH, a listing has appeared for an RTX 5090 with 96 GB, as much memory as the RTX Pro 6000. It was spotted by repair specialist VIK-on on Alibaba's second-hand marketplace Xianyu, and VideoCardz reported it first. The GB202 chip sits on a custom board with Samsung memory chips on both sides. Besides the card, the seller also offers board schematics and a patched BIOS, but only targets business customers with a confidentiality agreement. The listed price of 6,488,888 yuan, around 900,000 US dollars, is a placeholder; the actual price is negotiated privately. There are no benchmarks, so the card's functionality is unconfirmed.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "4c5d0781"}, "2026-11-12-swtor-directx12-test": {"titel": "Star Wars: The Old Republic starts public DirectX 12 test, graphics deliberately reduced at first", "schlagzeile": "SWTOR gets DirectX 12 – and looks worse for now", "kurz": "Almost 15 years after release, Star Wars: The Old Republic is testing a DirectX 12 client. The public test starts this week directly in the regular launcher. Many graphics effects are deliberately missing at first.", "zusammenfassung": "According to PC Games, developer Broadsword is modernizing the technology of the MMORPG Star Wars: The Old Republic. A public test of the new DirectX 12 client starts this week, with no sign-up or access code required. In the regular launcher, a small arrow lets you choose between the old and the new version; both use the same live servers and characters. Many environmental details and effects are still missing or simplified in the new client, and graphics options are limited too. This is intentional: the focus is first on stability, performance and compatibility with as many PCs as possible. Players are asked to report stutters, graphical glitches and crashes along with their hardware. The test is not available for Mac players for now. According to Broadsword, the project will run well into 2027, after which the graphics are to be gradually brought back to at least the old level.", "_src": "b512307b"}, "2026-11-12-apex-neural-rendering": {"titel": "Apex Neural Rendering: start-up promises a vendor-independent alternative to DLSS, FSR and XeSS", "schlagzeile": "Better than DLSS? Apex brings frame generation to all three GPU camps", "kurz": "The company Apex Compute has unveiled Apex Neural Rendering (ANR), with super resolution, ray reconstruction and frame generation for GeForce, Radeon and Arc. Frame generation is available now as a free beta on GitHub. The promises are big, but ComputerBase finds them hard to verify.", "zusammenfassung": "Apex Compute, so far specialized in edge AI accelerators, wants to take on DLSS, FSR and XeSS with Apex Neural Rendering (ANR). ANR is supposed to offer super resolution, ray reconstruction and frame generation independently of the vendor on Nvidia, AMD and Intel. According to the company, it is up to 2.4 times faster and delivers better image quality than DLSS. Only frame generation is available so far, as a free beta on GitHub; it is integrated via OptiScaler and offers 2×, 3× and 4× modes. According to Apex, super resolution and ray reconstruction are still in development. According to ComputerBase, frame generation runs on GeForce GTX 16 and RTX 2000 and newer, on Radeon RX 5000 and newer including the Steam Deck, and on Intel Arc A, under Windows 10, Windows 11 and Linux with Proton. ComputerBase criticizes inconsistencies in the company's claims, such as alleged FSR measurements with more than one AI-generated frame, and unclear factors in the comparison videos. There are no independent tests yet, so the performance and quality claims are unconfirmed.", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp", "Wccftech", "GamingOnLinux"], "_src": "6efb8d9d"}, "2026-11-12-samsung-hbm-onyang": {"titel": "Memory shortage: Samsung builds a new HBM packaging line and wants to finish it a year early", "schlagzeile": "RAM crisis: Samsung pulls new HBM fab forward by a year", "kurz": "Samsung has started building a new line for HBM packaging in Onyang. It is set to start operating in June 2028, a year earlier than planned. The reason is the ongoing memory shortage.", "zusammenfassung": "According to ComputerBase, Samsung has broken ground on its Onyang campus in Asan for a new production line that will package HBM memory. Operations are set to start in June 2028, a year earlier than originally planned. Samsung is investing 46 trillion won, around 31 billion euros, in Onyang, most of it in equipment. Around 31,000 square meters of cleanroom on three floors and around 700 new jobs are planned. In October, Samsung said it had already negotiated HBM supply volumes for 2027 and could not come close to meeting demand. HBM is mainly used in AI accelerators, but the shortage weighs on the entire memory market and thus also on RAM prices for PC users. In the short term, the new line will not change prices.", "_src": "7ecef997"}, "2026-11-12-outlook-mails-blockiert": {"titel": "Outlook.com: faulty spam rule rejected genuine emails for days – the messages are lost", "schlagzeile": "Outlook rejected emails for days – and they're not coming back", "kurz": "A faulty Microsoft spam rule rejected legitimate emails to Outlook.com, Hotmail and Live addresses for days. Microsoft has rolled back the update, and senders and recipients do not need to change anything. Rejected emails cannot be recovered, however, so you have to ask senders to resend them.", "zusammenfassung": "If you recently had a suspiciously quiet Outlook.com inbox, you may have been affected. According to Windows Latest, legitimate emails to Outlook.com, Hotmail, Live and MSN addresses were rejected from at least November 5. Senders received error messages saying their emails lacked SPF, DKIM or DMARC records, although that was partly untrue. Microsoft confirmed to Windows Latest that an update to its spam rules was the cause. The company has rolled it back, and according to Windows Latest mail flow has been working again since November 9. Neither senders nor recipients need to change any settings. The problem: the rejected emails did not land in the spam folder but never arrived. Microsoft therefore cannot restore them. Anyone who was expecting important emails should ask the senders to send them again. Admins can find the incident in the Microsoft 365 admin center under the ID EX1545193. Microsoft does not say how many users were affected.", "_src": "74d3487f"}, "2026-11-12-powershell-signatur-kb5132061": {"titel": "November update KB5132061: stricter checks make some signed PowerShell scripts fail", "schlagzeile": "Windows update trips up signed PowerShell scripts – here's the fix", "kurz": "With the November security update, Windows checks the text encoding of signed PowerShell scripts more strictly. Scripts with faulty UTF-8 may then be treated as unsigned and no longer run as usual in managed environments. Microsoft recommends saving them as UTF-8 with BOM and signing them again.", "zusammenfassung": "With update KB5132061 of November 10, Microsoft has tightened the verification of PowerShell signatures. Until now, Windows could still process scripts with invalid UTF-8 by replacing faulty characters. That no longer happens, and affected files are rejected. According to Microsoft, Get-AuthenticodeSignature then reports \"NotSigned\" for a script that is actually signed. Set-AuthenticodeSignature can abort with an error. On devices with App Control for Business, affected scripts may only run in constrained language mode. Mainly affected are scripts with faulty UTF-8, UTF-8 without BOM on systems with a different code page, and files in encodings such as Shift-JIS. Microsoft recommends checking the scripts, saving them as valid UTF-8 with BOM and signing them again. A sample script called Repair-SignedPowerShellUtf8.ps1 finds affected files and does not overwrite any originals. According to Neowin, the change applies not only to Windows 11 but also to Windows 10 Enterprise LTSC 2021 and Windows Server 2025. Home users without signed scripts will usually not notice anything.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft Support (KB5132061)", "Microsoft Support (encoding guidance)"], "_src": "22fabd49"}, "2026-11-12-tomb-raider-catalyst-switch2": {"titel": "Amazon lists Tomb Raider: Catalyst for Nintendo Switch 2 as well", "schlagzeile": "Tomb Raider: Catalyst is apparently coming to Switch 2 too", "kurz": "A post on Amazon's official news site names Switch 2 as a platform for both upcoming Tomb Raider games. This was known for Legacy of Atlantis, but not for Catalyst so far. Amazon is the publisher of Catalyst, but confirmation from Crystal Dynamics or Nintendo is still missing.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Insider Gaming, a post on Amazon News updated on November 9 states that both new Tomb Raider games will be released for PS5, Xbox Series X/S, Nintendo Switch 2 and Steam. For Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis (2027), the Switch 2 version was already official, and the game can be pre-ordered on the eShop. What is new is the statement for Tomb Raider: Catalyst. The game was delayed to 2028 this year. Catalyst is published by Amazon Game Studios, which gives the statement weight. However, Insider Gaming considers an error in the article possible, even though it has been online unchanged for two days. Crystal Dynamics and Nintendo have not yet confirmed the Switch 2 version. There are no technical details or a date for the Switch 2 version.", "_src": "de9ab1dc"}, "2026-11-12-steam-erfolge-linux-64bit": {"titel": "Steam client update: Achievement Sets for everyone, and the Linux client finally runs as a 64-bit program", "schlagzeile": "Steam update: new achievement sets and 64-bit for Linux", "kurz": "Valve has released a new Steam update for all users. Games can now group achievements into sets for the base game and DLC without losing a 100 percent completion. On Linux, the Steam client is now a 64-bit program and runs in a Steam Runtime container.", "zusammenfassung": "On November 11, Valve released a Steam client update to the stable channel. The most important new feature for everyone is Steam Achievement Sets. Developers can use them to group achievements by base game and DLC. New achievements or DLC achievements thus no longer make an already completed achievement collection incomplete. Seasonal achievements or ones that can no longer be earned can be archived. There is also a redesigned achievements page. On Linux, the Steam client is now a 64-bit application and runs in a Steam Runtime container. According to Valve, this should ensure consistent behavior across different distributions; it is the same technology that games use. According to TechPowerUp, Steam on Linux was previously still a 32-bit program. The update also fixes, among other things, a crash when resuming from standby. Whether developers actually use the new achievement sets is up to them.", "weitere_links": ["Steam (Achievement Sets announcement)", "9to5Linux"], "_src": "95507831"}, "2026-11-12-witcher3-ki-stimme-geralt": {"titel": "The Witcher 3: CD Projekt adjusts Geralt's Polish voice with AI in the new expansion – with the actor's consent", "schlagzeile": "After a stroke: AI makes Geralt's Polish voice sound young again", "kurz": "In the upcoming Witcher 3 expansion Songs of the Past, Geralt's Polish voice is being reworked with AI. Voice actor Jacek Rozenek records all lines himself, but his voice has changed noticeably after a stroke in 2019. With his consent, AI company Respeecher matches it to how he used to sound.", "zusammenfassung": "CD Projekt Red has confirmed that it is using AI for the Polish version of the new Witcher 3 expansion Songs of the Past. Game File reported it first, and PC Gamer, VGC and IGN have picked it up. Jacek Rozenek has always voiced Geralt in Polish, but suffered a stroke in 2019 and was temporarily unable to speak. After long training he returned, but today his voice sounds deeper and rougher. Because the expansion takes place in the middle of The Witcher 3's story, the difference could have been noticeable. Rozenek therefore still records all lines himself, and Respeecher then adjusts them to how he sounded around twelve years ago. The model was trained on his earlier recordings for the game. Rozenek explicitly supports this and says the voice should be as close as possible to his voice back then. Localization producer Mikołaj Szwed calls it a special case because of the illness and sees it as an ethical use with consent. According to CD Projekt, nothing similar is planned for Doug Cockle's English voice. CD Projekt already worked with Respeecher on Cyberpunk 2077: Phantom Liberty, back then with the consent of a late voice actor's family. The reports do not give a release date for Songs of the Past.", "weitere_links": ["VGC", "IGN"], "_src": "b5c1fa87"}, "2026-11-12-helldivers2-kosmetik-mods": {"titel": "Helldivers 2: after anti-cheat switch and review wave, cosmetic mods should work again with the next hotfix", "schlagzeile": "Helldivers 2: Arrowhead wants to allow harmless mods again", "kurz": "Since the switch to Easy Anti-Cheat, many mods no longer work in Helldivers 2, and more than 10,000 negative reviews followed on Steam. Arrowhead announces that some purely cosmetic mods should work again with the next hotfix. Mods that change gameplay remain banned.", "zusammenfassung": "Arrowhead switched the anti-cheat system in Helldivers 2 from GameGuard to Easy Anti-Cheat. According to the studio, the goal was to stop mods that give unfair advantages or harm others. In the process, however, harmless cosmetic mods also stopped working. The reaction was fierce: according to PC Gamer, more than 10,000 new negative Steam reviews came in, and recent reviews stand at \"Mostly Negative\". In its new developer blog, Arrowhead admits that PC players have lost fan mods. After adjustments, some cosmetic mods should work again with the next hotfix. Mods that change gameplay remain banned because they are technically indistinguishable from cheats. Mods are still not officially supported. Arrowhead also apologizes for an inaccurate roadmap and missed patch dates. Planned for early December are, among other things, jetpacks that can be used while carrying two-handed items. The studio does not give a date for the hotfix.", "_src": "0f2f4919"}, "2026-11-12-marvel-1943-fast-fertig": {"titel": "Report: Marvel 1943: Rise of Hydra is said to be almost finished, but much smaller than planned", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Marvel 1943 almost done – but heavily cut down?", "kurz": "After rumors of a cancellation, Kotaku reports that Marvel 1943: Rise of Hydra is almost finished. However, the game is said to offer significantly less content and gameplay depth than planned. Skydance has not said anything official about it.", "zusammenfassung": "Marvel 1943: Rise of Hydra, Amy Hennig's Captain America and Black Panther game, was recently the subject of rumors about an imminent cancellation. According to Kotaku and Bloomberg reporter Jason Schreier, Skydance's leadership told employees via Slack that this is not true. Kotaku also reports that the game is \"close to done\", meaning almost finished. However, development is said to have been difficult and well over budget. As a result, scope and length are said to have been cut significantly. According to Kotaku's sources, the game is \"light on gameplay\", with much of it handled by a single button. Marvel 1943 reportedly started out as a Netflix game. It was announced in 2024 and has been delayed several times since. There is no release date. All details come from anonymous sources, and Skydance has not confirmed them.", "ursprungsquelle": "Kotaku (via IGN)", "_src": "3cff0819"}, "2026-11-12-nvidia-board-huang-abloesung": {"titel": "Reports: Nvidia's board is weighing the removal of CEO Jensen Huang and is already looking for a successor", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia facing a change at the top? Board weighs removing Huang", "kurz": "According to the Wall Street Journal, Nvidia's board is preparing to remove founder and CEO Jensen Huang. The trigger is a New York Times report about a second extramarital relationship, this time with a manager who reports directly to him. According to Bloomberg, an outside firm is already searching for successors. As of midday today, Nvidia still has not announced a decision; the reports rely on anonymous sources.", "zusammenfassung": "The crisis around Nvidia chief Jensen Huang is escalating. According to the Wall Street Journal, the board wanted to meet on Wednesday evening (US time) to discuss Huang's future, with a removal on the table. The trigger is a new New York Times report: besides the affair he has already admitted, Huang is said to have had a relationship with a vice president who reports directly to him. The paper cites five former employees and says it has not seen an alleged video of an incident in March itself. Neither Nvidia nor those involved have confirmed the report. According to Bloomberg, the board is already working with an outside firm to find a successor, and an interim CEO is also being considered. The background is the investigation running since Sunday into Huang's affair with a manager at Nvidia customer Megaspeed, who US authorities are said to have classified as a suspected Chinese agent; China denies this. Huang has led Nvidia since its founding in 1993, and according to PCGH there is no named successor. According to PCGH, a simple majority of the directors is enough to remove him. After the reports, the stock lost around eight percent in after-hours trading and fell to a 52-week low. Nvidia reports quarterly results on November 17, and a confidential briefing in the US Congress is planned for November 18. No concrete effects on GeForce cards, prices or drivers are known so far. Important: everything is based on media reports with anonymous sources from the Wall Street Journal, the New York Times and Bloomberg; as of midday today, Nvidia has not announced a decision, and the situation can change.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware", "heise online", "Golem.de", "IGN", "PC Gamer"], "_src": "f0402e6d"}, "2026-11-12-golden-joystick-2026": {"titel": "Golden Joystick Awards 2026: Resident Evil Requiem is Game of the Year, Crimson Desert wins on PC", "schlagzeile": "Golden Joysticks: Resident Evil Requiem takes Game of the Year", "kurz": "At the 44th Golden Joystick Awards, Resident Evil Requiem won the top prize as Ultimate Game of the Year. Crimson Desert was named best PC game. Multiplayer hit Meccha Chameleon took four awards, and The Witcher 4 is the most wanted game.", "zusammenfassung": "The Golden Joystick Awards are considered the games industry's oldest public vote and were held for the 44th time in 2026. Capcom's Resident Evil Requiem took the top prize as Ultimate Game of the Year. The horror game also won Console Game of the Year, Best Game Trailer and Best Lead Performer for Angela Sant'Albano as Grace Ashcroft. According to TheGameVerse, Capcom was also named Studio of the Year. Crimson Desert was named PC Game of the Year, even though it is also out on consoles. Hide-and-seek game Meccha Chameleon won four awards: Best Multiplayer Game, Best Indie Game (self-published), Streamer's Choice and Developers' Choice. The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt Remastered was named best remaster, and The Witcher 4 most wanted game. Fans voted the Steam Controller best gaming hardware. Other awards went to Onimusha: Way of the Sword (audio), Control: Resonant (visual design), Doom: The Dark Ages – Revelations (expansion) and Subnautica 2 (early access). The awards are organized by PC Gamer's publisher.", "weitere_links": ["TheGameVerse on X (winners list)"], "_src": "d4e2e75f"}, "2026-11-12-gta6-clip-realistisch": {"titel": "GTA 6: Rockstar shares in-game clip that many take for a real phone video from Miami", "schlagzeile": "Real or GTA 6? New Rockstar clip fools the internet", "kurz": "A roughly 15-second first-person GTA 6 clip is sparking debate because many people think it is real footage. It recreates a real phone video of the GTA cars from the marketing stunt in Miami. Rockstar shared the clip in its Instagram story, which according to IGN points to genuine game footage.", "zusammenfassung": "One week before the launch of GTA 6, a short clip is causing amazement. It first appeared on the Instagram account \"Only in Dade\", which collects bizarre scenes from Miami-Dade. It shows a drive along Ocean Drive past a row of flashy cars, plus a second perspective from the sidewalk. According to IGN, Polygon and Insider Gaming, the clip recreates a real video taken in October during Rockstar's marketing stunt with recreated GTA cars in Miami. Many viewers initially took the footage for real recordings or for AI. Rockstar shared the clip in its Instagram story and liked it, which IGN sees as a strong sign of genuine game footage. According to Polygon, however, Rockstar has not explicitly confirmed it. Fans speculate that the look could show what recordings with the in-game phone camera look like. Insider Gaming stresses that the clip says nothing about a possible first-person mode. GTA 6 launches on November 19 for PS5 and Xbox Series X/S and, according to Rockstar, runs at 30 fps on consoles. Preloading is already under way.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming", "Polygon", "GamePro (news overview)"], "_src": "34198252"}, "2026-11-12-black-forest-games-unabhaengig": {"titel": "Black Forest Games buys itself out of Embracer and founds the studio group Third Signal", "schlagzeile": "German Destroy All Humans studio buys itself out of Embracer", "kurz": "German studio Black Forest Games has separated from THQ Nordic and Embracer through a management buyout. At the same time, it is founding Third Signal, a group of independent studios. The team will continue to work with THQ Nordic.", "zusammenfassung": "After nine years under the umbrella of THQ Nordic and Embracer, Black Forest Games is independent again. According to Eurogamer and PC Gamer, this was achieved through a management buyout. The studio developed Giana Sisters: Twisted Dreams and the remakes of the first two Destroy All Humans games, among others. It was founded by former employees of Spellbound Entertainment, known for Desperados and Arcania: Gothic 4. Together with its independence, it is launching Third Signal, a group of independent studios that is also meant to help other indie teams in the future. Third Signal CEO Andreas Tobler says, in essence, that many of the best games of the last decade came from teams of 50 rather than 500 people. According to the press release, THQ Nordic and Black Forest Games will continue to collaborate on development. The studio apparently has not taken over the rights to Destroy All Humans. Managing director Adrian Goersch announces a new project but gives no details. The studio was hit by Embracer's layoffs in 2024 and lost around 50 jobs at the time.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "7dfb6efd"}, "2026-11-12-nintendo-dmca-github": {"titel": "Nintendo has 144 GitHub repositories with Switch modchip firmware and two emulators removed via DMCA", "schlagzeile": "Nintendo cleans up GitHub: Switch emulators and modchip firmware gone", "kurz": "Nintendo has sent four DMCA notices to GitHub targeting the Switch emulators Yuzu and Citron Neo as well as modchip firmware. GitHub has removed 144 repositories with the firmware. According to TorrentFreak, however, it can still be found elsewhere on the platform.", "zusammenfassung": "Nintendo is once again taking action against tools for bypassing the Switch's copy protection. According to IGN, GitHub received four DMCA notices, which it has documented publicly. The targets are the emulators Yuzu and Citron Neo, but above all firmware for modchips such as Picofly. Such chips are soldered onto the Switch mainboard and bypass the copy protection. GitHub removed 144 repositories with the firmware and replaced them with a DMCA notice. In its notice dated November 6, Nintendo argues that the technical protection measures are meant to prevent playing pirated copies and playing on unauthorized devices. According to TorrentFreak, however, the firmware is still available elsewhere on GitHub. Back in 2024, Nintendo had around 8,500 copies of Yuzu taken down. IGN links the new wave to reports that emulators had shortly before made the new Ocarina of Time remake run on PC; a direct connection has not been proven. Whether Nintendo plans further steps is open.", "_src": "788c053c"}, "2026-11-12-id-veteranen-hidden-horses": {"titel": "Around 20 former id Software developers found the studio Hidden Horses and plan an arena shooter", "schlagzeile": "After Xbox layoffs: ex-id developers found their own shooter studio", "kurz": "Around 20 former id Software developers have founded Hidden Horses, a studio owned by its employees. Their first project is the single-player arena shooter Danger Pay. It is to be financed partly through Kickstarter.", "zusammenfassung": "In the Xbox layoffs of July 2026, id Software reportedly lost 136 developers. Around 20 of them have now founded Hidden Horses, a studio owned by its employees. According to PC Gamer, the founders bring more than 250 years of combined experience. The studio is to be run democratically and to put long-term stability ahead of fast growth and questionable monetization. Co-founder Dustin Land says they want to keep the team together and make classic shooters. The first game is called Danger Pay, a single-player arena shooter about a brutal TV game show. The studio names the 1987 film The Running Man and the arcade game Smash TV as inspirations. A Kickstarter campaign is planned for financing. Platforms, date and the Kickstarter start are not yet known.", "_src": "2eb4f3a4"}, "2026-11-12-tes6-sentinel-pause": {"titel": "Bethesda: no news on The Elder Scrolls 6: Sentinel for Skyrim's anniversary – and none \"for some time\"", "schlagzeile": "15 years of Skyrim, but no Elder Scrolls 6: Bethesda tempers fans", "kurz": "For Skyrim's 15th birthday, fans had hoped for news on The Elder Scrolls 6: Sentinel. Bethesda Game Studios made clear on Reddit that there will be no big announcement. There will be nothing new on Sentinel \"for some time\".", "zusammenfassung": "The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim turned 15 on November 11. In the subreddit for The Elder Scrolls 6, fans speculated about an anniversary surprise, fueled by a podcast teaser about a \"big announcement\". The podcaster later clarified that it had nothing to do with Bethesda. Then the official Bethesda Game Studios account also chimed in on Reddit. There would be no big announcement, and nothing new on Sentinel would be shown \"for some time\", the studio wrote. Bethesda only made the title Sentinel official in early November. The Elder Scrolls 6 was announced back in 2018. For the anniversary, Skyrim is discounted on all platforms. The Elder Scrolls Online is making the Greymoor chapter part of the base game for free, and a Skyrim event runs there until December 2. When there will be new information on Sentinel is open.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "85003521"}, "2026-11-11-xbox-cloud-ohne-game-pass": {"titel": "Xbox Cloud Gaming without Game Pass: buy playtime or stream free with ads", "schlagzeile": "Xbox Cloud Gaming opens up: buy hours or play free with ads", "kurz": "Since November 11, players in supported countries can buy Xbox cloud playtime even without a Game Pass subscription. Xbox is also promoting free streaming with ads, with a time limit per session. Only games you own or selected free-to-play titles can be streamed.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft is overhauling Xbox Cloud Gaming. According to Xbox Wire, players in supported markets have been able to buy cloud playtime in the Xbox Store since November 11 without subscribing to Game Pass. During the Insider test phase, the ad-free packs cost 3.99 dollars for 10, 7.99 dollars for 25 and 11.99 dollars for 50 hours; these were explicitly introductory prices, and euro prices are not given in the sources. Purchased hours do not expire and, according to Xbox, offer shorter wait times and better stream quality. On the official cloud gaming page and on X, Xbox also promotes free streaming with ads, where available, with time limits per session. In the Insider test, the limit was one hour according to The Verge. You can stream your own games, selected free-to-play titles and Game Pass games. Since November, Game Pass subscribers have monthly allowances: 15 hours with Ultimate, 10 with Premium and 5 with Essential. Once they are used up, you can buy more hours or switch to the ad-supported option. Right on time, GTA 6 also launches via the cloud on Xbox One on November 19. Which countries are included at launch is unclear.", "weitere_links": ["Xbox Wire (GTA VI via cloud, playtime from Nov 11)", "Xbox Cloud Gaming (official page)", "Xbox Wire (prices in the Insider test)", "Xbox Wire (monthly allowances)", "The Verge"], "_src": "cfedef5c"}, "2026-11-11-dark-souls-server-zurueck": {"titel": "Dark Souls 2 and 3: online features available again after almost two weeks of downtime", "schlagzeile": "Dark Souls 2 and 3 are back online – the cause remains a secret", "kurz": "After a break of almost two weeks, the online features of Dark Souls 2 and 3 are running again on all platforms. According to PC Gamer, invasions and messages work again. FromSoftware has not revealed what exactly the server problem was.", "zusammenfassung": "The servers of Dark Souls 2 and Dark Souls 3 are back in operation. Almost two weeks earlier, the multiplayer features of both games had been switched off on all platforms because of an unexplained server problem. The official Dark Souls site now states briefly that the investigation is complete, a fix has been applied and the online features have been restored. According to PC Gamer, invasions and messages work as usual again. FromSoftware still does not name the cause. For comparison: in 2022 the PC servers of all Dark Souls games were offline for almost a year, back then because of a security vulnerability that allowed malicious code to be executed. Whether a security problem was behind it this time as well is not known. During the break, fan mods such as Seamless Co-op, which run independently of the official servers, helped out. Anyone who wants to play the classic invasions can do so again now.", "_src": "76889d66"}, "2026-11-11-kb5132061-installationsfehler": {"titel": "Windows 11: Microsoft confirms KB5132061 installation failures and is rolling out an automatic repair", "schlagzeile": "Microsoft confirms KB5132061 failures – fix comes via Windows Update", "kurz": "Microsoft has now officially confirmed the installation problems with the November security update KB5132061. On affected Windows 11 PCs the installation aborts or is retried repeatedly, with typical error codes 0x800f0993, 0x800f0989 and 0x80070306. According to Microsoft, a repair is running automatically via Windows Update and should reach affected devices within 24 to 48 hours after it started on Wednesday at 19:00 Vienna time; the security update is then installed on its own. Users do not need to do anything except stay online and get updates through Settings.", "zusammenfassung": "The November security update KB5132061 cannot be installed on some Windows 11 PCs, the installation sometimes aborts only at 99 percent, and repeated attempts often do not help. The error codes 0x800f0993, 0x800f0989 and 0x80070306 are reported, and occasionally also 0x800f0922. Microsoft documented the problem on Wednesday as a known issue in the English release notes for KB5132061. According to the company, a repair runs automatically on affected devices that are connected to the internet and use Windows Update in Settings; no manual steps are required to receive it. All affected devices should get the fix within 24 to 48 hours after the rollout started on Wednesday at 19:00 Vienna time (10:00 Pacific Time), and should then download and install the security update automatically. A Microsoft service message quoted by BleepingComputer says only a subset of devices that installed the optional October preview update KB5127936 are affected; devices without that preview update are not affected. Microsoft does not name the exact cause. Windows Latest and the DrWindows site had previously reported the errors, but many systems were never affected. Earlier tips about turning off Windows Sandbox or running DISM and sfc are now secondary, because the company is telling users to wait for the automatic repair. Anyone who still cannot install the update after the 48 hours should, according to Microsoft, use Windows Help or contact Support. This remains a security update, so it should not be paused permanently.", "weitere_links": ["Dr. Windows", "BleepingComputer", "Neowin", "Windows Latest"], "_src": "7755549c"}, "2026-11-11-harada-xbox-series-s": {"titel": "Former Tekken boss Katsuhiro Harada: consoles like the Xbox Series S should not be released", "schlagzeile": "Tekken legend Harada on Series S: “extra work for a weaker child”", "kurz": "Katsuhiro Harada criticized the Xbox Series S at a developer conference in South Korea while an Xbox representative was in the room. The main problem, he said, is that it is so similar to the Series X but noticeably weaker. A CD Projekt developer countered that the optimization helps all platforms.", "zusammenfassung": "Katsuhiro Harada, long-time head of the Tekken series and now head of the new VS Studio, spoke bluntly about the Xbox Series S at the Console Game Developers Conference 2026 in South Korea. According to Inven Global, quoted by Eurogamer, he said in front of a senior Xbox representative in attendance that he wished hardware like the Series S would not be released. The biggest problem is not just the tight memory, but that the console is very similar to the Series X yet awkwardly weaker. After the best version, it feels like having to do extra work for a slightly weaker child. With Switch 2, on the other hand, you can mentally switch to a separate device for Nintendo fans. Because there are more Series S than Series X users in the US, for example, you cannot cut corners, and complaints about worse textures then land with the developers. Paweł Sasko of CD Projekt Red countered: optimizing for weaker hardware makes games run significantly better on all platforms, and the low price expands the market. Shift Up CTO DongKi Lee said he is looking forward to the next Xbox, codenamed Helix. This is an opinion voiced on a panel, not an official position of Microsoft or any studio.", "weitere_links": ["Video Games Chronicle", "PC Gamer"], "_src": "8dad0743"}, "2026-11-11-rtx5080-24gb-gestrichen": {"titel": "Reports: Nvidia has reportedly cancelled the 24 GB RTX 5080 – the 16 GB model stays", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Nvidia has reportedly scrapped the 24 GB RTX 5080", "kurz": "According to the Chinese industry channel Board Channels, Nvidia has told its board partners that the 24 GB RTX 5080 planned for January 2027 is cancelled. The reason is said to be the expensive 3 GB GDDR7 chips. The 16 GB RTX 5080 will reportedly stay in production. Nvidia has not confirmed any of this.", "zusammenfassung": "According to new reports, there will be no RTX 5080 with 24 GB of video memory for now. TechPowerUp cites the Chinese industry channel Board Channels, which says Nvidia officially informed its board partners that the planned January 2027 launch is off. Cost is given as the reason: according to the post quoted by PC Gamer, 3 GB GDDR7 chips cost about three times as much as the 2 GB chips used so far. With the more expensive memory, the card would have had to launch at a price that would barely sell. The familiar 16 GB RTX 5080 is therefore said to stay in production. According to earlier rumors, the 24 GB model would have had the same number of compute units but more memory, more bandwidth and slightly higher clocks. PC Gamer points out that it was previously even said the 24 GB version could replace the RTX 5090 and the 16 GB variant; however, Nvidia executive Jeff Fisher had stressed that RTX 5090 production has not been discontinued. According to TechPowerUp, no Super refresh is in sight, and the next big step would be the RTX 60 series. Important: the 24 GB model itself was never officially announced, so this is a rumor about the end of a rumor. Nvidia has not commented.", "ursprungsquelle": "Board Channels (via VideoCardz, Gazlog, harukaze5719)", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "PC Games Hardware", "Wccftech"], "_src": "2c9fc45e"}, "2026-11-11-gta6-de-cix-rekord": {"titel": "GTA 6 pre-load: internet exchange DE-CIX measures new data record", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 download breaks record: 22.3 terabits per second in Frankfurt", "kurz": "On the first evening of the GTA 6 pre-load, the DE-CIX internet exchange in Frankfurt measured a new peak of 22.30 terabits per second. The operator also reports a worldwide record. GTA 6 is playable from midnight on November 19.", "zusammenfassung": "The start of the Grand Theft Auto VI pre-load has left measurable traces on the internet. As the DE-CIX operator told Golem on request, the Frankfurt exchange reached a new peak of 22.30 terabits per second on November 10 at 8:20 pm. That is 19.06 percent more than the previous high since January 2026. Across all DE-CIX locations worldwide, 33.01 terabits per second were measured, also a record. DE-CIX CTO Thomas King explained that big game launches are among the events that can make traffic rise sharply very quickly. By data throughput, DE-CIX Frankfurt is considered Europe's largest internet exchange. The pre-load for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S started in the night to November 10, and the file is around 210 to 212 GB. According to PC Games, a German internet provider also reported a multiple of its usual gaming traffic. GTA 6 is playable from midnight on November 19. Whether launch day itself brings new records remains to be seen.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games"], "_src": "b0fe5f64"}, "2026-11-11-mh-wilds-ascendance-beta": {"titel": "Steam changes point to a beta for the Monster Hunter Wilds expansion Ascendance", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Monster Hunter Wilds: Ascendance getting a beta soon?", "kurz": "Capcom has quietly renamed the old Monster Hunter Wilds beta app on Steam to “Ascendance Beta test”, as SteamDB shows. This points to an upcoming test of the expansion. Capcom has not announced anything yet, and a date is unknown.", "zusammenfassung": "The first big expansion for Monster Hunter Wilds is called Ascendance and is due in 2027. According to Eurogamer and PC Gamer, Capcom has now renamed the old beta app of the main game on Steam. According to the SteamDB change log, it is now called Monster Hunter Wilds: Ascendance Beta test and has received new key art. This points to an upcoming beta test. Because the app has the same ID as the earlier Wilds beta, it could reappear in former testers' libraries; a separate sign-up might then not be necessary. When a beta could start is completely open; Eurogamer cautiously guesses early 2027. Capcom last showed Ascendance in the September State of Play and at Tokyo Game Show, including the returning Elder Dragon Teostra. The expansion is meant to be more challenging after many players found the main game too easy at launch. These are hints from Steam data, not an official announcement.", "ursprungsquelle": "SteamDB-Änderungsprotokoll (via PC Gamer)", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "2faf2355"}, "2026-11-11-radeon-ssd-fix-tool": {"titel": "Unofficial open-source tool stops atieclxx.exe from constantly writing to the SSD", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver wears out your SSD: free tool stops the constant writes", "kurz": "A community developer has released a free tool on GitHub against the Radeon bug in which atieclxx.exe copies itself to the SSD every second. It checks whether the PC is affected, estimates the wear and blocks the writes without disabling the service. It is an unofficial workaround, not from AMD.", "zusammenfassung": "On some PCs with a Radeon driver or AMD chipset driver, the file atieclxx.exe, which belongs to the AMD External Events Utility service, copies itself every second. This creates a constant write load on the system drive, and hundreds of gigabytes can quickly add up even without use, which ages SSDs unnecessarily. A community member called Necandi has now released the tool Radeon-atieclxx-SSD-Fix on GitHub, as ComputerBase and Wccftech report. It first checks whether the system is affected and estimates the SSD wear so far. This estimate is rough: it assumes the bug has existed since the AMD card was installed and, if the SSD reports no runtime, calculates with eight hours of operation per day. Instead of disabling the service, the tool only forbids the system account from overwriting the copy. As a result, the copy attempt fails, and FreeSync, frame pacing and hotkeys should keep working. Previous workarounds such as stopping the service or disabling Resizable BAR could cause problems exactly there. Anyone who does not want a tool can, according to ComputerBase, also revoke the rights themselves with an icacls command and restore them later. The developer stresses that he has nothing to do with AMD and that use is at your own risk. AMD has announced an official fix with driver 26.11.1, which is still pending.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech"], "_src": "3c8c1851"}, "2026-11-11-zen6-epyc-tests": {"titel": "AMD Epyc 9006 Venice on sale: first tests show big leaps for Zen 6", "schlagzeile": "First Zen 6 tests: AMD's 256-core chip is 58% faster than its predecessor", "kurz": "AMD is now officially selling the Epyc 9006 Venice server processors with Zen 6. In Phoronix's first independent tests, the top model Epyc 9996 was on average 1.58 times as fast as the previous Zen 5c flagship. For gamers, this is a first look at the architecture of future Ryzen chips.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD has announced the sales launch of the sixth Epyc generation, codenamed Venice, which was already presented in July. It starts with nine models for the SP7 socket; according to Golem, another 22 for SP8 will follow in early 2027. Phoronix was allowed to test the two top models. The Epyc 9996 has 256 Zen 6c cores, up to 4.1 GHz and a 600-watt TDP and costs 14,904 US dollars according to AMD's list. In a dual-socket system, it averaged 1.58 times the performance of its predecessor, the 192-core Epyc 9965, across all benchmarks. In HPC applications it was about twice as fast as Intel's Xeon 6980P and delivered the best performance per watt despite higher power draw. According to Golem, the compact cores benefit from larger chiplets with 32 instead of 12 cores. The second chip tested, the Epyc 9686F, has 96 Zen 6 cores at up to 5.3 GHz. For gamers these are server chips, but they show independently for the first time what the Zen 6 architecture delivers, which is later also expected in Ryzen processors. How much of this reaches games cannot be derived from server benchmarks. Phoronix also points out that full performance requires fast MRDIMM memory, which is likely to be very expensive in the current RAM crisis.", "weitere_links": ["Phoronix (Epyc 9996 review)", "PC Games Hardware", "AMD on X"], "_src": "f935df7f"}, "2026-11-11-zelda-oot-5-2-mio": {"titel": "Zelda: Ocarina of Time remake sells more than 5.2 million copies in four days", "schlagzeile": "Zelda remake breaks Switch 2 record: 5.2 million in just four days", "kurz": "Nintendo reports more than 5.2 million copies of the Ocarina of Time remake sold in the first four days. That is the fastest sales launch of a Nintendo game on Switch 2. According to Nintendo, these are actual sales, not just shipments to retail.", "zusammenfassung": "The remake of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time is a big success for Nintendo. According to a press release from the company, more than 5.2 million copies were sold worldwide in the first four days after launch on November 5. That makes it the most successful sales launch of a Nintendo-published Switch 2 game, according to Golem both worldwide and in Europe. According to Golem, Nintendo is talking about units actually sold, not just shipments to retail. There is no breakdown by region or between digital and physical. The record explicitly refers to Nintendo's own games, as Eurogamer stresses. The remake is also very well received by critics: Golem cites a Metacritic average of 96 points. New features include graphics, soundtrack, voice acting and reworked combat. The success is also remarkable because the game came out only two weeks before GTA 6. The remake is part of the celebrations for the Zelda series' 40th anniversary.", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de", "IGN Deutschland"], "_src": "6dbb5df2"}, "2026-11-11-ps5-100-millionen": {"titel": "Sony confirms: PlayStation 5 has sold more than 100 million units", "schlagzeile": "PS5 passes 100 million – now just behind the original PlayStation", "kurz": "Sony has confirmed that more than 100 million PS5 consoles had been shipped to retailers as of November 10. That puts it ahead of the PS3 and PSP and just behind the original PlayStation at 102.4 million. Recently, though, sales have been noticeably slower than a year earlier.", "zusammenfassung": "The PlayStation 5 has reached a milestone: according to Sony's official sales overview, more than 100 million consoles had been shipped by November 10, 2026. The figure counts shipments to retailers (sell-in), not sales to end customers. The PS5 has thus overtaken the PS3 (87.4 million) and the PSP (76.4 million). The original PlayStation is only just ahead at 102.4 million, while the PS4 at 117 million and the PS2 at more than 160 million are well ahead. The pace has slowed recently: according to Insider Gaming, 1.6 million units were shipped in the first quarter of the fiscal year instead of 2.5 million, and 2.6 million instead of 4 million in the second. The strongest year was fiscal 2023 with 20.8 million consoles. Sony also reports 127 million monthly active PlayStation users as of September 30. On the software side, PS4 and PS5 stand at 154.3 million units sold after two quarters of the current fiscal year. How strongly GTA 6 boosts console sales from November 19 will only show in the third-quarter figures.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming"], "_src": "0a83a0a1"}, "2026-11-11-nvidia-aktie-china-chips": {"titel": "Nvidia stock at its lowest since March: report says more than 240,000 AI systems reached China through a network of companies", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia stock keeps falling: chips worth $7.5B said to have gone to China", "kurz": "After two losing days, Nvidia stock closed at 168.89 US dollars on Tuesday, its lowest level since late March. Microsoft briefly overtook it in market value. According to a report by The Information, the woman with whom Jensen Huang admitted an affair is said to have brought Nvidia systems worth at least 7.5 billion dollars to China.", "zusammenfassung": "The scandal surrounding Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang keeps weighing on the company's stock. After falling more than 4 percent on Monday, the stock dropped another 5.5 percent on Tuesday and closed at 168.89 US dollars, its lowest level since March 30. That leaves the market value just above 4 trillion dollars; in early October it was still more than 5.5 trillion. Microsoft was briefly ahead of Nvidia on Tuesday, and Apple had already passed it before the allegations became public. The trigger is a new report by The Information, citing two people who know Alice Huang, with whom the Nvidia CEO has admitted an affair. She is said to have enabled shipments of more than 240,000 A100, H100 and H200 systems worth at least 7.5 billion dollars to China through a network of companies. A100 and H100 have been subject to US export restrictions since October 2022. According to the report, the Chinese data center company Century Litong and the Singapore-based firm Megaspeed, one of Nvidia's preferred cloud partners since October 2023, played a role. US agencies are reportedly pushing to put Megaspeed on a blacklist. China rejects the espionage allegation. Nvidia has launched an internal investigation, which an analyst quoted by CNBC expects to take four to six weeks. The same analyst puts the probability that Huang loses his post at about 15 percent. The figures on the chip shipments come from anonymous sources and have not been officially confirmed.", "weitere_links": ["heise online (report on the China shipments)"], "_src": "3a8f3e41"}, "2026-11-11-fortis-games-schliessung": {"titel": "Mobile studio Fortis Games closes, around 440 jobs affected as backer Las Vegas Sands ends funding", "schlagzeile": "Fortis Games shuts down – around 440 jobs lost as casino giant pulls funding", "kurz": "Mobile studio Fortis Games, founded in 2022, has closed, affecting around 440 jobs. According to a former employee, backer Las Vegas Sands ended funding and terminated all contracts worldwide. The studio's two games were still in an early test phase.", "zusammenfassung": "Another major closure in the games industry: Fortis Games is gone, affecting around 440 jobs. CEO Steven Chiang confirmed the closure to GamesBeat on November 10. He said the team was disappointed not to have reached its goals after more than five years and would now focus on helping staff find new jobs. A former producer wrote on LinkedIn that parent company Las Vegas Sands had decided to end funding and terminate all contracts worldwide. The San Francisco studio was founded in 2022 by Chiang, who previously worked at Electronic Arts and Zynga. Fortis was working on the mobile games Twilight Towers and Bloom & Breakfast, which were in an early soft launch; according to the producer, with solid metrics. A former communications director wrote, however, that the community-focused approach did not resonate enough with players. What happens to the two games is unknown.", "_src": "2298d3f0"}, "2026-11-11-windows11-speicherintegritaet": {"titel": "Windows 11 now turns on Memory Integrity (HVCI) automatically on more PCs, a protection that can slow down games", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 turns on Memory Integrity – what it means for gamers", "kurz": "With the November update, Windows 11 automatically enables Memory Integrity (HVCI) on more existing PCs. The protection blocks tampered drivers, but by Microsoft's own account it can cost performance in games. If you deliberately turned it off, it stays off, and it can still be disabled.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft is tightening a security setting that affects gamers. Since the optional October update, and now with the Patch Tuesday update KB5132061, Windows 11 can automatically enable Memory Integrity, also called HVCI, during updates. Until now it was mostly active only on new PCs and clean installs. According to Windows Latest, the change applies to Windows 11 25H2 and 26H2. Memory Integrity runs in an area isolated by the Windows hypervisor and checks there whether drivers and kernel code are trustworthy, so even a hijacked kernel cannot run unverified code. Some PCs will also get virtualization-based security (VBS) turned on for this. Before enabling it, Windows checks hardware, driver compatibility and performance, and the rollout is gradual. If you turned the feature off yourself before, Windows will not turn it back on; enterprise policies take precedence. The catch for gamers: Microsoft itself recommended a few years ago in a support article to turn off Memory Integrity for better gaming performance. It can be turned off under Windows Security, Device security, Core isolation details. Whether you should is a trade-off, because the protection targets malware that sneaks into the core of Windows through drivers.", "_src": "0b7240ab"}, "2026-11-10-fairgames-eingestellt": {"titel": "Sony cancels live-service shooter Fairgames after a disappointing playtest, no layoffs at Haven Studios", "schlagzeile": "Sony pulls the plug on Fairgames – another live-service shooter is gone", "kurz": "PlayStation has stopped development of Haven Studios' heist shooter Fairgames. According to an internal email reported by Bloomberg, player feedback and retention in a playtest fell short of its goals. There will reportedly be no layoffs; the studio will support other Sony teams.", "zusammenfassung": "Fairgames is history. Sony has ended development of the live-service shooter three years after its 2023 announcement, as Bloomberg first reported. An internal email from PlayStation executives Sean Decker and John Doyle says a recent playtest was convincing technically and organizationally, but feedback and player retention were mixed and fell short of the goals. Together with the difficult market for PvP shooters, they decided not to continue. According to the reports, developer Haven Studios will not be closed and no layoffs are planned; the team will instead support other Sony studios. Haven was founded in 2021 by Jade Raymond, who has since left the studio, and acquired by Sony in 2022. Fairgames is said to have been reworked several times since its reveal, and internal tests reportedly went poorly as early as 2025. Real gameplay was never officially shown, only rendered scenes from the announcement trailer. Sony's live-service strategy in 2022 planned at least ten such games by 2026. Alongside hits like Helldivers 2, there are now many cancelled projects and the Concord debacle.", "weitere_links": ["Polygon", "IGN"], "_src": "ff8dd113"}, "2026-11-10-nvidia-tsmc-bestellungen": {"titel": "Report from Taiwan: Nvidia could cut chip orders at TSMC, AMD and ASIC designers would benefit", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Nvidia cutting its chip orders at TSMC?", "kurz": "Taiwan's Commercial Times reports, citing unnamed supply chain sources, that Nvidia could order fewer chips from TSMC. It points to pressure from the scandal surrounding Jensen Huang and stricter export reviews. The report does not name a product, process node, volume or timeframe. Nvidia and TSMC have not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "Nvidia could scale back its orders at contract manufacturer TSMC. That is what the Taiwanese newspaper Commercial Times reports, citing unnamed supply chain sources; TechPowerUp picked up the report. It does not say which products, process node, volumes or timeframe are involved. As reasons, the report cites pressure from inside and outside: internally the scandal surrounding Jensen Huang and the Nvidia board's investigation, externally stricter export reviews. H200 chips are also said to be stockpiled in Hong Kong. The suspicion that some companies approved for H200 could be shell companies is mentioned too, but explicitly as a suspicion rather than a finding. If Nvidia gives up capacity, the newspaper expects AMD and developers of custom AI chips such as MediaTek, Alchip and GUC to take it. Suppliers such as TSMC and ASE would be hit hardest by cuts. For gamers this would not automatically mean cheaper graphics cards, because the memory that is currently scarce does not come from TSMC. The report relies on a single source; Nvidia and TSMC have not commented on it. Until confirmed, it should be treated as a rumor.", "ursprungsquelle": "Commercial Times (Taiwan), via TechPowerUp", "_src": "a929a8ec"}, "2026-11-10-gta6-xbox-fsr4-dateien": {"titel": "Dataminers find AMD FSR libraries in GTA 6's Xbox package, whether FSR 4.1.2 is used remains open", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Does GTA 6 on Xbox already use AMD's AI upscaling FSR 4?", "kurz": "GTA 6's Xbox preload contains two AMD files whose names match the FSR 4.1.2 integration for Xbox Series X|S. That is a hint, not proof: the game files are encrypted, and the same interface can also fall back to the older FSR 3.1. Rockstar has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "Shortly after GTA 6's Xbox preload started, dataminers discovered two AMD libraries in the installation package: amd_fidelityfx_loader_xbox.dll and amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_xbox.dll. They were found by dataminer Tex2, and other users compared the names with the documentation for FSR 4.1.2 on Xbox Series X|S. VideoCardz reported it first, and PC Games Hardware put the find into context. AMD and Microsoft released FSR 4.1.2 for Xbox on November 4; it is the first AI-based upscaler for the consoles and comes with two INT8 models, Full and Lite. However, the file names do not prove that GTA 6 actually uses FSR 4.1.2. The same AMD SDK also contains the classic FSR 3.1.6, and the interface can fall back to it. Since the game files are encrypted, the contents of the libraries cannot be checked yet. For consoles, Rockstar has so far only confirmed 30 fps on all models and PSSR on the PS5 Pro; there is no official statement on upscaling on Xbox. Analyses should show which method is used by the launch on November 19 at the latest.", "ursprungsquelle": "Dataminer Tex2 (X), first reported by VideoCardz", "_src": "548f3594"}, "2026-11-10-patchday-november-1235": {"titel": "Microsoft Patch Tuesday November 2026: 1,235 flaws fixed, including an actively exploited Outlook zero-day", "schlagzeile": "Record Patch Tuesday: 1,235 flaws – Outlook bug already exploited", "kurz": "Microsoft fixed 1,235 security flaws on November's Patch Tuesday, 66 of them critical. A spoofing flaw in Outlook is already being exploited to steal NTLM account data. Windows 11 gets KB5132061 and KB5131087, Windows 10 in the ESU program gets KB5131096.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft's November Patch Tuesday is huge again: according to BleepingComputer, the updates fix 1,235 security flaws; another 108 were fixed earlier in the month and are not counted. October even had 1,411; Microsoft increasingly uses AI to find vulnerabilities. 66 flaws are rated critical, 48 of which allow remote code execution. Around 639 affect Windows and Windows components. Most urgent is a spoofing flaw in Microsoft Outlook that is already being attacked. According to Microsoft, it is enough for a victim to open a crafted message file: Outlook then connects to an attacker's server without the usual warning and can leak credentials in the form of NTLM hashes. Windows 11 receives the cumulative updates KB5132061 and KB5131087, Windows 10 22H2 in the Extended Security Updates program gets KB5131096. For some users, installing KB5132061 fails with error 0x800f0993, according to Neowin. Anyone using Windows or Office should still install the updates soon, especially because of the Outlook flaw.", "weitere_links": ["Dr. Windows", "Neowin (installation error)"], "_src": "e3b7656c"}, "2026-11-10-fritzbox-5690-pro-speicher": {"titel": "Fritz!Box 5690 Pro: support data shows newer units with only half the RAM and flash, under the same article number", "schlagzeile": "Fritz!Box 5690 Pro: newer units with half the memory – same article number", "kurz": "Newer units of the Fritz!Box 5690 Pro apparently have only 1 GB RAM and 2 GB flash instead of 2 and 4 GB. Article number and hardware version are the same; the difference only shows in the hardware subrevision. Fritz speaks of industry-standard adjustments with no effect on performance.", "zusammenfassung": "If you buy a Fritz!Box 5690 Pro today, you don't necessarily get the same hardware as buyers at launch. A user with two units noticed: the newer one showed much higher RAM usage on the same Fritz!OS version. According to the support data, a unit from July 2024 has 2 GB RAM and 4 GB flash, one from June 2026 only 1 GB RAM and 2 GB flash. Usable system RAM accordingly drops from 1,754 to 742 MB, and internal storage, used for example by Fritz!NAS, shrinks from about 1.7 GB to 680 MB. The variants can only be told apart by the hardware subrevision, which rose from 3 to 5; article number and hardware version are the same, and the routers look identical from the outside. When exactly the switch happened is unclear; at times both variants appear to have shipped in parallel. Fritz told Router-FAQ.de that internal components such as memory chips are occasionally adjusted over a product's life cycle; that is common in the industry and does not change specification or performance. The company did not explicitly confirm the specific halving. There are no comparison tests of both variants yet, and whether this affects future updates is also open. It is still awkward, because Fritz explicitly advertised the large memory capacity at launch in June 2024.", "_src": "aa5e40e9"}, "2026-11-10-auto-sr-xbox-ally-ryzen": {"titel": "Microsoft Auto SR leaves preview on ROG Xbox Ally X and X20 and comes to Copilot+ PCs with AMD Ryzen, new mode up to 120 fps", "schlagzeile": "Windows upscaling Auto SR: now handheld, with HDR and up to 120 fps", "kurz": "Microsoft's AI upscaling Auto SR has officially launched on the ROG Xbox Ally X and X20 handhelds. New are a performance mode with up to 120 fps, handheld use without a dock and the combination with Auto HDR. Auto SR now also runs on selected Copilot+ PCs with AMD Ryzen.", "zusammenfassung": "On the DirectX blog, Microsoft announced the official launch of Automatic Super Resolution (Auto SR) on the ROG Xbox Ally X and ROG Xbox Ally X20 handhelds. Auto SR runs games internally at a lower resolution and upscales them with AI on the NPU, without the game needing to support it. Until now, the feature was only available as a preview and only when docked. Now it also works on the built-in screen and on battery. Games running at 1080p are supported as well, and on a monitor Auto SR can then upscale to 1440p. A new performance mode raises the limit from around 60 to 75 fps so far to up to 120 fps; in Microsoft's Rocket League example, the average rose from 70 to 115 fps. In addition, Auto SR and Auto HDR can be used at the same time for the first time. Handheld use, 1080p and the new AMD Ryzen Copilot+ PCs are available now. Performance mode and Auto HDR support will roll out gradually with Windows updates. Current Windows 11 updates, an up-to-date Game Bar and the Auto Super Resolution package from the Microsoft Store are required.", "_src": "539f5a74"}, "2026-11-10-gpu-taskman-vram": {"titel": "GPU Taskman: open-source tool shows exactly which programs use how much graphics memory", "schlagzeile": "What's eating your VRAM? Free tool shows it per program", "kurz": "Microsoft and GitHub developer Scott Hanselman has released the open-source tool GPU Taskman. It shows per program how much graphics memory is in use, plus GPU load, temperature and clock speed. The tool is still experimental.", "zusammenfassung": "Scott Hanselman, Vice President at Microsoft and GitHub, has developed GPU Taskman, a free command-line tool. It is meant to show more precisely than the Windows Task Manager where graphics memory goes. It displays VRAM usage, system memory used by the GPU and the individual processes, plus load, temperature, power draw, clock speed and PCIe values. The tool distinguishes between the desktop, browsers, games and AI applications, for example. For local AI models in llama.cpp, Ollama or LM Studio, it can estimate the memory for model weights and KV cache separately. For gamers, it can help find VRAM bottlenecks that cause stuttering. Hanselman warns, however, that system RAM in use does not automatically mean a VRAM overflow, and the tool cannot identify individual textures. GPU Taskman supports NVIDIA and AMD cards on Windows 10 and 11, plus Linux, WSL and Apple Silicon Macs; version 0.3.5 adds Intel GPUs on Linux. It is available under the MIT license on GitHub, with a portable version for Windows. The software is still experimental, and some values are estimates.", "_src": "43537581"}, "2026-11-10-ps-plus-pc-app-ende": {"titel": "Sony is shutting down the PlayStation Plus app for PC on December 10, Death Stranding 2 joins the Extra catalog", "schlagzeile": "PS Plus streaming on PC is ending – only 0.4% used it", "kurz": "Sony is shutting down the PlayStation Plus app for Windows on December 10, 2026, ending the streaming of PS Plus games to PC. According to Sony, fewer than 0.4 percent of Premium members used the app. In the same post, Sony announces the new Extra and Premium games, led by Death Stranding 2.", "zusammenfassung": "At the very end of its post about the new PS Plus games for November, Sony announced the end of the PC app. From December 10, the PlayStation Plus app for PC will no longer be available, and with it the cloud streaming of PS Plus Premium games to Windows computers. Sony cites low usage as the reason: fewer than 0.4 percent of eligible Premium members had used the app. Memberships and benefits on PS5 and PS4 are not affected, and Sony says it will notify affected users directly. This removes one way to play PlayStation games on PC without a console. New in the Extra and Premium catalog in November are Death Stranding 2: On the Beach, Atomfall and Dragon Quest III HD-2D Remake, among others. Hell Let Loose follows on November 11, Like a Dragon: Pirate Yakuza in Hawaii, Trepang2, MotoGP 26 and Cricket 26 on November 24. Soul Reaver 2 and Freedom Wars Remastered are added for Premium only.", "weitere_links": ["Eurogamer", "PlayStation on X"], "_src": "235d58ff"}, "2026-11-10-amd-zen6-ipc-epyc": {"titel": "AMD reveals Zen 6 architecture: 27 percent more IPC, Epyc 9006 “Venice” launches with up to 256 cores", "schlagzeile": "Zen 6 is here: AMD promises 27% more IPC – server Epyc comes first", "kurz": "AMD has revealed the technology behind Zen 6 and cites 27 percent more IPC than Zen 5. The first Zen 6 chips are the Epyc 9006 “Venice” server processors with up to 256 cores and up to 5.3 GHz. The IPC figure comes from an unusual comparison by AMD. AMD has not said anything yet about Ryzen desktop CPUs with Zen 6.", "zusammenfassung": "With the embargo lifted this evening, AMD published many details about the Zen 6 architecture. According to AMD, IPC, meaning performance per clock, rises by 27 percent on average over Zen 5, with around 20 percent in regular applications and around 31 percent in AI workloads. ComputerBase and heise point out, however, that AMD compared 16 Zen 6c cores in a single chiplet with 16 Zen 5 cores across two chiplets, which is not a classic IPC comparison. Technically the core gets wider: the op cache grows to 6,750 entries and delivers 18 instead of 12 micro-ops per clock, while the register file and reorder buffer grow to 352 and 640 entries. AVX-512 stays, and so does SMT. The regular Zen 6 cores come twelve to a chiplet with 48 MB of L3 cache, the compact Zen 6c cores 32 to a chiplet with 128 MB of L3, made on TSMC's 2 nm process. The first products are the Epyc 9006 “Venice” server CPUs with up to 256 cores, 16 DDR5 memory channels, PCIe 6.0 and up to 600 watts. The high-frequency models reach up to 5.3 GHz. AMD says it is already shipping, and the first systems are due this year. In heise's first remote measurements, a single Zen 5 core took around 22 percent longer in Blender than a Zen 6 core, which however also runs at a higher clock. In 2027 a smaller platform follows, along with Venice-X with 3D V-Cache and Verano with LPDDR5X memory. After that, the roadmap lists Zen 7 “Florence” for 2028 and Zen 8 “Ravenna”. AMD said nothing at the event about Ryzen processors for desktops and notebooks with Zen 6 or their timing.", "weitere_links": ["heise online", "AMD on X"], "_src": "d9fcfe1b"}, "2026-11-10-amd-mext-flash-statt-ram": {"titel": "AMD MEXT: software moves rarely used memory to flash to save expensive DRAM", "schlagzeile": "RAM crisis: AMD wants to save up to 75% of DRAM with flash storage", "kurz": "AMD has introduced MEXT, software that moves rarely used memory pages from DRAM to flash SSDs. This is meant to let servers run almost as fast with much less expensive memory. For now the offer only applies to Epyc servers. All performance figures come from AMD.", "zusammenfassung": "With MEXT, AMD is responding to the ongoing memory shortage. According to AMD, DRAM accounts for 75 to 90 percent of a server's cost depending on configuration, while a large share of the memory is unused or oversized. MEXT detects “cold” memory pages and moves them to flash storage, meaning NVMe SSDs. AI models are meant to predict which data will be needed again soon and bring it back into DRAM in time. According to Wccftech, the software consists of a Linux driver, an AI engine that runs on a single Epyc core, and a monitoring tool. AMD says this can cut DRAM requirements by 20 to 75 percent with similar performance. In a chip design example, a server with half the DRAM is said to still reach 95 percent of the performance. These figures are manufacturer claims, and independent tests are still missing. According to Phoronix, the Linux driver is not open source. For now, MEXT is intended only for Epyc servers with NVMe drives, and a license is to follow later. AMD hinted that something like this could also become interesting for regular PCs, but there are no concrete plans for it.", "weitere_links": ["ComputerBase", "Phoronix"], "_src": "f9b8ff0f"}, "2026-11-10-gta6-vorbestell-rekord-xbox-cloud": {"titel": "GTA 6 is the most pre-ordered game in their stores according to Sony and Microsoft, Xbox One gets it via the cloud, Xbox signs 10-year partnership with Take-Two", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 breaks pre-order records – and even comes to Xbox One via the cloud", "kurz": "Sony and Microsoft report that GTA 6 is the most pre-ordered game in the history of the PlayStation Store and the Microsoft Store. Via Xbox Cloud Gaming it will also run on the old Xbox One at launch. Xbox CEO Asha Sharma speaks of a new 10-year partnership with Take-Two. Nobody gives concrete sales figures.", "zusammenfassung": "On the PlayStation Blog, Sony writes that GTA 6 is the most pre-ordered game in the history of the PlayStation Store. Microsoft reports the same for the Microsoft Store on Xbox Wire. Neither gives numbers; Take-Two most recently only said that pre-orders were far above expectations. Because of the expected rush, Sony and Microsoft advise preloading the game as early as possible. On PlayStation, GTA 6 launches on November 19 at midnight local time, starting in New Zealand. Xbox Cloud Gaming offers the game from November 19 at 1 a.m. US Eastern Time, i.e. 7 a.m. in Austria, on Xbox One and Xbox Series X|S, with Series S graphics settings. Streaming to PC or smartphones is not planned. On X, Xbox CEO Asha Sharma called this the “first step” of a new 10-year strategic partnership with Take-Two, without giving details. According to Xbox Wire, more Rockstar games such as GTA V and Red Dead Redemption 2 will come to Xbox Cloud Gaming in the coming months. From November 11, players in supported countries can also buy cloud playtime without a Game Pass subscription.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation.Blog", "Asha Sharma on X", "IGN"], "_src": "1f6dc907"}, "2026-11-10-eu-dfa-lootboxen-entwurf": {"titel": "Leaked draft of the EU Digital Fairness Act: loot boxes off by default for minors, pay-to-win banned for children", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Does the EU want to switch off loot boxes for kids by default?", "kurz": "An alleged draft of the EU's Digital Fairness Act has surfaced early. It proposes that loot boxes be switched off by default for minors and that all players can turn them off. The official presentation is planned for November 11, and it is far from being law.", "zusammenfassung": "The French trade publication Contexte has published an alleged draft of the Digital Fairness Act, and Eurogamer reports on it. According to Eurogamer, the EU Commission intends to officially present the proposal on November 11. The draft targets unfair practices in the digital world, including monetization in games. All players are to be able to turn off loot boxes, meaning rewards with random contents; for minors they are to be off by default. Pay-to-progress and pay-to-win mechanics are not to be offered to children if a product is aimed at them or the provider knows that minors use it. For virtual currencies, the real price of purchases is to be made transparent, along with the odds of winning for loot boxes. The text also foresees a mandatory age rating for games. Besides games, it covers influencer advertising, hidden prices and subscriptions that are hard to cancel. Important: this is a leaked draft that may still change before the presentation. Negotiations follow; according to Eurogamer, the law could be adopted at the end of 2027 and applied broadly by 2030.", "ursprungsquelle": "Contexte (via Video Games Industry Memo)", "_src": "792e7165"}, "2026-11-10-asrock-vbios-tool-1-0-6": {"titel": "ASRock releases VBIOS flash tool 1.0.6 for RX 7900 XT/XTX after version 1.0.5 bricked cards", "schlagzeile": "After bricked RX 7900 XTX cards: ASRock ships a new BIOS tool – no explanation", "kurz": "ASRock has released the ASRVBFlash 1.0.6 flash tool for the Radeon RX 7900 XT and XTX. According to user reports, the previous version 1.0.5 had killed cards after the update. ASRock does not say what has changed or what the cause was.", "zusammenfassung": "In early November, reports piled up that ASRock Radeon RX 7900 XT and XTX cards no longer started after an official VBIOS update. The culprit was the ASRVBFlash 1.0.5 flash tool: after the restart, the system no longer booted. ASRock then apparently pulled the version from its download pages. Now version 1.0.6 has quietly appeared, which according to TechPowerUp is meant to prevent the bricking and correctly apply the firmware update for better security. There is no changelog or explanation of the cause, which PCGH also criticizes. It remains unclear how ASRock handles cards that are already broken. According to TechPowerUp, a customer in Japan was told that a card destroyed by the official update is covered by warranty. A customer in Europe, by contrast, was told that removing the cooler to reflash the BIOS chip voids the warranty. Affected users should therefore go the RMA route instead of tinkering themselves. Anyone who has not updated yet can also wait for other users' experiences with 1.0.6.", "weitere_links": ["PC Games Hardware", "Wccftech"], "_src": "a328de5f"}, "2026-11-10-gta6-30fps-ps5-pro": {"titel": "Rockstar confirms: GTA 6 targets 30 fps on all consoles, PS5 Pro gets PSSR and exclusive ray-traced shadows", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 runs at 30 fps – on PS5 Pro too, but with ray-traced shadows", "kurz": "Rockstar has confirmed that GTA 6 targets 30 frames per second on all consoles, including the PS5 Pro. In return, the Pro gets sharper images via PSSR and exclusive ray-traced shadows. Preloading has been live since today, and the launch is on November 19.", "zusammenfassung": "As preloading began, Rockstar Games officially explained GTA 6's console technology for the first time. The game was developed from the ground up for the current console generation and targets 30 frames per second while pushing both platforms “to their absolute limits”. According to Rockstar, this applies to PS5, PS5 Pro, Xbox Series X and Series S. Rockstar does not mention a 60 fps mode. The PS5 Pro gets a sharper image through Sony's AI upscaling PSSR and ray-traced shadows that are exclusive to it. On PS5, GTA 6 uses the DualSense's haptics, adaptive triggers and speaker, plus Tempest 3D Audio; Rockstar and Sony say the game plays best on PS5. Remote Play is supported on PlayStation and Xbox. Via Xbox Cloud Gaming the game can be streamed on Xbox consoles with Series S graphics settings, but not on PC. Rockstar has still not announced a PC version. Depending on the console, the download needs up to 212 GB. There is also a new preload trailer with almost 30 seconds of new footage.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation.Blog", "Eurogamer", "Rockstar Games on X"], "_src": "1689ad08"}, "2026-11-10-steam-deck-framerate-daten": {"titel": "Steam now shows players' average Steam Deck frame rates on store pages", "schlagzeile": "Steam now shows real fps numbers – how well does a game run on the Deck?", "kurz": "Valve now shows the average frame rate on the Steam Deck for many games in Steam. The figures come from players who agreed to share the data. More devices are to follow later.", "zusammenfassung": "Valve has added a new performance display to Steam. In the Steam Deck compatibility section of a store page, clicking “Learn more” now shows the average frame rate on the Steam Deck. A histogram also shows how often each frame rate was measured, so fluctuations are visible too. The data comes from players who agreed to share frame rate data. The value is shown for games that Valve has reviewed for Deck compatibility, i.e. those rated Verified, Playable or Unsupported. Valve explains that the existing rating is based on fixed test criteria and does not match every player's standard for smooth gameplay. An “Unsupported” game may still be quite playable for some, while a Verified game may have low fps. According to Valve, the feature is to be extended to more devices in the future. Whether that includes regular desktop PCs with their many hardware combinations is open.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "GamingOnLinux"], "_src": "6dbc5420"}, "2026-11-10-msi-rtx50-preise-china": {"titel": "Report from China: MSI is said to sharply raise distributor prices for RTX 50 cards in November, RTX 5080 by up to 8,000 yuan", "schlagzeile": "Leak: MSI is said to raise RTX 5080 prices in China by up to 8,000 yuan", "kurz": "According to the Chinese industry channel ChannelGate, MSI is raising distributor prices of all RTX 50 cards in November. For the RTX 5080, the increase is said to be 1,300 to 8,000 yuan, roughly 190 to 1,200 US dollars. These are distributor prices in China, not official consumer prices. MSI has not confirmed this.", "zusammenfassung": "The Chinese industry channel ChannelGate (Board Channels) reports on new MSI price lists for November. According to it, distributor prices of all RTX 50 models in China rise compared with October. For the RTX 5080 series, 1,300 to 8,000 yuan more is cited, for the RTX 5070 Ti 800 to 4,000 yuan and for the RTX 5070 500 to 1,000 yuan. The RTX 5060 Ti is said to rise by 200 to 400 yuan depending on memory, the RTX 5060 by 200 to 500 yuan and even the RTX 3050 by 100 yuan. Wccftech converts the maximum for the RTX 5080 to around 1,200 US dollars. Important: the maximum only applies to individual models, and these are prices for retailers in China, not a new worldwide MSRP. Whether and how strongly this affects Europe is open. The report follows earlier ChannelGate reports about price increases by other board partners. The main reason is said to be the sharply higher memory prices. MSI itself has not commented, so it remains an unconfirmed report.", "ursprungsquelle": "ChannelGate / Board Channels (WeChat), via harukaze5719", "weitere_links": ["IT之家 (ChannelGate)", "TechRadar"], "_src": "59a47e79"}, "2026-11-10-arc-raiders-17-mio": {"titel": "Nexon: Arc Raiders has sold more than 17 million copies after one year, revenue expected to fall in the fourth quarter", "schlagzeile": "Arc Raiders tops 17 million – but sales are slowing", "kurz": "According to publisher Nexon, the extraction shooter Arc Raiders has sold more than 17 million copies by its first birthday. In the third quarter, however, only one million were added. Nexon expects lower revenue in the fourth quarter than at launch a year ago.", "zusammenfassung": "In its quarterly report, Nexon gave new figures for Arc Raiders by Embark Studios. The extraction shooter was released at the end of October 2025 and has since sold more than 17 million copies. According to Nexon, however, only around one million were added in the third quarter of 2026, so sales have slowed significantly. For the fourth quarter, Nexon expects lower revenue from the game than in the prior-year quarter, which included its successful launch. Compared with the previous quarter, revenue is expected to stay roughly flat. According to Nexon, revenue was within its outlook, and the Frozen Trail update brought back former players and won new ones. Arc Raiders remains one of Nexon's most important titles and was the main reason for the revenue growth in the first nine months of the year. It is still open whether a dedicated PvE mode will come permanently; it already exists in China.", "_src": "95842a04"}, "2026-11-10-nvidia-fbi-sammelklagen": {"titel": "Espionage suspicion around NVIDIA CEO Huang: according to Trump the FBI is looking into the case, law firms seek investors for lawsuits", "schlagzeile": "NVIDIA spy affair: FBI looks into the case, investor lawsuits loom", "kurz": "In the case of the alleged Chinese spy close to NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang, the FBI is now looking into it, according to US President Trump. Whether any investigation also targets Huang is unclear. Several US law firms are seeking investors for possible class actions against NVIDIA.", "zusammenfassung": "The affair involving NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang and the alleged Chinese spy Alice Huang is widening. According to Spiegel and Reuters, US President Donald Trump said the FBI is looking into the case. It is unclear whether the review also concerns Jensen Huang himself; despite the same surname, the two are not related. Trump defended Huang and said, in essence, that he believes him that he knew nothing about any spying. Huang had previously admitted the relationship and publicly apologized, and NVIDIA's board has started an investigation with outside experts. According to PC Gamer, several US law firms, including Rosen Law Firm, are recruiting investors for possible lawsuits over misleading statements. According to the Guardian, a lawsuit has already been filed in San José accusing NVIDIA and Huang of concealing a possible security risk. Alice Huang's employer, Megaspeed, is suspected of bringing NVIDIA chips into China without permission; NVIDIA and Megaspeed had previously denied this. According to PC Gamer, Huang is to testify behind closed doors before congressional committees on November 18. None of the allegations have been settled in court so far.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "79f7d817"}, "2026-11-10-chrome-zero-day": {"titel": "Chrome 157 fixes nine vulnerabilities, including the actively exploited CVE-2026-125350", "schlagzeile": "Chrome flaw already under attack – update to version 157 now", "kurz": "Google has released a Chrome update with nine security fixes. A flaw in the browser's XML component is already being actively exploited. Safe versions are 157.0.8103.50/.51 for Windows and Mac and 157.0.8103.50 for Linux.", "zusammenfassung": "Google has released a security update for Chrome that closes nine vulnerabilities, reports Golem. According to Google, at least one of them is already being actively exploited: CVE-2026-125350. It is a use-after-free bug in the component that processes XML data; the severity is rated high, but Google has not yet given a CVSS score. Google does not say how or against whom the flaw is being exploited. It is also unclear whether users have to click anything for an attack. Six of the remaining eight flaws are rated high and two medium; affected components include the V8 JavaScript engine, WebGL and interfaces to the GPU and file system. As usual, Google is holding back technical details until most users have updated. Safe versions are 157.0.8103.50/.51 for Windows and macOS and 157.0.8103.50 for Linux. Other Chromium browsers such as Edge, Vivaldi or Brave are likely affected too and should receive updates in the coming days. Tip: Help › About Google Chrome starts the update check; then restart the browser.", "_src": "3c9a011f"}, "2026-11-10-switch-eshop-geschenke": {"titel": "Switch system update 23.5.0 prepares a gifting feature in the Nintendo eShop for family groups", "schlagzeile": "Switch and Switch 2: gifting games is coming soon – but only within the family", "kurz": "With system update 23.5.0, Nintendo is preparing the ability to gift eShop games. The feature goes live with an eShop update in mid-November. Gifts can only go to members of your own family group.", "zusammenfassung": "Nintendo has released system update 23.5.0 for Switch 2 and the original Switch. It prepares a new feature: digital games, DLC and upgrade packs from the eShop can soon be given as gifts. The catch: recipients must be members of your own Nintendo Account family group, which has up to eight members. According to Nintendo, supervised child accounts cannot send gifts, some products are excluded and the number of gift purchases per period is limited; Nintendo does not give exact limits. When buying, you tick \"Give as a Gift\" on the product page, choose the recipient and their console and pay as usual. The gift arrives immediately in the recipient's HOME Menu. The feature is only activated with an eShop update: the patch notes name November 17, while Nintendo of America writes November 16, probably because of the time zone. On Switch 2, 23.5.0 also lets you set accessibility options during initial setup. Anyone who wants to give games to friends outside the family group still has to use eShop gift cards.", "weitere_links": ["VGChartz (patch notes)", "Nintendo of America on X (hint)"], "_src": "51b1c15b"}, "2026-11-10-mesa-26-3": {"titel": "Mesa 26.3 released: AMD Anti-Lag for RADV, Nova Lake graphics enabled by default, Vulkan Video for NVK", "schlagzeile": "Linux graphics driver Mesa 26.3: Anti-Lag for Radeon and more Vulkan", "kurz": "The open-source graphics driver collection Mesa 26.3 is out. Radeon users get the Vulkan extension for AMD Anti-Lag via RADV, and Intel Nova Lake graphics is no longer experimental. There is also Vulkan Video for the NVIDIA driver NVK and many Vulkan improvements.", "zusammenfassung": "Mesa 26.3 has been released, the fourth major release of the year of the open-source OpenGL and Vulkan drivers for Linux, report Phoronix and 9to5Linux. For gamers with a Radeon card, the most important new feature is VK_AMD_anti_lag in the RADV Vulkan driver, the Vulkan interface for AMD's Anti-Lag to reduce input latency. RADV also brings improvements for early GCN GPUs and support for GFX1171. On the Intel side, Nova Lake graphics is now enabled by default and no longer experimental, and the new Jay shader compiler is switched on. Intel also enables buffer compression, which according to Phoronix should improve gaming performance with DXVK, i.e. for Windows games via Proton. The open-source NVIDIA driver NVK gets Vulkan Video for video acceleration. There are also many new Vulkan extensions for Arm Mali, PowerVR and other drivers. Mesa 26.3 is available on FreeDesktop.org; most distributions will ship it with upcoming package updates. How much Anti-Lag brings in individual games depends on whether the game or translation layer uses it; no measurements are available yet.", "weitere_links": ["9to5Linux"], "_src": "24e0a075"}, "2026-11-10-take-two-ki-decompiling": {"titel": "Take-Two strengthens technical and legal defences against AI-assisted reverse engineering of GTA 6", "schlagzeile": "Unofficial GTA 6 PC port via AI? Take-Two steps up tech and legal defences", "kurz": "Take-Two boss Strauss Zelnick takes AI-assisted decompiling seriously and wants to strengthen technical protection and legal action. The background is concern that GTA 6 could appear unofficially on PC. Take-Two says nothing about an official PC version or a disc; that will come from Rockstar.", "zusammenfassung": "Ahead of the GTA 6 launch on November 19, there is growing concern that AI tools could decompile console games faster and spread them as unofficial PC ports. IGN asked Take-Two CEO Strauss Zelnick about this in an interview and during the investor Q&A. Zelnick says the industry was long largely spared from piracy because of file sizes, complexity and server connections, but that is becoming harder. Take-Two is therefore focusing on strengthening its technical defences and its legal activities. He expects piracy to affect the business \"to a greater or lesser extent\", but considers it manageable and does not see it as a financial threat. According to IGN, part of the concern relates to PS5 security: the homebrew scene is working on jailbreaks for newer firmware, and GTA 6 is said to require a recent firmware. Zelnick left open when GTA 6 will officially come to PC. According to Insider Gaming (citing Variety), he pointed out that such information always comes from the label, i.e. Rockstar; the same applies to a possible disc version. At launch, GTA 6 is only released for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. A former Rockstar North technical director recently speculated that Rockstar could bring a PC port forward for this reason, but that is not confirmed.", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming"], "_src": "a25dcecd"}, "2026-11-10-sega-newsletter-leak": {"titel": "SEGA: attack on newsletter provider ARARA exposes around 2.2 million email addresses", "schlagzeile": "SEGA data leak: 2.2 million email addresses stolen from a service provider", "kurz": "In an attack on the Japanese newsletter provider ARARA, around 2.2 million email addresses of SEGA customers were stolen. According to SEGA, names, passwords and payment data are not affected, nor are SEGA Accounts. Customers should watch out for fake SEGA emails.", "zusammenfassung": "SEGA confirmed a data leak at its newsletter provider ARARA on November 9. 2,196,044 email addresses are affected; for 92,273 of them, information related to delivery also leaked, and exactly what is still being investigated. According to SEGA, it concerns eleven newsletters from SEGA and SEGA Fave sent between July and October 2026, for example about arcade games such as CHUNITHM and maimai, the Tokyo Game Show and lottery promotions. According to SEGA, names, dates of birth, addresses, phone numbers, credit card data and passwords are not affected. Email addresses from SEGA Account also run through a different system and are not part of the leak. Misuse of the data has not been confirmed so far. ARARA itself had reported the breach in early November; according to BleepingComputer and Infosecurity Magazine, around 77 million email addresses from about 380 corporate customers are affected there in total, apparently via a vulnerability in web servers. SEGA has suspended sending via ARARA and plans to inform those affected individually. Anyone who received SEGA newsletters should be especially alert to phishing in emails referring to SEGA.", "weitere_links": ["SEGA (notice, Japanese)", "Infosecurity Magazine"], "_src": "ba66609c"}, "2026-11-10-take-two-gta6-vorbestellungen": {"titel": "Take-Two: GTA 6 pre-orders far above expectations, up to $3.5 billion expected in the launch quarter", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: pre-orders \"far above expectations\" – Take-Two expects a record", "kurz": "Ten days before the launch of GTA 6, Take-Two reports pre-orders at \"unprecedented\" levels. For the current quarter the company expects net bookings of $3.35 to $3.5 billion. Take-Two still gives no concrete pre-order figures.", "zusammenfassung": "Take-Two presented its results for the second quarter of fiscal year 2027 on November 9, and GTA 6 was the centre of attention. According to CEO Strauss Zelnick, pre-orders are \"far above expectations\" and continue to reach \"unprecedented\" levels, report Insider Gaming, Eurogamer and PC Gamer. For the current third quarter, which includes the November 19 launch, Take-Two expects net bookings of $3.35 to $3.5 billion. According to PC Gamer, that is even slightly below the analyst estimate of $3.51 billion (LSEG, via Reuters). For the full fiscal year 2027 the company expects $8 to $8.2 billion. Take-Two still gives no concrete pre-order figures, because the raw numbers could be misleading without points of comparison. The past quarter was weaker: net bookings of $1.6 billion were below expectations and 18 percent below the previous year. One reason is NBA 2K27, which launched well but stayed below forecast; Zelnick sees anticipation for GTA 6 as a contributing factor. Take-Two also shared new sales figures: GTA 5 stands at around 235 million copies, and Red Dead Redemption 2 is approaching 90 million. The GTA series as a whole has sold almost 480 million units.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "Eurogamer", "Insider Gaming (GTA 5)", "Insider Gaming (RDR2)"], "_src": "38d7088e"}, "2026-11-10-skydance-games-entlassungen": {"titel": "Skydance Games lays off staff and scales down projects – one month after the Paramount–Warner Bros. merger", "schlagzeile": "After mega-merger: Skydance Games lays off developers and trims projects", "kurz": "Skydance Games has cut jobs and \"scaled down some of its projects\". This comes one month after the merger of Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery. The company does not say how many people are affected.", "zusammenfassung": "Skydance Games has confirmed layoffs, report IGN and PC Gamer, citing a statement to Variety. The company said it decided to scale down some projects, and roles are affected as a result; this is not a judgement on the talent or dedication of those affected. Employees of Paramount Games Studio, founded only in June, were the first to report that they had been let go. Paramount Games includes, among others, Skydance Interactive and Skydance New Media. Recently announced there were games such as Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles: The Last Ronin as well as adaptations of Yellowstone, Tulsa King and Lioness. It is not known which projects are being cut. Skydance does not say how many jobs are going; according to Insider Gaming, at least 30 developers are affected, probably more. The cuts come around a month after the merger of Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery under the Skydance umbrella was approved. What this means for the Warner Bros. Games division is still open.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer"], "_src": "a7836025"}, "2026-11-10-rdna5-gfx13-linux": {"titel": "AMD publishes Linux driver patches for GFX13, the next-generation graphics IP (probably RDNA 5)", "schlagzeile": "RDNA 5 draws closer: AMD sends first Linux drivers for GFX13", "kurz": "AMD has published more than 12,600 lines of Linux kernel driver code for GFX13, the next Radeon graphics generation. Most likely this is RDNA 5. So far the patches reveal no new details on performance or features.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD developer Alex Deucher has published a patch series that prepares the AMDGPU Linux kernel driver for GFX13, report Phoronix and VideoCardz. GFX13 is AMD's next graphics IP and very likely stands for RDNA 5; AMD has not officially confirmed the name. The eight patches comprise more than 12,600 lines of code, excluding the usual large header files. They also include support for the specific variants GFX 13.0.1 and GFX 13.0.4. According to Phoronix, the patches reveal little so far about the capabilities or new features of RDNA 5. GFX13 patches for the LLVM compiler have existed since the beginning of the year; now the kernel driver follows. Phoronix expects support in Linux kernel 7.5. Other building blocks that are likely part of RDNA 5 GPUs, such as Display Core Next 6, are already in the kernel. AMD often publishes early Linux drivers months before market launch; AMD gives no date for RDNA 5 graphics cards.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz"], "_src": "c780eb89"}, "2026-11-10-nvidia-megaspeed-nyt": {"titel": "NYT report: NVIDIA allegedly intervened in US investigation into suspected AI chip smuggler Megaspeed", "schlagzeile": "Report: NVIDIA allegedly slowed an investigation into chip smuggling", "kurz": "According to the New York Times, NVIDIA's general counsel contacted the US Commerce Department directly in 2025 while it was investigating the company Megaspeed over suspected chip smuggling to China. The investigation stalled and was handed to the Justice Department. This is a report; we do not have a statement from NVIDIA.", "zusammenfassung": "After the report on the NVIDIA board's investigation involving CEO Jensen Huang, new pressure is building: according to Wccftech, the New York Times reports on NVIDIA's role in investigations into the company Megaspeed. The Singapore-based data centre company was suspected of acting as a front to move smuggled NVIDIA AI accelerators past US export controls into China. Megaspeed is run by Alice Huang, who according to US intelligence agencies worked for Beijing; she is the same woman with whom Jensen Huang has admitted an affair. According to the report, NVIDIA's general counsel Tim Teter contacted the Commerce Department's Bureau of Industry and Security directly in 2025. He reportedly claimed that Trump nominee Jeff Kessler had allowed him this direct contact. Several officials are said to have seen this as a serious breach of normal procedure. The investigation then stalled and was handed over to the Justice Department. Company lawyers talking to authorities is normal in itself; according to the report, the nature of the contact is what is disputed. According to Wccftech, Huang faces a closed-door hearing in the US Congress on November 18. The allegations come from media reports; we did not have a statement from NVIDIA on them.", "_src": "12d2733c"}, "2026-11-09-dark-heresy-release": {"titel": "Owlcat's Warhammer 40,000: Dark Heresy launches on January 28, 2027 for PC, PS5 and Xbox Series", "schlagzeile": "Warhammer 40k: Dark Heresy has a date – launching January 28, 2027", "kurz": "Owlcat Games has announced the release date for Warhammer 40,000: Dark Heresy. The tactical RPG launches on 28.01.2027 for PC, PS5 and Xbox Series X/S, with a Switch 2 version to follow later. You play an Inquisitor hunting heretics.", "zusammenfassung": "Owlcat Games has announced the release date of its tactical RPG Warhammer 40,000: Dark Heresy with a press release and trailer, Eurogamer and GameStar report. The game launches on January 28, 2027 for PC, PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X/S. A date for Switch 2 is to follow \"at a later date\". Dark Heresy builds on Warhammer 40,000: Rogue Trader, which Owlcat released a few years ago. This time you play an Inquisitor who tracks down heretics and dark influences in the 41st millennium. According to Eurogamer, Owlcat has overhauled many of the underlying systems. A beta containing the complete first act has been running for some time and is playable by buyers of the Founders Edition. This beta will be switched off on January 7 while Owlcat prepares the game for launch. Eurogamer recalls that Rogue Trader was praised for its setting and combat but struggled with bugs and weak performance at launch. How well Dark Heresy runs at release therefore remains to be seen. Owlcat is also working on an RPG based on the science fiction series The Expanse.", "weitere_links": ["GameStar"], "_src": "e9845177"}, "2026-11-09-ps-portal-speicher-japan": {"titel": "Sony launches a new PlayStation Portal model in Japan with internal storage for future features", "schlagzeile": "New PS Portal with its own storage – Sony hints at more features", "kurz": "Sony is releasing a new model of the PlayStation Portal with internal storage in Japan on 10.12.2026. According to Sony Japan, the storage is intended for future features, with details to follow later. The price stays at 39,980 yen, pre-orders start on 13.11.2026, and whether the model will also come to Europe is unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "Sony is releasing a revised model of the PlayStation Portal in Japan, IGN reports, citing Sony Japan's official blog. The most important difference from the previous device is internal storage. Sony writes that it added the storage with future features in mind and will share details once they are finalized. Sony has not yet said what those features will be. At the same time, Sony is changing the official Japanese name from \"PlayStation Portal Remote Player\" to \"PlayStation Portal Player\". In the blog, Sony also stresses that even players without a PS5 can play PS5 games on the Portal; this refers to the cloud streaming for PS Plus Premium members that Sony introduced last year. IGN sees the storage and the name change as a possible step away from a pure Remote Play accessory towards a more standalone handheld; that is an assessment, not an announcement from Sony. The new model launches in Japan on December 10, pre-orders begin on November 13, and the price remains the same at 39,980 yen. It is set to Japanese only and requires a Japanese PSN account. Whether and when it will come to other regions is not known.", "_src": "e6a33542"}, "2026-11-09-sshole-angriffe": {"titel": "OpenSSH flaw \"SSHole\" (CVE-2026-123158) is being actively exploited, attackers gain root on Alpine systems", "schlagzeile": "OpenSSH flaw \"SSHole\" now actively exploited – update Alpine servers", "kurz": "The OpenSSH flaw on musl systems such as Alpine Linux that we reported on 05.11.2026 is now being actively exploited. Several security firms report attacks, and in one honeypot attackers gained root access. The flaw is now called \"SSHole\" (CVE-2026-123158); the fix is OpenSSH 10.6p2 followed by a restart of sshd.", "zusammenfassung": "The OpenSSH flaw we reported on November 5 is now being actively attacked, BleepingComputer, SecurityWeek and The Hacker News report. It now carries the nickname \"SSHole\" and the identifier CVE-2026-123158 (CVSS 8.1). Affected is OpenSSH before version 10.6p2 on Linux systems using the musl C library without PAM, such as the default configuration of Alpine Linux; the discoverer also names OpenWrt, Buildroot, Yocto and many Docker images as worth checking. With a very long password of 257 to 1,024 bytes, attackers can log in to accounts that are not supposed to accept a password at all. According to BleepingComputer, exploitation attempts began on November 5, when a proof of concept appeared a few hours after the fix. The firm Previdian confirms successful root access on its own honeypot running real Alpine Linux and counted 20 attempts from 13 IP addresses in nine countries by November 8. GreyNoise recorded the first successful exploitation in the wild on November 7 and observed 16 successful attack chains: the attackers explored the system and containers, queried cloud metadata, tried to read password hashes and root SSH keys, and attempted to add their own keys for persistent access. The fix is OpenSSH 10.6p2 or the distribution's patched package; Alpine has released packages for all branches from 3.16 onwards. Important: sshd must be restarted after the update, otherwise the old version keeps running; according to watchTowr, mainly botnets and crypto miners are using the flaw so far. As an immediate measure, PasswordAuthentication no helps. Admins should also check logs for unexpected \"Accepted password for\" entries on accounts without a password and for unknown SSH keys.", "weitere_links": ["SecurityWeek", "The Hacker News", "Help Net Security"], "_src": "36ee778e"}, "2026-11-09-gta6-festival-miami": {"titel": "Rockstar announces \"Grand Theft Auto VI: The Festival\" on November 21 in Miami with Travis Scott, Cardi B and Justice", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 gets its own music festival – with Travis Scott and Cardi B", "kurz": "Rockstar is celebrating the launch of GTA 6 with a music festival in Miami. \"Grand Theft Auto VI: The Festival\" takes place on 21.11.2026 at Mana Wynwood, featuring Travis Scott, Cardi B, Kodak Black and Justice, among others. Tickets are awarded by lottery, and the game itself comes out on 19.11.2026.", "zusammenfassung": "Rockstar Games has announced a music festival on X to mark the launch of GTA 6, VGC and Eurogamer report. \"Grand Theft Auto VI: The Festival\" takes place on November 21 at Mana Wynwood in Miami, two days after the game's release on November 19. According to Rockstar, artists from the game and the official soundtrack will perform. Confirmed acts, according to VGC, include Travis Scott, Don Toliver, Kodak Black, Sofaygo, Cardi B, Ca7riel and Paco Amoroso, Justice, Metro Boomin, Rauw & Friends, Suero and Tainy, plus several back-to-back DJ sets. Tickets are handled by the provider DICE and are distributed via a lottery. According to Rockstar, you have to sign up for the pre-sale lottery by Tuesday, November 10, 4 p.m. Eastern Time (10 p.m. in Austria); the chance at tickets then comes on Wednesday at 12 p.m. Eastern Time (6 p.m. our time). Two soundtracks for the game will be released on CD, vinyl and streaming services: \"GTA 6: The Album\" with 34 new songs on November 19, including Travis Scott and Keith Richards, and on December 11 \"Grand Theft Auto VI: Original Score\" with 30 pieces by the French electronic duo Justice.", "weitere_links": ["Rockstar Games on X", "Rockstar Games on X (ticket lottery)", "Eurogamer"], "_src": "31cad77d"}, "2026-11-09-amd-ssd-fix-26-11-1": {"titel": "AMD confirms constant SSD writes caused by Radeon driver, fix expected with Adrenalin 26.11.1", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver eats SSD lifespan: fix expected with 26.11.1", "kurz": "Follow-up to our report from 08.11.2026: according to TechPowerUp and PC Gamer, the bug in which a Radeon driver service constantly writes to the SSD is to be fixed with Adrenalin 26.11.1. According to TechPowerUp, versions 26.10.1 and 26.10.2 are affected, and there is no date for the new driver yet. Users report losing about 1 percent of SSD health per month.", "zusammenfassung": "There is a fix in sight for the Radeon driver bug with constant SSD writes that we reported on November 8. According to TechPowerUp, AMD has confirmed that the Adrenalin 26.10.1 and 26.10.2 drivers are affected and that the fix is to come with version 26.11.1. PC Gamer quotes AMD representative AMD_Vik on Reddit as saying the problem \"should be fixed\" in 26.11.1; there is no exact date, but according to PC Gamer the driver is expected later this month. The culprit is the atieclxx.exe service from AMD's External Events Utility, which handles things like detecting monitors and Radeon software hotkeys and apparently writes data in an endless loop. Reported rates range from 0.3 to 1.5 MB/s, and one Reddit user cites a sustained 5 MB/s. A user on X measured 19.5 GB of writes in 12 hours and believes the bug has existed since Adrenalin 26.7.1 from June. On Reddit, users report that their SSD health drops by about 1 percent per month as a result; these are user reports, not measurements by AMD. Not every system is affected, and PC Gamer could not reproduce the bug itself. As a workaround, TechPowerUp mentions disabling the AMD External Events Utility, which can cause display issues, or disabling Resizable BAR, which can cost performance. TechPowerUp rather advises waiting for the official driver.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer", "ComputerBase"], "_src": "fc743806"}, "2026-11-09-amdlss5-2-radeon": {"titel": "Mod AMDLSS5 2.0 brings DLSS 5-style neural rendering to Radeon cards with its own engine", "schlagzeile": "Mod brings DLSS 5 neural rendering to Radeon – now much faster", "kurz": "The unofficial mod AMDLSS5 has been released in version 2.0 and aims to bring DLSS 5-style neural rendering to Radeon cards. According to the developer, it now runs on its own engine and is significantly faster than other mods. The measurements come only from the developer. The mod has nothing to do with AMD or NVIDIA.", "zusammenfassung": "Wccftech reports on version 2.0 of the community mod AMDLSS5 by developer Wehaveall. It aims to bring DLSS 5-style neural rendering, meaning AI enhancements to lighting and materials, to AMD Radeon cards by hooking into existing DirectX 12 upscaling pipelines. New is a dedicated engine that replaces the previous reliance on another mod and is said to have less overhead. In a Reddit post, the developer shares PresentMon figures from Resident Evil Requiem at 4K with FSR on an RX 9070 XT: 101.2 fps on average and 78.5 fps in the 1% lows, compared with 91.3 and 66.0 with version 1.6.1 and 61.6 and 55.5 with other mods. That is where the advertised 64 percent more fps comes from, but only compared with other mods, not with the unmodded game or NVIDIA's actual DLSS 5. These are the developer's figures from a single scene with one card; there are no independent tests yet. Newly supported are PRAGMATA, Nioh 3 and GTA V Enhanced, the latter only in offline Story Mode with BattlEye disabled. The main targets are the RX 9070 and RX 9070 XT; the RX 9060 series should theoretically work, and RX 7000 cards have experimental alpha support, but according to Wccftech the developer has not validated either on real hardware. There are also 39 color presets, local tone mapping, improved ambient occlusion and indirect lighting, and revised 2x frame generation in selected games. The mod is free on GitHub, but the source code of the new engine has not been published yet.", "_src": "23e75a0d"}, "2026-11-09-amazon-us-amd-vor-nvidia": {"titel": "Amazon US in October: AMD sells more graphics cards than NVIDIA, RX 9070 XT is the best seller", "schlagzeile": "Amazon US: AMD sold more graphics cards than NVIDIA in October", "kurz": "According to Amazon US sales figures for October 2026, AMD sold slightly more graphics cards than NVIDIA: around 9,200 versus 8,900 units. The best-selling card was the Radeon RX 9070 XT with about 3,300 units. NVIDIA still made more revenue thanks to higher average prices. The figures come from a data collector, not from the manufacturers.", "zusammenfassung": "Wccftech reports on Amazon US sales figures for October 2026 compiled by the data collector TechEpiphany. According to them, AMD narrowly sold the most graphics cards there in October: around 9,200 units compared with about 8,900 for NVIDIA. Wccftech calls this notable because Amazon US is usually dominated by NVIDIA, while AMD more often leads in places like Germany. NVIDIA stays ahead in revenue, as its average selling price was $1,313 compared with $915 for AMD. The best seller was the Radeon RX 9070 XT with about 3,300 units; the RTX 5070 Ti managed only around a third of that. Second place went to the RTX 5060 Ti (8 and 16 GB combined) with about 2,250 units, followed by the RX 9060 XT with around 2,150. The RTX 5070 stayed below 2,000 units, and the RTX 5090 reached only about 150 due to poor availability. Even the old Arc A380 sold more often, with around 500 units. According to the data, Intel reached about 6.22 percent share, driven by the Arc B570, B580 and Arc Pro cards. Wccftech sees the sharply increased prices as the main reason buyers are turning to cheaper cards. Important: the figures cover only one shop in the US and do not come from AMD, NVIDIA or Amazon themselves; they are therefore only a snapshot, not market shares for the overall market.", "_src": "1307b37c"}, "2026-11-09-bit-reactor-entlassungen": {"titel": "Star Wars Zero Company: developer Bit Reactor lays off staff despite good reviews and a million sales", "schlagzeile": "Star Wars Zero Company: studio lays off staff – despite hit and 84 Metascore", "kurz": "Bit Reactor, the studio behind Star Wars Zero Company, has laid off staff. VGC reports this based on LinkedIn posts by affected developers. Yet the game was well reviewed and, according to EA, has sold one million copies. How many jobs are affected is unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "Bit Reactor, the developer of Star Wars Zero Company, has laid off staff, VGC reports, citing the site Bespin Bulletin. Several developers, including a senior environment artist, a UI engineer, a producer and a senior QA analyst, wrote on LinkedIn in recent days that they were affected. How many positions are being cut in total is not known. According to reports, the studio had furloughed around 80 percent of its staff without pay before the release in August because money was running short. In October, studio head Greg Foertsch said that some of the furloughed staff were returning; according to reports, this brought the studio back to more than half its former size. It is unclear whether returnees are now affected as well or only people who were not brought back after the furlough. At least one affected developer writes that he was laid off after three months of furlough. That is bitter because Star Wars Zero Company launched at the end of August to very good reviews and stands at 84 points on Metacritic. On October 9, the official EA Star Wars account reported one million units sold. VGC does not cite an official statement from Bit Reactor on the layoffs.", "weitere_links": ["GameStar"], "_src": "52d9b77e"}, "2026-11-09-notepadpp-7zip-luecken": {"titel": "Notepad++ 8.9.9 fixes six security flaws, 7-Zip 26.06 fixes unspecified vulnerabilities", "schlagzeile": "Notepad++ and 7-Zip: updates plug security holes – update them yourself", "kurz": "Notepad++ 8.9.9 fixes six security flaws, the most serious rated high. 7-Zip 26.06 also fixes vulnerabilities according to its developer, but gives no details. 7-Zip has no update function, so you have to update it yourself. On Windows, winget makes that easy.", "zusammenfassung": "Two widely used Windows tools have received security updates, heise online reports. Notepad++ 8.9.9 by developer Don Ho fixes six security flaws. The most serious is a heap buffer overflow in the SAML decoder of the mimeTools plugin: crafted SAML messages could overwrite memory when decoded and possibly execute malicious code. The advisory rates the risk as high but gives no CVSS score. The other five flaws are considered medium, and according to heise some of them can probably be used to escalate privileges on the system, for example via UAC saving of protected files or window messages. There are no CVE numbers yet. In addition, the version speeds up searching in files and updates the editor component Scintilla to 5.6.9. Notepad++ has its own update check; alternatively, winget update Notepad++.Notepad++ helps. The archiving tool 7-Zip was released in version 26.06 over the weekend. Developer Igor Pavlov only writes that some bugs and vulnerabilities were fixed, without saying which ones or how severe they are. He also improved support for files split with the Linux tool split. Because 7-Zip has no update check, users have to download the new version themselves or use winget upgrade 7zip.7zip on Windows. heise recommends installing all available updates at once with winget upgrade --all.", "weitere_links": ["heise online (7-Zip)"], "_src": "2abed807"}, "2026-11-09-sonicwall-sslvpn-angriffe": {"titel": "SonicWall: SSLVPN flaw under attack, firmware updates fix seven vulnerabilities", "schlagzeile": "SonicWall firewalls: VPN flaw under attack – update now", "kurz": "Attackers appear to be exploiting a flaw in the SSLVPN of SonicWall firewalls that allows SAML sign-in, and with it multi-factor authentication, to be bypassed. SonicWall and the US agency CISA advise updating quickly. The SSLVPN is only vulnerable if SAML is enabled for VPN sign-in. The new firmware fixes seven flaws in total.", "zusammenfassung": "SonicWall published a security advisory on Friday covering seven vulnerabilities in SonicOS, as heise online reports. For one of them, the manufacturer assumes it may already have been used in attacks; the US security agency CISA is also warning. It is CVE-2026-19868 (CVSS 7.1, high): anyone with valid credentials for an alternative sign-in method can use it to bypass SAML authentication, which is used for single sign-on, for example. This apparently also allows the multi-factor authentication enforced via SAML to be circumvented. According to SonicWall, the SSLVPN is only vulnerable if SAML is enabled for SSLVPN logins. The fix is SonicOS 7.3.4-7013 for Gen7 firewalls and 8.2.3-8015 for Gen8 devices, as well as newer versions. The updates close six further flaws, including two with CVSS 8.8 relating to cross-domain policy and session validation, and a heap buffer overflow in the SSL-VPN that can be triggered without authentication (CVSS 7.5). There are also two buffer overflows in TACACS+ and weak password hashing on virtual appliances, all rated medium risk. heise recalls that SonicWall had already reported a critical, maximum-score flaw in SMA1000 appliances in early October. Companies and admins are mainly affected; anyone who manages a SonicWall firewall at home or in the office should update the firmware now.", "_src": "6679ffee"}, "2026-11-08-windows11-app-updates": {"titel": "Windows 11 tests a central page for third-party app updates", "schlagzeile": "End of update pop-ups? Windows 11 tests central app updates", "kurz": "A new 'App updates' page has appeared in the Settings of a Windows 11 26H2 preview build. It is meant to collect updates for third-party programs such as browsers or media players in one place, instead of each app showing its own notices. This will only work if developers register their apps. In Windows Latest's test, not a single provider was registered yet.", "zusammenfassung": "Windows Latest discovered a page called 'App updates' under Settings > Apps in a Windows 11 26H2 preview build. The page was briefly visible in December 2025 and has now reappeared, which according to Windows Latest points to an imminent rollout. The goal is to bundle updates for programs outside the Microsoft Store in one place, instead of each app showing its own pop-ups, like the infamous Java updater used to. The basis is the 'Windows Update Orchestration Platform', which Microsoft presented in 2025. Developers can register their apps there as providers while keeping their own update servers and installers; Windows only handles coordination. MSIX and APPX packages as well as classic Win32 programs are to be supported. To register, developers must supply a script or program that checks for updates; by default, Windows runs this check every 22 hours. Windows is to schedule installation similarly to system updates, taking usage, battery and network into account so you are not interrupted in the middle of work. On Windows Latest's test machine, however, the page reported that no app provider was registered, not even Microsoft itself for Teams or Outlook, and the button to check for updates was greyed out. So this is a feature in testing that cannot be used yet. Whether it really helps depends on how many developers take part; Microsoft does not want to force anyone. Microsoft has not announced a launch date.", "_src": "06466579"}, "2026-11-08-nvidia-board-untersuchung-huang": {"titel": "NVIDIA board launches independent investigation into CEO Jensen Huang", "schlagzeile": "NVIDIA board opens investigation – Huang admits affair", "kurz": "NVIDIA's board has launched an independent investigation after media reported that CEO Jensen Huang had been the target of a foreign intelligence service. In a message to employees published by NVIDIA, Huang admitted he had been unfaithful to his wife. According to the board, there is so far no reason to believe national security or company secrets were compromised. Huang remains CEO.", "zusammenfassung": "NVIDIA published two statements on the evening of 8 November 2026. In the first, the board announces an independent investigation: a committee of independent directors, assisted by outside counsel, will examine whether founder and CEO Jensen Huang was the target of a foreign intelligence effort. The board writes that it has no reason to believe national security or NVIDIA secrets were compromised, but that it will examine all available information. Huang supports the review and will cooperate; the board expresses confidence in him and his leadership team. In the second statement, a message to employees first published by Axios, Huang apologizes to his family and staff and admits he was unfaithful to his wife. The background is reporting by the Financial Times and the New York Times in the preceding days. According to those reports, a memo based on US intelligence attributes a relationship to Huang with a woman named Alice Huang, a former executive at NVIDIA customer Megaspeed; according to the reports, US agencies believed she was an informant for China's Ministry of State Security. Despite the shared surname, the two are not related, according to the reports. Neither the memo nor its basis is public, and neither Huang nor the board addresses the espionage allegations in substance; according to Axios, Huang's message does not name Alice Huang. The board's statement therefore does not confirm the allegations. According to the NYT, the aim was to learn more about US AI chips. NVIDIA spokesperson John Rizzo said, according to ComputerBase, that the events would not slow the company's work. When results of the investigation will be available is unclear; the board says it will provide further updates as appropriate.", "weitere_links": ["heise online", "IGN"], "_src": "ae83deda"}, "2026-11-08-layden-ps5-300": {"titel": "Former PlayStation boss Shawn Layden: Sony needs a $300 PS5 rather than a $1,200 PS6", "schlagzeile": "Ex-PlayStation boss: No $1,200 PS6 – rather a $300 PS5", "kurz": "Former PlayStation boss Shawn Layden advises Sony to build a much cheaper PS5 instead of an expensive PS6. 'The innovation needs to come not from making PS6 for $1,200. It's to make another PS5 for $300,' he said on The Trophy Room podcast. The PS5 is the first platform that has become more expensive over time, he said. This says nothing about official PS6 plans.", "zusammenfassung": "Shawn Layden, former president and CEO of Sony Interactive Entertainment America, commented on the next PlayStation on The Trophy Room podcast, as IGN reports. In his view, a PS6 that mainly relies on more ray tracing and more teraflops does not offer enough real innovation. 'I think we have enough power in the machine,' Layden said. In his view, true innovation would not be a PS6 for 1,200 dollars, but another PS5 for 300 dollars. He pointed out that the PS2 was available for 99 dollars at the end of its life, while the PS5 is the first platform he has seen go up in price over time. Sony should make the console smaller and cheaper; the chip and operating system are good enough for the games people want to play. IGN adds context: at launch six years ago, the PS5 cost 499 dollars in the US and the Digital Edition 399 dollars. Directly from PlayStation, the standard version now costs 649, the Digital Edition 599 and the PS5 Pro 899 dollars. Sony attributes the increases to the difficult economic environment. There is little official information about the PS6: Sony said in May that it was still deciding on the timing, and a February report mentioned a possible delay to 2028 or 2029. Layden has not been at Sony for years; his statements are a personal opinion and not information about Sony's plans. No concrete PS6 price is known; the 1,200 dollars is Layden's pointed example.", "_src": "5da916e2"}, "2026-11-08-amd-radeon-ssd-writes": {"titel": "AMD confirms a Radeon driver bug that keeps writing to the SSD", "schlagzeile": "Radeon driver keeps writing to the SSD while idle", "kurz": "Some AMD Radeon users report that the graphics driver keeps writing to the system SSD even when the PC is otherwise idle. The process blamed is atieclxx, the AMD External Events Client Module. According to Wccftech and Neowin, AMD has acknowledged the issue and is working on a fix; it is not listed in the notes for Adrenalin 26.10.2 of 30.10.2026. Not every system appears to be affected, and how much this actually shortens an SSD's lifespan has not been established.", "zusammenfassung": "On 8.11.2026 Wccftech and Neowin reported a bug in AMD's Radeon graphics drivers that can cause constant writes to the system drive even when the computer is otherwise idle. The trigger is said to be the atieclxx process, the AMD External Events Client Module, which belongs to AMD External Events Utility and among other things handles monitor changes, hotkeys and FreeSync. User reports often sit between about 0.3 and 1.5 megabytes per second, while individual reports mention around 5 megabytes per second. Extrapolated, uninterrupted writes at 5 MB/s would theoretically mean about 432 gigabytes of host writes a day; Wccftech stresses that this is an upper bound under continuous load and does not automatically equal the amount actually written to NAND. Whether and how much the bug shortens an SSD's lifespan has not been established, according to the reports. The problem is said to be not entirely new and to appear on Windows 10 and Windows 11 across various Radeon cards and Adrenalin versions; some PCs on the current 26.10.2 driver show no unusual load, according to users. An AMD staffer named AMD_Matt is said to have confirmed the behaviour in October as a genuine issue under investigation. Another representative, AMD_Vik, later indicated that a fix had likely already been submitted but may have missed the cutoff for the next driver release. Adrenalin Edition 26.10.2, released on 30.10.2026, does not mention the bug in its official release notes. Neowin adds that AMD pointed to an interaction with Microsoft's PCIe filter driver and Resizable BAR. As workarounds, both outlets name temporarily stopping the AMD External Events Utility service through Windows' service manager or disabling Resizable BAR; either step can affect FreeSync, Adrenalin hotkeys or gaming performance. Some users nevertheless report that FreeSync and ReBAR kept working after the service was stopped. Anyone who wants to check whether their PC is affected should look in Resource Monitor on the Disk tab for sustained write activity from atieclxx. A driver update containing the fix is not yet available, according to the reports.", "weitere_links": ["Neowin"], "_src": "f2340f0a"}, "2026-11-08-gpu-preise-plus40": {"titel": "Graphics card prices: almost 40 percent higher on average since August", "schlagzeile": "Graphics cards have risen almost 40 percent since August", "kurz": "GameStar compared current graphics card street prices: since August 2026, the models it tracked have become almost 40 percent more expensive on average. Between January and August the change, excluding the RTX 5090, was still only around three percent. According to the analysis, the RTX 5090 itself rose from about 3,000 euros in January through 4,350 euros in August to around 7,500 euros now.", "zusammenfassung": "On 8.11.2026 GameStar published a new look at current street prices for graphics cards. In August the same review of 16 models from AMD, NVIDIA and Intel, excluding the RTX 5090, had still shown an average change of about three percent compared with January 2026. Since then the trend for virtually all of the cards covered has pointed only upward. The report deliberately leaves the RTX 5090 out of the average because, as a flagship with 32 gigabytes of memory, it occupies a special position. Its price is said to have risen from around 3,000 euros in January through 4,350 euros in August to about 7,500 euros now. Below that, down to the RTX 5050, the picture also looks grim: if the direction holds, the RTX 5080 will soon sit above 2,000 euros, and almost 400 euros would be due for the entry-level RTX 5050. Across the models tracked, GameStar arrives at an average increase of almost 40 percent since August. The text names the ongoing AI boom as the cause. Hardware companies such as AMD are also said to state clearly that they see themselves primarily as data-center firms rather than gaming companies. Every forecast of the memory and hardware crunch known to the author assumes the situation will last for years and get worse rather than better. Precise price predictions are difficult; the author nonetheless expects prices to keep rising and availability to get worse. The percentage figures come from GameStar's own price analysis; aside from the 5090, 5080 and 5050, the text does not list individual model prices in a table.", "_src": "cf2fd89d"}, "2026-11-08-12v2x6-kabel-rtx-pro-6000": {"titel": "Damaged 12V-2×6 cables found on two RTX PRO 6000 cards despite a premium power supply", "schlagzeile": "$32,000 PC: 12V-2×6 cables crumble on two RTX PRO 6000 cards", "kurz": "A Reddit user with two NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell cards found damaged sleeving on both 12V-2×6 power cables, even though the cards were limited to 500 watts. The damage appeared on both the GPU and PSU side, but nothing melted. The power supply is a Seasonic PRIME TX-1600 Noctua Edition. The cause has not been measured; this is a single case.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports on a Reddit post by user Doomslayer606, who runs two NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell cards in the 600-watt Workstation Edition with 96 GB of GDDR7 each in his workstation. According to VideoCardz, the cards together cost over 32,000 dollars. They are powered by a Seasonic PRIME TX-1600 Noctua Edition with two native 16-pin cables. Although the owner had limited both cards to 500 watts, he noticed on both cables that the sleeving of two individual wires was stiff, cracked and easy to peel off. The damage appeared both at the graphics card connectors and on the power supply side, where it was even worse, although those connectors were rarely touched. The actual wire insulation remained intact, and there were no visible signs of melting or discoloration on the cards or the power supply. Before that, the user had noticed that a GPU or an NVMe SSD occasionally disappeared from the PCIe bus, which is why he had reseated the cables several times. He suspects localized overheating caused by unevenly distributed current, but temperature and current were not measured. As a consequence, he has bought replacement cables with thermal protection and is considering limiting the cards to 450 watts; at 300 watts he lost 40 to 50 percent of performance in his workloads. According to the report, Seasonic and NVIDIA have not commented. It is a single case without manufacturer confirmation, but it fits the long series of problems surrounding the 16-pin connector. VideoCardz advises checking power connectors regularly without constantly unplugging and replugging them.", "_src": "a3d9d41a"}, "2026-11-08-rtings-woled-edge-rot": {"titel": "RTINGS long-term test: 14 of 16 older WOLED TVs show pixel failures along the edges", "schlagzeile": "'Edge rot': 14 of 16 WOLED TVs develop dead pixels at the edges", "kurz": "In RTINGS' 18,000-hour longevity test, 14 of 16 TVs with LG Display WOLED panels developed dead pixels along the screen edges. RTINGS calls this 'edge rot'; it has nothing to do with burn-in. The three QD-OLED TVs tested were not affected. Mostly 2020 to 2022 models are affected; newer panels from 2024 onward have not been tested.", "zusammenfassung": "The testing site RTINGS has published results from its accelerated longevity test, in which TVs ran for around 18,000 hours. Of 16 sets with LG Display WOLED panels, 14 developed dead pixels, small pixel clusters or visible damage along the screen edges, which is 87.5 percent. RTINGS calls the phenomenon 'edge rot'. Unlike burn-in, according to RTINGS it does not depend on whether static content is shown, and it cannot be avoided by watching varied content. Among the older WBC panels, 9 of 10 sets were affected, five of them severely; among the newer WBE panels, 5 of 6, including models from LG and Sony. The 2023 LG G3 showed no edge damage. The three QD-OLED TVs with Samsung Display panels had no edge rot; however, RTINGS stresses that three units are too few to declare QD-OLED immune. Three OLED monitors that were checked, including one WOLED model, also showed no edge damage. Two RTINGS employees also found the problem on their privately used sets from 2020 and 2021. The exact cause is unclear; possible explanations include contamination during manufacturing and weaknesses in the protective layer meant to keep moisture away from the panel. LG Electronics and LG Display confirmed to RTINGS that the phenomenon can occur in a small number of products exposed to prolonged heat, humidity or other harsh conditions, but is not expected under normal conditions. The 87.5 percent is a result from a small test pool under continuous load, not a failure rate for all sets sold. Whether panels from 2024 onward are affected has not yet been determined by RTINGS.", "weitere_links": ["Hardware Busters"], "_src": "d6fa466e"}, "2026-11-07-warzone-switch2": {"titel": "Call of Duty: Warzone is now free on Nintendo Switch 2", "schlagzeile": "Warzone is now free to play on Nintendo Switch 2", "kurz": "Call of Duty: Warzone has arrived on Nintendo Switch 2 and is available for free on the Nintendo eShop. You do not need to buy Modern Warfare 4, but you do need an Activision account. The launch coincided with Season 1; at the same time, support for PlayStation 4 and Xbox One ended.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Insider Gaming, Call of Duty: Warzone is available on Nintendo Switch 2 and can be downloaded from the eShop as a standalone free-to-play title. Anyone who does not own Modern Warfare 4 can still play the battle royale. An Activision account is required. The launch came together with Season 1; Activision says players can drop into Hajin, Zodiac and the other maps and playlists as the free-to-play game arrives on Nintendo’s handheld for the first time. Nintendo Life followed up on 7.11.2026 and measured a file size of 122 GB on its own device; we do not have an official download size from Activision. Insider Gaming frames the move as the series returning to Nintendo hardware: Modern Warfare 4 was, by that account, the first Call of Duty game on a Nintendo console since Ghosts on the Wii U. With Season 1, Activision ended support for PlayStation 4 and Xbox One; progress is said to carry over to supported platforms via the same linked Activision account. Resolution, frame rate and cross-play details for the Switch 2 version have not been specified in the reporting available to us. The launch itself was on 6.11.2026; the Insider Gaming report we used appeared on 7.11.2026.", "weitere_links": ["Nintendo Life (122 GB measurement)"], "_src": "88111250"}, "2026-11-07-pulse-elevate-verschoben": {"titel": "Sony indefinitely delays Pulse Elevate speakers over a production issue", "schlagzeile": "Sony delays Pulse Elevate indefinitely – just before launch", "kurz": "Sony has indefinitely delayed the sales launch of the wireless Pulse Elevate speakers. The 12 November date is off because quality testing found a production issue. Sony has not named a new date; what happens to existing pre-orders is unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "On 6.11.2026 Sony indefinitely delayed the launch of the Pulse Elevate speakers on the PlayStation Blog. Eurogamer and IGN picked up the statement on 7.11.2026. In the blog, Sony writes that ongoing quality testing identified a production issue with the product and that it therefore decided to delay the launch; the extra time is meant to ensure the product delivers the intended experience. Sony does not name a new date or describe the issue in detail. The speakers were due to go on sale worldwide on 12 November, only a few days after the statement. The recommended retail price on the updated blog page is 219.99 US dollars, 219.99 euros and 199.99 pounds. Pulse Elevate is Sony’s first wireless speaker pair for desktop gaming and sits alongside the Pulse Elite headset and Pulse Explore earbuds. They connect via PlayStation Link to the PS5, PCs, Macs and PlayStation Portal and can be paired with a phone over Bluetooth at the same time. The right speaker has a microphone with what Sony calls AI-enhanced noise rejection. The Midnight Black version was due to be available everywhere, the white version only in selected countries including Germany, Austria and the United Kingdom. Pre-orders had been open since September. Eurogamer writes that it is unclear what now happens to those orders.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation Blog (official statement)", "IGN"], "_src": "67242cb4"}, "2026-11-07-anno117-fsr3-rtx30": {"titel": "Anno 117 Update 3.0: FSR 3 Frame Generation now enabled by default on GeForce RTX 30", "schlagzeile": "Anno 117 now turns on AMD's Frame Generation on RTX 30 cards", "kurz": "With Update 3.0, Anno 117: Pax Romana enables AMD's FSR 3 Frame Generation by default on GeForce RTX 30 cards in the automatic graphics settings. Reason: NVIDIA's own DLSS Frame Generation only runs on RTX 40 and newer. More displayed fps do not mean lower input latency, though.", "zusammenfassung": "Ubisoft Mainz released Update 3.0 for Anno 117: Pax Romana on 5 November 2026 together with the expansion \"Dawn of the Delta\". According to the official patch notes, the automatic graphics detection now enables AMD's FSR 3 Frame Generation by default on GeForce cards of the RTX 30 series. PCGH picked this up on 7 November and explains the background: NVIDIA's DLSS Frame Generation is officially reserved for the RTX 40 and RTX 50 series, whereas FSR 3 works across vendors and does not need AI units. On systems that the game assigns the \"Low\" profile, however, Frame Generation is no longer enabled automatically, to avoid fluctuations on PCs close to the minimum requirements. Ubisoft does not give concrete figures for the fps gain. Frame Generation inserts intermediate frames: the displayed frame rate rises, but input latency does not decrease as a result. Further changes address stutters when panning over large cities, performance drops when highlighting roads, and the quest book archive. According to the patch notes, the update also fixes numerous crashes and bugs. Anyone who does not use the automatic setting or does not want Frame Generation can control it in the graphics options.", "weitere_links": ["Anno Union: Update 3.0 patch notes"], "_src": "e94737ea"}, "2026-11-07-assassins-creed-mars-rom": {"titel": "Report: Ubisoft working on Assassin's Creed \"Mars\" in ancient Rome and mobile spin-off \"Pocket\"", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Assassin's Creed heading back to Rome?", "kurz": "According to content creator J0nathan, Ubisoft is developing an Assassin's Creed codenamed \"Mars\" that is said to be set in ancient Rome, plus a mobile title \"Pocket\" set in Jerusalem. Insider Gaming knows the codenames but could not sufficiently verify the claims. According to the report, a release would only be conceivable around 2029/2030.", "zusammenfassung": "On 7 November 2026, Insider Gaming reported on claims by YouTuber J0nathan, who has often had accurate information about Assassin's Creed in the past. According to him, Ubisoft is working on an Assassin's Creed codenamed \"Mars\" that is said to be set in ancient Rome. Two sources with access to Ubisoft's internal systems are said to have confirmed this; a link to the planned Assassin's Creed TV series is considered possible. A second project codenamed \"Pocket\" is said to be a mobile game set in Jerusalem. Insider Gaming says it has also heard of the codenames but could not verify the details to its standards. The series has recently been in troubled waters, among other things after the departure of Marc-Alexis Côté. According to earlier Insider Gaming sources, the next big game, Assassin's Creed Hexe, was internally delayed by another year, probably to 2028. A Rome game would therefore not be expected before 2029/2030, according to the report. Ubisoft has not commented. Everything is unconfirmed; early projects can change or be cancelled.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: the origin is YouTuber J0nathan, who has a mixed but often accurate track record on Assassin's Creed. Insider Gaming knows the codenames but could not verify the details. No statement from Ubisoft.", "weitere_links": ["TheGamer: Codename Mars"], "_src": "ef82e5b6"}, "2026-11-07-microsoft-gpu-patent-ki": {"titel": "Microsoft patent application: spare GPU power of private devices for AI training in exchange for credits", "schlagzeile": "Money for your idle GPU? Microsoft patent describes AI training", "kurz": "A Microsoft patent application published on 5 November describes a system that splits AI training into small subtasks and distributes them to unused GPUs of end devices. Users would have to opt in and could receive credits. Microsoft has not announced a product.", "zusammenfassung": "Insider Gaming reports on a Microsoft patent application titled \"Opportunistic Micro-training on Edge Devices Using Spare GPU Utilization\" (US-20260349820-A1), published on 5 November 2026. It describes a system that splits large AI training tasks into independently trainable mini-tasks and distributes them to devices whose GPU currently has little to do. Whether a device is free is to be determined from GPU and CPU load, memory, temperature and power consumption. According to the text, the system should not disrupt use, i.e. not slow down programs, drain batteries or overheat devices. Only users who agree are to take part. The computing work performed is to be tracked and booked as a credit to the account, redeemable for software, model access or money, for example. Microsoft would act as an intermediary between third parties who need computing power and the device owners. Questions about privacy, permissions and additional wear on the graphics card remain open. Important: a patent application is not a product promise; many patents are never implemented. Microsoft has not announced any such service.", "_src": "1f47cb8a"}, "2026-11-07-hwinfo-rx7500-razor-lake": {"titel": "HWiNFO beta detects unannounced Radeon RX 7500 and Intel Razor Lake-H/HX/S", "schlagzeile": "Leak: HWiNFO knows RX 7500 and Razor Lake", "kurz": "HWiNFO beta 8.55 Build 6115 lists an AMD Radeon RX 7500 that AMD has not announced yet. The same build improves detection of Intel Razor Lake-H, -HX and -S as well as Nova Lake-E. Specs and launch of the RX 7500 remain unknown; name support in tools is not a launch guarantee.", "zusammenfassung": "TechPowerUp and VideoCardz report that HWiNFO beta version 8.55 Build 6115 detects \"AMD Radeon RX 7500\" for the first time. AMD has not officially introduced the card; the changelog only lists the name, without specifications or a date. TechPowerUp considers Navi 33 / RDNA 3 the most likely chip candidate, because that architecture already powers the RX 7400 and RX 7600 – a model in between would be tightly positioned. The name RX 7500 or RX 7500 XT already appeared in older rumors around 2024 according to reports, without a concrete launch. VideoCardz additionally points to earlier prototype hints of Navi 33 XE with 6 GB GDDR6 and device ID 749F; whether the final product looks like that is unconfirmed. The same HWiNFO build expands support for Intel Nova Lake-E and Razor Lake-H/HX/S. Razor Lake is considered a successor generation after Nova Lake; retail chips are far off, since Nova Lake-S is only expected around Q1 2027. CPU-Z 3.02 already added Razor Lake earlier this week; HWiNFO had provisional Razor Lake-AX support already in August. AMD and Intel have not confirmed the entries.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: Only name/ID support in HWiNFO beta 8.55-6115 plus reports from TechPowerUp and VideoCardz. No official announcement from AMD or Intel; specs and launch of the RX 7500 unknown. Tool detection is not a launch guarantee.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz: HWiNFO RX 7500 and Razor Lake", "HWiNFO Forum: Beta 8.55-6115"], "_src": "34935787"}, "2026-11-07-vulkan-1-4-368": {"titel": "Vulkan 1.4.368 with new extensions from Valve and NVIDIA", "schlagzeile": "Vulkan 1.4.368: Valve and NVIDIA bring new extensions", "kurz": "The Khronos Group has released Vulkan 1.4.368. The weekly update brings two new extensions: one from Valve's Mesa developer Mike Blumenkrantz for vertex data and an NVIDIA extension for internal driver handles. Nothing changes for players right away; it is a building block for drivers and engines.", "zusammenfassung": "Vulkan 1.4.368 is the latest weekly update to the specification of the cross-platform graphics and compute interface, as Phoronix reported on 7 November 2026. In terms of content, it is a small update: six internally reported issues in the specification were fixed. There are two new extensions. VK_EXT_vertex_address_binding_unrestricted comes from Mike Blumenkrantz of Valve's Linux graphics team, a well-known Mesa developer. It helps when vertex data for a draw call is moved into a separate buffer to save memory, and disables an address check for that case. The second, VK_NV_internal_handle, is an NVIDIA-specific extension: applications and engines can use it to query internal driver handles for certain Vulkan objects and pass them on to other NVIDIA interfaces. Both extensions first have to arrive in drivers and software before they make a difference in games. Vulkan is, among other things, the foundation of Proton on Linux and the Steam Deck, where Valve's contributions are particularly important. All details are in the Khronos Group's Vulkan-Docs repository on GitHub.", "weitere_links": ["Khronos Vulkan-Docs on GitHub"], "_src": "9f12e9de"}, "2026-11-07-razor-lake-lga1954-2028": {"titel": "Report: Intel Razor Lake-S to arrive in 2028 on Nova Lake's LGA 1954 socket", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Razor Lake could fit the Nova Lake socket in 2028", "kurz": "According to insider Jaykihn, Intel's Razor Lake-S is currently planned for 2028 and is said to use the same LGA 1954 socket as Nova Lake-S. Anyone switching to Nova Lake in 2027 could therefore upgrade one more CPU generation without a new motherboard. Intel has confirmed none of this.", "zusammenfassung": "On 7 November 2026, Wccftech and HotHardware summarized statements by Intel insider Jaykihn: Razor Lake-S is \"currently slated as a 2028 product\", and Intel has said nothing officially. Nova Lake-S, the next desktop generation, is expected in early 2027 and introduces the new LGA 1954 socket. According to the reports, Razor Lake-S is to run on the same socket, which would give Intel two desktop generations on one platform for the first time in a while. Back in June, Jaykihn had written that LGA 1954 will even support processors beyond Razor Lake on boards with 64 MB of BIOS flash, including all Z boards. The reports name Griffin Cove, a successor to Nova Lake's Coyote Cove, as Razor Lake's P-core architecture; the desktop chips are not supposed to have SMT. In addition, some variants originally planned for Nova Lake, such as Nova Lake-AX, are said to have moved into the Razor Lake family. No quarter in 2028 is known; Wccftech speculates about Computex 2028 or the second half of the year. Intel manager Robert Hallock hinted in March that the company is listening to criticism of frequent socket changes, but there is no concrete commitment. First preparations are visible: CPU-Z 3.02 and an HWiNFO beta already recognize Razor Lake. All details on timing and socket are unconfirmed and may change; purchase decisions should not be based on them.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: statements by insider Jaykihn (X), who has often been right about Intel roadmaps; picked up by Wccftech and HotHardware. No confirmation from Intel; timing and socket may change.", "weitere_links": ["HotHardware: Razor Lake-S on LGA 1954", "VideoCardz: LGA 1954 beyond Razor Lake (June)"], "_src": "4d9282a2"}, "2026-11-07-cpuz-ram-rueckgang": {"titel": "CPU-Z statistics: share of 32 and 64 GB PCs falls year over year for the first time", "schlagzeile": "Less RAM for the first time: CPU-Z sees 16 GB PCs on the rise again", "kurz": "According to CPU-Z Validator statistics, the share of PCs with 32 GB of RAM fell by 2.5% year over year, and by as much as 18% for 64 GB. 16 GB and 8 GB systems, on the other hand, are gaining, and DDR4 is gaining share over DDR5. The data only reflects submitted validations, not market figures.", "zusammenfassung": "Doc TB, one of the developers behind CPU-Z, published new figures from the CPU-Z Validator on 6 November 2026, and VideoCardz covered them on 7 November. According to them, the RAM configuration of the recorded PCs has declined year over year for the first time. 32 GB remains the most common configuration at 37.2%, but lost 2.5% of its share. For 64 GB the decline is 18%, with the share now at 7.3%. 16 GB systems grew by 12.9% to 33.0%, putting them just behind 32 GB. 8 GB also grew by 5.5% to 11.0%, and 24 GB by 19.7% to 2.3%. In terms of memory generation, DDR4 rose by 6.0% to 54.5%, while DDR5 fell by 2.9% to 32.9%. The figures do not name a cause, but they fit the sharply increased RAM prices of recent months, which the ticker has reported on several times. Important: the statistics are based only on systems that users actively submit to the validator and are not a market study. The changes are relative shares and do not mean that owners are removing RAM.", "weitere_links": ["Doc TB (CPU-Z) on X, 6 Nov 2026"], "_src": "299d8b24"}, "2026-11-07-custom-engine-wald-rtx3080": {"titel": "Own engine: developer renders dense forest at around 130 fps on an RTX 3080 – without hardware ray tracing", "schlagzeile": "130 fps on an RTX 3080: hobby engine renders forest without ray tracing", "kurz": "Developer and modder Toni Macaroni shows a self-written engine that is said to render a dense forest at 1440p at an average of around 130 fps on an RTX 3080. It relies on Nanite-like geometry, voxels and voxel lighting instead of hardware ray tracing. The figures come from the developer himself, and it is purely a tech demo.", "zusammenfassung": "PCGH and Wccftech report on a tech demo by developer and modder Toni Macaroni, whose YouTube video has more than 500,000 views according to PCGH. By his own account, he has been working on the engine for around eight months after using the open-source engine Godot for a long time. The scene shows a hilly landscape with dense forest, around one million instances and four million triangles. On a GeForce RTX 3080 at 1440p, it is said to reach about 130 fps on average, up to 200 in aerial shots and around 80 fps in dense undergrowth. Technically, the engine uses clustered levels of detail with Nanite-like virtual geometry, voxel representations for distant vegetation and simplified proxies for very distant objects. The lighting combines screen-space techniques with voxel-based global illumination and works without hardware-accelerated ray tracing, similar to the approach in Kingdom Come: Deliverance II. The engine is deliberately specialized: above all, it is meant to render many objects with high polygon counts well, and a weather system is only partially finished. The fps figures are the developer's own claims; the exact settings and any upscaling are not known. A demo without characters, physics and AI is not comparable to a finished game, and there is no public version so far.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech: Custom Forest Engine"], "_src": "9e0e5944"}, "2026-11-07-windows-hello-pin-parallel": {"titel": "Windows 11 Insider: PIN in parallel with Windows Hello face or fingerprint scan", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11: Type PIN while Windows Hello scans", "kurz": "In Windows 11 Insider Experimental Build 26340.9882 you can type the PIN while Windows Hello is still checking face or fingerprint. The lock screen shows \"Look at the camera or enter your PIN\"; whichever works first wins. The rollout is experimental; there is no retail date.", "zusammenfassung": "Windows Latest tests Build 26340.9882 from 6 November 2026 (based on Windows 11 26H2, Experimental channel): On the sign-in screen the PIN field appears in parallel with the Windows Hello check. Instead of waiting for face recognition to fail or awkwardly choosing sign-in options, Microsoft release notes say \"whichever method works first\". After a restart, PIN-first remains for security reasons. If Face fails, there is a direct \"Retry face sign-in\" hint. On devices with an IR camera and fingerprint sensor the prompt can name face and fingerprint, with PIN underneath. New are Event Log IDs 4628 and 4629 under Security for set-up or failed Hello methods; additional Operational events help IT. According to the test the feature appeared without ViVeTool. Experimental builds can contain bugs; Microsoft did not say when the behavior reaches the stable channel.", "_src": "fc64848d"}, "2026-11-07-tsmc-3d-dram-nvidia": {"titel": "TSMC is considering entering 3D DRAM – NVIDIA is said to have prompted the move", "schlagzeile": "TSMC considers 3D DRAM: NVIDIA is said to have prompted the move", "kurz": "According to a report by The Information dated 6.11.2026, contract chipmaker TSMC is considering entering 3D DRAM production. The prompt is said to have come from NVIDIA, TSMC’s largest customer. The report names no specific plants, investments or start date. TSMC declined to comment on market rumors to The Information and pointed to its role as a logic foundry; NVIDIA did not respond, according to the report.", "zusammenfassung": "The Information reported on 6.11.2026, citing two people familiar with the discussions, that TSMC is considering entering 3D DRAM manufacturing. The trigger is said to have been a request from NVIDIA. igor'sLAB picked up and assessed the report on 7.11.2026. According to that account, TSMC has begun working out possible production concepts for vertically structured DRAM; the options named are building new plants or acquiring an existing facility and converting it. No production start, investment figures or planned capacity were given. The initiative is said to be led by Hsu Kuo-chin, a TSMC vice president in Advanced Packaging who previously worked for Micron in Taiwan. TSMC told The Information that it does not comment on market rumors as a matter of principle and pointed to its focus as a logic-chip foundry. NVIDIA did not respond to an inquiry, according to the report, and Reuters could not independently confirm the information. Technically, 3D DRAM is different from already established High Bandwidth Memory: HBM stacks several separately manufactured DRAM chips, while 3D DRAM is meant to integrate the memory cell layers themselves vertically to raise density. A successful entry would take TSMC into a market still dominated mainly by Samsung, SK hynix and Micron. At the same time, the report does not imply a near-term start of mass production, because heat, process integration and adequate yields are seen as open hurdles and development could take years. Against the backdrop of scarce and expensive memory for PCs and data centers, an additional manufacturer would be significant, but for now there is only a media report and possible development discussions.", "weitere_links": ["The Verge (via The Information)", "Seoul Economic Daily", "Wccftech (update)"], "_src": "406e56e5"}, "2026-11-06-openai-gpt6-cyber-bugs": {"titel": "OpenAI presents GPT-6 Cyber: claims 81 Firefox and 948 Linux LPE finds", "schlagzeile": "OpenAI GPT-6 Cyber finds 81 Firefox and 948 Linux bugs", "kurz": "OpenAI has presented GPT-6 Cyber, a non-public security model. According to the company it found 81 previously unknown high-severity Firefox vulnerabilities and developed exploits for 948 Linux local privilege escalation cases. The figures come from OpenAI and are not an independent full-audit confirmation.", "zusammenfassung": "BleepingComputer, Phoronix and Golem report on OpenAI's announcement of GPT-6 Cyber. The model is not public and currently limited to enabled customers in the Daybreak Red program. OpenAI says it discovered 81 previously unknown high-severity vulnerabilities in Firefox and co-developed patches; many have already been rolled out at Mozilla. For Linux kernel research OpenAI cites 2308 potential finds, 1724 reproduced vulnerabilities and 948 local privilege escalation exploits from unprivileged to root. In the ExploitGym benchmark the company cites a 48.5 percent success rate versus 32.1 percent for predecessor GPT-5.6 Cyber. In the Preparedness Framework OpenAI rates the cyber capability as \"Critical\". Independent audit depth on the scope and severity of the finds is limited – the figures are company claims, not proof that \"Linux is generally insecure\". OpenAI warns of a limited time window in which defenders should use frontier models for hardening before similar capabilities become more widely available.", "weitere_links": ["Phoronix: OpenAI 948 Linux LPE Bugs", "Golem: OpenAI claims nearly 1000 root vulnerabilities found"], "_src": "1b3a3edb"}, "2026-11-06-zen6-tee-riscv": {"titel": "AMD Zen 6: Firmware hint of RISC-V-based TEE instead of ARM PSP", "schlagzeile": "Zen 6: AMD switches TEE from ARM to RISC-V", "kurz": "A linux-firmware commit for AMD PMF Trusted Application on Zen 6 client (Family 1Ah M80h) mentions a RISC-V-based TEE. Until now the Secure Processor typically ran on ARM Cortex-A5 with TrustZone. Whether RISC-V is truly new from Zen 6 or only newly documented remains open.", "zusammenfassung": "Phoronix reports on a linux-firmware commit that adds PMF TA firmware v4 for platform 1AH_M80H – that corresponds to upcoming AMD Ryzen Zen 6 client CPUs. The commit text says the Trusted Application now runs on a RISC-V-based TEE, uses a larger shared-memory layout and extended policy conditions including up to 20 custom BIOS inputs. The Platform Management Framework controls among other things power, thermal and system behavior. Traditionally the AMD Platform Security Processor / Secure Processor was based on ARM Cortex-A5 with TrustZone. Phoronix finds no older public hints of a RISC-V TEE in Ryzen/EPYC and leaves open whether the feature is new for Zen 6 or was simply never mentioned on older SoCs. The commit does not name a final marketing label for the Ryzen generation. For Linux enablement and security enthusiasts the architecture switch is still a rare Zen 6 detail ahead of product launch.", "_src": "73845857"}, "2026-11-06-epic-linux-launcher-distros": {"titel": "Epic Games Launcher Preview: broad Linux distro support and AppImage return planned", "schlagzeile": "Epic: new launcher to support many Linux distros", "kurz": "Epic confirms to GamingOnLinux that the new launcher in preview should support as many Linux distributions as possible – explicitly including Fedora, SteamOS, Cachy and Omarchy among others. Packaging is still changing; AppImage is to return later this month. Preview does not mean a finished distro matrix.", "zusammenfassung": "GamingOnLinux asked Jake Jones (Communications Director, Epic Games) about Linux support for the new Epic Games Launcher. According to the statement Epic plans to support \"as many Linux distributions as possible\", including Fedora, SteamOS, Cachy, Omarchy and others. The preview started with AppImage, later switched to a .deb for Debian/Ubuntu; the FAQ named Fedora as coming soon. Epic is testing and evaluating packaging formats and wants to restore AppImage later this month. Until the matrix is fixed, formats can come and go. Flatpak/Flathub remains open in the report. Launcher status is Preview, not a final store rollout for every distro. Fortnite or Easy Anti-Cheat v2 are a separate topic and are not sold here as \"Fortnite is coming to Linux\". Together with the already known GOG Galaxy Linux window for 2027, competition among store clients on Linux remains interesting.", "_src": "e2ba62e3"}, "2026-11-06-mindfactory-cyberangriff": {"titel": "Mindfactory reports cyberattack: customer passwords reset, authority informed", "schlagzeile": "Mindfactory: hacker attack – passwords reset", "kurz": "Hardware shop Mindfactory reported a cyberattack on 6 November 2026 and informed customers and the data protection authority. Possibly affected: address, email, phone and encrypted passwords; bank data is not in the shop system according to the shop. All shop passwords were reset; phishing caution is advised.", "zusammenfassung": "heise online and Golem report that Mindfactory has become the victim of a cyberattack and informed customers via notice. The company has filed a criminal complaint and involved the competent data protection authority. On current knowledge Mindfactory cannot rule out that attackers accessed address, email, phone as well as encrypted stored passwords. Cleartext passwords and bank/credit card data are not affected according to the company, because payment data sits with service providers. All customer passwords for the shop were reset as a precaution; the next login requires a new password, going forward with a modern hash method. Managing director Marcel Kirchner speaks of a forensic investigation, no extortion and a closed vulnerability. Customers should be careful with unexpected emails, SMS or calls, because contact data could be abused for fraud. Transparency note: Mindfactory has belonged to the heise group since mid-2025; heise online is part of the same corporate group. Scope and exact attack timing were still being clarified at reporting time.", "weitere_links": ["Golem: Hackers attack Mindfactory", "GameStar: Cyberattack at Mindfactory"], "_src": "c989d014"}, "2026-11-06-nier-366gb-update": {"titel": "NieR: Automata update accidentally demands 366 GB of storage – fix announced", "schlagzeile": "NieR: Automata update eats 366 GB – studio apologizes", "kurz": "A Steam update for NieR: Automata on November 6, 2026 (JST) demands far more storage than intended — Insider Gaming cites 366 GB versus about 50 GB for the base game. It was meant to add languages; a fix and a DLC-deselect workaround were communicated.", "zusammenfassung": "Insider Gaming reports a faulty Steam update for NieR: Automata: after the November 6, 2026 (Japan time) update, install size is far larger than intended — about 366 GB of storage versus roughly 50 GB for the base game. Update notes said simplified Chinese, traditional Chinese and Korean would be added. The NieR Series account on X apologized and announced a fix. As a workaround, players can open Properties → DLC, uncheck the DLC items and keep playing the base game for now. No new story DLC has shipped since 2024; the game passed 10 million copies shipped/sold in February 2026. The short note does not explain the exact cause of the inflated download.", "_src": "c9a67187"}, "2026-11-06-qnap-plex2shell": {"titel": "QNAP warns: attackers compromise NAS devices via Plex2Shell flaws in Plex Media Server", "schlagzeile": "QNAP: hackers breach NAS via Plex2Shell – update Plex now", "kurz": "QNAP reports compromises of NAS devices through the Plex2Shell vulnerability chain in Plex Media Server. Users should update Plex in the App Center to at least 1.43.3.10861; if compromise is suspected, a clean OS reinstall may be required. QTS itself is not affected.", "zusammenfassung": "BleepingComputer covers a QNAP security advisory: several users reported that Plex Media Server on their NAS devices was compromised via the Plex2Shell flaws. Plex2Shell covers four vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-96652, CVE-2026-96654, CVE-2026-96655, CVE-2026-96656) reported by Zach Main on July 27; exploitation began after technical details went public on October 16. CISA added the CVEs to its Known Exploited catalog on October 20, 2026, with a short deadline for agencies. QNAP says the flaws exist only in Plex Media Server, not in QTS/QuTS hero. It recommends updating to Plex 1.43.3.10861 from the QNAP App Center. Anyone running a vulnerable, publicly reachable Plex server should treat the device as potentially compromised: updating does not remove payloads already installed. QNAP advises a clean reinstall of QTS/QuTS hero, credential resets, and — if remote access is needed — VPN instead of forwarding port 32400.", "_src": "48cb0d6c"}, "2026-11-06-ratchet-ranger-rumble": {"titel": "Ratchet & Clank: Ranger Rumble shut down – servers end May 2027", "schlagzeile": "Ratchet & Clank: Ranger Rumble dies – servers off May 1, 2027", "kurz": "The mobile Ratchet & Clank spin-off Ranger Rumble is cancelled: final update on November 6, 2026, removed from stores on November 21, servers shut down on May 1, 2027. The game was still in soft launch ahead of a planned global release.", "zusammenfassung": "IGN reports the shutdown of Ratchet & Clank: Ranger Rumble. Per the developer statement, the final planned update rolls out on November 6, 2026; the app leaves stores on November 21, 2026. Owners can keep playing until May 1, 2027, when servers go offline for good. In-app purchases were removed; refunds point to Apple or Google. The arena-shooter spin-off came from Oh BiBi with Insomniac Games and PlayStation Studios and was still in soft launch before a worldwide start, per IGN. As recently as July the PlayStation Blog spoke of an upcoming global launch after a successful test phase. VGC likewise covers the cancellation of the free-to-play mobile shooter.", "weitere_links": ["VGC: Sony’s Ratchet & Clank mobile shooter cancelled"], "_src": "99d65582"}, "2026-11-06-poe2-1-0-exilecon": {"titel": "Path of Exile 2 full release on 11 December 2026: Shadow, Duelist and League Conquerors of Wraeclast", "schlagzeile": "Path of Exile 2 1.0: Shadow, Duelist, launch 11 Dec", "kurz": "Grinding Gear Games announced the full release of Path of Exile 2 for 11 December 2026 at ExileCon. New are the Shadow and Duelist classes plus finished campaign acts five and six. Also coming is the league \"Conquerors of Wraeclast\" with base and army building.", "zusammenfassung": "PC Gamer summarizes the ExileCon keynote on Path of Exile 2 version 1.0: The full release after about two years of Early Access is dated for 11 December 2026. Two new classes launch with it: the dagger- and trap-focused Shadow with stealth, and the sword-heavy Duelist. Shadow can ascend as Assassin according to the studio or choose the new Ascendancy Infiltrator; a third Ascendancy is planned later. Stealth prevents monsters from seeing the character at range, resets on kill and interacts with traps that only trigger from hiding when revealed. The campaign gets acts five and six including a return to Oriath and an introduction to the league mechanic. \"Conquerors of Wraeclast\" brings base building, armies, commanders and later faction-bound Atlas battles. The endgame heavily streamlines the Atlas skill tree, reworks gems and the passive tree including jewel slots, and adds many new bases and uniques. Exact launch time and further Ascendancy details may still follow after the ongoing ExileCon.", "weitere_links": ["PC Gamer: Shadow class for PoE2 1.0"], "_src": "6ec09cc3"}, "2026-11-06-nvidia-11mio-diebstahl": {"titel": "NVIDIA hardware worth $11.4 million stolen in transit from Oakland to Texas", "schlagzeile": "$11.4M NVIDIA hardware: six pallets vanish on the way to Texas", "kurz": "Oakland police are investigating the theft of six pallets of NVIDIA hardware worth $11.4 million. A truck with a food-transport logo picked up the load on August 29 and disappeared; the trail ended in San Bernardino County. No arrests have been announced.", "zusammenfassung": "According to VideoCardz and local broadcaster ABC7 News, Oakland police (California) are investigating a major theft of NVIDIA hardware. Six pallets with a declared value of $11.4 million were bound from Oakland to Fort Worth, Texas. On August 29, 2026, a truck bearing a food-transport company logo collected the load as planned — then the vehicle and drivers vanished. Investigators tracked several multi-hour stops and lost the trail in San Bernardino County. The theft was reported to police only on September 13. Which exact products were on the pallets (AI accelerators, complete systems, or consumer GPUs) has not been publicly confirmed; the average value is about $1.9 million per pallet. UC Berkeley professor Olaf Groth told ABC7 such chips sell for much more abroad and pose a security risk. VideoCardz also notes earlier NVIDIA-related thefts in the Bay Area (over $7.5 million in 2025) and a Brazil case involving stolen ZOTAC RTX 5090 cards. So far there are no arrests and no confirmation that the cargo was recovered.", "weitere_links": ["ABC7 News: $11.4M Nvidia cargo stolen from Oakland", "Wccftech: NVIDIA GPUs Worth $11.4 Million Stolen"], "_src": "8bfcec8e"}, "2026-11-06-micron-fab-stop": {"titel": "Micron reportedly pauses construction of a RAM fab in Taiwan amid union dispute", "schlagzeile": "Micron halts RAM fab build in Taiwan – clash with unions", "kurz": "PCGH reports, citing Bloomberg, that Micron has stopped construction on a semiconductor fab in Taoyuan and put expansion plans on ice. Background is a conflict with Taiwanese unions over profit sharing. A full exit is not confirmed.", "zusammenfassung": "According to PC Games Hardware and Bloomberg sources on the ground, Micron has stopped construction on a planned semiconductor fab in Taoyuan, Taiwan, and wants to pause expansion plans. PCGH puts the investment at around €4 billion. The move falls into a longer conflict with unions demanding employee participation in soaring profits. In Taichung a compromise was reached two weeks ago whose acceptance among workers is disputed; in Taoyuan talks continue, including a symbolic strike — the first in Taiwan’s semiconductor industry. The Taoyuan Labour Union rejects blame and says it does not want to endanger company profits. Whether the stop is permanent or a bargaining lever remains open. For PC buyers the story matters because extra RAM capacity is seen as a way out of the memory shortage — and that capacity is now stalled.", "_src": "2080eae5"}, "2026-11-06-switch2-verkauf-minus37": {"titel": "Switch 2: Nintendo reports 37.4% fewer hardware sales in the half-year comparison", "schlagzeile": "Switch 2: 37% fewer sales than record prior year – software up", "kurz": "Per Nintendo’s results and GameStar, Switch 2 sell-in from April to September 2026 fell 37.4% to 6.49 million units (prior year 10.36M). Software rose 18.8%; the full-year forecast of 16.5 million devices stands.", "zusammenfassung": "GameStar summarizes Nintendo’s half-year figures: from April to September 2026 Nintendo sold 6.49 million Switch 2 consoles to the trade — 37.4% fewer than the 10.36 million in the prior-year period. Q1 saw 3.82 million, July–September another 2.67 million. The year-ago comparison is skewed by the June 5, 2025 launch and pent-up demand. Since September the Switch 2 has been more expensive (Europe officially €499.99). Nintendo cites memory prices, exchange rates and oil prices for the hike. The full-year forecast of 16.5 million units through March 2027 remains unchanged per GameStar and VGC. Switch 2 software rose 18.8% to 24.49 million units in the half; net profit rose eleven percent. VGC also notes Switch 2 still leads original Switch and PS5 on a launch-aligned cumulative basis. These are sell-in figures, not necessarily end-customer sales.", "weitere_links": ["Nintendo IR: Financial Results Explanatory Material", "VGC: Switch 2 sales down 37%, still beating original"], "_src": "9aaf69f1"}, "2026-11-06-rtx5070ti-doppel-msrp": {"titel": "GeForce RTX 5070 Ti nears twice MSRP in US online stores", "schlagzeile": "RTX 5070 Ti hits $1,340 – nearly double MSRP in US shops", "kurz": "After the RTX 5090 and 5080, the RTX 5070 Ti is also surging: the cheapest tracked US online offer is $1,339.99, with some models at $1,499.99. Launch MSRP was $749. NVIDIA had previously denied discontinuation rumors.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports that the GeForce RTX 5070 Ti is now selling well above MSRP at major US online retailers. The card launched in February 2025 at a $749 MSRP; the cheapest tracked offer on November 6, 2026 is $1,339.99 (about 79% above MSRP). Individual models at B&H and Best Buy sit around $1,400 to $1,499.99 — near or at double the launch price. Within eight days the cheapest tracked price rose by $160 (from $1,179.99 on October 29). Cited examples: GIGABYTE AERO OC at Newegg for $1,339.99, ASUS PRIME OC and TUF GAMING OC at B&H for $1,399.99 and $1,499.99. In January 2026 NVIDIA denied discontinuation rumors for the 5070 Ti; ASUS then pointed to memory supply constraints. The card remains available, so a production stop is not proven — but the price spiral after the RTX 5090 and 5080 continues for the 5070 Ti.", "_src": "d18a0453"}, "2026-11-06-asus-xg-core-9060xt": {"titel": "ASUS XG Core: external Radeon RX 9060 XT LP 16 GB over USB4 for laptops and handhelds", "schlagzeile": "ASUS XG Core: external RX 9060 XT LP 16 GB via USB4", "kurz": "ASUS unveils XG Core: a compact external graphics box with Radeon RX 9060 XT LP 16 GB GDDR6 and USB4 for compatible laptops, mini PCs and handhelds such as the ROG Ally X. No official price yet; a Swedish shop lists about €1,207 incl. VAT per TechPowerUp.", "zusammenfassung": "In a press release published by TechPowerUp, ASUS announces XG Core: an external graphics unit with AMD Radeon RX 9060 XT LP (RDNA 4) and 16 GB GDDR6. The box measures about 144 × 117 × 39 mm and connects via USB4 to compatible hosts — ASUS also mentions Thunderbolt 3 systems and handhelds such as ROG Ally X and ROG Xbox Ally X. HDMI and DisplayPort are built in; tuning uses GPU Tweak III. ASUS pitches gaming, creative work and local AI workloads (e.g. ComfyUI, LM Studio, Ollama). An official list price is missing from the release; TechPowerUp comments cite a Swedish shop at about $1,346 / €1,207 incl. 25% VAT — not a confirmed MSRP. Availability in DE/AT is still unclear.", "_src": "e27a1951"}, "2026-11-06-medusa-point-6-8-kerne": {"titel": "More Zen 6 Medusa Point samples: 6 and 8 cores in Lenovo Geekbench entries", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Medusa Point 2/3 with 6 and 8 cores shows up at Lenovo", "kurz": "After the 10-core sample, two more AMD Zen 6 Medusa Point engineering samples supposedly appeared in Geekbench 7: 8 cores (2+6) and 6 cores (1+5), both labeled Medusa Point 2/3 on Lenovo systems. Unconfirmed; clocks and scores vary widely.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports two further Geekbench 7 entries for AMD Zen 6 Medusa Point, this time with 6 and 8 cores and the Medusa Point 2/3 label. Both samples were tested on Lenovo systems. The 8-core sample (100-000002152-50_Y) has 16 threads in 2+6 clusters and 8 MB L3; the 6-core sample (100-000001658-50_Y) has 12 threads in 1+5 and 4 MB L3. Both share CPU ID Family 26 Model 224 Stepping 0, unlike the 10-core Medusa Point 1 sample. Geekbench 7 scores: 8C later run 2,889 / 15,099 (max reported 5.28 GHz), earlier run much weaker; 6C 1,732 / 8,340 at only ~2.04 GHz. VideoCardz stresses that clock readings and scores for engineering samples fluctuate heavily and are not final. A Zen 6 mobile debut is expected around CES 2027. AMD has not confirmed the samples.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: Geekbench 7 entries of engineering samples on Lenovo systems, reported by VideoCardz. Clocks and scores vary widely between runs. Not a final product; AMD has not confirmed.", "_src": "66dba83d"}, "2026-11-06-windows11-27h2": {"titel": "Windows 11 27H2 is set to renew the technical platform for the first time in three years", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 27H2: real platform update, not just another UI year", "kurz": "Dr. Windows reports, citing The Verge: version 27H2 in 2027 should renew Windows 11’s kernel and driver foundation — the first change since 24H2/25H2/26H2, which were technically identical. Reports say Windows 12 is not planned for 2027.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Dr. Windows (citing The Verge), Windows 11 faces a platform update with version 27H2 in 2027. Since 24H2, versions 25H2 and 26H2 have been identical at the technical base (kernel, driver model and core components); new features mainly touched UI and swappable parts. 27H2 is set to change that base for the first time in three years. That can require compatibility checks — especially for system-near software such as security products. Whether some features will be artificially tied to 27H2 remains open. The reports also stress that this does not announce Windows 12 for 2027; it stays Windows 11. The story largely confirms plans Microsoft sketched earlier. The Verge itself is paywalled; the core claim is corroborated via Dr. Windows and Golem (“no Windows 12”).", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de: No Windows 12 likely next year"], "_src": "76b75cda"}, "2026-11-06-msi-claw-fsr41": {"titel": "MSI aims to bring FSR 4.1 to the Claw A8 in December via OEM driver", "schlagzeile": "MSI Claw A8: FSR 4.1 due in December via OEM driver", "kurz": "MSI confirms the Claw A8 (Ryzen Z2 Extreme / Radeon 890M) should get AMD FSR Upscaling 4.1 through its own graphics driver — target December 2026, subject to validation. A current driver fixes render bugs but does not yet include FSR 4.1.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz reports, citing MSI: the Claw A8 handheld should receive AMD FSR Upscaling 4.1 via a manufacturer graphics driver. MSI targets December 2026 if validation succeeds. The Claw A8 uses AMD’s Ryzen Z2 Extreme with Radeon 890M. AMD opened FSR 4.1 for Ryzen Z2 Extreme and other handheld APUs on October 20; standard Adrenalin drivers do not officially support handhelds, so makers such as MSI, ASUS or Lenovo must ship their own drivers. Driver 32.0.32016.5 for the Claw A8 BZ2EM is already available: it fixes wrong shadows, lighting glitches, FSR artifacts, particle issues and black squares — but still lacks FSR 4.1. That confirms an official FSR 4.1 path instead of unofficial modded drivers.", "_src": "fa2c559e"}, "2026-11-06-nvidia-dlss-override-19": {"titel": "NVIDIA App: DLSS Override for 19 more games, including Witcher 3 and PUBG", "schlagzeile": "NVIDIA App: DLSS Override enabled for 19 more games", "kurz": "An NVIDIA App update adds DLSS Override profiles for 19 more titles. They include older games such as The Witcher 3 and PUBG as well as upcoming or announced releases. Override lets users force newer DLSS models and modes where the driver supports it.", "zusammenfassung": "TechPowerUp reports NVIDIA App update 11.0.9.585 with DLSS Override support for 19 more games plus Optimal Settings profiles for six titles. The Override list includes Honeycomb: The World Beyond, WARDOGS, PUBG: Battlegrounds, Aniimo, 007 First Light, Active Matter, Enlisted, Dragon's Dogma 2, The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt, AION 2, Halloween: The Game, HOT WHEELS Infinite Rush, Silent Hill: Townfall, Control Resonant, Ace Combat 8: Wings of Theve, Dynasty Warriors 3 Complete Edition Remastered, Star Wars: Galactic Racer, Gears of War: E-Day and Clive Barker's Hellraiser: Revival. Optimal Settings arrive among others for AION 2, Aniimo, Control Resonant, EA Sports FC 27, Gears of War: E-Day and Star Wars: Galactic Racer. Some titles were already listed in earlier builds according to TechPowerUp; NVIDIA does not explain the duplicates and does not say which override options each game gets. DLSS Override sits under Graphics program settings and can force newer DLSS models or modes such as DLAA when a game does not offer them. The changelog otherwise only mentions general stability and security fixes.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz: 19 DLSS Override profiles"], "_src": "df35ce8c"}, "2026-11-06-unity-buyout-gespraeche": {"titel": "Reports: Silver Lake and Saudi PIF allegedly held preliminary talks on a Unity buyout", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Silver Lake and PIF allegedly talking about buying Unity", "kurz": "According to a Reuters report, Silver Lake and the Saudi Public Investment Fund held preliminary talks about acquiring Unity after the EA deal. Secondary reports mention valuation figures around about $25 billion. No deal is guaranteed; shares jumped on the buzz.", "zusammenfassung": "Several outlets, citing Reuters, report that Silver Lake and the Saudi Public Investment Fund held preliminary talks about a possible Unity acquisition. The same actors were recently involved in the large EA deal; Silver Lake reportedly already holds a minority stake in Unity. Insider Gaming cites a valuation on the order of about $25 billion and says Unity is reviewing options with a bank. These are explicitly early talks; a deal is not guaranteed. The rumors alone reportedly pushed the share price up noticeably, with one report citing nearly 15 percent. Unity is best known for its namesake engine and powers many large games. The situation remains unconfirmed until Unity or the investors comment officially. Reliability: medium because Reuters is the origin, but talks are preliminary.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: Reuters report on preliminary talks, picked up by PC Gamer, Insider Gaming and IGN. No completed deal; Unity is reviewing options with a bank. Figures and outcome open.", "ursprungsquelle": "Reuters", "weitere_links": ["Insider Gaming: Silver Lake and PIF allegedly want Unity", "IGN: Silver Lake and PIF reportedly seeking Unity"], "_src": "f1589ccc"}, "2026-11-06-amd-pc-markt-2027": {"titel": "AMD plans for a double-digit decline in PC shipments in 2027 due to high memory prices", "schlagzeile": "AMD: PC market set to shrink double-digit in 2027 – RAM prices weigh", "kurz": "On the earnings call, Lisa Su said AMD is planning for a double-digit decline in global PC unit shipments in 2027. The reason is higher memory and component prices weighing on demand. This is a planning assumption for the overall market, not measured decline yet.", "zusammenfassung": "On the Q3 2026 earnings call, AMD CEO Lisa Su said the company is planning for PC market unit shipments to decline by a double-digit percentage in 2027. She cites higher memory and component costs that make desktops and notebooks more expensive and weigh on demand. AMD will align sell-in with sell-through to keep customer and channel inventories healthy. Despite the expected market weakness, AMD expects to outperform via its Ryzen roadmap and growing commercial business. In parallel, AMD expects Data Center to account for more than 80 percent of company revenue in 2027. Client revenue rose 7 percent in Q3 to $2.9 billion; Gaming fell 40 percent to $773 million, mainly on weaker semi-custom sales in the console cycle. PCGH stresses this is a planning assumption, not a measured market result yet. VideoCardz covers the same earnings-call remarks. RAM prices barely register in Google Trends DE right now, but the story still matters for hardware buyers.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz: AMD expects double-digit PC market decline in 2027"], "_src": "093d57bb"}, "2026-11-06-rx9070xt-clustered-geometry": {"titel": "Microsoft Agility SDK: biggest DirectX ray tracing update since 2018 – Clustered Geometry and PTLAS", "schlagzeile": "DirectX: biggest ray tracing update since 2018 – Clustered Geometry", "kurz": "With Agility SDK 1.722 Preview, Microsoft released its most extensive DirectX ray tracing update since 2018. Clustered Geometry and Partitioned TLAS are meant to speed up building ray-tracing structures and cut memory use. In independent PCGH demo measurements, an RX 9070 XT rises from 1.7 to 91 fps; games still have to adopt the APIs.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft calls the new DirectX ray tracing features in Agility SDK 1.722 Preview the most extensive expansion since DXR launched in 2018. Key pieces are Clustered Geometry (CLAS), Partitioned Top-Level Acceleration Structures (PTLAS) and indirect acceleration-structure builds. Clustered Geometry splits geometry into reusable clusters of up to 256 triangles; that should make building ray-tracing structures in detailed, dynamic scenes much faster and enable more accurate reflections and shadows without costly proxy geometry. PTLAS is meant to update only changed scene regions. According to ComputerBase and Microsoft, an example on a Radeon RX 9070 rose from 1.2 to 79 fps, while structure memory fell from about 7519 to 774 MB; scratch memory rose sharply instead. PC Games Hardware also measured the D3D12RaytracingClusteredGeometry demo independently: an RX 9070 XT went from 1.7 to 91 fps at 1600×920 (about 54×), with BVH memory from 7518 to 771 MiB; an RTX 5080 from 1.4 to 310 fps. Without Clustered Geometry the Radeon was slightly ahead; with the feature the RTX 5080 was clearly faster. The preview runs on GeForce RTX, Radeon RX 9000, Intel Arc B-series and supported Core Ultra iGPUs; new hardware features are not required, but driver support is. Existing games do not benefit automatically: studios must integrate the APIs. Advanced Shader Delivery and other Agility SDK 1.620 features are part of the same release package but are not part of the ray-tracing demo numbers.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft DirectX Blog: Agility SDK 1.620 / 1.722 Preview", "Microsoft: Clustered Geometry and PTLAS Preview", "PCGH: RX 9070 XT / RTX 5080 in Clustered Geometry demo"], "_src": "3d54cb6e"}, "2026-11-05-asrock-rx7900-vbios": {"titel": "ASRock VBIOS for RX 7900 XT/XTX: owners report bricked GPUs after official update", "schlagzeile": "ASRock VBIOS bricks RX 7900 XT/XTX – downloads apparently pulled", "kurz": "After the official ASRock VBIOS from late October, owners of Radeon RX 7900 XT and XTX Phantom Gaming as well as Taichi report that their cards no longer start. The update was meant to address AMD-SN-6023 and ran via ASRVBFlash 1.0.5. HTTP downloads are reportedly now 404; some cards were only recovered with an external EEPROM programmer.", "zusammenfassung": "In late October ASRock released new VBIOS files for ten Radeon RX 7000 cards, including as part of AMD security measure AMD-SN-6023. Several owners now report that after flashing with ASRVBFlash 1.0.5 the system no longer POSTs with the GPU installed. Models named include RX 7900 XT Phantom Gaming as well as RX 7900 XTX Phantom Gaming and Taichi including the White edition. Reports involve different motherboards, for example from ASRock and MSI. VideoCardz documents the sequence: the tool checks compatibility, Windows restarts, then the PC no longer boots with the card. At least two users restored their RX 7900 XTX Phantom Gaming with external EEPROM programmers, including a T48 with a test clip. The October downloads reportedly return HTTP 404 now, while FTP links may still work. A user in Japan reportedly received confirmation from ASRock support that the failure would be covered under warranty; there is no public company-wide statement or official recovery procedure yet according to VideoCardz and Guru3D. Until ASRock clarifies and ships corrected firmware, owners of the named models should not install the October firmware. Source: VideoCardz, with Guru3D as secondary.", "weitere_links": ["Guru3D: ASRock RX 7000 VBIOS and brick reports"], "_src": "1ae75289"}, "2026-11-05-gog-galaxy-linux-2027": {"titel": "New GOG Galaxy coming in 2027 – with full Linux support", "schlagzeile": "GOG Galaxy 2027: new client with full Linux support", "kurz": "At its first GOG Showcase, GOG confirmed that a new Galaxy client with full Linux support will arrive in 2027. The Windows and Mac clients are being reworked in parallel. Galaxy remains optional; offline installers stay.", "zusammenfassung": "GamingOnLinux reports from the first GOG Showcase: in 2027 a completely new GOG Galaxy client for all platforms is to arrive, for the first time with full Linux support. GOG had already told GamingOnLinux in July it was working on this; the timeline is now public. According to GOG’s statement the client on Windows and Mac should become simpler and faster with a cleaner library view. The core promise remains: Galaxy is optional, and games can still be downloaded and kept via offline installers. Interested users can sign up for the beta on the GOG anniversary page once it opens. GOG is also working on GOG Social, a modernized community experience with threads, media and game-related tags. The report does not name further Linux-client feature details; nothing is speculated here.", "_src": "aa4b3b79"}, "2026-11-05-medusa-point-gb7": {"titel": "AMD Zen 6 Medusa Point appears in Geekbench 7: 10 cores, single-core above 9950X3D average", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Medusa Point in Geekbench 7 – 10C ES beats 9950X3D in SC?", "kurz": "An unconfirmed Geekbench 7 result shows an AMD Medusa Point engineering sample with 10 cores and 20 threads. The single-core score is 3100 points, slightly above the Ryzen 9 9950X3D average. Reported clocks around 2.0 GHz look implausible for a final product.", "zusammenfassung": "VideoCardz and TechPowerUp report a Geekbench 7 listing for engineering sample 100-000001713-32_Y on a Lenovo platform. It shows 10 cores and 20 threads in two clusters of 4 plus 6 cores, plus 16 MB L3 cache. The single-core score is 3100 points, about 1.6 percent above the Ryzen 9 9950X3D average of 3051 according to VideoCardz. Multi-core is 18313 points. Base and max frequency are listed around 2.0 GHz / 1996 MHz; that looks unbelievable for retail clocks and is treated as a typical ES or misread artifact. TechPowerUp describes the clusters as a possible Zen 6 and Zen 6c mix and notes AVX-512 support in the listing. This is not a final product; specs, clocks and launch date remain open. Earlier Geekbench 6 scores for the same product are not directly comparable due to different workloads. Reliability: medium, because only a public benchmark listing via leaker channels is available.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: Geekbench 7 listing of an engineering sample (100-000001713-32_Y) on a Lenovo platform, reported by VideoCardz and TechPowerUp via HXL. Clocks look implausible (around 2.0 GHz). Not a final product; AMD has not confirmed anything.", "ursprungsquelle": "Geekbench via HXL", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp: Medusa Point 10C/20T in Geekbench"], "_src": "ba3c17d9"}, "2026-11-05-switch2-keine-preiserhoehung": {"titel": "Nintendo rules out further Switch 2 price rises – despite weaker console sales", "schlagzeile": "Nintendo: no further Switch 2 price increase planned", "kurz": "Nintendo president Shuntaro Furukawa rules out further Switch 2 price increases. The company says it is sufficiently supplied with memory chips. At the same time, media report falling console sales and lower profit in the latest quarter.", "zusammenfassung": "Presenting the latest results, Nintendo president Shuntaro Furukawa said according to PC Games, Eurogamer, VGC and IGN that no further Switch 2 price increase is planned. Nintendo has secured enough memory capacity and currently sees no reason for another adjustment. Nintendo had already raised Switch 2 prices earlier, including by $50 / €30 in several regions. IGN cites Bloomberg with a 16 percent drop in operating profit to 73.9 billion yen in the quarter to end of September, and 2.67 million Switch 2 units sold in that period. VGC speaks of an about 37 percent decline in Switch 2 sales in the same reporting context, while Nintendo says Switch 2 still outsells its predecessor in the comparison window. By end of September about 26 million Switch 2 consoles had been sold in total. Nintendo is keeping its forecasts for the current fiscal year according to PC Games. Memory shortages remain an industry theme; Nintendo is positioning itself differently from recent PS5 and Xbox price hikes.", "weitere_links": ["IGN: Nintendo rules out further Switch 2 price rises", "Eurogamer: No plans for more Switch 2 price hikes", "VGC: Nintendo not considering Switch 2 price hike"], "_src": "487162c1"}, "2026-11-05-dlss5-hogwarts-legacy": {"titel": "Hogwarts Legacy gets DLSS 5 with 3D-Guided Neural Rendering on GeForce RTX 50", "schlagzeile": "DLSS 5 Neural Rendering now in Hogwarts Legacy", "kurz": "Since 5 November 2026 Hogwarts Legacy on PC supports NVIDIA DLSS 5 with 3D-Guided Neural Rendering. The feature needs a GeForce RTX 50 and a current Game Ready driver; Display settings have the \"Neural Rendering\" switch. Marketing FPS figures are not an everyday promise.", "zusammenfassung": "NVIDIA and Portkey Games report that Hogwarts Legacy on PC has received DLSS 5 with 3D-Guided Neural Rendering. The tech is meant to enrich lighting and material detail with AI while keeping the engine's geometry and textures as the foundation; developers can steer the result via artist controls. Requirement per support article: a GeForce RTX 50 series plus GeForce Game Ready Driver 616.64 or newer. Activation under Display settings: Upscale Type to NVIDIA DLSS, then enable Neural Rendering; shortcut Shift+Alt+B. Supported stores: Steam, Epic Games Store and Windows Store. Per NVIDIA blog of 5 November 2026, War Thunder follows with DLSS 5 mid-November, Where Winds Meet on 23 November. The feature is tied to RTX 50 or matching cloud/Spark paths and does not replace classic upscaling alone. We do not take FPS marketing from demos as a practice promise.", "weitere_links": ["Portkey Games: Enable DLSS 5 in Hogwarts Legacy", "NVIDIA Blog: GFN Thursday Hogwarts DLSS 5"], "_src": "beddaa04"}, "2026-11-05-xbox-pc-app-60": {"titel": "Xbox PC app: Microsoft promises up to 60 percent faster launch for Insiders", "schlagzeile": "Xbox PC app launches up to 60% faster – Insiders first", "kurz": "Xbox Insiders can try a revised Xbox PC app from 05.11.2026. Microsoft talks of an up to 60 percent faster launch as well as noticeably snappier pages and windows. In parallel, a refreshed web and cloud gaming experience is rolling out to more players.", "zusammenfassung": "Jason Beaumont, VP Xbox Experiences, announced a faster and clearer Xbox experience for PC, web and cloud on Xbox Wire on 05.11.2026. Xbox Insiders should be able to use the updated Xbox PC app right away. According to Microsoft tests, the app launches up to 60 percent faster; pages such as Home, Store and Game Pass load up to 50 percent faster, and in-app windows open up to 65 percent faster. The figures depend on device, network, configuration and usage, Microsoft notes. The library gets simpler navigation, new filters and better sorting. Friends and social features move into the main navigation. Search covers games including installed titles and add-ons as well as people. Visually there are revised game cards, Home, settings and animations. The web experience for Xbox Cloud Gaming previously shown to Insiders is meant to reach more players automatically in the coming weeks; anyone who wants to try earlier can open play.xbox.com. There is a Library tab for cloud games (purchased and Game Pass), a desktop mode for larger screens, plus dark/light mode and five high-contrast themes. A similar refresh is also beginning for cloud apps on supported TVs and VR headsets. Anyone who is not yet an Insider can join via the Xbox Insider Hub for Series X|S, Xbox One or Windows. The Verge, Neowin and IGN cover the announcement.", "weitere_links": ["The Verge: Xbox PC app redesign", "IGN: Xbox PC app 60% faster according to Microsoft", "Neowin: Redesign and faster launches"], "_src": "f708d215"}, "2026-11-05-nova-lake-h-foto": {"titel": "Leak: Photo allegedly shows an unreleased Intel Nova Lake-H package with multi-tile design", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Does this photo already show Intel's Nova Lake-H with 16 cores?", "kurz": "A photo shared by momomo_us allegedly shows an as-yet unreleased Intel processor package with several visible silicon tiles. When asked, Jaykihn confirmed a Nova Lake-H configuration with 4+8+4 cores. Intel has confirmed nothing; the image origin remains unclear.", "zusammenfassung": "Hardware leaker momomo_us (188号) shared a cropped photo on X on 05.11.2026 that, according to VideoCardz, is meant to show an as-yet unreleased Intel processor package with several visible silicon tiles. VideoCardz could not trace the industrial or embedded motherboard origin of the image; only the package is visible. Asked whether it was Nova Lake-H with a 4+8+4 configuration, leaker Jaykihn replied \"Yes\". In an update, momomo_us according to VideoCardz named 16 CPU cores, 4 Xe GPU cores and 18 MB of cache. That core count matches the rumored Core Ultra 9 4970H with 4+8+4, i.e. 16 CPU cores. In the VideoCardz table, however, the rumored 4970H is listed with 12 Xe3P graphics cores – that differs from momomo's \"4 Xe\" figure; which GPU figure is correct remains open. Whether the pictured sample is specifically the 4970H is unclear; VideoCardz does not mention clock speeds. For comparison, several Panther Lake-H models also use 4+8+4. TechPowerUp and Wccftech pick up the leak. Intel has not confirmed the claims.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: photo from leaker momomo_us (@momomo_us / 188号); Jaykihn replied \"Yes\" when asked about the 4+8+4 configuration. VideoCardz could not trace the origin of the cropped image. Intel has confirmed nothing; clock frequencies unknown.", "ursprungsquelle": "momomo_us (@momomo_us) on X", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp: Nova Lake-H SoC surfaces", "Wccftech: Nova Lake-H with six-tile setup"], "_src": "86f9c2aa"}, "2026-11-05-gta6-39-screenshots": {"titel": "Rockstar releases about 39 new official GTA 6 screenshots – two weeks to the US launch", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: Rockstar shows 39 new screenshots – two weeks to launch", "kurz": "Rockstar Games has released about 39 new official screenshots for Grand Theft Auto VI. The occasion is the countdown: in the US about two weeks remain until the 19.11.2026 launch. The images include scenes from Vice City / Leonida as well as Jason and Lucia.", "zusammenfassung": "Rockstar Games has officially released a large set of new screenshots for Grand Theft Auto VI. IGN and other outlets speak of 39 new images marking the final two weeks before the US launch. The US launch date 19.11.2026 is cited as the reference point. According to IGN, IGN Germany and PC Gamer, motifs include Vice City / Leonida scenes, protagonists Jason and Lucia, crime and nightlife moments, plus details such as dancers, combat dogs and very detailed skin pores. The screenshots come from Rockstar / the official site and the Rockstar X channel; they are confirmed marketing images, not leaks. Nothing beyond what the sources describe is speculated here. Google Trends DE shows GTA 6 at 60 as the highest of the compared terms over seven days; AT is at 41.", "weitere_links": ["IGN Germany: 39 new GTA 6 screenshots", "PC Gamer: launch screenshots with dancers, combat dogs and pores", "Rockstar Games (official site)"], "_src": "eb8f6ed6"}, "2026-11-05-discord-native-windows": {"titel": "Discord rebuilds Windows client in Rust: early build uses about 290 MB RAM instead of Electron gigabytes", "schlagzeile": "Discord leaves Electron: Rust client aims to end RAM hunger", "kurz": "Discord wants to move the Windows desktop client from Electron to a native Rust app with GPUI. An early build called Discord Phoenix shows about 290 MB RAM in a CTO screenshot. The current Electron app can reportedly reach the range of 4 GB.", "zusammenfassung": "Discord CTO Stanislav Vishnevskiy announced that Discord is dropping Electron for a Rust desktop app using GPUI. ComputerBase and Windows Latest cover the announcement. An early Windows 11 screenshot lists Discord Phoenix at 290.2 MB RAM. Windows Latest notes that Discord itself tested restarting the client when memory exceeds 4 GB, and that normal use is often under 1 GB while idle can easily reach 1 to 2 GB. Discord already uses Rust for infrastructure, voice and parts of the current client; now the whole client is to follow. When tests or the public rollout start is open. The move fits Microsoft’s Windows 11 efficiency agenda to run less memory-hungry apps on weaker PCs. It remains to be seen whether feature parity and stability will match the Electron version.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Latest: Electron out, Rust build at ~290 MB"], "_src": "5da0f5ef"}, "2026-11-05-fsr-412-xbox": {"titel": "AMD FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 available to Xbox Series X|S developers in the October 2026 GDK", "schlagzeile": "FSR 4.1.2 comes to Xbox – AI upscaling for the first time", "kurz": "With the Microsoft GDK from October 2026, developers can use AMD FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 on Xbox Series X and S. For the first time, ML-based AMD FSR upscaling is available on the consoles. Existing games do not get it automatically; studios must integrate it.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD announced on GPUOpen that FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 is available for Xbox Series X|S via the Microsoft Game Development Kit from October 2026. Alexander Blake-Davies writes that this brings ML-based AMD FSR upscaling to the Xbox consoles for the first time; previously only analytical FSR was available there. For Series X and Series S there are two INT8 models: Full and a new Lite. According to AMD, Lite is less than half the size and offloads the GPU more. Both run on Series X and Series S. Upscaler memory use depends on render and output resolution, not on the model – so the choice is a performance trade-off, not a memory one. The API matches the FSR SDK under Windows; quality modes are Native AA, Quality, Balanced, Performance and Ultra Performance. Via FSR SDK 2.4 and an ASUS preview driver, the technology also applies to ROG Xbox Ally handhelds (Ally X and X20 first). This is about developer access: studios must integrate it, there are no automatic updates for existing games, and AMD has not named specific titles. VideoCardz, PC Gamer and TechPowerUp report on it.", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz: FSR 4.1.2 with ML on Series X|S", "PC Gamer: FSR 4.1.2 on Xbox and handhelds", "TechPowerUp: FSR Upscaling 4.1.2 for Xbox"], "_src": "71d4e824"}, "2026-11-05-geforce-8800-gtx-demo": {"titel": "Free Steam demo \"GeForce 8800 GTX – 20 Years of a Legend\" celebrates 20 years of the CUDA GPU", "schlagzeile": "Nvidia lets you unbox the 8800 GTX – but needs an RTX 4070", "kurz": "Since 05.11.2026 the free demo \"GeForce 8800 GTX – 20 Years of a Legend\" is available on Steam. It lets you unbox the 2006 card and install it in a contemporary PC – rendered with path tracing and DLSS 4.5. An RTX 4070 is required as a minimum.", "zusammenfassung": "For the roughly 20th anniversary of the GeForce 8800 GTX (market launch on 08.11.2006), the free Steam demo \"GeForce 8800 GTX – 20 Years of a Legend\" was released on 05.11.2026. It was created by Unreal Engine artist Dylan Browne with support from NVIDIA. The semi-interactive demo lets you unbox the card, install it in a PC of the era and explore a 2006 gaming room with Easter eggs. Technically it uses path tracing, DLSS 4.5 with Ray Reconstruction and Dynamic Multi Frame Generation as well as RTX Mega Geometry. Steam system requirements list an RTX 4070, 32 GB RAM, 30 GB of storage and driver 621.12 or newer as the minimum; an RTX 5080 is recommended. The 8800 GTX was considered the first CUDA-capable GPU. A version for GeForce NOW Ultimate is said to follow soon according to reports from eTeknix and The Verge. VideoCardz and Wccftech also cover the campaign.", "weitere_links": ["eTeknix: 20th-anniversary Steam demo", "The Verge: 8800 GTX unboxing demo", "VideoCardz: Unboxing game needs RTX 4070", "Wccftech: GeForce 8800 GTX turns 20"], "_src": "16d23a91"}, "2026-11-05-openssh-musl-bypass": {"titel": "OpenSSH and musl: Long passwords can crack passwordless accounts – fix in 10.6p2", "schlagzeile": "OpenSSH flaw: long passwords crack locked logins (musl)", "kurz": "On some Linux systems with musl and without PAM, attackers can crack accounts without a password hash using a very long password. OpenSSH 10.6p2 and updated Alpine packages close the gap; sshd must be restarted afterwards. Until then, PasswordAuthentication no helps.", "zusammenfassung": "OpenSSH and Alpine Linux warn of a severe but niche flaw in OpenSSH without PAM on musl-based systems. According to Alpine and heise, the Alpine package openssh-server (without PAM) or openssh-server-pam with UsePAM no is mainly affected. If an attacker reaches the SSH port and PasswordAuthentication is enabled, they can log in without knowing a password – if at least one account has \"*\" in the shadow field (typical for key-only) and at the same time at least one local account has a $5$ or $6$ hash. The attack sends a very long password of 257 to 1024 bytes: musl-crypt() returns \"*\" as an error value for keys over 256 bytes, which matches the stored \"*\" and lets the check pass. No CVE had been assigned at the time of the advisories. The fix is in OpenSSH 10.6p2; Alpine has published updated packages. After the upgrade, sshd must be restarted. Workaround: set PasswordAuthentication no and restart sshd. OpenSSH developer Damien Miller advises disabling password logins immediately. According to heise, the project assumes the bug is rather not caused in OpenSSH itself, but 10.6p2 mitigates it. The issue was reported by Özgün Kültekin of Wakefield; BleepingComputer and Alpine describe the conditions in detail.", "weitere_links": ["heise: OpenSSH and Alpine warn of flaw", "BleepingComputer: Flaw in password-locked accounts"], "_src": "beadd996"}, "2026-11-04-gta6-vorbestellungen-750-mio": {"titel": "GTA 6: Sensor Tower estimates over 750 million US dollars in pre-order revenue", "schlagzeile": "Analysts: GTA 6 makes over $750M before it even launches", "kurz": "According to an estimate by analytics firm Sensor Tower, GTA 6 had been pre-ordered around 7.7 million times by 03.11.2026. That equals roughly 751 million US dollars in revenue on PS5 and Xbox. There are no official figures on this from Rockstar or Take-Two.", "zusammenfassung": "According to IGN, analytics firm Sensor Tower has analysed the pre-orders of Grand Theft Auto VI. By 03.11.2026, an estimated 7.71 million copies had been pre-ordered, which equals around 751 million US dollars in revenue. Most of it comes from the PlayStation 5: Sensor Tower sees about 74 percent of pre-orders and around 559 million US dollars there, and about 26 percent and around 192 million US dollars on Xbox. The Ultimate Edition costs 100 US dollars, the standard version 80 US dollars. According to IGN, Take-Two CEO Strauss Zelnick sees the pre-orders mainly as a sign of the most loyal fans. For comparison: according to IGN, GTA 5 made 800 million US dollars in its first 24 hours in 2013 and passed one billion after three days. Whether GTA 6 breaks that record will only be clear after launch. Important: this is an estimate by a market research firm, not figures from Rockstar or Take-Two. GTA 6 launches on 19.11.2026 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S, and a PC version has still not been announced.", "_src": "e55d6220"}, "2026-11-04-windows-paint-luecke": {"titel": "Windows 11: Security flaw in Paint (CVE-2026-83844) – patched version not reaching many users", "schlagzeile": "Flaw in Windows Paint: The fix exists, but many users aren't getting it", "kurz": "The Paint app in Windows 11 has a security flaw that attackers could use to run code remotely. Microsoft already shipped a fix via the Microsoft Store on 13.10.2026. According to reports, however, many users and admins are not offered the patched version at all.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft tracks the Paint vulnerability as CVE-2026-83844 and rates it 8.1 out of 10 points. Microsoft itself classifies it as \"Important\", one level below \"Critical\". It is an out-of-bounds read that, in the worst case, allows malicious code to be executed over the network without the user having to click anything. According to Microsoft, however, an attack is difficult to pull off, and no attacks in the wild are known so far. Because Paint is updated via the Microsoft Store, the regular Windows Update alone does not protect against the flaw. According to Windows Latest, Paint is considered safe from version 11.2609.401.0, but this version did not show up in the Store even with automatic updates enabled. Admins on Reddit and in the Microsoft forum also report that they cannot get the stated version. According to Neowin, Microsoft's security page initially listed a different version number, possibly a typo. According to Neowin, a staggered rollout is also possible. The installed version can be checked in PowerShell with the command \"Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.Paint\". If you don't need Paint, you can also uninstall the app for now.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Latest: Paint flaw and missing update", "Microsoft Security Update Guide: CVE-2026-83844"], "_src": "2d5490bd"}, "2026-11-04-nova-lake-90-grad-limit": {"titel": "Leak: Intel Core Ultra 4000 \"Nova Lake-S\" said to clock at most 5.1 GHz above 90 °C", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Intel's Nova Lake said to manage only 5.1 GHz above 90 °C", "kurz": "According to leaker Jaykihn, all desktop processors of the Nova Lake-S series will limit their clock to a maximum of 5.1 GHz above 90 °C. The limit reportedly cannot be raised. The information is preliminary and not confirmed by Intel.", "zusammenfassung": "On 04.11.2026, Intel leaker Jaykihn wrote on X that Intel's upcoming Core Ultra 4000 \"Nova Lake-S\" desktop processors will get a fixed temperature limit. Above 90 °C, the maximum core clock will reportedly be capped at 5.1 GHz on all models. This is said to work independently of the usual emergency brake at 100 °C (TjMax), at which the CPU throttles anyway. According to Jaykihn, the new 90-degree limit also cannot be shifted upwards. He explicitly calls the information preliminary. Models that don't clock above 5.1 GHz anyway would not be affected by the limit. Faster models could lose part of their boost if cooling is insufficient. TechPowerUp points out that the current Core Ultra 9 285K reaches up to 5.7 GHz and has a higher TjMax of 105 °C. In addition, according to earlier reports, the 28-core flagship is said to draw up to 296 W for short periods, which would likely require a strong cooler. According to TechPowerUp, Nova Lake-S is expected in the first quarter of 2027. Intel has not confirmed the details, so it remains a leak.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: The only source is Intel leaker Jaykihn on X, who himself calls the information preliminary. VideoCardz and TechPowerUp report on the post. Intel has confirmed nothing, and final clock speeds are not known.", "ursprungsquelle": "Jaykihn (@jaykihn0) on X", "weitere_links": ["Jaykihn on X (original post)", "TechPowerUp: Nova Lake-S throttles to 5.1 GHz above 90 °C"], "_src": "434bcacb"}, "2026-11-04-god-of-war-laufey-verschoben": {"titel": "God of War Laufey delayed: New date is 20.05.2027", "schlagzeile": "God of War Laufey delayed: Fans have to wait three months longer", "kurz": "Sony Santa Monica has officially delayed God of War Laufey. Instead of 16.02.2027, the game now launches on 20.05.2027. The studio wants to use the extra time for the final polish.", "zusammenfassung": "PlayStation studio Santa Monica announced on X on 04.11.2026 that God of War Laufey will release later. It was previously planned for 16.02.2027, and the new date is 20.05.2027. The studio explains the delay by saying it wants to give the game its final polish and push it to its full potential. Since the reveal in June, the team has been grateful for the fans' great excitement, the statement says. Laufey is the first mainline game in the series in which Kratos is not the main character. Instead, players take control of Faye, Kratos's wife and Atreus's mother, who died before the events of the 2018 God of War. According to the official description, she awakens after her death in a kind of afterlife of the gods, the \"Everywhen\". Eurogamer points out that the game thereby avoids a packed February with many big releases. The studio plans to share more news soon.", "weitere_links": ["Eurogamer: God of War Laufey delayed to May 2027", "Neowin: Sony delays God of War Laufey"], "_src": "87a1ab5a"}, "2026-11-04-amd-rekord-gaming-einbruch": {"titel": "AMD: Record revenue of $13.4 billion, gaming revenue down 40 percent – likely more revenue than Intel for the first time in Q4", "schlagzeile": "AMD earns more than ever – but gaming revenue collapses by 40 %", "kurz": "AMD made a record 13.4 billion US dollars in revenue in the third quarter of 2026, mainly thanks to data centers. Gaming revenue, on the other hand, fell by 40 percent because expensive memory is slowing down graphics cards, consoles and PCs. According to its own forecast, AMD is likely to make more revenue than Intel for the first time in the fourth quarter.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD reported record revenue of 13.4 billion US dollars for the third quarter of 2026. According to ComputerBase, 8.5 billion US dollars of that came from the data center business, which according to TechPowerUp grew 97 percent year over year. Gaming looks very different: this segment plunged 40 percent compared to the same quarter last year, to 773 million US dollars. AMD cites the shortages and price increases for memory, which make graphics cards, consoles with AMD chips and complete PCs more expensive. For the fourth quarter, AMD expects around 17 billion US dollars in revenue, plus or minus three percent. Intel only expects 15 to 16 billion US dollars for the same period. Even the low end of AMD's forecast is above the high end of Intel's, so according to TechPowerUp AMD would make more revenue than Intel for the first time. This only applies to revenue, not profit. At the same time, AMD CEO Lisa Su expects a double-digit decline in PC sales for 2027. For PC gamers, this means AMD's focus keeps shifting towards data centers and AI.", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp: AMD heading for its first quarter with more revenue than Intel", "PC Games Hardware: AMD quarterly results"], "_src": "0136260f"}, "2026-11-03-arc-b580-eol": {"titel": "Leak: Intel might discontinue the Arc B580 and focus on pricier Arc Pro cards", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Is Intel's budget graphics card Arc B580 about to be axed?", "kurz": "According to leaker Haze2K1, Intel might phase out the Arc B580 graphics card. The reason is said to be the more profitable Arc Pro cards using the same graphics chip. This is an unconfirmed rumor, and Intel has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "On 02.11.2026, leaker Haze2K1 wrote on X that the Intel Arc B580 might be discontinued. According to the post, Intel wants to focus more on pro and workstation cards such as the Arc Pro B50, which are said to be selling well for AI applications. TechPowerUp and Wccftech picked up the post. The Arc B580 launched in December 2024 at 249 US dollars as an affordable gaming card with 12 GB of graphics memory. According to TechPowerUp, the Arc Pro B60 uses the same graphics chip but has 24 GB of memory and costs around 500 US dollars, which likely brings more profit per chip. According to TechPowerUp, the B580 is already sold out at many retailers or only available above its original price. Haze2K1 phrases it cautiously and only says the card might be phased out. The rumor does not say whether the smaller Arc B570 would also be affected. Intel has not commented on the rumor, so it is unconfirmed.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: the only source is a post by leaker Haze2K1 on X, who himself only says “might”. TechPowerUp and Wccftech repeat the post; there is no independent second source. Intel has not commented.", "ursprungsquelle": "Haze2K1 on X", "weitere_links": ["Haze2K1 on X (original post)", "Wccftech: Intel might discontinue Arc B580"], "_src": "115ef362"}, "2026-11-03-windows11-8gb-ram": {"titel": "Windows 11 runs noticeably better on PCs with 8 GB of RAM – Microsoft gives details and requirements", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 on 8 GB PCs: up to 40% faster multitasking promised", "kurz": "Microsoft has optimized Windows 11 for PCs with only 8 GB of RAM. According to Microsoft, the system responds up to 20 percent faster, and multitasking is up to 40 percent faster in a lab test. You need Windows 11 26H2 build 26300.9818 or later and up-to-date apps.", "zusammenfassung": "On 03.11.2026, Microsoft explained on the Windows Experience Blog how Windows 11 should run better on PCs with 8 GB of RAM. According to Windows chief Pavan Davuluri, Start, Search, the context menu, Settings, Snipping Tool and File Explorer respond up to 20 percent faster on such devices, measured via telemetry data. The up to 40 percent faster multitasking time comes from a single lab test on an HP laptop with a Snapdragon X Plus, and Microsoft itself says it is not a general benchmark. Thanks to better-tuned memory compression, Windows can keep up to 2 GB more active data in RAM instead of moving it to the slower SSD. As a result, open apps and browser tabs should need to reload less often. Together with Edge and the Microsoft 365 apps, extra memory use during multitasking drops by up to 900 MB, with Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook alone saving around 360 MB. On 8 GB PCs, widgets only load when you open the widgets panel, which saves about 200 MB. The requirement is Windows 11 26H2 build 26300.9818 or later, which first arrives via the optional update of 28.10.2026 and, according to Windows Latest, rolls out to everyone on Patch Tuesday, 10.11.2026. Edge, Microsoft 365 and Teams should also be up to date, because some of the improvements come through app updates. For 3D modeling, demanding video editing or large datasets, Microsoft still recommends 16 GB or more.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Experience Blog (Microsoft): Raising the bar for 8 GB Windows 11 PCs", "TechPowerUp: up to 40% faster multitasking on 8 GB PCs"], "_src": "dd699a8a"}, "2026-11-03-rtx50-preise-china": {"titel": "Leak: board partners raise GeForce RTX 50 prices in China – up to 3,300 yuan more", "schlagzeile": "Leak: RTX 50 cards reportedly getting pricier again – up to 3,300 yuan", "kurz": "According to the Chinese industry platform Channelgate, NVIDIA board partners in China are raising GeForce RTX 50 prices again. The reported increases range from about 100 to 3,300 yuan depending on the model. This is not confirmed, and the figures only apply to China.", "zusammenfassung": "The Chinese industry platform Channelgate reports that graphics card makers in China are raising GeForce RTX 50 prices again in November. According to PC Games Hardware, Colorful has reportedly already implemented the new prices, and Galax is said to follow this week. According to TechPowerUp, the reported increases range from about 100 to 150 yuan for the RTX 5060 Ti with 8 GB up to 2,200 to 3,300 yuan for the China-only RTX 5090 D V2. For the RTX 5080 the report mentions 2,500 to 2,800 yuan, for the RTX 5070 Ti around 1,000 yuan and for the RTX 5070 about 600 to 900 yuan more. Converted, that would be roughly 15 to almost 500 US dollars. The report cites tight graphics memory supply and more expensive raw materials such as copper as reasons. According to TechPowerUp, the higher prices could reach retail one to two weeks later. Because RTX 50 cards are getting scarce in China, retailers are reportedly turning more to older models like the RTX 3060 and to Radeon cards, according to PCGH. NVIDIA and the named board partners have not officially confirmed the increases. Whether and how much this affects prices in Europe is unclear.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Unconfirmed: all reports are based on the Chinese industry platform Channelgate (Board Channels circle). NVIDIA, Colorful and Galax have not confirmed anything officially. The prices apply to China and cannot be transferred 1:1 to Europe.", "ursprungsquelle": "Channelgate (Board Channels), China", "weitere_links": ["TechPowerUp: RTX 50 set for price hike of up to 500 US dollars"], "_src": "1fa9041b"}, "2026-11-03-elder-scrolls-6-sentinel": {"titel": "The Elder Scrolls 6 is officially called “Sentinel” – Bethesda reveals title and logo", "schlagzeile": "After 8 years of silence: The Elder Scrolls 6 finally has a name", "kurz": "For its 40th anniversary, Bethesda revealed the full title of the next Elder Scrolls role-playing game: The Elder Scrolls VI: Sentinel. Sentinel is a city in the region of Hammerfell. There is still no release date.", "zusammenfassung": "On 03.11.2026, in a video celebrating the studio's 40th anniversary, Bethesda officially confirmed that The Elder Scrolls VI carries the subtitle “Sentinel”. The video shows the title and logo, and Todd Howard also speaks in it. Sentinel is a port city in the province of Hammerfell in the northwest of Tamriel. According to IGN, a quote in the video is dated to a time after the events of Skyrim. The game was first announced at E3 2018, and there has been little official information since then. A report had already predicted the name the week before, and now it is confirmed. Bethesda did not show a release date or gameplay. According to IGN, the platforms are Xbox and PC, while a PlayStation release remains open. Eurogamer speculates that more could be shown at The Game Awards in December, but that is not confirmed.", "weitere_links": ["IGN Germany: The Elder Scrolls 6 is called Sentinel", "PC Gamer: The Elder Scrolls 6: Sentinel is official"], "_src": "0e2f52ba"}, "2026-11-03-gta6-preload-212gb": {"titel": "GTA 6: Rockstar confirms pre-load from 10.11.2026 and a download of up to 212 GB", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6 eats up to 212 GB – and the pre-load starts earlier than expected", "kurz": "Rockstar Games has officially confirmed that the GTA 6 pre-download on PS5 and Xbox Series X|S begins on 10.11.2026. Depending on the console, the download is up to 212 GB. The game is still set to launch on 19.11.2026.", "zusammenfassung": "On the afternoon of 03.11.2026, Rockstar Games published the details of the Grand Theft Auto VI pre-download. On PS5, the pre-load starts on 10.11.2026 at midnight local time, on Xbox Series X|S on the same day at 0:00 GMT, which is 1 a.m. in Austria and Germany. According to Rockstar, the download is up to 212 GB depending on the device, and the PlayStation Blog also advises freeing up at least 212 GB of storage. This largely confirms a leak from late October that said the game would take up around 210 GB on PS5. According to the reports, the pre-load had originally been announced for 12.11.2026, so digital players can now start two days earlier. The boxed versions are due in stores on 12.11.2026 and, according to the reports, only contain a download code. The release stays on 19.11.2026 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. At launch, Rockstar also plans to offer a printable cover poster and a map of Leonida on its website. The information does not clearly say whether the Xbox Series S needs less storage space.", "weitere_links": ["PlayStation Blog: pre-download starts on November 10", "IGN Germany: pre-load times and install size confirmed", "VGC: Rockstar details pre-load date and file size"], "_src": "91689255"}, "2026-11-03-fedora-45": {"titel": "Fedora Linux 45 is out – with GNOME 51, KDE Plasma 6.8 and Linux kernel 7.2", "schlagzeile": "Fedora 45 is here: new desktop, new installer and verifiable builds", "kurz": "The Fedora Project has released Fedora Linux 45. The Workstation edition uses GNOME 51, the KDE edition Plasma 6.8, running on Linux kernel 7.2. New features include Stratis in the installer and reproducible package builds.", "zusammenfassung": "Fedora Linux 45 was released on 03.11.2026, about six months after Fedora 44 and, according to Phoronix, after two delays. The Workstation edition ships with GNOME 51, the KDE Plasma Desktop edition with Plasma 6.8. Linux 7.2 is used as the kernel. According to the official Fedora Magazine, one of the biggest new features is support for the Stratis storage system directly in the Anaconda installer. KMSCON now handles the virtual text console by default, and according to 9to5Linux Fedora relies on fully reproducible package builds. Signature checking for RPM packages is enabled by default and ptrace is restricted by default, which is meant to improve security. The Atomic variants such as Silverblue and Kinoite now install via the new WebUI installer. For developers, GCC 16.2, LLVM 23, Python 3.15, Go 1.27 and Podman 6 are among the included tools. The old VPN plugins NetworkManager-vpnc and NetworkManager-fortisslvpn are dropped, so anyone using them should migrate their connections before upgrading. Existing Fedora 44 installations can be upgraded via DNF system-upgrade.", "weitere_links": ["Fedora Magazine (official): Announcing Fedora Linux 45", "Phoronix: Fedora 45 Released"], "_src": "be19dcc2"}, "2026-11-02-zelda-oot-remake-puppenlook": {"titel": "Zelda: Ocarina of Time for Switch 2: Nintendo explains the remake's controversial puppet look", "schlagzeile": "The Zelda remake looks like a puppet show – Nintendo explains why", "kurz": "The remake of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time launches on November 5 for Nintendo Switch 2. Its art style with puppet-like characters divides fans. In an interview, the developers explain that they deliberately wanted a “puppet-show feel” instead of pure photorealism.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Polygon, Nintendo has commented on the controversial art style of the remake of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time. Link, Zelda and other characters look more like puppets than photorealistic people, which has sparked debate among longtime fans. Art director Aya Shida says in a developer interview that the goal was not simply to make everything look realistic. Hyrule was meant to feel like a dense world that could truly exist, while the colorful, quirky characters provide a contrast to it, just like in the original. According to Shida, the team's guiding keywords were a “puppet-show feel” and “the analog feel of practical effects films”. Series producer Eiji Aonuma explains that the team feels nostalgic when looking back at the Nintendo 64 original, and expressing that nostalgia led to the analog puppet look. According to Video Games Chronicle, the remake launches on Thursday, November 5, 2026, for Nintendo Switch 2. It is being developed by Nintendo's own division Nintendo EPD, which also made Breath of the Wild and Tears of the Kingdom. Whether the style convinces in the end will only become clear with the reviews after launch.", "weitere_links": ["Video Games Chronicle: Zelda: Ocarina of Time UK midnight launch"], "_src": "dda2e7e2"}, "2026-11-02-rtx5080-preis-heise": {"titel": "RTX 5080 barely available under 2,000 euros, report: 24 GB version could be delayed", "schlagzeile": "RTX 5080 breaks 2,000 euros: over 30% more expensive in just two weeks", "kurz": "According to heise online, the GeForce RTX 5080 can currently barely be found under 2,000 euros; its price has risen by more than 30 percent in two weeks. heise cites the rumors about the RTX 5090 being discontinued as the reason; that card now costs around 8,000 euros. According to an unconfirmed report by BenchLife, the expected 24 GB version of the RTX 5080 could be delayed.", "zusammenfassung": "After the RTX 5090, the RTX 5080 is now also becoming much more expensive, according to heise online: NVIDIA's second-fastest gaming graphics card is currently barely available under 2,000 euros. That is more than 30 percent more than just two weeks ago. In mid-October, rumors emerged that NVIDIA might take the RTX 5090 off the market, which according to heise fueled demand for the 5080. The RTX 5090 itself now costs around 8,000 euros; NVIDIA's last MSRP was 2,099 euros. NVIDIA denied that the 5090 is being discontinued, but only with the wording that the card will “continue to ship”. According to heise, this does not make clear whether it will continue to be manufactured. In October, there were also reports that an RTX 5080 with 24 instead of 16 GB of GDDR7 would be unveiled in January 2027. According to the Taiwanese site BenchLife, however, board partners have not yet received the necessary design documents from NVIDIA, even though they were reportedly planned for October. This is an unconfirmed report; NVIDIA has not commented on it. In addition, the stock of GB203 chips in China is said to be already sold and to last only one to two more months. heise names the AI boom as the cause of the shortage: the same chips and the scarce GDDR7 memory are also used in expensive workstation cards with higher margins. Anyone looking for a high-end card should therefore expect prices to stay high for now.", "weitere_links": ["Wccftech: RTX 5080 24 GB may miss January 2027 launch"], "_src": "ecd4a72d"}, "2026-11-02-windows11-smart-app-control-fix": {"titel": "Microsoft fixes bug: Smart App Control could no longer be turned on after the October update", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11: protection feature grayed out after October update – fix is here", "kurz": "After the October security update KB5127648, the Windows 11 protection feature Smart App Control could no longer be turned on on some PCs. Microsoft fixed the bug with the updates from October 28, 2026 onward, including the optional preview update KB5127936. Where Smart App Control was already active, protection remained in place the whole time.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, Microsoft has fixed a known bug in Windows 11 that appeared after the October 2026 security update KB5127648. On affected devices running Windows 11 24H2 and later, the Smart App Control option in Windows Security was grayed out and could not be turned on. Smart App Control works together with SmartScreen and Microsoft Defender to block potentially harmful apps. Only PCs on which the feature had previously been turned off were affected. Where it was already active, the devices remained protected, according to Microsoft. The bug is fixed with the Windows updates from October 28, 2026 and later, including the optional preview update KB5127936. Microsoft recommends installing the latest update. For company PCs that don't want to wait for the next Patch Tuesday, Microsoft provides a workaround via two registry entries or special Group Policies, each requiring a restart. According to BleepingComputer, KB5127936 also fixes Remote Desktop problems when “Administrator protection” is enabled and VPN errors after the September 2026 updates. Home users don't need to do anything except install the update.", "_src": "2c58e168"}, "2026-11-02-raspberry-pi5-16gb-preis": {"titel": "Raspberry Pi 5 with 16 GB RAM gets more expensive for the fourth time: 385 instead of 305 US dollars", "schlagzeile": "Raspberry Pi 5 with 16 GB now costs $385 – three times its launch price", "kurz": "Raspberry Pi is raising the list price of the Raspberry Pi 5 with 16 GB of RAM from 305 to 385 US dollars. It is the fourth increase since December 2025; at launch the price was 120 US dollars. The reason is rising RAM prices, but the Raspberry Pi 500+ is not getting more expensive this time.", "zusammenfassung": "According to heise online, the Raspberry Pi 5 with 16 GB of LPDDR4 RAM is getting more expensive again. The list price rises by 80 to 385 US dollars. It is already the fourth increase after December 2025, February 2026 and April 2026. At launch, this version cost 120 US dollars or around 135 euros, according to heise. The manufacturer cites constantly rising RAM prices as the reason. Raspberry Pi CEO Eben Upton explains that there is no alternative supplier for the 16 GB memory chip. The same chip is also used in the Compute Module 5 and the Raspberry Pi 500+. The 16 GB version of the Compute Module 5 becomes 40 US dollars more expensive, while the Raspberry Pi 500+ does not this time. According to heise, some other Raspberry Pi models are also getting more expensive. Because of the shortages, the manufacturer has introduced additional assembly options for several products so that memory chips from other manufacturers can be used. Golem.de reports that a Pi 5 now costs almost 350 euros. How much prices rise in stores depends on the retailer.", "weitere_links": ["Golem.de: Pi 5 und Compute Module – Raspberry Pi kostet mittlerweile fast 350 Euro"], "_src": "7815dfa5"}, "2026-11-02-rtx5090-pro5500-igorslab": {"titel": "RTX 5090 vs. RTX PRO 5500: igor'sLAB examines whether NVIDIA's pro card is taking chips away from the gaming GPU", "schlagzeile": "Over €8,000 for an RTX 5090: Is NVIDIA's pro card stealing its chips?", "kurz": "According to igor'sLAB, an RTX 5090 available for immediate delivery cost €8,059 at a German retailer on 1 November 2026, while the Founders Edition MSRP is €2,099. The analysis examines whether NVIDIA prefers to put suitable GB202 chips into the upcoming RTX PRO 5500 pro card, which has the same number of compute units. The verdict: economically plausible, but not publicly proven.", "zusammenfassung": "igor'sLAB has looked into why the GeForce RTX 5090 is hardly available at its original price anymore. In a retailer sample from 1 November 2026, an INNO3D RTX 5090 iCHILL X3 available for immediate delivery cost €8,059 at ALTERNATE, and a ZOTAC Solid OC White cost €8,499 at Caseking. The German MSRP of the Founders Edition is €2,099, but the Founders Edition is listed as unavailable there. The focus is on the upcoming RTX PRO 5500 Blackwell Workstation Edition: according to partner listings, it also uses the large GB202 chip with 170 active streaming multiprocessors and 21,760 CUDA cores, but has 84 GB of GDDR7 with ECC instead of 32 GB. Citing anonymous sources, Reuters reported on 20 October 2026 that more than three million PRO 5500 cards had been ordered from China at around $11,400 each. That would give NVIDIA an incentive to put suitable chips into the expensive pro card rather than the gaming card. However, igor'sLAB stresses that this has not been publicly proven: there is no data on chip yields or on how chips are split between the two products. In addition, supply of gaming cards was already tight before the reported PRO 5500 orders, and regular deliveries of the pro card are only expected to start in the first quarter of 2027. The analysis names GDDR7 memory as a further bottleneck, which according to TrendForce is increasingly being allocated to AI and server applications. The cost and margin examples in the article are explicitly based on freely chosen assumptions and are not real NVIDIA figures. The igor'sLAB verdict: the pro card is a serious competitor for chips and memory, but a measurable displacement of the RTX 5090 has not been proven.", "_src": "bff68b5d"}, "2026-11-01-linux-7-4-rc1": {"titel": "Linux 7.4-rc1 released: Largest merge window in kernel history, much of it triggered by AI", "schlagzeile": "Linux 7.4: Record update thanks to an AI flood – and Torvalds likes it", "kurz": "Linus Torvalds has released the first test version of Linux 7.4. With almost 20,000 commits, the merge window was the largest in kernel history, and a large part of it was triggered by AI tools. New features include preparations for AMD's Zen 6 processors and HDMI 2.1 enabled by default in the AMDGPU driver.", "zusammenfassung": "Linus Torvalds released Linux 7.4-rc1 on Sunday evening, closing the merge window on schedule. According to Torvalds, it was unusually large with almost 20,000 commits instead of the usual 15,000 or so, and according to Phoronix the largest in kernel history. Torvalds names the flood of AI-triggered changes as the main reason. He sees it positively: he would much rather have this work land in the merge window than as a wave of fixes during the test phase. According to Torvalds, another reason could be that Linux 7.4 is expected to become the next long-term support version. In his words, a third of the patch consists of AMD GPU register definitions alone. According to Phoronix, the new features include support for upcoming Ryzen processors with Zen 6, HDMI 2.1 enabled by default in the AMDGPU driver and the AMD PerfOpt feature for better AI performance on Radeon iGPUs. There is also Intel IPU8 support for upcoming Nova Lake laptops, more support for Snapdragon X2 laptops, initial groundwork for Apple's M4 (not yet ready for everyday use) and faster kernel builds. Several test versions will now follow before the final release. If everything goes to plan, Linux 7.4 will be released on 20 December 2026, according to Phoronix. Regular users are best off waiting until their distribution ships the new kernel.", "weitere_links": ["LWN.net: Kernel prepatch 7.4-rc1"], "_src": "4f089b1b"}, "2026-11-01-gta6-210gb-download": {"titel": "GTA 6: 210 GB download size for PS5 surfaces", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Does GTA 6 really need a whopping 210 GB on PS5?", "kurz": "According to the data account PlayStation Game Size, the PS5 download of GTA 6 is said to be around 210 GB, and Insider Gaming says it can corroborate this. Rockstar has not officially stated a size, so the figure is unconfirmed. What is certain: digital pre-orders can pre-load from 12 November 2026, and the game launches on 19 November 2026.", "zusammenfassung": "The X account PlayStation Game Size (@PlaystationSize), which specialises in store data, named a download size of 210 GB for the standard edition of Grand Theft Auto VI on PlayStation on 27 October 2026. Insider Gaming reported on it on 1 November 2026 and writes that it can corroborate the figure. According to Insider Gaming, that would make GTA 6 one of the largest games ever. Rockstar Games and Take-Two have not officially confirmed the size, so the figure is considered unconfirmed. Insider Gaming also points out that the size may still change before launch and that a day-one patch could take up additional storage. The source gives no figure for the Xbox version. The dates, on the other hand, are officially confirmed: according to Rockstar, digital pre-orders can pre-load from 12 November 2026, and the game launches on 19 November 2026 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. According to Rockstar, the boxed version only contains a download code and is also available from 12 November 2026. According to Rockstar, the standard edition costs $79.99 and the Ultimate Edition $99.99. Anyone who wants to play at launch should plan plenty of free space on their console in good time.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Comes from the data account @PlaystationSize (analyses store data); Insider Gaming says it can corroborate the figure. Not officially confirmed by Rockstar or Take-Two; the size may change before launch and through a day-one patch.", "ursprungsquelle": "PlayStation Game Size (@PlaystationSize) on X, 27 October 2026", "weitere_links": ["Take-Two/Rockstar: pre-orders, pre-load from 12 November 2026, launch 19 November 2026 (official)"], "_src": "386ea700"}, "2026-11-01-windows11-26h2-alle": {"titel": "Windows 11 26H2 now available for all eligible PCs, including directly from Windows 10", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 26H2 is now available to everyone – including Windows 10 PCs", "kurz": "Microsoft has completed the phased rollout of Windows 11 26H2: according to Microsoft, the update has been available for all eligible devices since 28 October 2026. According to Neowin, it is now also offered directly via Windows Update to compatible Windows 10 PCs. The requirement remains that the PC meets the hardware requirements of Windows 11.", "zusammenfassung": "Microsoft made Windows 11 26H2 generally available at the end of September 2026, but rolled it out in phases as usual. This is meant to prevent major problems from hitting many devices at once, which matters especially for businesses. According to Neowin, the rollout first reached full availability for devices running Windows 11 25H2 and 24H2. Microsoft now writes that, as of 28 October 2026, Windows 11 26H2 is available for all eligible devices. According to Neowin, this also applies to compatible Windows 10 PCs, which are now offered the update directly via Windows Update. The outlet says it observed this on one of its own Windows 10 machines. Anyone already on Windows 11 24H2 or 25H2 who has not yet been offered the update can manually install the eKB5121794 enablement package, according to Neowin. However, this does not work from Windows 10 or older Windows 11 versions. For a clean install, current ISO files are available via Microsoft's Media Creation Tool. According to Neowin, 26H2 needs less RAM and feels snappier, though that is the outlet's own assessment. One catch remains: only PCs that meet the hardware requirements of Windows 11 get the offer.", "_src": "7b79cfea"}, "2026-11-01-rtx2080ti-22gb-pcgh": {"titel": "Used RTX 2080 Ti with 22 GB: PCGH tests the memory mod from China", "schlagzeile": "22 GB on an old RTX 2080 Ti: how good is the China mod really?", "kurz": "PC Games Hardware tested an RTX 2080 Ti whose video memory was doubled from 11 to 22 GB in China. At 1440p the difference is usually small, but in 4K and AI workloads the modded card clearly beats the original. There is no warranty for a conversion like this.", "zusammenfassung": "PC Games Hardware tested a modified GeForce RTX 2080 Ti with doubled video memory that a reader had bought via Alibaba. Instead of 11 GB, the board carries eleven 2 GB Samsung chips, i.e. 22 GB of GDDR6 on the unchanged 352-bit interface with 616 GB/s. A changed strap resistor lets the card run without a modified BIOS and with normal drivers. At 1440p with DLSS Quality, the differences to the 11 GB version are mostly small, but frame times are more even. In Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 and Spider-Man 2, the original card was around 20 percent behind according to the test. In 4K with DLSS Performance and FSR Frame Generation, the 11 GB card stuttered heavily, and Indiana Jones even crashed. Memory usage of up to 13.9 GB was measured in Spider-Man 2. In the AI test with ComfyUI, the 22 GB card needed about 315 seconds instead of around 540 seconds – an RTX 5070 Ti did the same in about 85 seconds. For buyers of used hardware this means: the mod can be worth it, but it is a modification without manufacturer warranty, and the quality of such conversions varies.", "weitere_links": ["PCGH test (original)"], "_src": "03eb821d"}, "2026-11-01-larrabee-fund": {"titel": "Complete Intel Larrabee developer system discovered in storage unit", "schlagzeile": "Storage unit find: unreleased Intel GPU discovered along with developer PC", "kurz": "A Reddit user discovered a complete developer system for Intel's Larrabee GPU, which never came to market, in a storage unit bought at auction. The PC boots Windows 7 and is even said to run Crysis, although the FPS figures have not been independently verified. The original software is now on the Internet Archive.", "zusammenfassung": "A Reddit user found a complete development system for Intel's never-released Larrabee GPU when a storage unit was auctioned off. The PC contains an Intel DX58SO motherboard with a C0-stepping engineering sample referred to as 'Intel Visual Adrenaline'. It came with two USB sticks containing the original software, which the finder has since uploaded to the Internet Archive. The system boots Windows 7 and supports Direct3D. According to the owner, Crysis ran at 720p on medium details at about 17 FPS, and allegedly at around 36 FPS with a different driver – these figures have not been independently verified. Intel cancelled Larrabee as a graphics card in 2010; the technology later lived on in the Xeon Phi accelerators. For hardware collectors, a complete system like this with software is a real rarity.", "_src": "e8e20545"}, "2026-10-31-nv-uefi-unlocker": {"titel": "Open-source tool unlocks more AI performance on RTX 20, 30 and 40", "schlagzeile": "Free tool gets up to 75% more AI performance from RTX cards – with a catch", "kurz": "The open-source tool “nv-uefi-unlocker” unlocks throttled compute units for AI workloads on RTX 20, 30 and 40 cards. In the reported tests, performance rose by around 29 to 75 percent depending on card and task. No benefit for games has been shown, Secure Boot must be off, and you use it at your own risk.", "zusammenfassung": "Developer physicsdolphin has released 'nv-uefi-unlocker', an open-source tool meant to unlock throttled compute units on GeForce cards for AI workloads. The tool boots from a USB stick before the actual driver and then also works under Windows. The change is not permanent and has to be reapplied after every cold boot. RTX 20, 30 and 40 are supported, GTX 16 only experimentally, RTX 50 not at all. Secure Boot must be disabled, and Turing cards also need GSP firmware. Reported results: an RTX 2070 gained 67 to 75 percent in FP32 GEMM, and an RTX 4060 laptop GPU rose from 29.89 to 49.33 TFLOPS in FP16. A user with an RTX 3080 LHR reported about 29 percent more speed in ComfyUI with SDXL, while the tool brings little for text generation with LLMs. Anyone who tries this does so at their own risk – no benefit for gaming performance has been shown.", "_src": "111abea6"}, "2026-10-31-amd-adrenalin-26-10-2": {"titel": "AMD Adrenalin 26.10.2: Optional Radeon driver fixes ten bugs, several issues remain open", "schlagzeile": "Radeon crashes: AMD's new driver fixes ten bugs – but not all of them", "kurz": "AMD has released the optional Adrenalin 26.10.2 graphics driver, which fixes ten bugs, including driver timeouts, crashes and system shutdowns on Radeon RX 7000 and RX 9000. It does not add support for new games. Several known issues, for example in Cyberpunk 2077 and Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced, remain open.", "zusammenfassung": "AMD released the optional Adrenalin Edition 26.10.2 graphics driver for Windows on 30 October 2026. According to the official release notes, it is a pure bug-fix update with ten fixes. Among other things, it fixes crashes or driver timeouts when other overlays such as the Xbox Game Bar are opened or closed while AMD's performance overlay is active. The Steam client also sometimes crashed on launch on Radeon cards, which should now be fixed. On the RX 7600, the driver fixes system shutdowns in Valor Mortis, and on the rest of the RX 7000 series driver timeouts in the same game. For the RX 9000 series, AMD fixes hangs in Death Stranding 2 with FSR enabled and crashes when switching between applications with FSR Frame Generation. There are also fixes for video playback on Windows 11 with hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling (HAGS) and a bug in the AMD Install Manager. Not everything is solved: in Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced, crashes can still occur on the RX 7000, and in War Thunder timeouts on the RX 5000. For War Thunder, AMD recommends the older 26.9.1 driver for now. In Cyberpunk 2077, some RX 9000 cards can crash when FSR upscaling, Anti-Lag and frame generation are active while a video plays on a second display; AMD then recommends turning off the in-game frame generation. According to AMD, Smart Access Memory may also be disabled after installation on Windows 10, so it is worth checking in the driver if in doubt. If you don't have any of the fixed problems, there's no need to install the optional driver right away.", "weitere_links": ["AMD: Release notes Adrenalin Edition 26.10.2 (official)"], "_src": "f1d0f566"}, "2026-10-31-altman-pc-ram": {"titel": "Sam Altman: PC RAM is a 'quite terrible' use of scarce DRAM capacity", "schlagzeile": "Sam Altman: the RAM in your PC is “quite terrible” use of memory", "kurz": "On the “Cheeky Pint” podcast, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman called it “quite terrible” that DRAM sits in PCs which, by his rough estimate, run only about five percent of the time. The background is the memory shortage, as manufacturers produce more and more server and AI memory. For PC builders this means RAM is unlikely to get cheaper any time soon.", "zusammenfassung": "OpenAI CEO Sam Altman talked about the current memory shortage on the 'Cheeky Pint' podcast with Stripe co-founder John Collison. He called it 'quite terrible' that DRAM sits in PCs that are only used about five percent of the time. The five percent is his own rough estimate, not a verified figure. The background is that memory manufacturers are increasingly shifting production to server and AI memory, which drives up prices for consumer RAM. VideoCardz clearly disagrees with Altman in its commentary. For PC builders, the statement is above all a sign that RAM prices are unlikely to fall again any time soon.", "_src": "be0c42aa"}, "2026-10-30-linux-kernel-tcp-luecke": {"titel": "Linux kernel: severe flaw in TCP code enables remote root attacks on MPTCP servers", "schlagzeile": "Linux: kernel flaw allows remote root access – update now", "kurz": "A use-after-free flaw in the Linux kernel's IPv4 TCP code (CVE-2026-98432) affects kernels as far back as version 4.4. Researchers have demonstrated remote root access on servers that offer Multipath TCP (MPTCP). Debian already has updates, other distributions are following.", "zusammenfassung": "According to BleepingComputer, the IPv4 TCP code of the Linux kernel contains a use-after-free flaw caused by a race condition (CVE-2026-98432). Kernels as far back as version 4.4 are affected. The kernel's CVE team rates the flaw 9.8 out of 10, while Red Hat rates it only 5.9 because exploitation is complex and crashes are the main risk. Researchers from Anthropic demonstrated remote root access on servers with an MPTCP listener; according to the report, an unreleased Claude model created the exploit in around 53 minutes. Regular TCP is also affected, but code execution has not been shown there. Attacks in the wild have not been confirmed. Tricky: programs built with Go 1.24 or later enable MPTCP on Linux by default. The Go security team nevertheless recommends a kernel update rather than disabling MPTCP per program, and according to the report, simply disabling MPTCP is not enough anyway. Debian has released fixed kernels for Bookworm and Trixie; for Ubuntu, updates were in progress on 30 October. RHEL 8 to 10 are affected; SUSE, Oracle and Amazon Linux had some updates at that time. The flaw is fixed in kernel versions 6.1.190, 6.6.159, 6.12.113, 6.18.56 and 7.3, among others. Anyone running Linux servers should update the kernel promptly and reboot.", "weitere_links": ["oss-security: notice from the Go security team on MPTCP", "LWN.net: new stable kernels"], "_src": "d946d2fe"}, "2026-10-30-windows-insider-suche": {"titel": "Windows Insider builds: new search with sliders and phone actions, Beta sets app permissions individually", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11 tests new search with sliders and phone actions", "kurz": "In new Insider builds, Microsoft is testing a revamped Windows search. It shows sliders, for example for volume and brightness, directly in the results and can start calls or text messages via Phone Link. Beta build 26220.9836 also allows camera, microphone and location permissions per desktop app.", "zusammenfassung": "On 30 October, Microsoft released new Windows 11 Insider builds, including Beta 26220.9836 and Experimental 26340.9843. A new Windows search is starting in the Experimental channels. It shows sliders for volume, brightness or mouse pointer size directly in the results. Phone Link is meant to control calls, text messages and “Do not disturb” on the phone – initially with Android, with iPhone support due early next year. There are also more detailed results with file previews, web answers such as weather and stocks, and apps from the Store; this can be turned off under Privacy & security > Search. Results can be filtered and rated with thumbs up or down. For now, the search opens at the bottom centre; according to Microsoft, adapting it to the taskbar position is in the works. According to Windows Report, the Beta build also brings camera, microphone and location permissions for individual desktop apps, with previous decisions kept. As with all Insider features, it is unclear whether and when they will reach the regular version of Windows.", "weitere_links": ["Windows Report: Beta build 26220.9836 with per-app permissions"], "_src": "bbfec2ce"}, "2026-10-30-nova-lake-28c-prognose": {"titel": "Nova Lake-S with 28 cores: internal projection cites 16 to 33% more gaming performance", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Intel's next gaming CPU said to be up to 33% faster", "kurz": "According to VideoCardz, internal Intel projections promise 16 to 33 percent more gaming performance for Nova Lake-S than the Core Ultra 9 285K, depending on the variant. However, part of the lead comes from the faster DDR5-8000 memory used in the comparison. These are unconfirmed target values that may still change before launch.", "zusammenfassung": "According to VideoCardz, internal Intel projections from August 2026 show how much faster Nova Lake-S is supposed to be in games. The basis is Intel's own 'Gaming Index', compared against the Core Ultra 9 285K. A 28-core variant with a 285 W PL1 is said to be up to 1.16 times as fast as the 285K at 250 W. A variant with two compute tiles and 296 W is said to be up to 1.33 times as fast. Important: Nova Lake ran with DDR5-8000 via XMP, Arrow Lake only with DDR5-6400 – so part of the lead comes from the faster memory. Further claims by X user Haze, such as +8 percent single-thread without and +17 percent with a large last-level cache, have not been verified according to VideoCardz. Such early projections are target values and may still change before launch. Officially, Intel has so far only confirmed that Nova Lake is based on the 18A-P process and that more details will follow at CES in January.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Alleged internal Intel slides shared via third parties; not independently verified, targets may have changed.", "ursprungsquelle": "Haze (@Haze2K1) / alleged Intel slides", "_src": "6e13f4ff"}, "2026-10-30-rtx5080-marketplace": {"titel": "RTX 5080 disappears from NVIDIA's US store – after the RTX 5090", "schlagzeile": "First the RTX 5090, now the RTX 5080: NVIDIA's US store is emptying", "kurz": "The GeForce RTX 5080 has disappeared from NVIDIA's official marketplace in the US, a good two weeks after the RTX 5090. At US retailers, the cheapest RTX 5080 costs about twice its MSRP of 999 dollars. This does not prove an end of production, but supply is visibly tight.", "zusammenfassung": "The GeForce RTX 5080 has disappeared from NVIDIA's official marketplace in the US; Reddit users first noticed it in the filter list. The RTX 5090 had already been removed on 16 October, briefly reappeared at 5,599 US dollars and disappeared again – its MSRP is 1,999 dollars. On 28 October, the cheapest RTX 5080 cost 1,979.99 dollars at US retailers and 1,999.99 dollars at Best Buy, against an MSRP of 999 dollars. NVIDIA had previously denied that the RTX 5090 was discontinued. All cards in the RTX 50 series are currently selling well above MSRP. A card being dropped from the store does not by itself prove an end of production – but it does show how tight supply is.", "_src": "99a9c410"}, "2026-10-30-witcher4-sprecher": {"titel": "The Witcher 4: voice actors' statements fuel rumours about familiar characters", "schlagzeile": "Leak: are Dandelion and Yennefer returning in The Witcher 4?", "kurz": "Several voice actors have commented on The Witcher 4, sparking speculation about familiar characters. Dandelion's Polish voice actor says he has recorded a few lines, while Geralt's voice actor Doug Cockle has not recorded anything yet. CD Projekt RED has not commented.", "zusammenfassung": "According to ixbt.games, Geralt's voice actor Doug Cockle said on the Kinda Funny Games podcast in late October that he has not yet recorded anything for The Witcher 4 and does not know the scope of Geralt's role. He expects a supporting role rather than a lead. According to VGTimes, Jacek Kopczyński, the Polish voice of Dandelion, said at the PSX Extreme Party on 5 September that he has already recorded a few lines for The Witcher 4 – “not much”. For the also-announced project “Songs of the Past”, however, he has not recorded anything yet. According to Notebookcheck, a Reddit user reported that Yennefer's voice actress Denise Gough said at a signing session that she had recorded new dialogue involving Ciri; it is unclear for which project. In 2025, Gough had told Eurogamer that her involvement in The Witcher 4 was uncertain. CD Projekt RED has not commented on any of these statements. Officially confirmed: Ciri is the main character, and the game is coming to PC, PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. In August, co-CEO Michał Nowakowski named 2028 as the targeted release window. CD Projekt will present its next quarterly results on 24 November.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Statements by voice actors, partly only second-hand (Reddit, event reports) and partly unclear which project they recorded for; CD Projekt RED has confirmed nothing.", "ursprungsquelle": "Statements by the voice actors (Kinda Funny Games podcast, PSX Extreme Party 2026, signing session according to a Reddit user)", "weitere_links": ["VGTimes: Dandelion's voice actor has recorded lines for The Witcher 4", "Notebookcheck: Witcher 4 leak hints at return of popular character"], "_src": "9d06ea0f"}, "2026-10-30-amd-preiserhoehung": {"titel": "AMD reportedly raising Radeon and GDDR6 prices again in November", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Radeon cards could get more expensive again as soon as November", "kurz": "According to the Chinese retailer forum Board Channels, AMD raised Radeon wholesale prices in October and could follow up in November. Separately, graphics card prices rose by around 35 percent in three months according to Hardware Unboxed. AMD has not confirmed the planned increase.", "zusammenfassung": "According to information from the Chinese retailer forum Board Channels, AMD raised wholesale prices for Radeon GPUs on 1 October and could follow up in November. AMD reportedly reviews its prices quarterly. GDDR6 memory also became about 8 to 10 percent more expensive in the third quarter. Separately, Hardware Unboxed recorded graphics card prices in ten countries: over three months they rose by around 35 percent, by 10 percent in October alone. According to the data, the RX 9060 XT 16GB became 17 percent more expensive, and the RX 9070 and RX 9070 XT about 12 percent each. AMD has not confirmed the planned increase. Anyone who needs a graphics card should keep an eye on prices – the used market is likely to be affected too.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Retailer forum Board Channels; Hardware Unboxed's price data is documented, the planned AMD increase is not.", "ursprungsquelle": "Board Channels", "_src": "61551511"}, "2026-10-30-intel-q3-nova-lake-18a-p": {"titel": "Intel quarterly results: Nova Lake on 18A-P ahead of schedule, details at CES", "schlagzeile": "Intel steps on the gas: Nova Lake is ahead of schedule", "kurz": "On its third-quarter earnings call, Intel confirmed that Nova Lake will be the first client product on the 18A-P process and that development is ahead of schedule. Details are to follow at CES in January. However, Intel sees the PC market in a correction because of high memory prices.", "zusammenfassung": "On its earnings call for the third quarter of 2026 (29 October, US time), Intel confirmed that Nova Lake will be the first client product on the 18A-P process. Development is ahead of schedule, and Intel expects twice as many design wins as with Panther Lake. More details are to follow at CES in January. According to Intel, 18A yields are improving by double-digit percentages, and 18A-P is on track by the end of the year. At the same power, 18A-P is said to deliver about 9 percent more clock speed, or around 18 percent lower power at the same clock. For 14A, PDK 0.9 was released in October, version 1.0 follows in the first quarter of 2027, and production is planned for 2028. On the server side, Diamond Rapids arrives in 2027 on 18A-P and Coral Rapids in 2028 on 14A. Intel, however, sees the PC market in a correction until memory prices normalise – it expects the overall market to be around 10 percent smaller. According to Tom's Hardware, Intel is also taking Panther Lake capacity offline to build more Granite Rapids server CPUs.", "datum_hinweis": "Time estimated (published on the morning of 30 Oct)", "weitere_links": ["Transcript (The Motley Fool)", "Notes by harukaze5719 on X"], "_src": "728b9684"}, "2026-10-30-rtx5080-24gb": {"titel": "RTX 5080 with 24 GB said to arrive by January 2027 and replace the 16 GB version", "schlagzeile": "Leak: RTX 5080 with 24 GB said to arrive around the turn of the year", "kurz": "According to Board Channels, NVIDIA is planning a GeForce RTX 5080 with 24 instead of 16 GB, launching first in China between December 2026 and January 2027. The 16 GB version is to be phased out there. Name, clock speeds and price are unknown, and NVIDIA has confirmed nothing.", "zusammenfassung": "According to a report from the Chinese retailer forum Board Channels (ChannelGate), NVIDIA is planning a GeForce RTX 5080 with 24 GB of memory. It is to launch in China in December 2026 at the earliest and January 2027 at the latest. The current 16 GB version and the RTX 5090 D V2 are to be phased out there; the remaining stock of 16 GB GPUs is said to last about two more months. BenchLife had already reported a launch in the first quarter of 2027 on 12 October, but board partners had reportedly only received verbal hints. The 50 percent more memory would likely come from 3 GB GDDR7 modules on the same interface. Name, clock speeds and price are unknown. In early October, the X accounts hongxing2020 and MEGAsizeGPU had also speculated about the end of the 16 GB variant and of GB202 shipments for the RTX 5090, respectively. NVIDIA has confirmed none of this.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Retailer forum Board Channels (China) plus BenchLife; several sources, but no NVIDIA confirmation.", "ursprungsquelle": "Board Channels / BenchLife", "weitere_links": ["harukaze5719 on X", "hongxing2020 on X (10 Oct)", "MEGAsizeGPU on X (10 Oct)"], "_src": "60b93d53"}, "2026-10-29-windows11-kb5127936": {"titel": "Windows 11: optional update KB5127936 brings new context menu and cloud reinstall", "schlagzeile": "Windows 11: preview update brings new context menu and cloud repair", "kurz": "Microsoft has released the optional preview update KB5127936 with 41 changes for Windows 11 25H2 and 26H2. They include a faster, customisable context menu in File Explorer and a reinstall via Windows Update without a USB stick. The new features are to roll out to everyone from Patch Tuesday on 10 November.", "zusammenfassung": "On 28 October, Microsoft released the optional preview update KB5127936 for Windows 11 25H2 and 26H2; it contains no security fixes. According to BleepingComputer, the builds rise to 26200.9818 and 26300.9818 respectively, with 41 changes and fixes in total. The context menu in File Explorer is said to open faster and become customisable. “Cloud Rebuild” lets you reinstall Windows via Windows Update without a USB stick or ISO file – even if the system no longer boots. Xbox mode gets a revamped task view with a navigation bar, for example for “Go to desktop” and the power options. The “Privacy & security” settings page groups camera, microphone and location, and the WinRE recovery environment can use saved Wi-Fi profiles. Hibernation becomes adaptive: above 80 percent battery it kicks in less often, below 10 percent sooner. Because Secure Boot certificates are being updated, an additional restart may be required. The update is installed via Settings > Windows Update or the Microsoft Update Catalog. Microsoft is rolling out the features gradually, so they will not appear on every PC right away. According to Thurrott, the new features are to roll out to everyone from Patch Tuesday on 10 November.", "weitere_links": ["Microsoft Support: KB5127936 (builds 26300.9818 and 26200.9818)", "Thurrott: Week D preview updates for Windows 11"], "_src": "b3b29ee6"}, "2026-10-29-gta6-edge-polizei": {"titel": "GTA 6: Rockstar shows police with K-9 unit, scheduled buses and dynamic weather", "schlagzeile": "GTA 6: police with sniffer dogs, buses and trains on a timetable", "kurz": "In a cover story for the British magazine Edge, Rockstar revealed new details about GTA 6. The police track players via cameras, trackers in cars and witness tips, and there is also a K-9 unit. GTA 6 launches on 19 November 2026 for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S.", "zusammenfassung": "According to Polygon, Rob Nelson, co-studio head of Rockstar North, gave the British magazine Edge exclusive new details about Grand Theft Auto VI. The police are said to track players via their last sighting, surveillance cameras, trackers in cars and tips from passers-by. New is a K-9 unit: in the demo shown, a German shepherd caught Jason after a motorcycle crash. Pedestrians are said to have their own character traits – some flee, others attack. Buses and trains run on fixed routes according to a timetable; development director Phil Hooker said he places the greatest importance on them always arriving on time. The weather is dynamic, with clouds shaped by wind, humidity, fog, time of day and season. Rockstar itself pointed to the cover story in Edge issue 430 on X. According to Take-Two, GTA 6 launches on 19 November 2026 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. The Standard Edition costs 79.99 US dollars in the US, the Ultimate Edition 99.99 US dollars. The digital pre-load and the physical edition are planned from 12 November.", "weitere_links": ["Rockstar Games on X: pointer to the Edge cover story (30 Oct 2026)", "Take-Two: GTA VI pre-orders, date and prices"], "_src": "e7ef25df"}, "2026-10-28-galax-dementi": {"titel": "Rumour debunked: GALAX is not leaving the graphics card business", "schlagzeile": "GALAX shutting down? The manufacturer says clearly: no", "kurz": "A Spanish site had reported “exclusively” that GALAX was leaving the graphics card business. GALAX and partner Palit have officially denied this, and production continues as normal. Nothing changes for buyers of KFA2 cards, as GALAX is called in Europe.", "zusammenfassung": "The Spanish site El Chapuzas Informático had reported 'exclusively' that GALAX was leaving the GPU market due to a lack of NVIDIA chips and that Palit was closing the associated factory. GALAX denied this in an official statement: no production facilities had been closed, and business continues as normal. Palit, which shares factories with GALAX, also confirmed to media that production is continuing. A similar rumour had already circulated in April in connection with a restructuring under Palit's headquarters in Taiwan. Only on 22 October, GALAX had unveiled the RTX 5080 HOF Extreme. For buyers of KFA2 cards – as GALAX is called in Europe – nothing changes regarding warranty or support as things stand. The case shows why we label 'exclusive' single reports without a second source as unconfirmed.", "datum_hinweis": "Time estimated", "weitere_links": ["VideoCardz", "Tom's Hardware", "Original rumour (El Chapuzas Informático)"], "_src": "cf83f08b"}, "2026-10-25-ddr6-camm2": {"titel": "DDR6: 192-bit memory interfaces and CAMM2 instead of classic DIMMs", "schlagzeile": "DDR6 is coming – and classic RAM sticks could disappear", "kurz": "As things stand, DDR6 is set to use the flat CAMM2 format instead of classic DIMM sticks, and desktop CPUs are to get a 192-bit memory interface. Data rates from 8,800 to over 17,600 MT/s are mentioned. According to an SK Hynix roadmap, however, consumers should not expect DDR6 before 2030.", "zusammenfassung": "3DCenter has compiled what is known about the upcoming DDR6 standard and added an update on 25 October. DDR6 is to use PAM4 signalling and work with 24-bit-wide memory chips. A module would consist of four 24-bit channels, and CPU memory interfaces grow in 96-bit steps – typically to 192 bits on the desktop. CAMM2 is planned as the form factor instead of today's UDIMM and SO-DIMM sticks. Data rates from 8,800 to over 17,600 MT/s are mentioned. According to an SK Hynix roadmap, DDR6 is not expected before 2029 in servers and 2030 for consumers. The JEDEC specification is not yet final, and an alternative proposal with 16-bit channels is also being discussed.", "datum_hinweis": "Date of the update; time estimated", "_src": "eef0b055"}, "2026-10-02-core-ultra-4000-lineup": {"titel": "Core Ultra 4000 'Nova Lake-S': lineup topped by Core Ultra 9 4970K BFC", "schlagzeile": "Leak: Intel's 28-core flagship with huge cache said to hunt AMD's X3D chips", "kurz": "A leaked list names seven desktop CPUs in the Core Ultra 4000 series, topped by a Core Ultra 9 4970K with 28 cores and a large cache. The extra cache is seen as Intel's answer to AMD's X3D processors. Intel has not confirmed any model names, and details may still change.", "zusammenfassung": "In early October, a list of seven desktop processors from the upcoming Core Ultra 4000 series surfaced. At the top is a Core Ultra 9 4970K 'BFC' with 28 cores, a large last-level cache (bLLC) and 125 W base power, ranking even above the 4950K. The bLLC is seen as Intel's answer to AMD's X3D processors with 3D V-Cache. Well-known leaker kopite7kimi commented on the report on 13 October: the large cache is supposed to rescue Nova Lake's gaming performance, because the regular models without bLLC are about as fast as Arrow Lake in games. Intel itself has not named any models so far – officially, only the 18A-P process and an unveiling at CES are confirmed. Model names, core counts and TDP values may still change before launch.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "Lineup leak commented on by kopite7kimi (high reliability); not confirmed by Intel.", "weitere_links": ["kopite7kimi on X (13 Oct)"], "_src": "53d234c7"}, "2026-09-21-kopite-gr20x-2028": {"titel": "kopite7kimi: NVIDIA's GR20x generation not until 2028", "schlagzeile": "Leak: we'll probably have to wait until 2028 for NVIDIA's next gaming GPUs", "kurz": "Well-known leaker kopite7kimi writes that NVIDIA's GR20x chips are a 2028 product, meaning the next generation is slipping. For 2027, refreshes of the RTX 50 series would then be more likely. NVIDIA has not confirmed this timeline.", "zusammenfassung": "Well-known NVIDIA leaker kopite7kimi writes on X that the GR20x chips are a product for 2028 – meaning NVIDIA has postponed again. By the common reading, this refers to the gaming generation after Blackwell, which is likely to be named after NVIDIA's data centre architecture 'Rubin'. He also announced that he will post fewer updates until there is solid news, citing 'lessons learned' – apparently a reaction to changed plans in earlier leaks. Our take: for 2027, refreshes of the RTX 50 series would then be more likely, for example with more memory like the reported RTX 5080 24GB. NVIDIA itself has confirmed nothing about this timeline. Even with reliable leakers: dates shift more often than technical specs.", "zuverlaessigkeit_hinweis": "kopite7kimi has a long track record with NVIDIA leaks; timing claims, however, are less certain than technical details.", "ursprungsquelle": "kopite7kimi", "_src": "89b4f8c9"}};
